{"abstract":"The expansion of Carbon Capture, Utilization, and Storage (CCUS) highlights the growing need for carbon dioxide (CO2) pipeline transportation. While pure CO2 is non-corrosive, impurities such as H2O and NO2 create a corrosive environment that risks pipeline integrity. This study investigates how H2O and NO2 concentrations, along with temperature, influence corrosion under CO2 pipeline conditions. The investigation was performed in an autoclave setup emulating a linear velocity of 0.96 m/s at 100 bar and temperatures of 5 °C and 25 °C, testing X52 and GR70, and a more corrosion-resistant 9Cr alloy. The results indicated that the presence of NO2 elevated the corrosion rate compared to scenarios without. Low H2O concentration led to a corrosion rate of up to five times higher at 5 °C, compared to at 25 °C, in the presence of NO2. Low to moderate corrosion was observed for the carbon steels without NO2 and with 70 ppmv H2O at both temperatures. Reducing the H2O concentration below 70 ppmv and removing NO2, while SO2 and O2 are present, will only result in low to moderate corrosion in the carbon steel CO2 pipeline. The corrosion rate for X52 and GR70 was 0.065 mm/y and 0.016 mm/y higher or 5 and 3 times greater, respectively, at 5 °C compared to 25 °C. The study concludes that H2O should be maintained below 70 ppmv and NO2 should be eliminated to prevent severe corrosion. Emphasizing the importance of CO2 specification compliance and the need for further research into CO2 compositions that align with the specifications.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Simonsen, Kenneth René","Goebel, Jacalyn","Hansen, Dennis Severin","Pedersen, Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-804731"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CCUS","Corrosion","Pipeline","Transport"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the influence of temperature h000000000002o and no000000000002 on corrosion in co000000000002 transportation pipelines","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psep.2025.107190","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-804731","identifier":[{"id":"105002901888","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-164b879e-4c8e-440d-b4be-4df4f24be849"],"keyword":["CCUS","CO impurities","Corrosion","Dense CO","Pipeline","Transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DC1D0F3D3C27CC068F456352E35E0FB6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psep.2025.107190","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/776998180/Paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kenneth René","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"18f6d31b-80a4-4605-bd2a-548205326536","name":"Simonsen, Kenneth René","orcid":"0000-0001-6542-2085","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacalyn","key":"goebelpau","last":"Goebel","name":"Goebel, Jacalyn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dennis Severin","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3ef0fc7c-ea22-40da-ab21-a2a2e8e46c65","name":"Hansen, Dennis Severin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b784e2a8-004f-4040-80ad-fc67161cee9f","name":"Pedersen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-2928-7813","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.psep.2025.107190","issn":["09575820","17443598"],"issn_org":["09575820"],"journal":"Process Safety and Environmental Protection","paperid":"107190","publisher":"Institution of Chemical Engineers","status":"p","title":"Process Safety and Environmental Protection","volume":"198"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002901888"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-164b879e-4c8e-440d-b4be-4df4f24be849"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Influence of Temperature, H2O, and NO2 on Corrosion in CO2 Transportation Pipelines","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-804731","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Ischemic heart disease (IHD) has been linked to an increased risk of atrial fibrillation (AF). However, data are sparse regarding the role of IHD in AF recurrence after catheter ablation. Objective: We sought to investigate whether preexisting or new-onset IHD is associated with a greater risk of AF recurrence after ablation. Methods: With use of Danish nationwide registries, all patients undergoing first-time AF ablation in Denmark from 2010 to 2020 were identified. The primary outcome was AF recurrence defined by AF-related hospital admission or antiarrhythmic drug use within 1 year after ablation excluding a 3-month blanking period. IHD was defined as an International Classification of Diseases, Tenth Revision diagnosis of IHD or prior coronary revascularization. Results: Of 12,162 patients undergoing first-time ablation for AF (mean age, 62 years; 30% female), 20% had preexisting IHD. Preexisting IHD was associated with an increased risk of AF recurrence in univariable log-binomial logistic regression (relative risk, 1.09; 95% CI, 1.04–1.14; P < .001). However, after multivariable adjustment including procedural year, preexisting IHD was no longer associated with an increased risk of AF recurrence (relative risk, 1.02; 95% CI, 0.97–1.06; P = .42). In a nested case-control study of those without preexisting IHD before ablation (n = 9778), newly diagnosed IHD after ablation was associated with an increased risk of AF recurrence in multivariable analysis (hazard ratio, 3.03; 95% CI, 1.84–4.99; P < .001). Conclusion: The presence of IHD does not appear to reduce the effectiveness of AF ablation procedures. However, the emergence of IHD after AF ablation may serve as a trigger for AF that is insufficiently suppressed by prior ablation.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Espersen, Caroline","Modin, Daniel","Johansen, Niklas Dyrby","Janstrup, Kira Hyldekær","Johannessen, Arne","Hansen, Jim","Eskesen, Kristian","Iversen, Allan Zeeberg","Worck, René H.","Ruwald, Martin H.","Hansen, Morten Lock","Gislason, Gunnar","San José Estépar, Raúl","Marcus, Gregory M.","Biering-Sørensen, Tor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811323"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","University of California San Francisco"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Catheter ablation","Ischemic heart disease","Nationwide cohort study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic importance of ischemic heart disease for patients with atrial fibrillation undergoing catheter ablation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-811323","identifier":[{"id":"85203811166","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39147302","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e64a14ef-b979-4758-b39b-8dd0b3db526a"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Atrial fibrillation recurrence","Catheter ablation","Ischemic heart disease","Nationwide cohort study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4ADA8D370EABA3A77D6673FD3E2567AB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-