27","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Damgaard","key":"sandahlpau","last":"Sandahl","locid":"bd08d3a7-55c4-4273-9c7c-68cbc546c563","name":"Sandahl, Thomas Damgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9807-6852","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"27 28","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bettina E","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"77224394-0003-4d98-90b3-d8f796214c58","name":"Hansen, Bettina","name_org":"Hansen, Bettina E","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40742203"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/liv.70251","issn":["13991698","14783223"],"issn_org":["14783223"],"issue":"9","journal":"Liver International","paperid":"e70251","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Liver International","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105012789322"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ac7ee29d-e448-4458-95a8-62ac545a200d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Phenotypic Divergence of JAG1- and NOTCH2-Associated Alagille Syndrome &amp; Disease-Specific NOTCH2 Variant Classification Guidelines","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-826096","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) is a major public health problem. This study aims to describe the international variations in the practices related to the initiation, termination, and refraining from resuscitation of adult patients (≥18 years) with a non-traumatic OHCA. Methods: An exploratory descriptive study was conducted using a cross-sectional online survey. The respondents were recruited using snowball sampling technique. Framework analysis was used to identify key themes in responses, with descriptive statistics summarising data trends. Results: The study collected responses from 59 countries. Our findings reveal that respondents from 59.3% of countries reported that they initiate resuscitation in all cases where the patients do not show obvious signs of irreversible death or do not have confirmed advance directives. Respondents from 15.3% of countries reported that once started, prehospital resuscitation attempts are not terminated. Prehospitally respondents from 20.3% of the countries reported that they rely exclusively on specific criteria to decide when to terminate resuscitation efforts while in 45.8%, these decisions are made at the discretion of the provider. Respondents from most countries (91.5%) reported that they refrain from resuscitation in the presence of obvious signs of irreversible death. Respondents from 57.6% of countries, reported that they refrained from resuscitation if the patient had a confirmed do-not-attempt-cardiopulmonaryresuscitation (DNACPR), while 15.3% mentioned staff safety as a reason to abstain from attempting resuscitation. Conclusion: This study reveals global variation in EMS resuscitation practices, reflecting disparities in resources, healthcare infrastructure, EMS system design, community acceptability given cultural and societal norms, and legislation.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Kjær, Jeannett","Milling, Louise","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Lippert, Freddy","Blomberg, Stig Nikolaj","Christensen, Helle Collatz","Holgate, Robyn","Morrison, Laurie J.","Bakhsh, Abdullah","Mikkelsen, Søren","Alsulimani, Loui K.","Popela, Stanislav","Vidunová, Jana Kruba","Peran, David","Gregor, Roman","Papousek, René","Simić, Anđela","Cairol, Andrés","Ingelmo, Vicente Sánchez Brunete","Björnsson, Hjalti Már","Stammet, Pascal","Escalante-Kanashiro, Raffo","Nikolaidou, Olympia","Karageorgos, Vlasios","Aslanidis, Theodoros","Wallner, Bernd","Rief, Martin","Eichinger, Michael","Chakra Rao, Siddha S.C.","SinghMD, Baljit","Birkun, Alexei A.","Aguilera, Pablo","Bakker, Jan","Zaher, Muhammad Sultan","Alwajeeh, Sultan Ali","Tanabe, Seizan","Iwami, Taku","Saito, Shunsuke","Fraga-Sastrias, Juan Manuel","Kittivo, June Eva","Achiro, Kephas Ochieng","Ndinda, Caroline","Monsieurs, Koen","Jacobsen, Lars","Hansen, Troels Martin","Steinmetz, Jacob","Lunen, Thomas Bech","Bach, Vagn","Lohse, Nicolai"],"cuid":["S02-089.97-822942"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Global Prehospital Resuscitation Network","The Global Prehospital Resuscitation Network"],"corresponding_author":["Kjær, Jeannett"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Canada","Chile","Costa Rica","Croatia","Czechia","Greece","Greenland","Iceland","India","Japan","Kenya","Luxembourg","Mexico","Norway","Peru","Saudi Arabia","South Africa","Ukraine"],"glorg":["Al-Malae'b St","Al-Malae’b St, Jeddah 22254, Saudi Arabia","All Global Affiliations","Asesores en Emergencias","Chairman Indian Resuscitation Council Federation","Charles University","County Government of Turkana","EMS South Moravian region","EMS of Moravian-Silesian Region","EMS of Pilsen Region","ER24","ER24, Emergency Management Services, 25 Du Toit Street, Stellenbosch 7600, South Africa","Educational Ins