lism","paperid":"155760","publisher":"WB  Saunders","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders","status":"p","title":"Metabolism","title_org":"Metabolism: Clinical and Experimental","volume":"152"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180311452"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5ded36fc-293f-452c-bc55-7ec3759d8002","au-84504f65-4e4c-460a-9e1a-138fbd7ee925","ku-274a2ec8-2733-4639-a0dd-edc966dd0e5f","sdu-16fa74e1-622b-4320-8fd5-62314d9688e0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Plasma proteome profiling reveals metabolic and immunologic differences between Anorexia Nervosa subtypes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-093.68-724163","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Transportation of CO₂ is essential for multiple applications in Carbon Capture, Utilisation and Storage (CCUS), e.g., for utilisation in methanol production, enhanced oil recovery, or permanent storage. Currently, the CCUS industry is still in its fancy, and the transportation regulation is still defined from project to project, where the existing quality specifications are tailored to the specific storage or utilisation site. It is estimated that transportation accounts for ~25% of the total costs of a CCUS project, and commercialisation cannot be achieved with an infrastructure of high-grade steel together with high purity CO₂. The current transportation infrastructure is based on point-to-point transport, where it is believed that it will be challenging to upscale CCUS without a common quality standard. This leaves a knowledge gap in the design, operation, and investment of CO₂ transportation. This study includes an evaluation of the challenges that halt the progression in CO₂ transportation based on a survey of the literature. Analysing the benefit of establishing an international quality standard for CO₂ transportation for CCUS to become a global industry. A detailed description of the initiative policies within CCUS along with the challenges associated with designing the CO₂ transportation infrastructure, which arises when chemical reactions form corrosive or scaling compounds. As a result, this study proposes a future action plan to make CO₂ transport more feasible by forming a common CO₂ quality specification and a material selection based on CO₂ quality.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Simonsen, Kenneth René","Hansen, Dennis Severin","Pedersen, Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705833"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Simonsen, Kenneth René"],"keyword":["CCS","CCUS","CO transport","Power to X","Quality standard","Transportation cost"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenges in co transportation trends and perspectives","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2023.114149","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The research was funded by Innovation Fund Denmark through the 3-P6 CarbonAdapt project."],"id":"S01-000.00-705833","identifier":[{"id":"85183472370","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b784e124-fa78-44d4-a463-95b843350ea8"],"keyword":["CCS","CCUS","CO quality","CO transport","Power-to-X","Quality standard","Transportation cost"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A489B8B31C409DB0D432603871FDD3A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/610201011/1-s2.0-S1364032123010079-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2023.114149","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kenneth René","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"18f6d31b-80a4-4605-bd2a-548205326536","name":"Simonsen, Kenneth René","orcid":"0000-0001-6542-2085","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dennis Severin","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3ef0fc7c-ea22-40da-ab21-a2a2e8e46c65","name":"Hansen, Dennis Severin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b784e2a8-004f-4040-80ad-fc67161cee9f","name":"Pedersen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-2928-7813","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.rser.2023.114149","issn":["13640321","18790690"],"issn_org":["13640321"],"journal":"Renewable and Sustainable Energy Reviews","paperid":"114149","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Renewable and Sustainable Energy Reviews","volume":"191"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183472370"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b784e124-fa78-44d4-a463-95b843350ea8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Challenges in CO₂ transportation : Trends and perspectives","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705833","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Guidelines recommend prioritizing treatment with antiarrhythmic drugs before referral of patients with atrial fibrillation to ablation, delaying a potential subsequent ablation. However, delaying ablation may affect ablation outcomes. We sought to investigate the impact of duration from diagnosis to ablation on the risk of atrial fibrillation recurrence and adverse events. METHODS AND RESULTS: Using Danish nationwide registries, all patients with first-time ablation for atrial fibrillation were identified and included from 2010 to 2018. Patients were divided into 4 groups by diagnosis-to-ablation time: <1.0 year (early ablation), 1.0 to 1.9 years, 2.0 to 2.9 years, and >2.9 years (late ablation). The primary end point was atrial fibrillation recurrence after the 90-day blanking period, defined by admission for atrial fibrillation, cardioversions, use of antiarrhythmic drugs, or repeat atrial fibrillation ablations. The secondary end point was a composite end point of heart failure, ischemic stroke, or death, and each event individually. The study cohort consisted of 7705 patients. The 5-year cumulative incidence of atrial fibrillation recurrence in the 4 groups was 42.9%, 54.8%, 55.9%, and 58.4%, respectively. Hazard ratios were 1.20 (95% CI, 1.07-1.35), 1.29 (95% CI, 1.13-1.47), and 1.40 (95% CI, 1.28-1.53), respectively, with the early ablation group as reference. The hazard ratio for the combined secondary end point was 1.22 (95% CI, 1.04-1.44) in the late ablation group compared with the early ablation group. CONCLUSIONS: In patients undergoing ablation for atrial fibrillation, early ablation was associated with a significantly lower risk of atrial fibrillation recurrence. Furthermore, the associated risk of heart failure, ischemic stroke, or death was significantly lower in early-compared with late-ablation patients.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Tønnesen, Jacob","Ruwald, Martin H.","Pallisgaard, Jannik","Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","Johannessen, Arne","Hansen, Jim","Worck, Rene H.","Zörner, Christopher R.","Riis-Vestergaard, Lise","Middelfart, Charlotte","Sørensen, Samuel K.","Sattler, Stefan","Gislason, Gunnar","Hansen, Morten Lock"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730845"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ablation","Atrial fibrillation","Recurrence of atrial fibrillation","diagnosis to ablation time"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lower recurrence rates of atrial fibrillation and mace events after early compared to late ablation a danish nationwide register study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.123.032722","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730845","identifier":[{"id":"38533962","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11179760","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85189751718","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-37f29baa-5847-4ebe-a259-eef3346861c5"],"keyword":["ablation","atrial fibrillation","diagnosis‐to‐ablation time","recurrence of atrial fibrillation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B38494AD6356C6BDA8305866F1384523"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/388946529/t_nnesen_et_al_2024_lower_recurrence_rates_of_atrial_fibrillation_and_mace_events_after_early_compared_to_late_ablation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.123.032722","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region 