"first":"Pavel F.","key":"kuznetsovpavelfpau","last":"Kuznetsov","name":"Kuznetsov, Pavel F.","rank":136,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"48","first":"Alexey A.","key":"tishkinalexeyapau","last":"Tishkin","name":"Tishkin, Alexey A.","rank":137,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Patrick","key":"winckerpatrickpau","last":"Wincker","name":"Wincker, Patrick","rank":138,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"30","first":"Katherine","key":"kannekatherinepau","last":"Kanne","name":"Kanne, Katherine","rank":139,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"30","first":"Alan","key":"outramalanpau","last":"Outram","name":"Outram, Alan","rank":140,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ludovic","key":"orlandoludovicpau","last":"Orlando","name":"Orlando, Ludovic","rank":141,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38843826"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-024-07597-5","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"8022","journal":"Nature","pages":"819-825","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"631"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196261598"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-38ed3e0b-107b-494c-91d2-11aef7f8764b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Widespread horse-based mobility arose around 2200 bce in Eurasia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759766","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background/Objectives: Co-delivering dual-drug systems have proven to be effective in, for example, anticancer therapy or HIV prophylaxis due to a higher target selectivity and therapeutic efficacy from compound synergism. However, various challenges regarding physical stability can arise during the formulation definition when multiple drug compounds are included in the same formulation. In this work, the focus was on aqueous suspensions, which could be applied as long-acting injectable formulations to release the drug compounds over weeks to months after administration. Methods: It was possible to gain insights into dual-drug nano- and microsuspensions containing two acidic compounds (indomethacin and naproxen) prepared by milling with dual centrifugation. Information regarding the physical stability of individual suspensions was subtracted and compared to dual-drug suspensions when prepared with the same milling conditions and stored at elevated temperatures of 40 °C. Results: Distinct particle size profiles after milling were obtained dependent on the stabilizer used in both individual and dual-drug suspensions. Most notably, the combination of indomethacin and naproxen in one formulation resulted in smaller sizes of drug particles compared to individual suspensions under the presence of some stabilizers. The obtained particle size profiles further indicated that at least one of the model compounds needed to be sufficiently stabilized from a stabilizer to obtain physically stable dual-drug suspensions over 28 days when stored at 40 °C. Similarly, the particle size distribution was dependent on the individual distribution of the suspensions, which showed a monomodal distribution could be achieved for dual-drug suspensions when at least one of the individual suspensions demonstrated a monomodal distribution in the presence of the stabilizer alone. Over a 28-day period, the smallest particle size was obtained in dual-drug suspensions stabilized with a combination of polysorbate 85 and poloxamer 338 compared to dual-drug suspensions stabilized with only a single stabilizer during preparation, indicating tendencies towards stabilization synergism from a combination of stabilizers as well as the model compounds. Conclusion: Overall, the study showed insights into the preparation and physical stability of dual-drug suspensions containing indomethacin and naproxen.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zulbeari, Nadina","Hansen, Signe Malig","Holm, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-792287"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Holm, René"],"keyword":["Dual centrifuge","Long acting injectables","Media milling","Nano and microsuspensions","Physical stability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"two in one size characterization and accelerated short term physical stability of dual drug suspensions with two acidic compounds indomethacin and naproxen","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/pharmaceutics16121495","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-792287","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11676886","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85213329703","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39771474","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-f6c25857-e850-43a4-bb53-341260ea7169"],"keyword":["dual centrifuge","dual compound","long acting injectables","media milling","nano- and microsuspensions","physical stability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CD9518DDD1DC81635445A6232EBB49B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/280852585/pharmaceutics-16-01495.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/pharmaceutics16121495","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy, Chemistry and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadina","key":"zulbearipau","last":"Zulbeari","locid":"8e968584-2e62-4bc3-808b-e946a595354d","name":"Zulbeari, Nadina","orcid":"0009-0005-3609-5042","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Malig","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"4ff49add-7cfc-4961-969b-7949d8d4bfb5","name":"Hansen, Signe Malig","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"2b25cebf-dae4-4529-b115-f80b158ab957","name":"Holm, René","orcid":"0000-0003-4894-7765","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39771474"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/pharmaceutics16121495","issn":["19994923"],"issue":"12","journal":"Pharmaceutics","paperid":"1495","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Pharmaceutics","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85213329703"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f6c25857-e850-43a4-bb53-341260ea7169"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Two in One : Size Characterization and Accelerated Short-Term Physical Stability of Dual-Drug Suspensions with Two Acidic Compounds (Indomethacin and Naproxen)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-792287","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background Genetic susceptibility to inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) has been widely studied, whereas the genetic contribution to disease progression over time remains largely unknown. In a unique population-based cohort, we explored if genetic susceptibility to IBD associated with disease course severity. Methods In a Danish nationwide cohort of 3688 patients with Crohn’s disease (CD), 4491 patients with ulcerative colitis (UC), and 9469 controls, we estimated polygenic scores (PGS) for IBD susceptibility. We then investigated the association between susceptibility PGS and severe versus less severe disease courses. Patients were categorized as having a severe disease course if needing I) at least two IBD-related hospitalizations exceeding two days, II) at least two IBD-related major surgeries, III) one hospitalization and one major surgery not overlapping in time, or IV) total use of minimum 5000 mg systemic corticosteroids within the first three years of diagnosis. Secondary analyses explored the association with other severity measures including inflammatory markers, exposure to biologics and immunomodulators, and time to hospitalization and major IBD-related surgery. Statistical analyses included logistic, linear, and Cox proportional hazards regression, and predictive modeling using random forest. Findings Patients with severe disease courses had higher susceptibility PGS than patients with less severe disease courses (CD: OR=1·27, P=7·73×10−10, UC: OR=1·35, P=7·29×10−17 per SD increase in susceptibility PGS). When comparing the highest versus lowest PGS quintile, we observed a hazard ratio (HR) for major surgery of 2·74 (P=7·19×10−18) in patients with CD and 2·04 (P=4·36×10−7) in patients with UC. A higher susceptibility PGS was also associated with longer and more frequent hospitalizations, higher levels of C-reactive protein, decreased hemoglobin, and a higher need for corticosteroids, immunomodulators, and biologic therapies. Interpretation Patients with a higher genetic burden for developing IBD also experience a more severe disease course, suggesting a shared genetic architecture between disease susceptibility and severity.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Vestergaard, Marie Vibeke","Allin, Kristine H.","Nøhr, Anne Krogh","Lominchar, Jesus Vicente Torresano","Christensen, Heidi Søgaard","Krarup, Henrik","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Jacobsen, Henrik Albæk","Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","Bækvad-Hansen, Marie","Brøndum, Rasmus Froberg","Bøgsted, Martin","Larsen, Lone","Sazonovs, Aleksejs","Jess, Tine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805194"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Vestergaard, Marie Vibeke"],"keyword":["Allergy and Immunology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic risk of inflammatory bowel disease is associated with disease course severity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.11.01.24316569","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-805194","ids":["aau-81694fb2-43d9-480f-9782-1bfc523252d4"],"keyword":["allergy and immunology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-23C4CE8A6EB355BEA9CAFED77795F7F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.11.01.24316569","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for Molecular Prediction of Inflammatory Bowel Disease"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Vibeke","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"13392224-0850-4c5f-941f-d3249a366824","name":"Vestergaard, Marie Vibeke","orcid":"0009-0006-1409-1945","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristine Højgaard","key":"allinpau","last":"Allin","locid":"eaf730c8-2c38-4a9c-ab42-d8a01518f4f2","name":"Allin, Kristine H.","name_org":"Allin, Kristine Højgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-6880-5759","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Krogh","key":"nøhrpau","last":"Nøhr","locid":"86da955c-89a5-4127-90c7-2ef61a6eb0fd","name":"Nøhr, Anne Krogh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesus Vicente Torresano","key":"lomincharpau","last":"Lominchar","locid":"a71c3be5-000e-4610-b404-05477c1a5cdd","name":"Lominchar, Jesus Vicente Torresano","orcid":"0009-0009-9356-1504","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"cou