, Laura","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter-Martin","key":"kraruppau","last":"Krarup","name":"Krarup, Peter-Martin","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","name":"Pfeiffer, Per","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"qvortruppau","last":"Qvortrup","name":"Qvortrup, Camilla","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39692004"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/sla.0000000000006611","issn":["00034932","15281140"],"issn_org":["00034932"],"journal":"Annals of Surgery","paperid":"10.1097/SLA.0000000000006611","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"e","title":"Annals of Surgery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212944416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["aau-f4826155-7b8b-42aa-aeeb-f44a539e4ead","au-e038ae03-ffe3-4334-b2cf-e479248056cc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Neoadjuvant Pembrolizumab in Stage I-III Deficient Mismatch Repair Colon Cancer: A Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.84-784965","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Social trust is a heritable trait that has been linked with physical health and longevity. In this study, we performed genome-wide association studies of self-reported social trust in n = 33,882 Danish blood donors. We observed genome-wide and local evidence of genetic similarity with other brainrelated phenotypes and estimated the single nucleotide polymorphism-based heritability of trust to be 6% (95% confidence interval = (2.1, 9.9)). In our discovery cohort (n = 25,819), we identified one significantly associated locus (lead variant: rs12776883) in an intronic enhancer region of PLPP4, a gene highly expressed in brain, kidneys, and testes. However, we could not replicate the signal in an independent set of donors who were phenotyped a year later (n = 8063). In the subsequent metaanalysis, we found a second significantly associated variant (rs71543507) in an intergenic enhancer region. Overall, our work confirms that social trust is heritable, and provides an initial look into the genetic factors that influence it.","author_count":38,"contributors":["Sequeros, Celia Burgos","Hansen, Thomas","Westergaard, David","Louloudis, Ioannis","Kalamajski, Sebastian","Röder, Timo","Rohde, Palle Duun","Schwinn, Michael","Clemmensen, Line Katrine Harder","Didriksen, Maria","Nyegaard, Mette","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Erikstrup, Christian","Mikkelsen, Susan","Sørensen, Erik","Banasik, Karina","Bay, Jakob","Boldsen, Jens Kjærgaard","Brodersen, Thorsten","Brunak, Søren","Burgdorf, Kristoffer","Chalmer, Mona Ameri","Didriksen, Maria","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Dowsett, Joseph","Erikstrup, Christian","Feenstra, Bjarke","Geller, Frank","Gudbjartsson, Daniel","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Hindhede, Lotte","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jacobsen, Rikke Louise","Jemec, Gregor","Jensen, Bitten Aagaard","Kaspersen, Katrine","Kjerulff, Bertram Dalskov","Kogelman, Lisette","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Louloudis, Ioannis","Lundgaard, Agnete","Mikkelsen, Susan","Mikkelsen, Christina","Nissen, Ioanna","Nyegaard, Mette","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Pedersen, Ole Birger Vestager","Pil Henriksen, Alexander","Rohde, Palle Duun","Rostgaard, Klaus","Schwinn, Michael","Stefansson, Kari","Stefánsson, Hreinn","Sørensen, Erik","Thorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Topholm Bruun, Mie","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas","Westergaard, David","Pedersen, Ole Birger Vestager","Brunak, Søren","Banasik, Karina","Giordano, Giuseppe Nicola"],"cuid":["S05-091.69-724413"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genomic Consortium","Danish Blood Donor Study Genomic Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Banasik, Karina"],"country":["Iceland","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","deCODE Genetics"],"keyword":["Blood Donors","Denmark","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Wide Association Study","Humans","Phenotype","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Statistics Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a genome wide association study of social trust in 000000000033 000000000882 danish blood donors","src":["aau","au","dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-51636-0","version":"Published Version"},"fun