-s2.0-85182480285"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fa7612ed-04a9-4ea6-b6f2-7d1c9d82f691","au-bbcae93d-c8b2-4b79-818d-5827389dda88","dtu-bccf0810-e40c-4182-843f-11d3cdfce956","ku-51141d7c-acf1-466d-a3c9-3fd35c1516d7","sdu-2dc6a5cd-98bc-4ec2-a16b-65f0936fc2a6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A genome‑wide association study of social trust in 33,882 Danish blood donors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-091.69-724413","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In the summer of 2020, ESA changed the orbit of CryoSat-2 to align periodically with NASA's ICESat-2 mission, a campaign known as CRYO2ICE, which allows for near-coincident CryoSat-2 and ICESat-2 observations in space and time over the Arctic until summer 2022, where the CRYO2ICE Antarctic campaign was initiated. This study investigates the Arctic CRYO2ICE radar and laser freeboards acquired by CryoSat-2 and ICESat-2, respectively, during the winter seasons of 2020–2022, and derives snow depths from their differences along the orbits. Along-track snow depth observations can provide high-resolution snow depth distributions which are vital for air-ice-ocean heat and momentum transfer, understanding light transmission, and snow-ice-interactions. Generally, ICESat-2 is backscattered at a surface above the elevation of the CryoSat-2 signal. CRYO2ICE snow depths are thinner than the daily model- or passive-microwave-based snow depth composites used for comparison, with differences being most pronounced in the Atlantic and Pacific Arctic. Satellite-derived and model-based snow estimates show similar seasonal accumulation over first-year ice, but CRYO2ICE has limited seasonal accumulation over multi-year ice which is linked to a slow increase in ICESat-2, and to some extent CryoSat-2, freeboards. We present a first estimation of spaceborne along-track snow depth estimates with average uncertainty of 10–11 ± 2–3 cm for 7-km segments, with random and systematic contributions of 7 and 4 cm. These observations show the potential for along-track dual-frequency observations of snow depth from the future Copernicus mission CRISTAL; but they also highlight uncertainties in radar penetration and the correlation length scales of snow topography that still require further research.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fredensborg Hansen, Renée Mie","Skourup, Henriette","Rinne, Eero","Høyland, Knut V.","Landy, Jack C.","Merkouriadi, Ioanna","Forsberg, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738152"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fredensborg Hansen, Renée Mie"],"country":["Finland","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Finnish Meteorological Institute","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","University Centre in Svalbard","University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway"],"keyword":["CRYO2ICE","CryoSat 2","ICESat 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"arctic freeboard and snow depth from near coincident cryosat 000000000002 and icesat 000000000002 cryo000000000002ice observations a first examination of winter sea ice during 000000002020 000000002022","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2023EA003313","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-738152","identifier":[{"id":"85190835851","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-06d4c596-9ab5-4438-bfd4-a5d5708cc096"],"keyword":["CRISTAL","CRYO2ICE","CryoSat-2","ICESat-2","Sea ice topography","Snow depth on sea ice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F69726978ACC2A16E1CF33E7FC2367A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/360090329/Earth_and_Space_Science_-_2024_-_Fredensborg_Hansen_-_Arctic_Freeboard_and_Snow_Depth_From_Near_Coincident_CryoSat_2_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2023EA003313","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Geodesy and Earth Observation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university centre in svalbard","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University Centre in Svalbard","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"university of tromsø the arctic university of norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fi","key":"finnish meteorological institute","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Finnish Meteorological Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Renée M.","key":"fredensborghansenpau","last":"Fredensborg Hansen","locid":"fb1ad80c-3a89-42f9-8d80-293328b301e6","name":"Fredensborg Hansen, Renée Mie","name_org":"Fredensborg Hansen, Renée M.","orcid":"0000-0002-3426-347X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henriette","key":"skouruppau","last":"Skourup","locid":"f5fe613f-20e5-4a69-9eff-f03779801182","name":"Skourup, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-4468-8033","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eero","key":"rinnepau","last":"Rinne","name":"Rinne, Eero","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Knut V.","key":"høylandpau","last":"Høyland","name":"Høyland, Knut V.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jack C.","key":"landypau","last":"Landy","name":"Landy, Jack C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ioanna","key":"merkouriadipau","last":"Merkouriadi","name":"Merkouriadi, Ioanna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1029/2023ea003313","issn":["23335084"],"issue":"4","journal":"Earth and Space Science","paperid":"e2023EA003313","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Earth and Space Science","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190835851"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-06d4c596-9ab5-4438-bfd4-a5d5708cc096"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Arctic Freeboard and Snow Depth From Near-Coincident CryoSat-2 and ICESat-2 (CRYO2ICE) Observations : A First Examination of Winter Sea Ice During 2020–2022","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738152","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Coronary computed tomography angiography (CCTA) is recommended as the first-line diagnostic imaging modality in low-to-intermediate-risk individuals suspected of stable coronary artery disease (CAD). However, CCTA exposes patients to ionizing radiation and potentially nephrotoxic contrast agents. Invasive coronary angiography is the gold-standard investigation to guide coronary revascularisation strategy; however, invasive procedures incur an inherent risk to the patient. Coronary magnetic resonance angiography (CMRA) avoids these issues. Nevertheless, clinical implementation is currently limited due to extended scanning durations, inconsistent image quality, and consequent lack of diagnostic accuracy. Several technical CMRA innovations, including advanced respiratory motion correction with 100% scan efficiency (no data rejection), fast image acquisition with motion-corrected undersampled image reconstruction, and deep-learning–based automated planning, have been implemented and now await clinical validation in multi-center trials. Methods: The objective of the image navigator–based, automated CMRA prospective multi-center study is to evaluate the diagnostic accuracy of a newly developed, state-of-the-art, standardized, and automated CMRA framework compared to CCTA in 201 patients undergoing clinical investigation for CAD. The study protocol mandates the administration of oral beta-blockers to decrease heart rate to below 60 bpm and the use of sublingual nitroglycerine spray to induce vasodilation. Additionally, the study incorporates the utilization of standardized postprocessing with sliding-thin-slab multiplanar reformatting, in combination with evaluation of the source images, to optimize the visualization of coronary artery stenosis. Discussion: If proven effective, CMRA could provide a non-invasive, needle-free, yet also clinically viable, alternative to CCTA. Trial Registration: This study is registered at ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05473117).","author_count":16,"contributors":["Wood, Gregory","Hajhosseiny, Reza","Pedersen, Alexandra Uglebjerg","Littlewood, Simon","Hansen, Tina Juul","Neji, Radhouene","Kunze, Karl P.","Wetzl, Jens","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Maeng, Michael","Madsen, Per Lav","Vejlstrup, Niels","Prieto, Claudia","Botnar, René M.","Kim, Won Yong"],"cuid":["S02-093.04-767801"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Botnar, René M."],"country":["Chile","Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","King's College London","Millenium Institute for Intelligent Healthcare Engineering","Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile","Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile","Siemens","Siemens Healthcare Limited","Siemens Healthineers/Healthcare (Germany)","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Coronary artery disease","Coronary magnetic resonance angiography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"image navigator based automated coronary magnetic resonance angiography for the detection of coronary artery stenosis","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jocmr.2024.101097","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.04-767801","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11647470","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39293786","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85210534535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b5fb47bd-fbcc-4a49-97df-9d0516696ca9","ku-6f0931f7-7651-4172-8f61-5d84446195c0"],"keyword":["Coronary artery disease","Coronary magnetic resonance angiography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EC2031287A3A717A9176318A03613462"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jocmr.2024.101097","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/414296060/1_s2.0_S1097664724011244_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's College London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"siemens healthcare limited","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Siemens Healthcare Limited","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"siemens healthineers healthcare","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Siemens Healthineers/Healthcare (Germany)","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"siemens","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Siemens","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"ku