René M.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Won Yong","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","locid":"5124a60e-0d6b-4fce-947f-75ec72c482e6","name":"Kim, Won Yong","orcid":"0000-0003-1302-1671","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39293786"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jocmr.2024.101097","issn":["10976647","1532429X"],"issn_org":["10976647"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Magnetic Resonance","pages":"101097","paperid":"101097","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Magnetic Resonance","title_org":"Journal of cardiovascular magnetic resonance : official journal of the Society for Cardiovascular Magnetic Resonance","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85210534535"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b5fb47bd-fbcc-4a49-97df-9d0516696ca9","ku-6f0931f7-7651-4172-8f61-5d84446195c0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Image navigator–based, automated coronary magnetic resonance angiography for the detection of coronary artery stenosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.04-767801","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This study aimed to determine the compatibility of pre-fermented sugar beet pulp to support the growth of Pleurotus ostreatus mycelium in submerged fermentation. The goal was to create a meat alternative based on mycelial-fermented pulp. It was further explored whether pre-fermentation with lactic acid bacteria (LAB) on the pulp increased meat-like properties, such as aroma, springiness, and hardness, in the final product. Three strains were selected from a high throughput screening of 105 plant-derived LAB based on their acidification and metabolite production in the pulp. Two homofermentative strains (Lactococcus lactis) and one heterofermentative strain (Levilactobacillus brevis) were selected based on their low ethanol production, high lactic acid production, and overall acidification of the pulp. Mycelium of P. ostreatus was grown in submerged fermentations on the pre-fermented pulp, and the biomass was removed by centrifugation. The fungal strain consumed all available sugars and acids and released arabinose to the media. Volatiles were detected using GC–MS, and a large increase in concentrations of hexanal, 1-octen-3-ol, and 2-octenal was measured. Concentration of 1-octen-3-ol was lower in the pre-fermented samples vs. the non-pre-fermented. LC-MS amino acid analysis showed the presence of all essential amino acids on day 0 and 7 of fermentation. The highest concentration of amino acids was for glutamic acid/glutamine and aspartic acid/asparagine. A decrease in all amino acids after 7 days of fungal fermentation was measured for all fermentations. The decrease was more significant for pre-fermented samples. This was also confirmed through a total protein determination, except for samples pre-fermented with Lactococcus lactis strain NFICC142 which increased in total protein content after fungal fermentation. The protein digestibility increased after fungal fermentation, and the highest increase was seen for non-pre-fermented samples. The springiness of the fermented product indicated similarities to meat alternatives, while the hardness was much lower than other meat alternatives. The results indicate that dried sugar beet pulp can be used for submerged cultivation of P. ostreatus, but that pre-fermentation does not improve the physical or nutritional properties of the end product significantly, except for an increased protein content for NFICC142 pre-fermented media. This is the first known attempt to use LAB and P. ostreatus in mixed fermentation to produce fungal mycelium, as well as the first attempt at using SBP in a liquid fermentation for mycelial production of P. ostreatus.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Madsen, Sanne Kjærulf","Tomasikova, Frantiska","Hansen, Mikkel","Shetty, Radhakrishna","Jansen, Celia L.","Jacobsen, Charlotte","Hobley, Timothy John","Lametsch, René","Bang-Berthelsen, Claus Heiner"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-756186"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Bang-Berthelsen, Claus Heiner","Lametsch, René"],"keyword":["Alternative protein","Cross kingdom fermentation","Edible fungi","Fermentation","Lactic acid bacteria","Pleurotus ostreatus","Sugar beet pulp"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using pre fermented sugar beet pulp as a growth medium to produce i pleurotus ostreatus i mycelium for meat alternatives","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijfoodmicro.2024.110872","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-756186","identifier":[{"id":"85201480045","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39163813","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-c7d493f4-4383-4357-b299-c1d87ca1a268","ku-3a1c8ba2-b181-473e-aa68-5266302d86a1"],"keyword":["Alternative protein","Cross-kingdom fermentation","Edible fungi","Fermentation","Lactic acid bacteria","Pleurotus ostreatus","Sugar beet pulp"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4BA78DBEF0D78545AB739112FBA2D83E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/374943637/1-s2.0-S0168160524003167-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijfoodmicro.2024.110872","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/403999622/1_s2.0_S0168160524003167_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Microbial Biotechnology and Biorefining"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Analytics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne Kjærulf","key":"todorovpau","last":"Todorov","locid":"7c2e922d-6327-4d1d-a3f5-1289ca5727e0","name":"Madsen, Sanne Kjærulf","name_org":"Todorov, Sanne Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0001-5256-5730","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frantiska","key":"tomasikovapau","last":"Tomasikova","locid":"1d2c7911-4a2e-47a5-908b-0f00c60dcfe6","name":"Tomasikova, Frantiska","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8e4aa573-5333-48b1-a3e4-a943f1d5d080","name":"Hansen, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-1029","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Radhakrishna","key":"shettypau","last":"Shetty","locid":"e5e10f02-e62b-4699-b78e-56ece1a460c8","name":"Shetty, Radhakrishna","orcid":"0000-0003-1393-1712","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Celia L.","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","locid":"5fc71fc3-fcee-4e9c-94b9-726833703454","name":"Jansen, Celia L.","orcid":"0000-0002-8443-6666","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"36158d7c-a1ce-4b85-a240-93c6218ea6be","name":"Jacobsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-3540-9669","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Timothy John","key":"hobleypau","last":"Hobley","locid":"1ee66441-2571-4d64-a99b-37f7d03d63f2","name":"Hobley, Timothy John","orcid":"0000-0002-1355-6214","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"René","key":"lametschpau","last":"Lametsch","locid":"70bd350a-6869-4a4a-b9bc-56a756376784","name":"Lametsch, Rene","name_org":"Lametsch, René","orcid":"0000-0002-4189-806X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Heiner","key":"bangberthelsenpau","last":"Bang-Berthelsen","locid":"6f400aa2-d0d7-42fe-a03e-d90689308574","name":"Bang-Berthelsen, Claus Heiner","orcid":"0000-0003-4541-2538","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39163813"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijfoodmicro.2024.110872","issn":["01681605","18793460"],"issn_org":["01681605"],"journal":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","paperid":"110872","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","volume":"425"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201480045"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c7d493f4-4383-4357-b299-c1d87ca1a268","ku-3a1c8ba2-b181-473e-aa68-5266302d86a1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using pre-fermented sugar beet pulp as a growth medium to produce <i>Pleurotus ostreatus</i> mycelium for meat alternatives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-756186","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Doxorubicin is a chemotherapeutic agent used for more than fifty years to treat a great variety of cancers in both children and adults. Despite hereof, pharmacokinetic knowledge is almost solely based on systemic plasma concentrations. Microdialysis is a catheter-based pharmacokinetic sampling tool enabling simultaneous target site sampling of unbound molecules of interest. The aim of this study was to thoroughly evaluate the feasibility of applying microdialysis for sampling of Doxorubicin in both in vitro experiments and an in vivo setting. Doxorubicin relative recovery by gain and by loss was tested for different catheter types, perfusion fluids, concentrations and collection vials. Adsorption tests revealed polystyrene/santoprene vials to be the biggest contributor of unwanted adsorption between Doxorubicin and the microdialysis equipment, and confirmed LoBind Eppendorf tubes to be a suitable alternative. The methodological combination of polyamide membranes, saline as perfusion fluid and LoBind Eppendorf sampling tubes demonstrated no statistically significant differences for relative recovery by gain and by loss, and the relative recovery was also found to be concentration independent. We conclude, that a proper microdialysis set-up can be used to collect samples containing concentrations of the chemotherapeutic drug Doxorubicin in vitro and in vivo, which encourage future pharmacokinetic studies to evaluate current treatment regimens to find the most effective and least toxic anti-neoplastic treatment for the patients.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Andrea René","Hansen, Jakob","Bue, Mats","Hanberg, Pelle","Stilling, Maiken"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-717265"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Andrea René"],"keyword":["Adsorption","Adult","Child","Doxorubicin","Humans","Microdialysis","Polyamide","UHPLC MS MS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microdialysis as a sampling tool for the chemotherapeutic agent doxorubicin","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpba.2023.115872","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by a grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( NNF19OC0058501 ). The funding source had no involvement in the work presented in this article."],"id":"S01-000.00-717265","identifier":[{"id":"85179110652","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38039870","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-15dd815e-3ffc-4755-8b19-6033bc02ab8c"],"keyword":["Adsorption","Adult","Child","Doxorubicin","Humans","LoBind","Microdialysis","Polyamide","UHPLC-MS/MS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE45CA60FBFE5234A0A6261166E66172"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/384321325/1-s2.0-S0731708523006416-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpba.2023.115872","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Orthopaedic surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrea René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"105e5e1d-0600-4cd5-94cb-68291474afab","name":"Jørgensen, Andrea René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"97064afe-b889-4cea-afe6-cb4d16191ff6","name":"Hansen, Jakob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mats","key":"buepau","last":"Bue","locid":"2a35a61c-3bf9-4bf7-9569-73178247b08c","name":"Bue, Mats","orcid":"0000-0001-7215-8323","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pelle","key":"hanbergpau","last":"Hanberg","locid":"242cb61c-bb82-4d48-9af7-8c84a17ab00e","name":"Hanberg, Pelle","orcid":"0000-0002-6845-1874","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maiken","key":"stillingpau","last":"Stilling","locid":"bb005d3f-27c9-4157-8101-db5059373d32","name":"Stilling, Maiken","orcid":"0000-0002-4530-2075","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38039870"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpba.2023.115872","issn":["07317085","1873264X"],"issn_org":["07317085"],"journal":"Journal of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Analysis","paperid":"115872","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Analysis","volume":"239"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179110652"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-15dd815e-3ffc-4755-8b19-6033bc02ab8c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Microdialysis as a sampling tool for the chemotherapeutic agent Doxorubicin","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-717265","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"As anthropogenic carbon dioxide (CO2) emissions increase in the atmosphere yearly, there is an increased need to reduce the emissions to limit global warming, where one approach is through CO2 capture. After capturing CO2, different components and levels of impurities will be present, depending on the source. These impurities can cause corrosion to the transportation infrastructure, where corrosion costs billions of dollars in the oil and gas industry every year. Therefore, investigating corrosion under different conditions is essential and makes emulating CO2 transportation processes within Carbon Capture, Utilization, and Storage (CCUS) necessary. In this study, experimental approaches to emulate CO2 transportation and the pitfalls within these are dissected. Flow loops and autoclaves can emulate pipeline and ship transportation, respectively, which will give a greater understanding of the impact of impurities on the transportation infrastructure. There is a tendency to include variables and factors that do not represent any CO2 transportation scenarios within CCUS. This gives a wrong impression of the corrosion rate of a real CO2 transportation scenario within CCUS for the investigated material. This study presents the process conditions of four scenarios within CCUS and how to emulate them. Afterward, these process conditions are compared to experimental work from the literature to investigate their alignment with the real CO2 transport conditions. Lastly, this study suggests a recommended practice for emulating CO2 transportation processes within CCUS. It is concluded that by aligning the experiments with industrial conditions, the data can be utilized to improve future CO2 and material specifications for the CCUS industry, together with life cycle assessments.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Simonsen, Kenneth René","Hansen, Dennis Severin","Pedersen, Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-742866"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-24","place":"Calgary, ca","start":"2024-10-20","title":"International Conference on Greenhouse Gas Control Technologies","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental approaches for emulating co000000000002 transportation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.5030102","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-742866","ids":["aau-648df8af-f55b-43bc-b9b7-7f91eced2b26"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B62DE3C126898048C5AF00D680FEBB6D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.5030102","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kenneth René","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"18f6d31b-80a4-4605-bd2a-548205326536","name":"Simonsen, Kenneth René","orcid":"0000-0001-6542-2085","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dennis Severin","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3ef0fc7c-ea22-40da-ab21-a2a2e8e46c65","name":"Hansen, Dennis Severin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b784e2a8-004f-4040-80ad-fc67161cee9f","name":"Pedersen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-2928-7813","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2139/ssrn.5030102","publisher":"SSRN: Social Science Research Network","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 17th Greenhouse Gas Control Technologies Conference (GHGT-17) 20-24 October 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","9. Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-648df8af-f55b-43bc-b9b7-7f91eced2b26"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Experimental Approaches for Emulating CO2 Transportation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-742866","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Doxorubicin is a widely used chemotherapeutic drug that can be administered intravenously as both a bolus infusion and a continuous infusion. The latter is believed to lower the risk of cardiotoxicity, which is a critical long-term complication of doxorubicin treatment. The local tissue concentrations of doxorubicin will be reflected in both treatment efficacy and toxicity, but very limited information is available. The aim of this study was to measure the concentration of doxorubicin after continuous and bolus infusion in tissue compartments around a typical location of a bone tumour. Methods: Sixteen pigs (female, Danish Landrace, mean weight 77 kg) were randomized into two groups of eight. Both groups received an intravenous infusion of 150 mg doxorubicin; Group 1 received a bolus infusion (10–15 min) and Group 2 received a continuous infusion (6 h). Before infusion, microdialysis catheters were placed intravenously and in four bone tumour-relevant tissue compartments (cancellous bone, subcutaneous tissue, synovial fluid of the knee joint and muscle tissue). Sampling was done (n = 15) over 24 h, and venous blood samples were collected as a reference. Results: Area under the concentration–time curve (AUC0–24 h) for plasma (total concentration) was significantly different between the two groups, while peak drug concentration (Cmax) was significantly higher in two compartments (plasma and synovial fluid of the knee joint) in Group 1 compared to Group 2. Overall, the unbound tissue concentrations were extremely low with values below 0.20 µg/mL. Conclusion: The pharmacokinetic profile for doxorubicin in the investigated tissues is very similar when comparing bolus and 6 h continuous infusion.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Andrea René","Bue, Mats","Hanberg, Pelle","Petersen, Elisabeth Krogsgaard","Harlev, Christina","Hansen, Jakob","Baad-Hansen, Thomas","Safwat, Akmal","Stilling, Maiken"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-743737"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Andrea René"],"keyword":["Bone cancer","Doxorubicin","Doxorubicinol","Infusion","Microdialysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"doxorubicin concentrations in bone tumour relevant tissues after bolus and continuous infusion a randomized porcine microdialysis study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00280-023-04637-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-743737","identifier":[{"id":"38332155","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11130026","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85184414330","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-158c1ec3-2b55-4fc5-a3da-263eafbba50b"],"keyword":["Bone Cancer","Doxorubicin","Doxorubicinol","Infusion","Microdialysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A401157412DFC3F0C10C05C24D39F9AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00280-023-04637-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/434179764/Doxorubicin_concentrations_in_bone_tumour_relevant_tissues_after_bolus_and_continuous_infusion_a_randomized_porcine_microdialysis_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Orthopaedic surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrea René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"105e5e1d-0600-4cd5-94cb-68291474afab","name":"Jørgensen, Andrea René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mats","key":"buepau","last":"Bue","locid":"2a35a61c-3bf9-4bf7-9569-73178247b08c","name":"Bue, Mats","orcid":"0000-0001-7215-8323","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pelle","key":"hanbergpau","last":"Hanberg","locid":"242cb61c-bb82-4d48-9af7-8c84a17ab00e","name":"Hanberg, Pelle","orcid":"0000-0002-6845-1874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elisabeth Krogsgaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"82e0010f-5a0e-41df-a42b-4c0d22d66404","name":"Petersen, Elisabeth Krogsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5164-5197","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina","key":"harlevpau","last":"Harlev","locid":"2d4595f9-dc94-4fe1-b318-b99718c59d87","name":"Harlev, Christina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"97064afe-b889-4cea-afe6-cb4d16191ff6","name":"Hansen, Jakob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"baadhansenpau","last":"Baad-Hansen","locid":"73f367ed-4c3c-432c-95d9-73ab20b05f09","name":"Baad-Hansen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4826-8412","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Akmal","key":"safwatpau","last":"Safwat","locid":"8d664922-6cc3-4d2a-a032-44cdfc5febb3","name":"Safwat, Akmal","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maiken","key":"stillingpau","last":"Stilling","locid":"bb005d3f-27c9-4157-8101-db5059373d32","name":"Stilling, Maiken","orcid":"0000-0002-4530-2075","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38332155"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00280-023-04637-1","issn":["03445704","09439404"],"issn_org":["03445704"],"issue":"6","journal":"Cancer Chemotherapy and Pharmacology","pages":"555-564","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Cancer Chemotherapy and Pharmacology","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184414330"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-158c1ec3-2b55-4fc5-a3da-263eafbba50b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Doxorubicin concentrations in bone tumour-relevant tissues after bolus and continuous infusion : a randomized porcine microdialysis study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743737","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Cryoballoon ablation is a safe and efficient rhythm control strategy in atrial fibrillation (AF) patients. The impact of time from diagnosis to ablation is unclear. The aim of this study was to examine the impact of timing of first-time cryoballoon ablation on AF recurrence in a nationwide cohort of AF patients. Methods and Results: From nationwide registers, all AF patients ≥18 years of age who underwent first-time AF cryoballoon ablation in Denmark from 2012 to 2018 were included. The AF patients were stratified by ablation timing: Early group (≤1 year after AF diagnosis), intermediate group (1–3 years after AF diagnosis), and late group (≥3 years after AF diagnosis). By adjusted Cox regression models, the effect of timing on AF recurrence was examined. This study included 1064 AF patients with a median age of 63 years. Most patients were male (66%) and had paroxysmal AF (67%). The 1-year risk of AF recurrence increased from 31% in the early group to 41% and 44% in the intermediate and late group. The hazard ratios (95% confidence intervals) were 1.28 (0.95, 1.74) in the intermediate group and 1.42 (1.09, 1.86) in the late group when compared to the early group. Continuous diagnosis-to-ablation time seemed to have the greatest impact on AF recurrence within the first 2 years. Conclusion: In AF patients undergoing cryoballoon ablation, late timing of ablation was associated with a significantly higher AF recurrence rate when compared to early timing of ablation. These findings support early cryoballoon ablation to improve the outcomes after ablation.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hein, Regitze","Da Riis-Vestergaard, Lise","Tønnesen, Jacob","Zörner, Christopher Ryan","Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","Ruwald, Martin Huth","Johannessen, Arne","Worck, René Husted","Hansen, Jim","Middelfart, Charlotte","Gislason, Gunnar","Hansen, Morten Lock"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754454"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Catheter ablation","diagnosis to ablation time"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of early cryoballoon ablation on atrial fibrillation recurrence a danish nationwide register study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jce.16303","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754454","identifier":[{"id":"38757241","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85193322946","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5b9099eb-7aea-4424-a638-e6ff576ea29f"],"keyword":["atrial fibrillation","catheter ablation","cryo-ablation","diagnosis-to-ablation time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD8468EAA2F375862AAA25FF62C7A780"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/400877924/Cardiovasc_electrophysiol_2024_Hein_Effect_of_early_cryoballoon_ablation_on_atrial_fibrillation_recurrence_A_Danish.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jce.16303","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"danish heart foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-HJER","l3nn":"Danish Heart Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Heart Foundation","namevar":["The Danish Heart Foundation"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-HJER","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Regitze","key":"heinregitzepau","last":"Hein","name":"Hein, Regitze","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise","key":"dariisvestergaardlisepau","last":"Da Riis-Vestergaard","name":"Da Riis-Vestergaard, Lise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"tønnesenjacobpau","last":"Tønnesen","name":"Tønnesen, Jacob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher Ryan","key":"zörnerchristopherryanpau","last":"Zörner","name":"Zörner, Christopher Ryan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Vibe","key":"rasmussenpetervibepau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Huth","key":"ruwaldmartinhuthpau","last":"Ruwald","name":"Ruwald, Martin Huth","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"johannessenarnepau","last":"Johannessen","name":"Johannessen, Arne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René Husted","key":"worckrenéhustedpau","last":"Worck","name":"Worck, René Husted","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jim","key":"hansenjimpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jim","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"middelfartcharlottepau","last":"Middelfart","name":"Middelfart, Charlotte","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Gunnar Hilmar","key":"gislasongunnarpau","last":"Gislason","locid":"c0f678a6-eb13-49a3-9485-8fae1e72e2a1","name":"Gislason, Gunnar","name_org":"Gislason, Gunnar Hilmar","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Morten Lock","key":"hansenmortenlockpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"870786a1-f42f-40fa-b820-1608236b578c","name":"Hansen, Morten Lock","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38757241"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jce.16303","issn":["10453873","15408167"],"issn_org":["10453873"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","pages":"1429-1439","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Electrophysiology","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193322946"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5b9099eb-7aea-4424-a638-e6ff576ea29f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of early cryoballoon ablation on atrial fibrillation recurrence — A Danish nationwide register study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754454","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The variability of ice thickness in the Barents Sea is poorly described, with irregular import events of deformed ice intrusions with strong spatial and temporal variability. In contrast, the primary export of sea ice from the Arctic Ocean occurs through the Fram Strait where most sea ice studies have been performed. Here, we present sea ice pressure ridge statistics for the Fram Strait and Barents Sea derived from high-resolution surface topography information from NASA’s laser altimeter, ICESat-2, acquired during the period 2018-2022. These ICESat-2-derived statistics are compared against keel draft ridge statistics derived from moored upward looking sonars (ULS) using established keel-to-sail-ratios from literature. Ridges are identified using two detection thresholds (0.6 or 0.2 m above local ice elevation). Using 0.2 m, sail heights in the Barents Sea are ~34% smaller than the Fram Strait. In comparison, a 0.6 m threshold observes sail heights in the Barents Sea being 85% of those in the Fram Strait. Of individual ridges on basin scales, 1140-2658% more ridges were observed by ICESat-2 compared to ridges identified at the moored stations. Comparison with ULS-derived statistics shows comparable results when accounting for different detection thresholds (minimum sails/drafts) and reference levels (water or ice level); when unaccounted for, a difference of >1 m in median keel draft, depending on ratio used, is observed. More than 40% of the ICESat-2-detected ridges in the Fram Strait (using 0.6 m threshold) had smaller estimated drafts than detectable with current methods applied to the ULS observations in the Fram Strait, high-lighting the importance of comparable reference levels.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Fredensborg Hansen, Renée Mie","Høyland, Knut V.","Duncan, Kyle","Farrell, Sinéad L.","Rinne, Eero","Forsberg, René","Skourup, Henriette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764306"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-13","place":"Gdańsk , pl","start":"2024-06-09","title":"27th IAHR International Symposium on Ice","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fredensborg Hansen, Renée Mie"],"country":["Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","University Centre in Svalbard","University of Maryland, College Park"],"keyword":["ICESat 2","Satellite laser altimetry","Sea ice"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sea ice pressure ridge statistics of the barents sea and fram strait from icesat 000000000002 laser altimetry observations during 000000002018 000000002022","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376054516/27th_IAHR_ICE_RareIce_Barents_sea_ridge_statistics_IS2_v2_RMFH.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764306","ids":["dtu-8c5480b1-a3ee-489c-80b2-b7cdf2a562b8"],"keyword":["Barents Sea and Fram Strait","ICESat-2","Pressure ridges","Satellite laser altimetry","Sea ice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5C261785311244CD6F3BAA29635C1B56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376054516/27th_IAHR_ICE_RareIce_Barents_sea_ridge_statistics_IS2_v2_RMFH.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Geodesy and Earth Observation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of maryland college park","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Maryland, College Park","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"university centre in svalbard","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University Centre in Svalbard","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Renée Mie","key":"fredensborghansenpau","last":"Fredensborg Hansen","locid":"fb1ad80c-3a89-42f9-8d80-293328b301e6","name":"Fredensborg Hansen, Renée Mie","orcid":"0000-0002-3426-347X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Knut V.","key":"høylandpau","last":"Høyland","name":"Høyland, Knut V.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kyle","key":"duncanpau","last":"Duncan","name":"Duncan, Kyle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sinéad L.","key":"farrellpau","last":"Farrell","name":"Farrell, Sinéad L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Eero","key":"rinnepau","last":"Rinne","name":"Rinne, Eero","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henriette","key":"skouruppau","last":"Skourup","locid":"f5fe613f-20e5-4a69-9eff-f03779801182","name":"Skourup, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-4468-8033","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tomasz","key":"kolerskipedh","last":"Kolerski","name":"Kolerski, Tomasz","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"issn":["24146331"],"publisher":"International Association for Hydro-Environment Engineering and Research (IAHR)","series":"IAHR International Symposium on Ice","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 27th IAHR International Symposium on Ice (Gdansk, 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85210070131"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8c5480b1-a3ee-489c-80b2-b7cdf2a562b8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Sea ice pressure ridge statistics of the Barents Sea and Fram Strait from ICESat-2 laser altimetry observations during 2018-2022","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764306","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Aims/hypothesis: Metabolic risk factors and plasma biomarkers for diabetes have previously been shown to change prior to a clinical diabetes diagnosis. However, these markers only cover a small subset of molecular biomarkers linked to the disease. In this study, we aimed to profile a more comprehensive set of molecular biomarkers and explore their temporal association with incident diabetes. Methods: We performed a targeted analysis of 54 proteins and 171 metabolites and lipoprotein particles measured in three sequential samples spanning up to 11 years of follow-up in 324 individuals with incident diabetes and 359 individuals without diabetes in the Danish Blood Donor Study (DBDS) matched for sex and birth year distribution. We used linear mixed-effects models to identify temporal changes before a diabetes diagnosis, either for any incident diabetes diagnosis or for type 1 and type 2 diabetes mellitus diagnoses specifically. We further performed linear and non-linear feature selection, adding 28 polygenic risk scores to the biomarker pool. We tested the time-to-event prediction gain of the biomarkers with the highest variable importance, compared with selected clinical covariates and plasma glucose. Results: We identified two proteins and 16 metabolites and lipoprotein particles whose levels changed temporally before diabetes diagnosis and for which the estimated marginal means were significant after FDR adjustment. Sixteen of these have not previously been described. Additionally, 75 biomarkers were consistently higher or lower in the years before a diabetes diagnosis. We identified a single temporal biomarker for type 1 diabetes, IL-17A/F, a cytokine that is associated with multiple other autoimmune diseases. Inclusion of 12 biomarkers improved the 10-year prediction of a diabetes diagnosis (i.e. the area under the receiver operating curve increased from 0.79 to 0.84), compared with clinical information and plasma glucose alone. Conclusions/interpretation: Systemic molecular changes manifest in plasma several years before a diabetes diagnosis. A particular subset of biomarkers shows distinct, time-dependent patterns, offering potential as predictive markers for diabetes onset. Notably, these biomarkers show shared and distinct patterns between type 1 diabetes and type 2 diabetes. After independent replication, our findings may be used to develop new clinical prediction models. Graphical Abstract: (Figure presented.)","author_count":26,"contributors":["Lundgaard, Agnete T","Westergaard, David","Röder, Timo","Burgdorf, Kristoffer S","Larsen, Margit H","Schwinn, Michael","Thørner, Lise W","Sørensen, Erik","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Erikstrup, Christian","Kjerulff, Bertram D","Hindhede, Lotte","Hansen, Thomas F","Nyegaard, Mette","Birney, Ewan","Stefansson, Hreinn","Stefánsson, Kári","Pedersen, Ole B V","Ostrowski, Sisse R","Rossing, Peter","Ullum, Henrik","Mortensen, Laust H","Vistisen, Dorte","Banasik, Karina","Brunak, Søren"],"cuid":["S03-099.98-761597"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genomic Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Brunak, Søren"],"country":["Germany","Iceland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Molecular Biology Laboratory","European Molecular Biology Laboratory (EMBL)","deCODE Genetics"],"keyword":["Molecular biomarkers","Multi omics","Polygenic risk scores","Temporality","Time to event prediction","Type 1 diabetes mellitus","Type 2 diabetes mellitus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Danmarks Statistik"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"longitudinal metabolite and protein trajectories prior to diabetes mellitus diagnosis in danish blood donors a nested case control study","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-024-06231-3","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Copenhagen University. ATL, DW, TR, KB and SB were supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grants NNF14CC0001 and NNF17OC0027594). BDK was supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation Challenge Programme (grant NNF17OC0027864). LHM acknowledges support from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grants NNF17OC0027812 and NNF17OC0027594). DV has received research grants from Bayer A/S, Sanofi A/S, Novo Nordisk A/S, and Boehringer Ingelheim; all fees were given to the Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen. PR reports receipt of honoraria to Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen for education and consultancy from Abbott, AstraZeneca, Bayer A/S, Boehringer Ingelheim, Lexicon Inc, Novartis and Novo Nordisk A/S."],"id":"S03-099.98-761597","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11446992","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85200036310","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39078488","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-6c917466-b5f7-4197-95c8-91459725a39a","au-218fe9a2-4683-4fda-b051-47371f088e53","ku-fdcfda29-d963-4117-a2f7-092e264d2890"],"keyword":["Molecular biomarkers","Multi-omics","Polygenic risk scores","Temporality","Time-to-event prediction","Type 1 diabetes mellitus","Type 2 diabetes mellitus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A0D6F53EE83D15AE27E73E8048B27275"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type