unak, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-0316-5866","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39078488"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-024-06231-3","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"10","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"2289-2303","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200036310"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Novo Nordisk","Other Research","Private Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6c917466-b5f7-4197-95c8-91459725a39a","au-218fe9a2-4683-4fda-b051-47371f088e53","ku-fdcfda29-d963-4117-a2f7-092e264d2890"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Longitudinal metabolite and protein trajectories prior to diabetes mellitus diagnosis in Danish blood donors : a nested case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.98-761597","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The prevalence of undocumented medical treatments among children is a significant issue, as well as many EU countries lack access to newly developed children-friendly medicines. Consequently, there is a pressing need for supplementary resources that can facilitate informed decision-making regarding children's medication. We therefore aim to describe the process of establishing a children's Drug and Therapeutics Committee (cDTC), as well as the preparing and implementation of recommendations for children in the capital region of Denmark. Following the guidelines outlined by the World Health Organization, we established a cDTC, and recommendations for paediatric medication practice were constructed from assessments of medication use patterns among children in the capital region between 2019 and 2021. The recommendations were meticulously crafted based on evaluation of the current marketing authorization landscape and existing best available evidence. In 2019, the capital region established the first cDTC supported by expert councils and an editorial board. A total of 2429 purchase item numbers covering 1 222 846 defined daily doses and 592 088 purchased packages covering 10 200 000 defined daily doses were identified in the secondary and primary sectors, respectively. Three comprehensive lists covering recommendations for newborns and children were published between 2021 and 2020 totaling 331 recommended pharmaceutical products. The recommendations primarily intended for use in the secondary healthcare sector were implemented through the revision of 38 paediatric- and six neonatal product ranges throughout capital region. In conclusion, recommendation lists for children governed by a cDTC provide a rational auxiliary tool that can be immediately implemented in the clinic.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Holst, Sara Sommer","Møller, Camilla Holten","Vermehren, Charlotte","Trolle, Stine","Hansen, Bente","Kirkedal, Ann Britt Kiholm","Christensen, Hanne Rolighed","Jacobsen, Thorkild","Mathiasen, René","Andersen, Jon Trærup","Gade, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719291"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical pharmacology","Neonatal","Paediatrics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"establishment of a children s drugs and therapeutics committee to ensure evidence based and cost effective medical treatment for children","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381145865/IKM_Brit_J_Clinical_Pharma_2023_Holst_Establishment_of_a_Children_s_Drugs_and_Therapeutics_Committee_to_ensure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-719291","identifier":[{"id":"37879905","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85178882062","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0fa91bc1-a829-4305-8ca3-3d60eb163537"],"keyword":["Drugs and Therapeutics Committee","clinical pharmacology","formulary list","neonatal","paediatrics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F283ECDB77FDD8348D441CC0E2EE256"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381145865/IKM_Brit_J_Clinical_Pharma_2023_Holst_Establishment_of_a_Children_s_Drugs_and_Therapeutics_Committee_to_ensure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Translational and Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Social and Clinical Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sara Sommer","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Sara Sommer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Holten","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Camilla Holten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Charlotte","key":"vermehrenpau","last":"Vermehren","locid":"02426acb-0a63-416b-90c9-bcc33d0851c6","name":"Vermehren, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine","key":"trollepau","last":"Trolle","name":"Trolle, Stine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Bente","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ann Britt Kiholm","key":"kirkedalpau","last":"Kirkedal","name":"Kirkedal, Ann Britt Kiholm","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Rolighed","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Hanne Rolighed","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thorkild","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Thorkild","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"René","key":"mathiasenpau","last":"Mathiasen","locid":"20973b1c-9489-4d6c-b32f-584a790fab80","name":"Mathiasen, René","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jón Þór Traerup","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"2fe4a9af-2462-4bba-8df4-2a518ea59342","name":"Andersen, Jon Trærup","name_org":"Andersen, Jón Þór Traerup","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"gadepau","last":"Gade","locid":"005d308f-c88b-40be-a1b8-9b6ff08fc1ff","name":"Gade, Christina","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37879905"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcp.15944","issn":["02643774","03065251"],"issn_org":["03065251"],"issue":"2","journal":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","pages":"378-387","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178882062"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0fa91bc1-a829-4305-8ca3-3d60eb163537"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Establishment of a children's Drugs and Therapeutics Committee to ensure evidence-based and cost-effective medical treatment for children","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719291","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Focal pulsed field ablation (FPFA) is a novel and promising method of cardiac ablation. The aim of this study was to report the feasibility, short-term safety, and procedural findings for a broad spectrum of ablated atrial arrhythmias. Methods: Patients (n = 51) scheduled for ablation of atrial arrhythmias were prospectively included and underwent FPFA using the Galvanize CENTAURI generator with energy delivery through commercially available ablation catheters with ultrahigh-density (UHDx) 3D electroanatomic voltage/local activation time map evaluations. Workflow, procedural data, and peri-procedural technical errors and complications are described. Results: Planned ablation strategy was achieved with FPFA-only in 48/51 (94%) of the cases. Ablation strategy was first-time pulmonary vein isolation (PVI) in 17/51 (36%), repeat ablation in 18/51 (38%), PVI + in 13/51 (28%), and cavotricuspid isthmus block (CTI)-only in 3/51 (6%). The mean procedure time was 104 ± 31 min (first-time PVI), 114 ± 26 min (repeat procedure), 152 ± 36 min (PVI +), and 62 ± 17 min (CTI). Mean UHDx mapping time to assess lesion formation and block after ablation was 7 ± 4 min with 5485 ± 4809 points. First pass acute (linear) isolation with bidirectional block for anatomical lesion sets was 120/124 (97%) for all PVs, 17/17 (100%) for (any) isthmus, and 14/17 (82%) for left atrium posterior wall (LAPW). We observed several time-consuming integration errors with the used ablation system (mean 3.4 ± 3.7 errors/procedure), one transient inferior ST elevation when ablating CTI resolved by intravenous nitroglycerine and one transient AV block requiring temporary pacing for > 24 h. Conclusions: FPFA was a highly versatile method to treat atrial arrhythmias with high first-pass efficiency. UHDx revealed acute homogenous low-voltage lesions in ablated areas. More data is needed to establish lesion durability and limitations of FPFA.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ruwald, Martin H.","Johannessen, Arne","Hansen, Morten Lock","Haugdal, Martin","Worck, Rene","Hansen, Jim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719975"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Electrophysiology","Mapping","Pulsed field ablation","Safety"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"focal pulsed field ablation and ultrahigh density mapping versatile tools for all atrial arrhythmias initial procedural experiences","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10840-023-01570-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-719975","identifier":[{"id":"85160621501","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10769919","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37249807","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3ef789c4-c5b2-48b3-a470-e46739e393fb"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Electrophysiology","Mapping","Pulsed field ablation","Safety","Ultrahigh density"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-82737D27D8E7D203BC026E1B01F9AF98"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10840-023-01570-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379168880/s10840_023_01570_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martin H.","key":"ruwaldmartinhpau","last":"Ruwald","name":"Ruwald, Martin H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"johannessenarnepau","last":"Johannessen","name":"Johannessen, Arne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten Lock","key":"hansenmortenlockpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"870786a1-f42f-40fa-b820-1608236b578c","name":"Hansen, Morten Lock","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"haugdalmartinpau","last":"Haugdal","name":"Haugdal, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rene","key":"worckrenepau","last":"Worck","name":"Worck, Rene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jim","key":"hansenjimpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jim","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37249807"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10840-023-01570-4","issn":["1383875X","15728595"],"issn_org":["1383875X"],"journal":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","pages":"99-109","status":"p","title":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160621501"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3ef789c4-c5b2-48b3-a470-e46739e393fb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Focal pulsed field ablation and ultrahigh-density mapping — versatile tools for all atrial arrhythmias? Initial procedural experiences","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719975","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Denne bog samler 21 artikler skrevet af Matthew Driscoll, professor i norrøn filologi ved Københavns Universitet, i perioden 1991-2024. Artiklerne er tidligere udkommet i tidsskrifter, antologier, håndbøger og festskrifter og omhandler primært skabelse, formidling og reception af litteratur på Island i middelalderen og det der kan kaldes den ‘præmoderne’ periode, dvs. omtrent fra trykkerkunstens komme i starten af 1500-tallet og frem til etableringen af RÚV (Ríkisútvarpið, det statslige islandske radio- og tv-organ) i begyndelsen af det 20. århundrede.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Driscoll, Matthew James","Hansen, Anne Mette","Hernández Vera, René","Yavuz, N. Kivilcim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738662"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Leeds"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scripta minora selected essays on icelandic manuscripts and texts 000000001991 000000002024","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-738662","ids":["ku-0b6f59e6-170c-4ced-8bf5-a67965e9cf37"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D069C9E034B6FA20F9E7921BE6A320CB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of leeds","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Leeds","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Matthew James","key":"driscollpau","last":"Driscoll","locid":"5469d8c2-fe74-4336-9e19-27cf1dc94925","name":"Driscoll, Matthew James","orcid":"0000-0001-9662-1271","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Mette","key":"hansenped","last":"Hansen","locid":"71166bb7-5004-48c8-b137-aee38f614890","name":"Hansen, Anne Mette","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","first":"René","key":"hernándezveraped","last":"Hernández Vera","locid":"2e62d3c0-2ef1-41bd-a122-f5bffef1ca39","name":"Hernández Vera, René","orcid":"0000-0002-1444-015X","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","first":"N. Kivilcim","key":"yavuzped","last":"Yavuz","name":"Yavuz, N. Kivilcim","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788763547277"],"issn":["00677841"],"pages":"516","place":"Charlottenlund","publisher":"Museum Tusculanum","series":"Bibliotheca Arnamagnaeana","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0b6f59e6-170c-4ced-8bf5-a67965e9cf37"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Scripta Minora : Selected essays on Icelandic manuscripts and texts, 1991–2024","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738662","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Rapidly waning immunity against severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) requires continued global access to affordable vaccines. Globally, inactivated SARS-CoV-2 vaccines have been widely used during the SARS-CoV-2 pandemic. In this proof-of-concept study we adapted an original-D614G SARS-CoV-2 virus to Vero cell culture as a strategy to enhance inactivated vaccine manufacturing productivity. A passage 60 (P60) virus showed enhanced fitness and 50-fold increased virus yield in a bioreactor compared to the original-D614G virus. It further remained susceptible to neutralization by plasma from SARS-CoV-2 vaccinated and convalescent individuals, suggesting exposure of relevant epitopes. Monovalent inactivated P60 and bivalent inactivated P60/omicron BA.1 vaccines induced neutralizing responses against original-D614G and BA.1 viruses in mice and hamsters, demonstrating that the P60 virus is a suitable vaccine antigen. Antibodies further cross-neutralized delta and BA.5 viruses. Importantly, the inactivated P60 vaccine protected hamsters against disease upon challenge with original-D614G or BA.1 virus, with minimal lung pathology and lower virus loads in the upper and lower airways. Antigenicity of the P60 virus was thus retained compared to the original virus despite the acquisition of cell culture adaptive mutations. Consequently, cell culture adaptation may be a useful approach to increase yields in inactivated vaccine antigen production.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Offersgaard, Anna","Duarte Hernandez, Carlos Rene","Zhou, Yuyong","Duan, Zhe","Gammeltoft, Karen Anbro","Hartmann, Katrine Top","Fahnøe, Ulrik","Marichal-Gallardo, Pavel","Alzua, Garazi Peña","Underwood, Alexander P.","Sølund, Christina","Weis, Nina","Bonde, Jesper Hansen","Christensen, Jan Pravsgaard","Pedersen, Gabriel K.","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Holmbeck, Kenn","Bukh, Jens","Gottwein, Judith Margarete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754287"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Dynamics of Complex Technical Systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an inactivated sars cov 000000000002 vaccine based on a vero cell culture adapted high titer virus confers cross protection in small animals","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-67570-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754287","identifier":[{"id":"39048693","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001276798400066","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC11269720","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85199371325","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-314335f7-f844-46ce-884a-9f90c901ff3e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3CDE25167F5F3BACCDA220FF55CFBD9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-67570-0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/399660169/s41598_024_67570_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for dynamics of complex technical systems","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Dynamics of Complex Technical Systems","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anna","key":"offersgaardpau","last":"Offersgaard","locid":"4e5a0d9d-f326-477e-9b1a-f490e0204f57","name":"Offersgaard, Anna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Carlos R.","key":"duartehernandezpau","last":"Duarte Hernandez","locid":"c64db4bf-404a-4521-bd7a-82d73ea40978","name":"Duarte Hernandez, Carlos Rene","name_org":"Duarte Hernandez, Carlos R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Yuyong","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"a08d3db0-78c9-4832-b406-f4c7c286c763","name":"Zhou, Yuyong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zhe","key":"duanpau","last":"Duan","name":"Duan, Zhe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Karen Anbro","key":"gammeltoftpau","last":"Gammeltoft","locid":"5756cbe9-98ab-43be-a9bb-0871c609eec9","name":"Gammeltoft, Karen Anbro","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine T.","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"24872909-edcd-41d3-ac0e-6d89e6fef67b","name":"Hartmann, Katrine Top","name_org":"Hartmann, Katrine T.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ulrik","key":"fahnøepau","last":"Fahnøe","locid":"af7d26fe-7626-47c3-8851-4c49157a2198","name":"Fahnøe, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2527-5751","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Pavel","key":"marichalgallardopau","last":"Marichal-Gallardo","name":"Marichal-Gallardo, Pavel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Garazi Peña","key":"alzuapau","last":"Alzua","locid":"d6fa8f55-b9f7-4f55-862f-d115310d1a40","name":"Alzua, Garazi Peña","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Alexander P.","key":"underwoodpau","last":"Underwood","locid":"6bcab5f0-7463-4162-a31c-534dbb306ddb","name":"Underwood, Alexander P.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"sølundpau","last":"Sølund","name":"Sølund, Christina","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Nina","key":"weispau","last":"Weis","locid":"3a88aaad-c729-432b-b725-999664af7a45","name":"Weis, Nina","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper Hansen","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","name":"Bonde, Jesper Hansen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan P.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"042fb583-4cb8-4de1-bcb5-5ac3b53d0d48","name":"Christensen, Jan Pravsgaard","name_org":"Christensen, Jan P.","orcid":"0000-0002-4299-9479","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 4","first":"Gabriel K.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"06527a2a-205e-403a-b284-b1b1a5cc2bf3","name":"Pedersen, Gabriel K.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kenn","key":"holmbeckpau","last":"Holmbeck","locid":"5cc75d05-d9de-46dc-b5cb-4ae12d1295f9","name":"Holmbeck, Kenn","orcid":"0000-0002-4472-3257","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jens","key":"bukhpau","last":"Bukh","locid":"ed84ce10-678e-4b40-9651-982bf9977abc","name":"Bukh, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-7815-4806","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Judith Margarete","key":"gottweinpau","last":"Gottwein","locid":"25b6c448-64fe-42f4-89af-110cd5694f40","name":"Gottwein, Judith Margarete","orcid":"0000-0003-2805-0256","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39048693"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-024-67570-0","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"17039","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199371325"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-314335f7-f844-46ce-884a-9f90c901ff3e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An inactivated SARS-CoV-2 vaccine based on a Vero cell culture-adapted high-titer virus confers cross-protection in small animals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754287","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Aims Catheter ablation (CA) is a well-established treatment option for atrial fibrillation (AF), where sedation and analgesia are pivotal for patient comfort and lesion formation. The impact of anaesthesia type on AF recurrence rates remains uncertain. This study aimed to examine AF recurrence rates depending on conscious sedation (CS) vs. general anaesthesia (GA) during CA. Methods Utilizing nationwide data from the Danish healthcare registries, we conducted this cohort study involving adults (≥18 years) and results undergoing first-time CA for AF between 2010 and 2018. Patients were categorized by anaesthesia type (CS or GA), with the primary endpoint being AF recurrence, defined by a composite endpoint of either antiarrhythmic drug (AAD) prescriptions, AF-related hospital admissions, electrical cardioversions, or AF re-ablation. The impact of anaesthesia type was evaluated using multivariable Cox proportional hazards analysis. The study cohort comprised 7957 (6421 CS and 1536 GA) patients. Persistent AF, hypertension, and heart failure, as well as use of AAD, were more prevalent in the GA group. Cumulative incidences of recurrent AF were higher in the CS group at 1 (46% vs. 37%) and at 5 (68% vs. 63%) years. Multivariate analysis revealed CS as significantly associated with increased risk of AF recurrence at 5-year follow-up [hazard ratio 1.26 (95% confidence interval 1.15–1.38)], consistent across paroxysmal and persistent AF subtypes. Conclusion This nationwide cohort study suggests a higher risk of AF recurrence with CS during CA compared to GA. These results advocate for considering GA as the preferred anaesthesia type for improved CA outcomes.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Da Riis-Vestergaard, Lise","Tønnesen, Jacob","Ruwald, Martin H.","Zörner, Christopher R.","Middelfart, Charlotte","Hein, Regitze","Johannessen, Arne","Hansen, Jim","Worck, Rene Husted","Gislason, Gunnar","Hansen, Morten Lock"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-760204"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anaesthesia","Atrial fibrillation","Catheter ablation","Conscious Sedation","General anaesthesia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"general anaesthesia compared to conscious sedation for first time atrial fibrillation catheter ablation a danish nationwide cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euae203","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-760204","identifier":[{"id":"001296244000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85202014533","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11342248","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39106218","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a2ba1642-bca6-412b-8d02-e3a446fbfb3c"],"keyword":["Anaesthesia","Atrial fibrillation","Catheter ablation","Conscious sedation","General anaesthesia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6A8161D70AD887A6CB6FB52A78E78696"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/403271086/euae203.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euae203","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"danish heart foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-HJER","l3nn":"Danish Heart Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Heart Foundation","namevar":["The Danish Heart Foundation"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-HJER","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lise","key":"dariisvestergaardlisepau","last":"Da Riis-Vestergaard","name":"Da Riis-Vestergaard, Lise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"tønnesenjacobpau","last":"Tønnesen","name":"Tønnesen, Jacob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin H.","key":"ruwaldmartinhpau","last":"Ruwald","name":"Ruwald, Martin H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher R.","key":"zörnerchristopherrpau","last":"Zörner","name":"Zörner, Christopher R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"middelfartcharlottepau","last":"Middelfart","name":"Middelfart, Charlotte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Regitze","key":"heinregitzepau","last":"Hein","name":"Hein, Regitze","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"johannessenarnepau","last":"Johannessen","name":"Johannessen, Arne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jim","key":"hansenjimpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jim","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rene Husted","key":"worckrenehustedpau","last":"Worck","name":"Worck, Rene Husted","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Gunnar","key":"gislasongunnarpau","last":"Gislason","locid":"c0f678a6-eb13-49a3-9485-8fae1e72e2a1","name":"Gislason, Gunnar","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Morten Lock","key":"hansenmortenlockpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"870786a1-f42f-40fa-b820-1608236b578c","name":"Hansen, Morten Lock","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39106218"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/euae203","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"issue":"8","journal":"Europace","paperid":"euae203","status":"p","title":"Europace","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85202014533"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a2ba1642-bca6-412b-8d02-e3a446fbfb3c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"General anaesthesia compared to conscious sedation for first-time atrial fibrillation catheter ablation - a Danish nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-760204","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Fault injection is a sophisticated attack in which an attacker may sidestep security of an application by inducing bit-flips in the underlying platform. These attacks are typically performed by tampering with the system hardware, but recent RowHammer attacks have shown that bit-flips can be induced predictably and on a large scale through software alone [12]. It is practically impossible for a developer to evaluate and assess if and how much an application is vulnerable to RowHammer attacks. In this paper, we leverage statistical model checking (SMC) to help with these challenges by modelling and analysing potential effects of bit-flips as well as measure the efficacy of proposed mitigation. We illustrate our approach on SUDO, one of several security critical applications recently targeted in the RowHammer-based Mayhem attacks [1].","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bøgedal, Tobias Worm","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, Axel","Poulsen, Danny Bøgsted"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786028"],"event":{"end":"2024-11-03","place":"Crete, gr","start":"2024-10-30","title":"AISoLA 2024<br/>","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Université catholique de Louvain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statistical analysis of the impact of bit flips in security critical code","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-786028","identifier":[{"id":"85215821442","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8059c45b-deac-4c4b-a9c8-7c2ffa4daa9a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-594C8D730E7866192E20CFE6DE1C4E49"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"université catholique de louvain","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université catholique de Louvain","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Worm","key":"bøgedalpau","last":"Bøgedal","locid":"3d1bf4b0-adde-469b-bd4c-26d452725bf4","name":"Bøgedal, Tobias Worm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Guldstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"legaypau","last":"Legay","name":"Legay, Axel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Danny Bøgsted","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"dfb3337d-6acd-49e8-a38c-d819a6efca6c","name":"Poulsen, Danny Bøgsted","orcid":"0000-0001-9623-0748","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-75434-0_25","edition":"1","eisbn":["9783031754340"],"isbn":["9783031754333"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"379-397","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Second International Conference, AISoLA 2024, Crete, Greece, October 30 – November 3, 2024, Proceedings","title":"Bridging the Gap Between AI and Reality"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215821442"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8059c45b-deac-4c4b-a9c8-7c2ffa4daa9a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Statistical Analysis of the Impact of Bit-Flips in Security Critical Code","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786028","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Childhood spinal tumors often present with musculoskeletal symptoms, potentially causing a misdiagnosis and delays in diagnosis and treatment. This study aims to identify, characterize, and compare children with spinal tumors who had prior musculoskeletal misdiagnoses to those without, analyzing clinical presentation, diagnostic interval, and outcome. Study design: This retrospective cohort study evaluated all children aged 0–14 years diagnosed with a spinal tumor in Denmark from 1996 to 2018. The cohort was identified through the Danish Childhood Cancer Registry, and the registry data were supplemented with data from medical records. The survival was compared using the Kaplan–Meier method. Results: Among 58 patients, 57% (33/58) received musculoskeletal misdiagnoses before the spinal tumor diagnosis. Misdiagnoses were mostly nonspecific (64%, 21/33), involving pain and accidental lesions, while 36% (12/33) were rheumatologic diagnoses. The patients with prior misdiagnosis had less aggressive tumors, fewer neurological/general symptoms, and 5.5 months median diagnostic interval versus 3 months for those without a misdiagnosis. Those with prior misdiagnoses tended to have a higher 5-year survival of 83% (95% confidence interval [CI]: 63%–92%) compared to 66% (95% CI: 44%–82%) for those without (p =.15). Conclusion: Less aggressive spinal tumors may manifest as gradual skeletal abnormalities and musculoskeletal symptoms without neurological/general symptoms, leading to misdiagnoses and delays.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Dybedokken, Aurora","Mathiesen, Rene","Hasle, Henrik","Herlin, Troels","Callesen, Michael Thude","Hansen, Søren Holm","Jensen, Laura Hallundbæk","Amstrup, Jesper","Hagstrøm, Søren","Brix, Ninna"],"cuid":["S03-096.80-741538"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Brix, Ninna"],"keyword":["Adolescent","CNS tumors","Child","Child Preschool","Denmark epidemiology","Diagnostic Errors","Diagnostic interval","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Infant","Infant Newborn","Male","Misdiagnosis","Musculoskeletal Diseases diagnosis","Pediatric","Prognosis","Registries","Retrospective Studies","Spinal Neoplasms diagnosis","Survival Rate","musculoskeletal symptoms","spinal tumors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"musculoskeletal misdiagnoses in pediatric patients with spinal tumors","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pbc.31024","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-096.80-741538","identifier":[{"id":"85192206767","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38706386","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-cbee17d8-bcc3-4a9d-9403-64ed1852341c","au-46491d38-f616-4201-a14d-1114e50349f1","sdu-eda8b14c-99d5-45b4-8233-486491868932"],"keyword":["Adolescent","CNS tumors","Child, Preschool","Denmark/epidemiology","Diagnostic Errors","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Infant","Infant, Newborn","Male","Musculoskeletal Diseases/diagnosis","Prognosis","Registries","Retrospective Studies","Spinal Neoplasms/diagnosis","Survival Rate","child","diagnostic interval","misdiagnosis","musculoskeletal symptoms","pediatric","spinal tumors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-90E92ECC014E995E0164C524FB34E9C3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/720779195/Dybedokken_et_al._2024_._Musculoskeletal_misdiagnoses_in_pediatric_patients_with_spinal_tumors.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pbc.31024","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/263846758/Pediatric_Blood_Cancer_-_2024_-_Dybedokken_-_Musculoskeletal_misdiagnoses_in_pediatric_patients_with_spinal_tumors.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","us