{"abstract":"Objectives: Lung volume reduction surgery (LVRS) has proven an effective treatment for emphysema, by decreasing hyperinflation and improving lung function, activity level and reducing dyspnoea. However, postoperative air leak is an important complication, often leading to reoperation. Our aim was to analyse reoperations after LVRS and identify potential predictors. Methods: Consecutive single-centre unilateral VATS LVRS performed from 2017 to 2022 were included. Typically, 3–5 minor resections were made using vascular magazines without buttressing. Data were obtained from an institutional database and analysed. Multivariable logistic regression was used to identify predictors of reoperation. Number and location of injuries were registered. Results: In total, 191 patients were included, 25 were reoperated (13%). In 21 patients, the indication for reoperation was substantial air leak, 3 patients bleeding and 1 patient empyema. Length of stay (LOS) was 21 (11–33) vs. 5 days (3–11), respectively. Only 3 injuries were in the stapler line, 13 within < 2cm and 15 injuries were in another site. Multivariable logistic regression analysis showed that decreasing DLCO increased risk of reoperation, OR 1.1 (1.03, 1.18, P = 0.005). Resections in only one lobe, compared to resections in multiple lobes, were also a risk factor OR 3.10 (1.17, 9.32, P = 0.03). Patients undergoing reoperation had significantly increased 30-day mortality, OR 5.52 (1.03, 26.69, P = 0.02). Conclusions: Our incidence of reoperation after LVRS was 13% leading to prolonged LOS and increased 30-day mortality. Low DLCO and resections in a single lobe were significant predictors of reoperation. The air leak was usually not localized in the stapler line. Graphical abstract: Key question: What characterizes reoperations after lung volume reduction surgeries? Key findings: Lung injuries were predominantly located away from the original surgical site. Take home message: Lung injuries remote from the stapler line is frequent during reoperation after lung volume reduction surgery. Location of lung injuries found during reoperation after lung volume reduction surgery [Figure not available: see fulltext.].","author_count":10,"contributors":["Lund, Alberte","Soldath, Patrick","Nodin, Erika","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Perch, Michael","Jensen, Kristine","Hornbech, Kåre","Kalhauge, Anna","Mortensen, Jann","Petersen, René Horsleben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731581"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["COPD","Prolonged air leak","Reoperation","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predictors of reoperation after lung volume reduction surgery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00464-023-10559-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731581","identifier":[{"id":"38017156","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85177733483","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10830766","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-7b3f025d-a333-4216-9fbe-dbaa8c7842e4"],"keyword":["COPD","Lung volume reduction surgery","Prolonged air leak","Reoperation","Risk factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0CB25137F7D1DD5305511D0CC6CF530D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00464-023-10559-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/382982469/s00464_023_10559_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alberte","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Alberte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Patrick","key":"soldathpau","last":"Soldath","locid":"84a27122-a106-4683-b020-a65acbfa59d0","name":"Soldath, Patrick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erika","key":"nodinpau","last":"Nodin","name":"Nodin, Erika","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Michael","key":"perchpau","last":"Perch","locid":"e0a136a6-8b36-4735-9db2-8847ce581fc6","name":"Perch, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristine","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Kristine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kåre","key":"hornbechpau","last":"Hornbech","name":"Hornbech, Kåre","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna","key":"kalhaugepau","last":"Kalhauge","name":"Kalhauge, Anna","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jann","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"6ab8049c-d821-464b-ad25-c541f1511a41","name":"Mortensen, Jann","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38017156"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00464-023-10559-z","issn":["09302794","14322218"],"issn_org":["09302794"],"issue":"2","journal":"Surgical Endoscopy","pages":"679-687","status":"p","title":"Surgical Endoscopy","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85177733483"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7b3f025d-a333-4216-9fbe-dbaa8c7842e4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Predictors of reoperation after lung volume reduction surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731581","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The diverse range of organizations contributing to the global research ecosystem is believed to enhance the overall quality and resilience of its output. Mid-sized autonomous research institutes, distinct from universities, play a crucial role in this landscape. They often lead the way in new research fields and experimental methods, including those in social and organizational domains, which are vital for driving innovation. The EU-LIFE alliance was established with the goal of fostering excellence by developing and disseminating best practices among European biomedical research institutes. As directors of the 15 EU-LIFE institutes, we have spent a decade comparing and refining our processes. Now, we are eager to share the insights we've gained. To this end, we have crafted this Charter, outlining 10 principles we deem essential for research institutes to flourish and achieve ground-breaking discoveries. These principles, detailed in the Charter, encompass excellence, independence, training, internationality and inclusivity, mission focus, technological advancement, administrative innovation, cooperation, societal impact, and public engagement. Our aim is to inspire the establishment of new institutes that adhere to these principles and to raise awareness about their significance. We are convinced that they should be viewed a crucial component of any national and international innovation strategies.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Superti-Furga, Giulio","Agostinho, Marta","Bury, Jo","Cook, Simon","Durinx, Christine","Ender, Anita","van Luenen, Henri","Lund, Anders H","Medema, René H","Miączyńska, Marta","Nickel, Dorthe","Pelicci, Pier Giuseppe","Puisieux, Alain","Ripatti, Samuli","Sander, Maike","Schubeler, Dirk","Serrano, Luis","Sommer, Thomas","Sonne-Hansen, Katrine","Tomančák, Pavel","Vives, Joan","Vontas, John","Bettencourt-Dias, Mónica"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749499"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Czechia","Finland","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Poland","Portugal","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Austrian Centre for Digital Humanities and Cultural Heritage, Austrian Academy of Sciences, Vienna","Central European Institute of Technology","Centre for Genomic Regulation","Curie Institute / Institut Curie","EU-LIFE","Flanders Institute for Biotechnology","Foundation for Research and Technology-Hellas","Friedrich Miescher Institute for Biomedical Research, Basel, Switzerland.","IRCCS Istituto Europeo di Oncologia - Milano","Instituto Gulbenkian de Ciência","International Institute of Molecular and Cell Biology in Warsaw","Max Delbrück Center for Molecular Medicine in the Helmholtz Association","Medical University of Vienna","Netherlands Cancer Institute","The Babraham Institute","University of Helsinki"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eu life charter of independent life science research institutes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/1873-3468.14855","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749499","identifier":[{"id":"38514456","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85188840776","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f49dbbc4-1f68-4e04-ac13-9dec3c0a41de"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-55F90CDAA033E90C0D17578FB07DE9CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/392576494/FEBS_Letters_2024_Superti_Furga_EU_LIFE_charter_of_independent_life_science_research_institutes.pdf","version":"Published Vers