rchives of Virology","volume":"168"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146576877"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fa17a52a-50d7-4d4b-a01d-a2aeb7089100"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Three novel <i>Erwinia billingiae</i> phages isolated from organic waste represent three new genera","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-542696","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Posterior wall isolation (PWI) added to pulmonary vein isolation (PVI) is increasingly used in ablation for persistent atrial fibrillation (PeAF) despite limited evidence of clinical benefit. We investigated the 5-year outcomes of a PVI + PWI ablation strategy with mandatory repeat procedures in PeAF. Methods: Twenty-four patients with PeAF participated in this single-arm prospective study and underwent radiofrequency ablation (RFA) with wide area circumferential ablation (WACA), roof, and inferior lines for PVI + PWI which was reinforced if required during mandated repeat procedures after 6 months. Then, patients were followed for 60 months using continuous heart rhythm monitoring by implanted cardiac monitors (ICM) and atrial fibrillation effect on quality-of-life scoring (AFEQT; range: 20–100 points) for the initial 30 months. Results: ICM-verified cumulated AF recurrence was 54% after 30 months but the ensuing AF burden was only median 0‰ [0 to 4.8‰] overall and 1‰ [0 to 8 ‰] among patients with any recurrence. AFEQT scores increased from baseline 60 points [48 to 72] to 93 points [84 to 96] at repeat procedures P < 0.0001 and further to 96 points [93 to 99] P = 0.03 after 30 months. After 60 months, at least one episode of AF had been documented in 63% and two patients (8%) were in permanent AF. Conclusion: Reinforced PVI + PWI was associated with low long-term AF burden and corresponding improvements in quality-of-life. Reinforced (or durable) PVI + PWI appears to be a promising strategy to treat PeAF. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov. Identifier: NCT05045131.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Worck, René","Sørensen, Samuel K.","Johannessen, Arne","Ruwald, Martin H.","Hansen, Morten Lock","Haugdal, Martin","Hansen, Jim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677683"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Continuous rhythm monitoring","Long term outcomes","Persistent atrial fibrillation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"posterior wall isolation in persistent atrial fibrillation long term outcomes of a repeat procedure strategy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-677683","identifier":[{"id":"36327059","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85141184292","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1ebdd542-32a9-4c88-b976-b54eead54162"],"keyword":["Continuous rhythm monitoring","Long-term outcomes","Mandated repeat ablation","Persistent atrial fibrillation","Posterior wall"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-10B3A52DD0C4A888387DDD491A0AAD5C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"René","key":"worckrenépau","last":"Worck","name":"Worck, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Samuel K.","key":"sørensensamuelkpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Samuel K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"johannessenarnepau","last":"Johannessen","name":"Johannessen, Arne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin H.","key":"ruwaldmartinhpau","last":"Ruwald","name":"Ruwald, Martin H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten Lock","key":"hansenmortenlockpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"870786a1-f42f-40fa-b820-1608236b578c","name":"Hansen, Morten Lock","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"haugdalmartinpau","last":"Haugdal","name":"Haugdal, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jim","key":"hansenjimpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jim","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36327059"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10840-022-01402-x","issn":["1383875X","15728595"],"issn_org":["1383875X"],"journal":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","pages":"971-979","status":"p","title":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141184292"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1ebdd542-32a9-4c88-b976-b54eead54162"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Posterior wall isolation in persistent atrial fibrillation. Long-term outcomes of a repeat procedure strategy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677683","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The glycan moiety Lewis X (LeX) has been implicated in defining progenitor cells as well as playing a role in the progression of solid tumors, including breast cancer. Here, we used the original stage-specific embryonic antigen-1 (SSEA-1) antibody, MC-480, targeting the LeX motif to examine the expression pattern of this marker within the context of a differentiation hierarchy as well as functional properties of breast cancer cells. Immunohistochemical staining revealed the presence of SSEA-1 in a progenitor zone in the normal breast gland. In breast cancer, 81 of 220 carcinomas (37%) were positive for SSEA-1 and a distinct pattern could be correlated to major subtypes. Specifically, estrogen receptor alpha (ERα)-negative tumors showed a higher frequency of SSEA-1 expression compared to ERα-positive tumors, which are generally considered more differentiated (56% vs 29%, p<0.005). Functional assays performed on two representative breast cancer cell lines demonstrated that SSEA-1-expressing cells exhibited cancer stem cell properties as well as having more invasive potential, regardless of ERα status. A potential role of SSEA-1 in metastasis was confirmed by pairwise staining of primary- and corresponding lymph node tumors. Altogether, our data suggest that expression of SSEA-1 in breast cancer contributes to the malignant phenotype.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kohler, Katharina Theresa","Møller Hansen, Anna A","Kim, Jiyoung","Villadsen, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-696532"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ssea 000000000001 correlates with the invasive phenotype in breast cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10424578/pdf/10.1369_00221554231189312.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-696532","identifier":[{"id":"37477396","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001032097800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85167472222","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10424578","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-e31eefb6-25c9-4b3a-b20d-c66dde800856"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9D6B4FC571F8A3F654A7E64617BA401"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10424578/pdf/10.1369_00221554231189312.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Morphogenesis and Differentiation Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Katharina T","key":"kohlerpau","last":"Kohler","locid":"4a5e600f-ee42-4a4a-b64b-b9e8b6c7a4c6","name":"Kohler, Katharina Theresa","name_org":"Kohler, Katharina T","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna A","key":"møllerhansenpau","last":"Møller Hansen","locid":"f2b3d6e1-9653-48fe-83ce-a5e233ed2b9c","name":"Møller Hansen, Anna A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiyoung","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","locid":"46214e7c-add8-4a08-b7de-47bd09e1792b","name":"Kim, Jiyoung","orcid":"0000-0002-0049-2039","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René","key":"villadsenpau","last":"Villadsen","locid":"0537b6ee-7669-46e5-bec9-6f6985878934","name":"Villadsen, René","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37477396"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1369/00221554231189312","issn":["00221554","15515044"],"issn_org":["00221554"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Histochemistry and Cytochemistry","paperid":"221554231189312","status":"p","title":"Journal of Histochemistry and Cytochemistry","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85167472222"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e31eefb6-25c9-4b3a-b20d-c66dde800856"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SSEA-1 Correlates With the Invasive Phenotype in Breast Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-696532","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
