, Sisse R.","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13 14 15","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin L.","key":"olssonmartinlpau","last":"Olsson","name":"Olsson, Martin L.","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 6","first":"Ole B.","key":"pedersenolebirgerpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0d43956a-6e43-42d7-8b29-4505d03ea5c8","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","name_org":"Pedersen, Ole B.","orcid":"0000-0003-2312-5976","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37921035"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/trf.17575","issn":["00411132","15372995"],"issn_org":["00411132"],"issue":"12","journal":"Transfusion","pages":"2297-2310","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Transfusion","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175740684"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5877af24-7f63-4a94-9bda-1d9e306a89e5","au-d31acf3a-bd94-4379-8bfc-73ddb781f267","ku-272f130c-39f3-49a3-8e78-7dc4c35c8b99","ruc-1ea63b49-19de-439e-bf03-8897c822297b","sdu-74686168-0a3f-483e-945e-173e99c9e7ab"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Genetic prediction of 33 blood group phenotypes using an existing genotype dataset","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-099.93-715668","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"(1) Introduction: Piperacillin is a common antibiotic choice in the treatment of periprosthetic joint infections (PJI) caused by Pseudomonas aeruginosa. The aim of this study was to assess and compare the time with free piperacillin concentration above the minimum inhibitory concentration (fT > MIC) at steady state in target tissues relevant for PJI treatment following continuous and intermittent short-term infusion. (2) Methods: 16 pigs were randomized to receive either continuous or intermittent short-term infusion of piperacillin. Steady state piperacillin concentrations were assessed using microdialysis in tibial cortical bone, tibial cancellous bone, synovial fluid of the knee joint, and subcutaneous tissue. MIC-targets of 4, 8, 16, and 64 mg/L were applied. Plasma samples were obtained as reference. (3) Results: Continuous infusion resulted in longer fT > MIC for MIC targets of 4 mg/L and 8 mg/L compared to intermittent short-term infusion in all compartments with the exception of tibial cortical bone. For the MIC-target of 16 mg/L, continuous infusion resulted in a longer fT > MIC in all compartments except for the bone compartments. No differences between groups were seen when applying a MIC-target of 64 mg/L. (4) Conclusions: An aggressive dosing strategy may be necessary to obtain sufficient piperacillin concentrations in all bone compartments, particularly if more aggressive targets are applied. Based on the present study, continuous infusion should be considered in the treatment of PJI.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Hans Christian","Hanberg, Pelle","Knudsen, Martin Bruun","Tøstesen, Sara Kousgaard","Jørgensen, Andrea René","Petersen, Elisabeth Krogsgaard","Öbrink-Hansen, Kristina","Søballe, Kjeld","Stilling, Maiken","Bue, Mats"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-134194"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Hans Christian"],"keyword":["Microdialysis","Pharmacokinetics","Piperacillin","Porcine model","Prosthetic joint infections","Pseudomonas aeruginosa"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"piperacillin steady state concentrations in target tissues relevant for pji treatment a randomized porcine microdialysis study comparing continuous infusion with intermittent short term infusion","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/antibiotics12030577","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-134194","identifier":[{"id":"36978444","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10044349","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85151336200","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0895811f-1f68-4a5f-9054-98231ed9a5b1"],"keyword":["Pseudomonas aeruginosa","microdialysis","pharmacokinetics","piperacillin","porcine model","prosthetic joint infections"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-689A976526E166FE1B41F3BD47A96DFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/antibiotics12030577","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Orthopaedic surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Christian","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"93f47ffc-0862-4e2e-9efc-e048c9fd95d1","name":"Rasmussen, Hans Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-9101-9302","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"