,"key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","locid":"ef594d49-5aeb-4d32-80b4-4bfc281b5cbb","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"erikstruppau","last":"Erikstrup","name":"Erikstrup, Christian","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12 13 14","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin L.","key":"olssonpau","last":"Olsson","name":"Olsson, Martin L.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sisse R","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","name_org":"Ostrowski, Sisse R","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ole B","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0d43956a-6e43-42d7-8b29-4505d03ea5c8","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","name_org":"Pedersen, Ole B","orcid":"0000-0003-2312-5976","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36271437"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/trf.17170","issn":["00411132","15372995"],"issn_org":["00411132"],"issue":"1","journal":"Transfusion","pages":"47-58","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Transfusion","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141350949"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fe559b1d-ac84-4b65-8eef-d583df94bb55","au-640c45e1-3524-4ad2-9999-bcbd3892c308","ku-613f9b02-6dac-4bb0-902a-932674251466","sdu-86a446fc-12c5-4398-a87d-038234dcea06"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A large cohort study of the effects of Lewis, ABO, 13 other blood groups and secretor status on COVID-19 susceptibility, severity, and long COVID-19","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.17-703916","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Anorexia nervosa (AN) is an eating disorder with a high mortality. About 95% of cases are women and it has a population prevalence of about 1%, but evidence-based treatment is lacking. The pathogenesis of AN probably involves genetics and various environmental factors, and an altered gut microbiota has been observed in individuals with AN using amplicon sequencing and relatively small cohorts. Here we investigated whether a disrupted gut microbiota contributes to AN pathogenesis. Shotgun metagenomics and metabolomics were performed on faecal and serum samples, respectively, from a cohort of 77 females with AN and 70 healthy females. Multiple bacterial taxa (for example, Clostridium species) were altered in AN and correlated with estimates of eating behaviour and mental health. The gut virome was also altered in AN including a reduction in viral–bacterial interactions. Bacterial functional modules associated with the degradation of neurotransmitters were enriched in AN and various structural variants in bacteria were linked to metabolic features of AN. Serum metabolomics revealed an increase in metabolites associated with reduced food intake (for example, indole-3-propionic acid). Causal inference analyses implied that serum bacterial metabolites are potentially mediating the impact of an altered gut microbiota on AN behaviour. Further, we performed faecal microbiota transplantation from AN cases to germ-free mice under energy-restricted feeding to mirror AN eating behaviour. We found that the reduced weight gain and induced hypothalamic and adipose tissue gene expression were related to aberrant energy metabolism and eating behaviour. Our ‘omics’ and mechanistic studies imply that a disruptive gut microbiome may contribute to AN pathogenesis.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Fan, Yong","Støving, René Klinkby","Berreira Ibraim, Samar","Hyötyläinen, Tuulia","Thirion, Florence","Arora, Tulika","Lyu, Liwei","Stankevic, Evelina","Hansen, Tue Haldor","Déchelotte, Pierre","Sinioja, Tim","Ragnarsdottir, Oddny","Pons, Nicolas","Galleron, Nathalie","Quinquis, Benoît","Levenez, Florence","Roume, Hugo","Falony, Gwen","Vieira-Silva, Sara","Raes, Jeroen","Clausen, Loa","Telléus, Gry Kjaersdam","Bäckhed, Fredrik","Oresic, Matej","Ehrlich, S. Dusko","Pedersen, Oluf"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-672499"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Oluf"],"country":["Belgium","Finland","France","Germany","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","FHU CARNAVAL","Flanders Institute for Biotechnology","Groupe Hospitalier du Havre","INRAE","Institut national de la santé et de la recherche médicale","Institute of Molecular Biology (IMB)","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","KU Leuven","Paris-Saclay University","Rega Institute for Medical Research","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Universite Paris-Saclay","Universite de Rouen","University College London","University Medical Center Mainz","University of Gothenburg","University of Paris-Saclay","University of Turku","Université Paris-Saclay","Université de Rouen","VIB","Åbo Akademi University","Örebro University"],"keyword":["Animals","Anorexia Nervosa microbiology","Bacteria genetics","Feces microbiology","Feeding Behavior","Female","Gastrointestinal Microbiome","Humans","Male","Metabolomics","Mice"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the gut microbiota contributes to the pathogenesis of anorexia nervosa in humans and mice","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu