},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregor B. E.","key":"jemecpau","last":"Jemec","name":"Jemec, Gregor B. E.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Ole","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09066705","14791250"],"issn_org":["09066705"],"issue":"1","journal":"Experimental Dermatology","pages":"43","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Experimental Dermatology","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1c8b9093-59f8-4448-b680-eb648f44f4a5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The differentiating effect of COVID-19-associated stress on the morbidity of healthy blood donors with symptoms of hidradenitis suppurativa","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-058386","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The purpose was to investigate differences in reliability of running economy measurements between familiar and unfamiliar shoes. Thirty-seven runners were included who all ran in familiar and unfamiliar running shoes while running economy was measured at steady state using a treadmill. Each participant was tested on two different visits (three sessions in total), with two trials in each of the three shoe conditions completed at each visit. Coefficient of variation, standard deviation of differences, and limits of agreement of running economy were used to quantify the repeatability (within-visit variation) and reproducibility (between-visit variation). The coefficient of variation showed a marginal difference in reproducibility across shoe conditions, whereas no differences were seen in coefficient of variation, standard deviation of the differences, or limits of agreement for repeatability across shoes. All three shoe conditions showed greater repeatability than reproducibility for running economy, and enhanced repeatability at visit 3 compared to visit 2. Our results indicate that familiarisation to shoes might not be needed for reliable measurements of running economy. Based on our results, when evaluating benefits in running shoes we suggest that running economy be assessed within the same day. Further, our data suggest a beneficial effect of using multiple familiarisation sessions if small differences between shoe conditions are expected.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anders","Heyde, Christian","Simonsen, Morten Bilde","Larsen, Ryan Godsk","Hansen, Rasmus Kopp","Kersting, Uwe","de Zee, Mark","Brund, René Børge Korsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-073304"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["Adidas Group","All Global Affiliations","German Sport University Cologne"],"keyword":["Reliability","Repeatability","Reproducibility","Running economy","Running shoes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reliability of running economy measurements influence of shoe familiarisation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85135737919&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-073304","identifier":[{"id":"35926512","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85135737919","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-503b4778-7326-4114-a4f8-f59c8191943f"],"keyword":["Reliability","Repeatability","Reproducibility","Running economy","Running shoes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2DDEE89E721F2E91A3A80C24B70C3D6F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"adidas group","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Adidas Group","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german sport university cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Sport University Cologne","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"56136ff8-3354-4fe5-9d96-ab0a3b6e4c6b","name":"Nielsen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"heydepau","last":"Heyde","name":"Heyde, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Bilde","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"7d1393c0-2905-4e87-9a3d-80cca4dbeee6","name":"Simonsen, Morten Bilde","orcid":"0000-0001-6645-3596","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ryan Godsk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"86d31e60-1de1-4284-a688-596cc17dca1c","name":"Larsen, Ryan Godsk","orcid":"0000-0002-4622-1453","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Kopp","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"83f77f8a-c042-4766-a894-5e64cd6f1978","name":"Hansen, Rasmus Kopp","orcid":"0000-0001-8515-8779","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Uwe","key":"kerstingpau","last":"Kersting","name":"Kersting, Uwe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"dezeepau","last":"de Zee","locid":"25caa881-65a0-4f66-9d65-b760fc4787b3","name":"de Zee, Mark","orcid":"0000-0003-0584-271X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Børge Korsgaard","key":"brundpau","last":"Brund","locid":"b2374431-6b1e-4efe-9345-01733ef94596","name":"Brund, René Børge Korsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7246-4811","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35926512"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1055/a-1820-7023","issn":["01724622","0943917X"],"issn_org":["01724622"],"issue":"13","journal":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","pages":"1113-1117","publisher":"Georg Thieme Verlag","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135737919"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-503b4778-7326-4114-a4f8-f59c8191943f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Reliability of Running Economy Measurements : Influence of Shoe Familiarisation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-073304","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Piperacillin is a central drug in the treatment of Pseudomonas aeruginosa spondylodiscitis. Intermittent short-term infusion (STI) remains standard treatment in most centres, although the application of continuous infusion (CI) has shown promising results in other clinical settings. We aimed to evaluate time above the minimal inhibitory concentration (f T > MIC) of the free fraction of piperacillin in steady state conditions in porcine cervical spine tissue following CI and STI using microdialysis with MIC targets of 4, 8, and 16 µg/mL. Methods: 16 female pigs were randomized to receive piperacillin/tazobactam as STI (4/0.5 g every 6 h) or CI (4/0.5 g as a bolus followed by 12/1.5 g) for 18 h. Microdialysis catheters were placed for sampling of piperacillin concentrations from the intervertebral disc, vertebral cancellous bone, paravertebral muscle, and adjacent subcutaneous tissue during the third dosing interval (12–18 h). Blood samples were collected as reference. Results: CI resulted in f T > MIC > 82% across all compartments and targets, except for intervertebral disc (37%) and vertebral cancellous bone (28%) at MIC = 16 µg/mL. In Group STI, >72% f T >MIC was reached for MIC = 4 µg/mL in all investigated compartments, while for MIC = 16 µg/mL only subcutaneous tissue exhibited f T > MIC > 50%. Conclusion: CI of piperacillin resulted in higher f T > MIC compared to STI infusion across the investigated tissues and targets. CI should therefore be considered in spondylodiscitis cases requiring piperacillin treatment.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Petersen, Elisabeth Krogsgaard","Hanberg, Pelle","Knudsen, Martin Bruun","Tøstesen, Sara Kousgaard","Jørgensen, Andrea René","Öbrink-Hansen, Kristina","Søballe, Kjeld","Stilling, Maiken","Bue, Mats"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-180252"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Petersen, Elisabeth Krogsgaard"],"keyword":["Microdialysis","Pharmacokinetics","Piperacillin","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Spondylodiscitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intermittent short term infusion vs continuous infusion of piperacillin steady state concentrations in porcine cervical spine tissue evaluated by microdialysis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/antibiotics11070910","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-180252","identifier":[{"id":"35884164","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9312177","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85133794502","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5953db83-9989-4859-84eb-f19a5350242f"],"keyword":["Pseudomonas aeruginosa","microdialysis","pharmacokinetics","piperacillin","spondylodiscitis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-64A8EF7091C42F36BEA59239084880E1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/antibiotics11070910","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Orthopaedic surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elisabeth Krogsgaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"82e0010f-5a0e-41df-a42b-4c0d22d66404","name":"Petersen, Elisabeth Krogsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5164-5197","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pelle","key":"hanbergpau","last":"Hanberg","locid":"242cb61c-bb82-4d48-9af7-8c84a17ab00e","name":"Hanberg, Pelle","orcid":"0000-0002-6845-1874","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"2ea83f79-a875-4f1c-b1ff-12dc504ed698","name":"Knudsen, Martin Bruun","name_org":"Knudsen, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sara Kousgaard","key":"tøstesenpau","last":"Tøstesen","locid":"fe641f6e-6c0d-4bcc-a6d7-862158d0831c","name":"Tøstesen, Sara Kousgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2960-2342","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrea René","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"105e5e1d-0600-4cd5-94cb-68291474afab","name":"Jørgensen, Andrea René","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"öbrinkhansenpau","last":"Öbrink-Hansen","locid":"ad46bc19-97e8-4c7c-aab9-c4e569877dad","name":"Öbrink-Hansen, Kristina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjeld","key":"søballepau","last":"Søballe","locid":"288247bb-1768-4f37-a538-18727fed269b","name":"Søballe, Kjeld","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maiken","key":"stillingpau","last":"Stilling","locid":"bb005d3f-27c9-4157-8101-db5059373d32","name":"Stilling, Maiken","orcid":"0000-0002-4530-2075","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mats","key":"buepau","last":"Bue","locid":"2a35a61c-3bf9-4bf7-9569-73178247b08c","name":"Bue, Mats","orcid":"0000-0001-7215-8323","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35884164"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/antibiotics11070910","issn":["20796382"],"issue":"7","journal":"Antibiotics","paperid":"910","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Antibiotics","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133794502"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5953db83-9989-4859-84eb-f19a5350242f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Intermittent Short-Term Infusion vs. Continuous Infusion of Piperacillin : Steady State Concentrations in Porcine Cervical Spine Tissue Evaluated by Microdialysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-180252","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Along with technology trends like extended reality, wearables, IoT, and exergames, new design approaches have emerged, focusing on full-body interactions by actively working with the lived body's capacity to sense, feel, and create. Thus, designers are recommended to use movement as part of the design activity when designing for and of movement, regardless of the targeted application domain. However, designing for bodily experiences is challenging. We have identified a gap of no movement-based design framework available, including the moving body as the centre part and core material of the design processes. We recognise the human body is more than a physical object in the world, but a feeling, perceptualising body, that creates meaning in interaction with the environment. It thus frustrates and challenges us to reach a bodily grounded design process embracing the lived body. A common framework informed by the theoretical aspect of embodied cognition and the practical element of movement design can be a starting point for embodied design research. Recognising these challenges, we see a need for creating a bridge between practice and theory. Based on the bridging concept from Dalsgaard and Dindler, this paper presents a movement-based design framework to bridge the abstract idea of embodied cognition theory with the 4E perspectives of embodied, embedded, enactive and extended and concrete movement-based design practices. We created a movement-based design framework structuring the movement-based methods of different perspectives. The 4M model we propose contains three types of facilitator-mediated methods: 1) Mood-setters stimulating a creative body being, 2) Movement-based design methods for creating immersion in creative bodily activities, and 3) Movement concepts as knowledge and evidence for developing and validating movement artefacts. Besides the facilitator cards, the participants have access to Modifiers that can be used in conjunction with the other methods as creative inspiration for exploring, trying, or performing new movement possibilities.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Elbæk, Lars","Lekbo, Søren","Hansen, René Engelhardt","Kaos, Maximus","Andersen, Rasmus Vestergaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-598238"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-07","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2022-10-06","title":"16th European Conference on Games Based Learning, ECGBL 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Elbæk, Lars"],"keyword":["Design framework","Design methods","Embodiment","Exergames","Movement based design"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mind the gap the 000000000004m bridge between 000000000004e cognition and movement based design","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85141150815","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-598238","identifier":[{"id":"85141150815","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-5767db72-a9a9-4163-841c-6808a080c2fa"],"keyword":["Design framework","Design methods","Embodiment","Exergames","Movement-based design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-24A32AE9177665BF0B1DC71BCA119F9C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Soren","key":"lekbopau","last":"Lekbo","locid":"562a4a49-9ea9-4ae7-aedc-600242887a57","name":"Lekbo, Søren","name_org":"Lekbo, Soren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Engelhardt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2d887e76-ae82-4a8d-962e-5e927394748e","name":"Hansen, René Engelhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-4940","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maximus","key":"kaospau","last":"Kaos","locid":"b176e615-c51c-4cbc-9036-dc60def2d982","name":"Kaos, Maximus","orcid":"0000-0001-7233-370X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Vestergaard","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"933ed4e5-af40-4b7f-af1e-209e6ed31970","name":"Andersen, Rasmus Vestergaard","orcid":"0000-0002-9073-925X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Conceicao","key":"costapedh","last":"Costa","name":"Costa, Conceicao","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Filipe","key":"luzpedh","last":"Luz","name":"Luz, Filipe","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nuno","key":"fachadapedh","last":"Fachada","name":"Fachada, Nuno","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/ecgbl.16.1.667","eisbn":["9781914587511"],"issn":["20490992"],"issue":"1","pages":"208-215","publisher":"Academic Conferences and Publishing International","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Games-based Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 16th European Conference on Games Based Learning, ECGBL 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141150815"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5767db72-a9a9-4163-841c-6808a080c2fa"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Mind the gap : The 4M Bridge Between 4E-Cognition and Movement-Based Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-598238","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This report presents the case of a woman successfully treated with thoracoscopic detorsion of the right lung after she was diagnosed with a 180-degree torsion, 6 months after a video-assisted thoracoscopic right upper lobectomy for a stage 1 adenocarcinoma.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Timane, Jon Pedro","Jessen Hansen, Henrik","Petersen, René Horsleben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-670226"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lobectomy","VATS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"right lung torsion diagnosed 000000000006 months after a thoracoscopic right upper lobectomy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/icvts/ivac116","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-670226","identifier":[{"id":"85137134589","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35512206","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9419683","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-5910c1ea-0b5c-4990-94e2-c154a4fa484e"],"keyword":["Lobectomy","Lung torsion","VATS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BEEFA748016B6E7AD7B971E05E4031D3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346455091/Right_lung_torsion.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/icvts/ivac116","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn