Pedersen, Ole Birger","name_org":"Pedersen, Ole Birger Vesterager","orcid":"0000-0003-2312-5976","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16 17","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephanie Le","key":"hellardpau","last":"Hellard","name":"Hellard, Stephanie Le","rank":51,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13 1 2 30 3 31","corresponding":null,"first":"Unnur A","key":"valdimarsdóttirpau","last":"Valdimarsdóttir","name":"Valdimarsdóttir, Unnur A","rank":52,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35020900"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ije/dyab234","issn":["03005771","14643685"],"issn_org":["03005771"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Epidemiology","paperid":"dyab234","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132816164"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2fb0a8a1-cc19-4265-abc4-dce315e3cd71","au-a8e6ba47-0df8-4804-8cac-b03c18feb982","ku-e51a2f82-a73f-4c13-b8c5-e344a2605f9e","sdu-91e83597-37cf-41d3-8b49-e1010b6dbfe3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cohort Profile : COVIDMENT: COVID-19 cohorts on mental health across six nations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.78-002386","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The real-world use of triptans in the treatment of migraine is disappointing. Only 12% of the Danish migraine population purchased a triptan between 2014 and 2019, and only 43% repurchased a triptan after first prescription. The aim of the present study was to assess whether physicians and patients adhere to the therapeutic guideline on acute migraine treatment. We interviewed 299 triptan experienced participants with migraine and 101 triptan naïve participants with migraine from the Danish Migraine Population Cohort, using a semi-structured questionnaire. Descriptive statistical analyses were used to study the association with triptan use and the assessed factors. Among triptan naïve participants with migraine, 64% had consulted their general practitioner about their migraine, of whom only 23% received information about the possibility of triptan treatment. Among triptan experienced participants, 77% had only tried one type of triptan. Only 12% could recall they had been informed by their general practitioner to try each triptan three times before giving up. Twenty percent were informed to try three different triptans in total, if the first did not work. In disagreement with the guideline, participants who reported a low pain reduction by a triptan had only tried one type of triptan. Our study shows a low adherence to therapeutic guideline for the attack treatment of migraine. There is a need for better education of general practitioners regarding treatment of migraine. Future campaigns should aim to inform both the public and the general practitioner about antimigraine treatments.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Olesen, Astrid","Schytz, Henrik Winther","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Topholm, Mie","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Erikstrup, Christian","Mikkelsen, Susan","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Olesen, Jes","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Chalmer, Mona Ameri"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-008608"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contri