,"first":"G. B. E.","key":"jemecpau","last":"Jemec","locid":"b963b007-18b6-4432-897f-28b6a08275be","name":"Jemec, Gregor B E","name_org":"Jemec, G. B. E.","orcid":"0000-0002-0712-2540","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34862994"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jdv.17857","issn":["09269959","14683083"],"issn_org":["09269959"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of the European Academy of Dermatology and Venereology","pages":"717-725","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the European Academy of Dermatology and Venereology","title_org":"Journal of the European Academy of Dermatology and Venereology : JEADV","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121609588"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c92479d9-082a-42c2-8772-776f911c5250","au-6d94c344-709e-4769-9fbe-25d0bd9a6a97","ku-0e52733c-94f0-4863-a1dc-2185b847f6f3","sdu-dc432b18-9a98-4189-b23f-7b473e37e719"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Incidence and remission rates of self-reported hidradenitis suppurativa - A prospective cohort study conducted in Danish blood donors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.06-009654","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Detailed knowledge of how diversity in the sequence of the human genome affects phenotypic diversity depends on a comprehensive and reliable characterization of both sequences and phenotypic variation. Over the past decade, insights into this relationship have been obtained from whole-exome sequencing or whole-genome sequencing of large cohorts with rich phenotypic data1,2. Here we describe the analysis of whole-genome sequencing of 150,119 individuals from the UK Biobank3. This constitutes a set of high-quality variants, including 585,040,410 single-nucleotide polymorphisms, representing 7.0% of all possible human single-nucleotide polymorphisms, and 58,707,036 indels. This large set of variants allows us to characterize selection based on sequence variation within a population through a depletion rank score of windows along the genome. Depletion rank analysis shows that coding exons represent a small fraction of regions in the genome subject to strong sequence conservation. We define three cohorts within the UK Biobank: a large British Irish cohort, a smaller African cohort and a South Asian cohort. A haplotype reference panel is provided that allows reliable imputation of most variants carried by three or more sequenced individuals. We identified 895,055 structural variants and 2,536,688 microsatellites, groups of variants typically excluded from large-scale whole-genome sequencing studies. Using this formidable new resource, we provide several examples of trait associations for rare variants with large effects not found previously through studies based on whole-exome sequencing and/or imputation.","author_count":82,"contributors":["Halldorsson, Bjarni V.","Eggertsson, Hannes P.","Moore, Kristjan H. S.","Hauswedell, Hannes","Eiriksson, Ogmundur","Ulfarsson, Magnus O.","Palsson, Gunnar","Hardarson, Marteinn T.","Oddsson, Asmundur","Jensson, Brynjar O.","Kristmundsdottir, Snaedis","Sigurpalsdottir, Brynja D.","Stefansson, Olafur A.","Beyter, Doruk","Holley, Guillaume","Tragante, Vinicius","Gylfason, Arnaldur","Olason, Pall I.","Zink, Florian","Asgeirsdottir, Margret","Sverrisson, Sverrir T.","Sigurdsson, Brynjar","Gudjonsson, Sigurjon A.","Sigurdsson, Gunnar T.","Halldorsson, Gisli H.","Sveinbjornsson, Gardar","Norland, Kristjan","Styrkarsdottir, Unnur","Magnusdottir, Droplaug N.","Snorradottir, Steinunn","Kristinsson, Kari","Sobech, Emilia","Jonsson, Helgi","Geirsson, Arni J.","Olafsson, Isleifur","Jonsson, Palmi","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Erikstrup, Christian","Brunak, Søren","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Andersen, Steffen","Banasik, Karina","Burgdorf, Kristoffer Sølvsten","Didriksen, Maria","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Folkmann Hansen, Thomas","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jemec, Gregor Borut Ernst","Jennum, Poul","Johansson, Pär Ingemar","Hørup Larsen, Margit Anita","Mikkelsen, Susan","Nielsen, Kasper René","Nyegaard, Mette","Sækmose, Susanne","Sørensen, Erik","Thorsteinsdottir, Unnur","Brun, Mie Topholmt","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Jonsson, Frosti","Melsted, Pall","Jonsdottir, Ingileif","Rafnar, Thorunn","Holm, Hilma","Stefansson, Hreinn","Saemundsdottir, Jona","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Magnusson, Olafur T.","Masson, Gisli","Helgason, Agnar","Jonsson, Hakon","Sulem, Patrick","Stefansson, Kari"],"cuid":["S05-096.70-009498"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genetic Consortium","Danish Blood Donor Study Genomic Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Halldorsson, Bjarni V.","Stefansson, Kari"],"country":["Iceland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Landspitali University Hospital","Reykjavik University","Reykjavík University","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University of Iceland","deCODE Genetics","deCODE genetics, Inc"],"keyword":["Africa ethnology","Asia ethnology","Biological Specimen Banks","Cohort Studies","C