},{"affno":"13","first":"Krzysztof","key":"smietankapau","last":"Smietanka","name":"Smietanka, Krzysztof","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"grundpau","last":"Grund","name":"Grund, Christian","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"beerpau","last":"Beer","name":"Beer, Martin","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Timm","key":"harderpau","last":"Harder","name":"Harder, Timm","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35726917"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/mbio.00609-22","issn":["21507511","21612129"],"issn_org":["21612129"],"issue":"4","journal":"mBio","paperid":"e0060922","status":"p","title":"mBio","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137124851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0a7fe757-9ded-46af-a613-46ba0630ec8f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Has Epizootic Become Enzootic? Evidence for a Fundamental Change in the Infection Dynamics of Highly Pathogenic Avian Influenza in Europe, 2021","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-399728","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Germline pathogenic variants in CDKN2A predispose to various cancers, including melanoma, pancreatic cancer, and neural system tumors, whereas CDKN2B variants are associated with renal cell carcinoma. A few case reports have described heterozygous germline deletions spanning both CDKN2A and CDKN2B associated with a cancer predisposition syndrome (CPS) that constitutes a risk of cancer beyond those associated with haploinsufficiency of each gene individually, indicating an additive effect or a contiguous gene deletion syndrome. We report a young woman with a de novo germline 9p21 microdeletion involving the CDKN2A/CDKN2B genes, who developed six primary cancers since childhood, including a very rare extraskeletal osteosarcoma (eOS) at the age of 8. To our knowledge this is the first report of eOS in a patient with CDKN2A/CDKN2B deletion.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jensen, Marlene Richter","Stoltze, Ulrik Kristoffer","Hansen, Thomas van Overeem","Bak, Mads","Sehested, Astrid","Rechnitzer, Catherine","Mathiasen, René","Scheie, David","Larsen, Karen Bonde","Olsen, Tina Elisabeth","Muhic, Aida","Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","Rossing, Maria","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Wadt, Karin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532583"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Astrocytoma","Cutaneous melanoma","Osteosarcoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000009p000000000021 000000000003 microdeletion involving cdkn000000000002a 000000000002b in a young patient with multiple primary cancers and review of the literature","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/mcs.a006164","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-532583","identifier":[{"id":"85133101227","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9235845","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35422439","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e90439de-080f-4b95-8892-2d1c030bd6ad"],"keyword":["astrocytoma","cutaneous melanoma","neoplasm of the skin","neurofibromas","osteosarcoma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0F53A576100BBE1B28E50395FA4D6434"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/334019868/Cold_Spring_Harb_Mol_Case_Stud_2022_Jensen_a006164.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/mcs.a006164","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marlene Richter","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Marlene Richter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ulrik","key":"stoltzepau","last":"Stoltze","locid":"510a8cf1-5da9-40ee-a527-c3edd2a56478","name":"Stoltze, Ulrik Kristoffer","name_org":"Stoltze, Ulrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas Van Overeem","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c16bc086-759e-4400-ad4b-7826d837784a","name":"Hansen, Thomas van Overeem","name_org":"Hansen, Thomas Van Overeem","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","name":"Bak, Mads","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Astrid","key":"sehestedpau","last":"Sehested","name":"Sehested, Astrid","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Catherine","key":"rechnitzerpau","last":"Rechnitzer","name":"Rechnitzer, Catherine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"René","key":"mathiasenpau","last":"Mathiasen","locid":"20973b1c-9489-4d6c-b32f-584a790fab80","name":"Mathiasen, René","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"David","key":"scheiepau","last":"Scheie","locid":"88f5350d-9e09-4c54-933e-a854bd33b9a5","name":"Scheie, David","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen Bonde","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Karen Bonde","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tina Elisabeth","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Tina Elisabeth","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Aida","key":"muhicpau","last":"Muhic","name":"Muhic, Aida","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jane","key":"skjøthrasmussenpau","last":"Skjøth-Rasmussen","locid":"549d7d96-8a0c-4f6e-8a8e-2f9697a2aedc","name":"Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maria","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","locid":"21caea2d-4f85-4f9b-bb36-a8ec34cac4a8","name":"Rossing, Maria","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Karin","key":"wadtpau","last":"Wadt","locid":"f0aafc9d-1182-4952-871c-91446d121a5b","name":"Wadt, Karin","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35422439"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/mcs.a006164","issn":["23732865","23732873"],"issn_org":["23732865"],"issue":"4","journal":"Cold Spring Harbor molecular case studies","paperid":"a006164","status":"p","title":"Cold Spring Harbor molecular case studies","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133101227"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e90439de-080f-4b95-8892-2d1c030bd6ad"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"9p21.3 Microdeletion involving CDKN2A/2B in a young patient with multiple primary cancers and review of the literature","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532583","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Students often express that they feel stressed and struggle to engage actively in their own learning. Teachers often experience that the students struggle to engage in discussions and knowledge-sharing sessions. Innovation and design are constructive disciplines with which the students often have little or no experience. Students need to develop and mature as active and reflective learners to succeed in the design discipline and as Lifelong learners. Our basic assumption is that students are genuinely interested in being active and reflective learners but feel challenged on how to do so in practice. Therefore, we designed a framework consisting of a reflective learning log template and technical and evaluative criteria to be integrated into a course. At TAL2022 we would like to share how, after years of mixed success, we have succeeded in encouraging active and reflective learning by introducing technical and evaluative criteria as part of the learning activity. This includes: - The Reflection log template which is tailored to include key aspects of the educational programme and course assessment. The students are required to use the reflection log template to inform their reflections on their learning in and across courses. - Activities to provide knowledge on how to engage in reflective processes and develop reflective writing skills - Clear evaluation criteria in the form of an assessment rubric - Individual formative assessment feedback on students’ ability to reflect based on the assessment rubric Compared to previous years' use of the reflective learning log as a learning activity in the course, the clear framework provided enhanced students' ability to engage in reflective learning processes. The reflective learning log entries revealed a development in reflective writing skills, and the students were able to use the DIEP format to create coherent reflections in in-class knowledge-sharing sessions and discussions. Although some students found it hard and somewhat intrusive to engage in structured reflective processes, the technical and evaluative criteria provided were acknowledged as a support to achieve the learning objectives. The potential value of keeping a reflective learning log to engage in active learning is unquestionable. However, it does require resources in the form of time and mental effort which must be taken into consideration. The presented example of a reflection log template and associated technical and evaluative criteria can alleviate some of the mental effort required and thereby make reflective learning logs work in practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, René Engelhardt","Elbæk, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-603231"],"event":{"end":"2022-11-08","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2022-11-08","title":"Teaching for Active Learning - TAL 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, René Engelhardt"],"keyword":["Reflective practice","Teaching"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"making reflective learning logs work increasing students reflective abilities through educational practice","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-603231","ids":["sdu-68ef0c4d-78e5-4f8a-a10f-548fe01155a8"],"keyword":["Learning log","Reflective practice","Sports education","Teaching"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5AFE685F83B9F86DAE3C2E33EF5A13A7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Engelhardt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2d887e76-ae82-4a8d-962e-5e927394748e","name":"Hansen, René Engelhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-4940","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-68ef0c4d-78e5-4f8a-a10f-548fe01155a8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Making Reflective learning logs work : Increasing students’ reflective abilities through educational practice","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-603231","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Ependymoma is the second most common malignant brain tumor in children. The etiology is largely unknown and germline DNA sequencing studies focusing on childhood ependymoma are limited. We therefore performed germline whole-genome sequencing on a population-based cohort of children diagnosed with ependymoma in Denmark over the past 20 years (n = 43). Single nucleotide and structural germline variants in 457 cancer related genes and 2986 highly evolutionarily constrained genes were assessed in 37 children with normal tissue available for sequencing. Molecular ependymoma classification was performed using DNA methylation profiling for 39 children with available tumor tissue. Pathogenic germline variants in known cancer predisposition genes were detected in 11% (4/37; NF2, LZTR1, NF1 & TP53). However, DNA methylation profiling resulted in revision of the histopathological ependymoma diagnosis to non-ependymoma tumor types in 8% (3/39). This included the two children with pathogenic germline variants in TP53 and NF1 whose tumors were reclassified to a diffuse midline glioma and a rosette-forming glioneuronal tumor, respectively. Consequently, 50% (2/4) of children with pathogenic germline variants in fact had other tumor types. A meta-analysis combining our findings with pediatric pan-cancer germline sequencing studies showed an overall frequency of pathogenic germline variants of 3.4% (7/207) in children with ependymoma. In summary, less than 4% of childhood ependymoma is explained by genetic predisposition, virtually restricted to pathogenic variants in NF2 and NF1. For children with other cancer predisposition syndromes, diagnostic reconsideration is recommended for ependymomas without molecular classification. Additionally, LZTR1 is suggested as a novel putative ependymoma predisposition gene.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Foss-Skiftesvik, Jon","Stoltze, Ulrik Kristoffer","van Overeem Hansen, Thomas","Ahlborn, Lise Barlebo","Sørensen, Erik","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Kullegaard, Solvej Margrete Aldringer","Laspiur, Adrian Otamendi","Melchior, Linea Cecilie","Scheie, David","Kristensen, Bjarne Winther","Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Wadt, Karin","Mathiasen, René"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-037607"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Foss-Skiftesvik, Jon"],"keyword":["DNA methylation profiling","Genetic susceptibility","Genomics","Molecular classification","Pediatrics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"redefining germline predisposition in children with molecularly characterized ependymoma a population based 000000000020 year cohort","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40478-022-01429-1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work is part of Childhood Oncology Network Targeting Research, Organization & Life expectancy (CONTROL) and supported by the Danish Cancer Society (R-257-A14720), the Danish Childhood Cancer Foundation (2019-5934), the Danish Childhood Brain Tumor Foundation and the European Union’s Interregional Oresund–Kattegat–Skagerrak Grant."],"id":"S02-100.00-037607","identifier":[{"id":"85137038508","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36008825","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9404601","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-dfbb0bc2-f527-441f-bc49-27e1164960d2","ku-42bc992c-8438-49fc-b539-ff6abe1e7a39"],"keyword":["DNA methylation profiling","Genetic susceptibility","Genomics","Molecular classification","Pediatrics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Tec