i":"10.1007/978-3-030-91625-1_11","eisbn":["9783030916251"],"isbn":["9783030916244"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"192-211","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"26th Nordic Conference, NordSec 2021, Virtual Event, November 29–30, 2021, Proceedings","title":"Secure IT Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119856071"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-16cec89e-036d-435c-a30e-f4b9ffcaf90e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Preliminary Security Analysis, Formalisation, and Verification of OpenTitan Secure Boot Code","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-056753","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this work was to describe the leg-muscle-generated push force characteristics in sprint kayak paddlers for females and males on water. Additionally, the relationship between leg pushing force characteristics and velocity was investigated. Twenty-eight paddlers participated in the study. The participants had five minutes of self-chosen warm-up and were asked to paddle at three different velocities, including maximal effort. Left-and right-side leg extension force were collected together with velocity. Linear regression analyses were performed with leg extension force characteristics as independent variables and velocity as the dependent variable. A second linear regression analysis investigated the effect of paddling velocity on different leg extension force characteristics with an explanatory model. The results showed that the leg pushing force elicits a sinus-like pattern, increasing and decreasing throughout the stroke cycle. Impulse over 10 s showed the highest correlation to maximum velocity (r = 0.827, p < 0.01), while a strong co-correlation was observed between the impulse per stroke cycle and mean force (r = 0.910, p < 0.01). The explanatory model results revealed that an increase in paddling velocity is, among other factors, driven by increased leg force. Maximal velocity could predict 68% of the paddlers’ velocity within 1 km/h with peak leg force, impulse over 10 s, and stroke rate (p-value < 0.001, adjusted R-squared = 0.8). Sprint kayak paddlers elicit a strong positive relationship between leg pushing forces and velocity. The results confirm that sprint kayakers’ cyclic leg movement is a key part of the kayaking technique.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Klitgaard, Kent","Rosdahl, Hans","Brund, René Børge Korsgaard","Hansen, John","de Zee, Mark"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094272"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Klitgaard, Kent"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swedish School of Sport and Health Sciences"],"keyword":["Biomechanics","Footrest force","Force measurements"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of leg push forces and their relationship to velocity in on water sprint kayaking","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/s21206790","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094272","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8539159","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85116990154","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34696005","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-988c05cc-8cb1-4a76-9cdd-152cf781fa10"],"keyword":["Biomechanics","Footrest force","Force measurements","Leg forces","Sprint kayak"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F52A0EE1AE41B99189B2C39D4958A04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/450757463/sensors_21_06790.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/s21206790","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"swedish school of sport and health sciences","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish School of Sport and Health Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kent Kongsøre","key":"klitgaardpau","last":"Klitgaard","locid":"3748f398-b410-4024-9e66-d7c5dcee0b81","name":"Klitgaard, Kent","name_org":"Klitgaard, Kent Kongsøre","orcid":"0000-0001-8489-6374","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"rosdahlpau","last":"Rosdahl","name":"Rosdahl, Hans","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Børge Korsgaard","key":"brundpau","last":"Brund","locid":"b2374431-6b1e-4efe-9345-01733ef94596","name":"Brund, René Børge Korsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7246-4811","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ae89da32-d0ea-4a39-8295-a7cc351013f6","name":"Hansen, John","orcid":"0000-0003-4989-8117","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"dezeepau","last":"de Zee","locid":"25caa881-65a0-4f66-9d65-b760fc4787b3","name":"de Zee, Mark","orcid":"0000-0003-0584-271X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34696005"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/s21206790","issn":["14248220","14248239"],"issn_org":["14248220"],"issue":"20","journal":"Sensors","paperid":"6790","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Sensors","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116990154"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-988c05cc-8cb1-4a76-9cdd-152cf781fa10"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Characterization of Leg Push Forces and Their Relationship to Velocity in On-Water Sprint Kayaking","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094272","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
