{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Gislum, René","Hansen, Elly Møller","Thomsen, Ingrid Kaag"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-250856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["T0 2021"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kommentarer til oplæg til brug på workshop i pilotprojekt biomasse og efterafgrøder","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/226206594/Levering_Kommentarer_til_opl_g_til_brug_p_workshop_i_pilotprojekt_biomasse_og_efterafgr_der.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-250856","ids":["au-d4da0d9c-3cb7-41ce-9d4e-9f6726f803cb"],"keyword":["T0-2021"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-977BF2085E6486AD10953542B345B6DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/226206594/Levering_Kommentarer_til_opl_g_til_brug_p_workshop_i_pilotprojekt_biomasse_og_efterafgr_der.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René","key":"gislumpau","last":"Gislum","locid":"cad294b9-9707-4ac9-9596-aaae83673a95","name":"Gislum, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elly Møller","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5c906936-1ec6-4847-8322-c5643841a25a","name":"Hansen, Elly Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ingrid Kaag","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"d8cdf50c-86be-4cbc-bed1-575a8bdce5da","name":"Thomsen, Ingrid Kaag","orcid":"0000-0002-5108-5847","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"9","publisher":"DCA - Nationalt Center for Fødevarer og Jordbrug","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d4da0d9c-3cb7-41ce-9d4e-9f6726f803cb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Kommentarer til oplæg til brug på workshop i pilotprojekt biomasse og efterafgrøder","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-250856","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: There is currently a lack of imaging modalities that can be used as a sensitive measure in tendinopathy. Recent findings suggest the applicability of ultra-short echo time (UTE) magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) T2* mapping in tendons, but the reproducibility remains unknown. Purpose: To evaluate test–retest reproducibility of UTE MRI T2* mapping of tendinopathic patellar tendons and to evaluate the intra- and inter-observer reproducibility of the measurement. Material and Methods: Fifteen patients with chronic patellar tendinopathy were evaluated with UTE MRI twice in a 3.0-T scanner on the same day. Manual segmentation of the patellar tendon was performed by two blinded investigators and automated T2*map reconstruction was performed in custom-made software. Results: There was a significant and numerically small difference in test–retest T2* values (T2*meandiff = 0.06 ± 0.07 ms ≈ 3.7%; P = 0.006) with an ICC = 0.91 (95% confidence interval [CI] 0.58–0.98; typical error of 3.0%). The intra- and inter-observer reproducibility showed no significant bias (P = 0.493 and P = 0.052), and generally substantial reproducibility was demonstrated for T2* (intra-observer ICC = 0.99; 95% CI 0.98–1.00 and inter-observer ICC = 0.99; 95% CI 0.96–1.00, and typical error 1.3% and 1.3%, respectively). Conclusion: These data demonstrate a small bias between repeated measurements for UTE T2*, but with a very low associated mean difference (3.7%) between the two tests. The high ICC values and low typical error % demonstrate reproducibility of repeated T2*-mapping sessions. Further, the method showed substantial intra- and inter-observer reproducibility for T2* values proving feasibility for use of UTE T2* mapping in research and clinical practice.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Agergaard, Anne Sofie","Malmgaard-Clausen, Nikolaj M.","Svensson, Rene B.","Nybing, Janus D.","Boesen, Mikael","Kjaer, Michael","Magnusson, S. Peter","Hansen, Philip"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429182"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Patellar tendon","Reproducibility","T2 mapping","Tendinopathy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ute t000000000002 mapping of tendinopathic patellar tendons an mri reproducibility study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-429182","identifier":[{"id":"85084853803","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32340475","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3bdf1fed-5087-44c6-bf77-f9d42b05cb69"],"keyword":["Patellar tendon","T2* mapping","reproducibility","tendinopathy","ultra-short echo time imaging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-32A9C058E134575B092FB21319A1E062"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Healthy Ageing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Sofie","key":"agergaardpau","last":"Agergaard","name":"Agergaard, Anne Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nikolaj M.","key":"malmgaardclausenpau","last":"Malmgaard-Clausen","locid":"839d7576-e09c-4bf6-acfc-0b7ccc0bd358","name":"Malmgaard-Clausen, Nikolaj M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rene B.","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"fe236d1a-ef32-4a22-8125-31211110d8c8","name":"Svensson, Rene B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janus D.","key":"nybingpau","last":"Nybing","name":"Nybing, Janus D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mikael","key":"boesenpau","last":"Boesen","locid":"b449f652-d441-4b23-836f-2d5111ef64dd","name":"Boesen, Mikael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"7937b8ab-7820-4d25-982f-1d2f58b033a3","name":"Kjaer, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"S. Peter","key":"magnussonpau","last":"Magnusson","locid":"6f430caa-ac01-4dfe-9a62-e3a49afba21a","name":"Magnusson, S. Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philip","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Philip","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32340475"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0284185120918807","issn":["02841851","16000455"],"issn_org":["02841851"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Radiologica","pages":"215-224","status":"p","title":"Acta Radiologica","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084853803"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3bdf1fed-5087-44c6-bf77-f9d42b05cb69"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"UTE T2* mapping of tendinopathic patellar tendons : an MRI reproducibility study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-429182","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Loading intervention is currently the preferred management of tendinopathy, but to what extent different loading regimes influence the mechanical response in tendons is scarcely investigated. Therefore, the purposes of the investigation were to examine the effect of exercise interventions with either high or low load magnitude applied to the tendinopathic patellar tendon and the influence on its mechanical, material, and morphological properties. Forty-four men with chronic patellar tendinopathy were randomized to 12 weeks of exercising with either; 55% of 1RM throughout the period (MSR group) or 90% of 1RM (HSR group), and with equal total exercise volume in both groups. Mechanical (stiffness), material (T2* relaxation time), and morphological (cross-sectional area (CSA)) properties were assessed at baseline and after 12 weeks of intervention. MRI with ultra-short echo times (UTE) and T2*-mapping was applied to explore if T2* relaxation time could be used as a noninvasive marker for internal material alteration and early change thereof in response to intervention. There was no effect of HSR or MSR on the mechanical (stiffness), material (T2* relaxation time) or morphological (CSA) properties, but both regimes resulted in significant strength gain. In conclusion, there were no statistically superior effect of exercising with high (90%) compared to moderate (55%) load magnitude on the mechanical, material or morphological properties.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Agergaard, Anne Sofie","Svensson, Rene B.","Hoeffner, Rikke","Hansen, Philip","Couppé, Christian","Kjaer, Michael","Magnusson, S. Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489702"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Mechanical properties","Patellar tendon","Tendinopathy","load magnitude","loading based treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mechanical properties and ute t000000000002 in patellar tendinopathy the effect of load magnitude in exercise based treatment","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-489702","identifier":[{"id":"34189760","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85109856674","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a0fd7017-e97e-400a-ae40-b044a86e8d92"],"keyword":["Tendinopathy","UTE-T2 mapping","load magnitude","loading-based treatment","mechanical properties","patellar tendon"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-150784F5BE5A30391694C3D7774B9150"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Healthy Ageing","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anne Sofie","key":"agergaardpau","last":"Agergaard","name":"Agergaard, Anne Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rene B.","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"fe236d1a-ef32-4a22-8125-31211110d8c8","name":"Svensson, Rene B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rikke","key":"hoeffnerpau","last":"Hoeffner","locid":"324e02c5-665e-4479-af4e-adceafb55774","name":"Hoeffner, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philip","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Philip","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian","key":"couppépau","last":"Couppé","locid":"cad96e2a-ff10-4b12-a6a7-276468235915","name":"Couppé, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Michael","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"7937b8ab-7820-4d25-982f-1d2f58b033a3","name":"Kjaer, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"S. Peter","key":"magnussonpau","last":"Magnusson","locid":"6f430caa-ac01-4dfe-9a62-e3a49afba21a","name":"Magnusson, S. Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34189760"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sms.14013","issn":["09057188","16000838"],"issn_org":["09057188"],"issue":"10","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","pages":"1981-1990","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine and Science in Sports","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109856674"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a0fd7017-e97e-400a-ae40-b044a86e8d92"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mechanical properties and UTE-T2* in Patellar tendinopathy : The effect of load magnitude in exercise-based treatment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-489702","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Antarctic surface mass balance (SMB) is largely determined by precipitation over the continent and subject to regional climate variability related to the Southern Annular Mode (SAM) and other climatic drivers at the large scale. Locally however, firn and snowpack processes are important in determining SMB and the total mass balance of Antarctica and global sea level. Here, we examine factors that influence Antarctic SMB and attempt to reconcile the outcome with estimates for total mass balance determined from the GRACE satellites. This is done by having the regional climate model HIRHAM5 forcing two versions of an offline subsurface model, to estimate Antarctic ice sheet (AIS) SMB from 1980 to 2017. The Lagrangian subsurface model estimates Antarctic SMB of 2473.5±114.4ĝ€¯Gtĝ€¯yr-1, while the Eulerian subsurface model variant results in slightly higher modelled SMB of 2564.8±113.7ĝ€¯Gtĝ€¯yr-1. The majority of this difference in modelled SMB is due to melt and refreezing over ice shelves and demonstrates the importance of firn modelling in areas with substantial melt. Both the Eulerian and the Lagrangian SMB estimates are within uncertainty ranges of each other and within the range of other SMB studies. However, the Lagrangian version has better statistics when modelling the densities. Further, analysis of the relationship between SMB in individual drainage basins and the SAM is carried out using a bootstrapping approach. This shows a robust relationship between SAM and SMB in half of the basins (13 out of 27). In general, when SAM is positive there is a lower SMB over the plateau and a higher SMB on the westerly side of the Antarctic Peninsula, and vice versa when the SAM is negative. Finally, we compare the modelled SMB to GRACE data by subtracting the solid ice discharge, and we find that there is a good agreement in East Antarctica but large disagreements over the Antarctic Peninsula. There is a large difference between published estimates of discharge that make it challenging to use mass reconciliation in evaluating SMB models on the basin scale.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hansen, N.","Langen, Peter L.","Boberg, F.","Forsberg, R.","Simonsen, S. B.","Thejll, P.","Vandecrux, B.","Mottram, R."],"cuid":["S02-082.58-013448"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Hansen, N.","Hansen, Nicolaj"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-DMI","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-DMI","DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"downscaled surface mass balance in antarctica impacts of subsurface processes and large scale atmospheric circulation","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/tc-15-4315-2021","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.58-013448","identifier":[{"id":"000695494700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85114700927","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0bad94cd-4bd9-4874-a3a0-460ea2fccbf1","dtu-1ffda4cd-be7b-466e-a1ff-3aa77a4bf098"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-351F1A669C660C3366E18732CDFB1B7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/256931029/tc_15_4315_2021_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/tc-15-4315-2021","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":