4bfc281b5cbb","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingileif","key":"jonsdottiringileifpau","last":"Jonsdottir","name":"Jonsdottir, Ingileif","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hreinn","key":"stefanssonhreinnpau","last":"Stefansson","name":"Stefansson, Hreinn","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kari","key":"stefanssonkaripau","last":"Stefansson","name":"Stefansson, Kari","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33602968"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-021-82736-w","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"4188","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101028953"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-74160301-07d8-45b3-9782-7afa993b997a","au-bb0f8e26-2678-4e85-98a0-a9085e46ea2e","ku-27117702-be39-497c-b753-67d36669db74","sdu-e95e5a2d-91cd-4652-b6fb-e9aca02f07d6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A meta-analysis uncovers the first sequence variant conferring risk of Bell’s palsy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.71-005628","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Allergic rhinitis (AR), allergic conjunctivitis (AC), and asthma composing multiple phenotypes and improved understanding of these phenotypes and their respective risk factors are needed. Objectives: The objective of this study was to define the prevalence of AR, AC, and asthma and their association with allergen-specific immunoglobulin E (sIgE) sensitization in a large cohort of blood donors and identify risk factors. Methods: From the nationwide population-based Danish Blood Donor Study, 52,976 participants completed an electronic questionnaire including AR, AC, asthma, allergic predisposition, and childhood residence. Of these, 25,257 were additionally tested for sIgE to inhalation allergens (Phadiatop). Results: The prevalence of sIgE sensitization, AR, AC, and asthma was 30%, 19%, 15%, and 9%, respectively. The youngest birth cohorts had the highest prevalence of sIgE sensitization and symptoms of asthma, AR, and AC, and for asthma, they apparently experienced symptoms at an earlier age. The sIgE sensitization was positively associated with male sex. The sIgE seroprevalence was higher in participants with both AR and AC (ARC) than in participants with either AR or AC. Allergic predisposition and sIgE sensitization increased the risk of the diseases, while farm upbringing was associated with reduced prevalence of ARC, however, only in sIgE sensitized participants. Conclusion: Birth year, childhood residence, sIgE sensitization, and allergic predisposition were associated with asthma, AR, and AC prevalence. Individuals with self-reported ARC represent a primarily sIgE-positive phenotype, while those with either AR or AC represent more diverse phenotypes.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Susan","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Boldsen, Jens Kjærgaard","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Holst, Gitte Juel","Petersen, Mikkel Steen","Kaspersen, Kathrine Agergård","Møller, Bjarne Kuno","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Paarup, Helene Martina","Rostgaard, Klaus","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Sørensen, Erik","Handgaard, Linda Jenny","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Banasik, Karina","Burgdorf, Kristoffer Sølvsten","Ullum, Henrik","Sigsgaard, Torben","Erikstrup, Christian"],"cuid":["S04-099.96-011972"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Mikkelsen, Susan"],"keyword":["ADULTS","Allergic rhinitis","Association","Asthma","Conjunctivitis","Donation","Environment","Exposure","LIFE","Prevalence","Rhinitis","Symptoms","allergic IgE sensitization","blood donor","urban rural gradient"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Regionernes Kliniske Kvalitetsudviklingsprogram (RKKP)"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combinations of self reported rhinitis conjunctivitis and asthma predicts ige sensitization in more than 000000000025 000000000000 danes","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/clt2.12013","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Henrik Ullum has received unrestricted departmental grants from Novartis. No other conflicts of interest declared. None of the funders had any influence on study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of this manuscript."],"id":"S04-099.96-011972","identifier":[{"id":"85104888834","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8099331","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33900050","type":"p