al Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112483671"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-029c0cb1-2b9a-42e1-867a-32c6500cbbd3","au-3245144f-29f1-4b03-b84c-7fb17ee0df61","ku-9c34ce07-6fd6-4d67-b332-7d6f31052c0f","sdu-83df39ad-2a5d-452a-8615-8a09831246c9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of COVID-19 Pandemic on Sleep Quality, Stress Level and Health-Related Quality of Life-A Large Prospective Cohort Study on Adult Danes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-000137","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Iron is essential for many biological functions and iron deficiency and overload have major health implications. We performed a meta-analysis of three genome-wide association studies from Iceland, the UK and Denmark of blood levels of ferritin (N = 246,139), total iron binding capacity (N = 135,430), iron (N = 163,511) and transferrin saturation (N = 131,471). We found 62 independent sequence variants associating with iron homeostasis parameters at 56 loci, including 46 novel loci. Variants at DUOX2, F5, SLC11A2 and TMPRSS6 associate with iron deficiency anemia, while variants at TF, HFE, TFR2 and TMPRSS6 associate with iron overload. A HBS1L-MYB intergenic region variant associates both with increased risk of iron overload and reduced risk of iron deficiency anemia. The DUOX2 missense variant is present in 14% of the population, associates with all iron homeostasis biomarkers, and increases the risk of iron deficiency anemia by 29%. The associations implicate proteins contributing to the main physiological processes involved in iron homeostasis: iron sensing and storage, inflammation, absorption of iron from the gut, iron recycling, erythropoiesis and bleeding/menstruation.","author_count":78,"contributors":["Bell, Steven","Rigas, Andreas S.","Magnusson, Magnus K.","Ferkingstad, Egil","Allara, Elias","Bjornsdottir, Gyda","Ramond, Anna","Sørensen, Erik","Halldorsson, Gisli H.","Paul, Dirk S.","Burgdorf, Kristoffer Sølvsten","Eggertsson, Hannes P.","Howson, Joanna M. M.","Thørner, Lise W.","Kristmundsdottir, Snaedis","Astle, William J.","Erikstrup, Christian","Sigurdsson, Jon K.","Vukovic, Dragana","Dinh, Khoa M.","Tragante, Vinicius","Surendran, Praveen","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Vidarsson, Brynja","Jiang, Tao","Paarup, Helene M.","Onundarson, Pall T.","Akbari, Parsa","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Lund, Sigrun H.","Juliusson, Kristinn","Magnusson, Magnus I.","Frigge, Michael L.","Oddsson, Asmundur","Olafsson, Isleifur","Kaptoge, Stephen","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Runarsson, Gudmundur","Wood, Angela M.","Jonsdottir, Ingileif","Folkmann Hansen, Thomas","Sigurdardottir, Olof","Stefansson, Hreinn","Rye, David","Andersen, Steffen","Banasik, Karina","Brunak, Søren","Burgdorf, Kristoffer","Erikstrup, Christian","Jemec, Gregor Borut Ernst","Jennum, Poul","Johanssond, Pär I.","Nyegaard, Mette","Petersen, Mikkel","Werge, Thomas","Peters, James E.","Westergaard, David","Holm, Hilma","Soranzo, Nicole","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Ouwehand, Willem H.","Thorsteinsdottir, Unnur","Roberts, David J.","Sulem, Patrick","Butterworth, Adam S.","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Danesh, John","Brunak, Søren","Angelantonio, Emanuele Di","Ullum, Henrik","Stefansson, Kari"],"cuid":["S05-096.79-009808"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genomic Consortium","Danish Blood Donor Study Genomic Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Magnusson, Magnus K.","Stefansson, Kari"],"country":["Iceland","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Akureyri Hospital","All Global Affiliations","Emory University","John Radcliffe Hospital","Landspitali University Hospital","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","RAM","Rannsóknasetrið í Mjódd","The Laboratory in Mjodd","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University Medical Center Utrecht","University of Cambridge","University of Iceland","Utrecht Medical Center","Utrecht University","Wellcome Sanger Institute","Wellcome Trust","Wellcome Trust Genome Campus","deCODE Genetics","deCODE genetics, Inc"],"keyword":["Anemia Iron Deficiency blood","Biomarkers blood","Denmark","Ferritins blood","Genetic Loci","Genetic Variation","Genome Wide Association Study","Genotype","Homeostasis","Humans","Iceland","Iron Overload blood","Iron blood","Phenotype","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Transferrin metabolism","United Kingdom"],"le