{"abstract":"Purpose: Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) is one of the most lethal solid tumors. Most patients are diagnosed at an advanced stage where curative surgery is not an option. The aim of this study was to identify a panel of circulating proteins that could distinguish patients with PDAC from non-PDAC individuals. Experimental Design: We investigated 92 proteins known to be involved in inflammation, development, and progression of PDAC using the Olink immuno-oncology panel in serum samples from 701 patients with PDAC (stage I-IV), 102 patients with nonmalignant pancreatic diseases, and 180 healthy blood donors. Patients were included prospectively between 2008 and 2018. Plasma carbohydrate antigen 19-9 (CA19-9) was measured in all samples. The protein panels with the best diagnostic performances were developed by two bioinformaticians working independently, using LASSO and Ridge regression models. Results: Two panels of proteins (index I, containing 9 proteins+ CA19-9, and index II, containing 23 proteins + CA19-9) were identified. Index I was able to discriminate patients with PDAC from all patients with non-PDAC, with a ROC AUC value of 0.92 [95% confidence interval (CI), 0.89-0.96] in the discovery cohort and 0.92 (95% CI, 0.87-0.97) in the replication cohort. For index II, the AUC value was 0.96 (95% CI, 0.95-0.98) in the discovery cohort and 0.93 (95% CI, 0.90-0.96) in the replication cohort. All nine serum proteins of index I were found in index II. Conclusions: This study identified two circulating protein indices with the potential to discriminate between individuals with and without PDAC.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Lindgaard, Sidsel C.","Sztupinszki, Zsófia","Maag, Emil","Chen, Inna M.","Johansen, Astrid Z.","Jensen, Benny V.","Bojesen, Stig E.","Nielsen, Dorte L.","Hansen, Carsten P.","Hasselby, Jane P.","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Szallasi, Zoltan","Johansen, Julia S."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007537"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lindgaard, Sidsel C."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating protein biomarkers for use in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma identification","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85105351484&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["S.C. Lindgaard reports grants from Celgene, VELUX Foundation, The Danish Cancer Society, Harboe Foundation, Beckett Foundation, Foundation of Merchant M. Kristjan Kjær and wife Margrethe Kjær, and Memorial Fund of Carpenter Holm during the conduct of the study. Z. Sztupinszki reports grants from Velux Foundation during the conduct of the study. No disclosures were reported by the other authors."],"id":"S02-100.00-007537","identifier":[{"id":"85105351484","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33737308","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-9b666d7c-61df-4fb8-bd9c-ad0df22dad91","ku-54309954-e8c5-436b-844b-d9ec3c7b098f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-466ED16EF26353E3FAFCE969A4A1FCEB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Bioxpedia A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Immunology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1}],"person":[{"a