University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-85940323-cd2b-40e5-a765-34710c532b54","au-3def4ad2-ea0b-4843-881b-322d2bc94b85","ku-9c492ab9-d0ad-464a-aaad-b5edbe127607"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Superficial fungal infections and patients with Hidradenitis suppurativa - a study under the Danish Blood Donor Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.43-672375","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The risk factors and disease implications of hyper-hidrosis are unknown. The objectives of this retrospective cohort study were to estimate the prevalence of hyperhidrosis and to compare demographic, life-style, and socioeconomic parameters in blood donors with and without self-reported or hospital-diagnosed hyperhidrosis. The study included blood donors from the Danish Blood Donor Study for the period 2010-2019. Registry data were collected from Statistics Denmark. Overall, 2,794 of 30,808 blood donors (9.07%; 95% confidence interval (95% CI) 8.75-9.40) had self- reported hyperhidrosis and 284 of 122,225 (0.23%; 95% CI 0.21-0.26) had hospital-diagnosed hyperhidrosis. Self-reported hyperhidrosis was associated with smoking (odds ratio (OR) 1.17; 95% CI 1.05-1.31), overweight (OR 1.72; 95% CI 1.58-1.87), \"unemployed\" (OR 1.60; 95% CI 1.24-2.08), \"short education\" (OR 0.76; 95% CI 0.64-0.90), and lower income (beta-coefficient -26,121; 95% CI -37,931, -14,311). Hospital-diagnosed hyperhidrosis did not differ from controls. Thus, self-reported hyperhidrosis was associated with potential hyperhidrosis risk factors (smoking, overweight) and disease implications (unemployment, low education level and income).","author_count":16,"contributors":["Henning, Mattias A S","Ibler, Kristina S","Loft, Isabella","Ullum, Henrik","Erikstrup, Christian","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Topholm Bruun, Mie","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Sørensen, Erik","Burgdorf, Kristoffer S","Mikkelsen, Susan","Hansen, Thomas F","Pedersen, Ole B","Jemec, Gregor B E"],"cuid":["S04-097.96-006228"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Henning, Mattias A. S."],"keyword":["Blood Donors","Cohort Studies","Daily life","Denmark epidemiology","Health","Humans","Hyperhidrosis","Hyperhidrosis diagnosis","IMPACT","Overweight","PRIMARY PALMAR HYPERHIDROSIS","Prevalence","Questionnaire","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Smo king","Socioeconomic Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epidemiology of hyperhidrosis in danish blood donors","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/00015555-3790","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-097.96-006228","identifier":[{"id":"33734420","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9364250","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85105763711","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000654751700011","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-80c43cfb-c434-4e18-9ff0-6e9f1dc33e80","au-c86cc428-92b1-467e-ba57-d4b0e6f441d4","ku-431a8e36-5b91-4002-8d34-cef8bb1be7de","sdu-70dcf741-22d4-4321-816f-64d520383970"],"keyword":["Blood Donors","Cohort studies","DAILY-LIFE","Denmark/epidemiology","HEALTH","Humans","Hyperhidrosis","Hyperhidrosis/diagnosis","IMPACT","Overweight","PREVALENCE","PRIMARY PALMAR HYPERHIDROSIS","QUESTIONNAIRE","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Smo-king","Socioeconomic Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-DD128FBC0EF9E062F48C66EC8E58F7B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/439279307/Henning_et_al._2021_._Epidemiology_of_Hyperhidrosis_in_Danish_Blood_Donors.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/192916843/6035.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"o