{"abstract":"Randomness beacons are services that periodically emit a random number, allowing users to base decisions on the same random value without trusting anyone: ideally, the randomness beacon does not only produce unpredictable values, but is also of low computational complexity for the users, bias-resistant and publicly verifiable. Such randomness beacons can serve as an important primitive for smart contracts in a variety of contexts. This paper first presents a structured security analysis, based on which we then design, implement, and evaluate a trustworthy and efficient randomness beacon. Our approach does not require users to register or run any computationally intensive operations. We then compare different implementation and deployment options on distributed ledgers, and report on an Ethereum smart contract-based lottery using our beacon.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Dharanikota, Samvid","Jensen, Michael Toft","Kristensen, Sebastian Rom","Michno, Mathias Sass","Pignolet, Yvonne Anne","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Schmid, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-070685"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Schmid, Stefan"],"country":["Austria","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DFINITY Foundation","University of Vienna"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"breeding unicorns developing trustworthy and scalable randomness beacons","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0232261","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors received no specific funding for this work. The first four authors were immatriculated as students at university during the study, while the last three authors acted as supervisors and individual contributors."],"id":"S01-000.00-070685","identifier":[{"id":"32343754","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85083915758","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4732210a-65e1-4b43-8a13-21318d76542c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-5-8-ABFF7CDF90F80BC35DD18F4E76CF1A56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/404706842/pone.0232261.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0232261","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"at","key":"university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Vienna","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"dfinity foundation","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"DFINITY Foundation","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samvid","key":"dharanikotapau","last":"Dharanikota","name":"Dharanikota, Samvid","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Toft","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"074a0078-4dbc-4d84-99f8-673898fda707","name":"Jensen, Michael Toft","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian Rom","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"7c1614ce-7148-47c4-bd55-5e26fa11c185","name":"Kristensen, Sebastian Rom","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias Sass","key":"michnopau","last":"Michno","locid":"83e7d891-0b39-448d-ab29-7d6995b3a856","name":"Michno, Mathias Sass","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne Anne","key":"pignoletpau","last":"Pignolet","name":"Pignolet, Yvonne Anne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","name_org":"Hansen, René Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"schmidpau","last":"Schmid","name":"Schmid, Stefan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32343754"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0232261","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0232261","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078700404","2-s2.0-85083915758"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4732210a-65e1-4b43-8a13-21318d76542c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Breeding unicorns : Developing trustworthy and scalable randomness beacons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-070685","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We develop an approach to security of adaptive agents that is based on respecting the local security policies of agents rather than imposing a global security policy on all agents. In short, an agent can be assured, that it will not be able to observe any violation of its own security policy due to the changing presence of other agents in its environment. The development is performed for a version of Dijkstra’s Guarded Commands with relocation primitives, channel based communication, and explicit non-determinism. At the technical level a type system enforces local security policies whereas a reference monitor ensures that relocation is permissible with local security of all agents.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielson, Flemming","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Nielson, Hanne Riis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-089425"],"event":{"acronym":"ISoLA","end":"2020-10-30","place":"Rhodes, gr","start":"2020-10-20","title":"9th International Symposium on Leveraging Applications of Formal Methods, Verification and Validation, ISoLA 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielson, Flemming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adaptive security policies","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/431351823/2020_Adaptive_Security_Policies.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Acknowledgement. The first author was supported in part by the EU H2020-SU-ICT-03-2018 Project No. 830929 CyberSec4Europe (cybersec4europe.eu). The third author is currently on leave from the Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Technical University of Denmark, Kgs. Lyngby, Denmark."],"id":"S01-000.00-089425","identifier":[{"id":"85096527479","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8738fcd1-eb08-4408-8c74-ef147c922ae0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-E4BDCE877DCBFA672F9566930F60B415"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://orbit.dtu.dk/files/238027779/2020_Adaptive_Security_Policies.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/431351823/2020_Adaptive_Security_Policies.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"nielsonflemmingpau","last":"Nielson","name":"Nielson, Flemming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Rydhof","key":"hansenrenerydhofpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","name_or