{"abstract":"There is a continuing need for innovation across social, economic, and environmental domains in dealing with societal challenges. The continuing requirement for innovation is also evident in the field of sports and health, as gaining well-being and preventing physical inactivity is an ever-present challenge despite the innovativeness of the growing sports and health sector. In recent years, the development of 21stcentury skills have been proposed as a key to enable future generations to develop innovation competencies. This elevates the need for education which supports student acquisition of knowledge, and development of competencies and personal values. Mediating 21stcentury skill learning and developing innovation competence, a 36-hour camp for 80 students in K12 PE was designed. The camp was designed and facilitated by four sports and health graduate students in collaboration with six local PE teachers. Informed by the Gamestorming approach, the camp was designed as a game space consisting of a string of design methods to propose solutions for sport and well-being design challenges. Three challenges were formed in collaboration with the local municipality: 1) Creating better mental health in youth education, 2) Promoting physical activity for teenage girls, 3) Creating facilities for a water sports and adventure park. This paper aims to investigate 21stcentury skills and social-emotional learning experiences at high school students participating in a sports innovation camp. The students learning experience was captured through: 1) Students self-reported learning expectations 2) Students self-reported learning outcome, 3) Facilitator observations, and 4) Informal interviews. Students indicated that they gained creative skills, got better at communicating, collaborating, and critical thinking. The students mentioned that they got better at listening to each other, gained more patience with, and attention to each other, and they gained competences to concentrate under pressure. Altogether we conclude that a 36-hour high school innovation-camp in physical education have documented qualitative learning outcomes in the development of competences (to act) and personal character qualities (to value) for students in upper secondary education.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Elbæk, Lars","Hansen, René Engelhardt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-575860"],"event":{"acronym":"ECGBL","end":"2020-09-25","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2020-09-24","title":"14th European Conference on Game Based Learning, ECGBL 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design game","Design thinking","Innovation","Physical education","Social emotional learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"innovation camp as 000000000021 sup st sup century skill learning game in k000000000012 pe teaching","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85096679611","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-575860","identifier":[{"id":"85096679611","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-09560dde-5e42-4cf7-943b-f0edefaf338a"],"keyword":["21Century Skills","Design Game","Design Thinking","Innovation","Physical Education","Social-Emotional Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-4074192B3D01F552AE81164C3FAEC79E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbaekpau","last":"Elbaek","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","name_org":"Elbaek, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Engelhardt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2d887e76-ae82-4a8d-962e-5e927394748e","name":"Hansen, René Engelhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-4940","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Panagiotis","key":"fotarispedh","last":"Fotaris","name":"Fotaris, Panagiotis","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/gbl.20.041","eisbn":["9781912764716"],"pages":"142-150","publisher":"Academic Conferences and Publishing International","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 14th European Conference on Game Based Learning, ECGBL 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096679611","2-s2.0-85097788988"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-09560dde-5e42-4cf7-943b-f0edefaf338a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Innovation camp as 21<sup>st</sup>century skill learning game in k12 pe teaching","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-575860","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Roux-en-Y-gastric bypass (RYGB) surgery is an effective treatment for morbid obesity. A possible overlooked side effect is negative bone metabolic consequences. Design: A seven-year prospective study following ten women and seven men after RYGB (baseline mean age 43 ± 8 years, BMI 42 ± 6 kg/m2). Methods: Lumbar spine and total hip bone mineral density (BMD) using dual energy x-ray absorptiometry, distal radius and tibia bone geometry, volumetric BMD, microarchitecture and finite element estimated bone strength using high-resolution peripheral quantitative CT and biochemical markers of bone remodelling were assessed at baseline, 2 and 7 years. Results: Compared to baseline, body weight was 24 ± 10% lower after 2 years and 21 ± 11% after 7 years. During the 7 years of follow-up, radius and tibia vBMD had declined 13 ± 8% and 8 ± 7% from baseline to 2 years and further 10 ± 7% and 7 ± 8% from 2 to 7 years (all P < 0.001). At both radius and tibia, cortical thickness declined and cortical porosity increased. From baseline to 7 years, there were clear indications of deteriorations of the trabecular network with fewer, more widely spaced and more in-homogeneously distributed trabeculae in both radius and tibia. Overall, declines in estimated bone strength of 16 ± 9% in radius and 16 ± 7% in tibia were observed (both P < 0.001). Conclusion: Seven years after RYGB, evidence of continuous declines in BMD and ongoing deterioration of bone microarchitecture and reduced estimated bone strength compared to baseline and 2 years post-surgery results were found. These findings emphasize the need for regular assessment of bone health in patients with prior RYGB.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Stinus","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Hermann, Anne Pernille","Støving, Rene Klinkby"],"cuid":["S02-091.63-045355"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"continuous decline in bone mineral density and deterioration of bone microarchitecture 000000000007 years after roux en y gastric bypass surgery","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-19-0741","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.63-045355","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7087496","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31940278","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85079201315","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-af839f12-8809-4ae7-984c-5705a7d9365a","sdu-eb42b47d-8f10-4225-b250-5e694c3a8be1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6EE8A089325E5B625D7A45110EC46F1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/160855505/_1479683X_European_Journal_of_Endocrinology_Continuous_decline_in_bone_mineral_density_and_deterioration_of_bone_microarchitecture_7_years_after_Roux_en_Y_gastric_bypass_surgery.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-19-0741","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/253191486/_1479683X_European_Journal_of_Endocrinology_Continuous_decline_in_bone_mineral_density_and_deterioration_of_bone_microarchitecture_7_years_after_Roux_en_Y_gastric_bypass_surgery.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU Univers