{"abstract":"Nitrogen (N) management in modern farming needs to balance the interests of yield quantity and quality with environmental impact of reactive N lost to the atmosphere and aquatic environments. Mechanistic agroecosystem models are useful tools to analyse the combined effects of management options and natural conditions, including soil fertility and climate, site‐specific optimal N application rates and environmental impact. An important component of the system description is the crop module, including the responses to N status and N stress. To improve the description of crop growth response to N status in the DAISY model system, we implemented an empirical model for N status effects in winter wheat on the partitioning of assimilated dry matter and N between leaves and stems, originally described by Ratjen and Kage (Journal of Agronomy and Crop Science , 2016, 202, 576s). To our knowledge, this mechanism has not been included in any of the most widespread and commonly used mechanistic agroecosystem models. We tested and compared the model performance with and without the new N status response against data from a two‐season winter wheat experiment in Denmark, where crop growth and partitioning of dry matter and N were measured. Implementation of the new N status response function improved model performance and ensured a more robust crop growth description, especially in scenarios with periods of low crop N status or N stress. The mechanism mimics an adaptation strategy, where the crop balances N stress and growth potential by dynamically adjusting the leaf‐stem ratio and thereby N demand. This behaviour opens a discussion regarding the empirical concept of a biomass driven critical N curve.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gyldengren, Jacob Glerup","Abrahamsen, Per","Olesen, Jørgen E","Styczen, Merete","Hansen, Søren","Gislum, René"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-029151"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gislum, René"],"keyword":["Calibration","Crop physiology","Dynamic modelling","Faculty of Science","GROWTH","Management","Season","Sensors","Use efficiency","Winter wheat","critical N dilution curve","nitrogen status","nitrogen stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of winter wheat n status on assimilate and n partitioning in the mechanistic agroecosystem model daisy","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85085019954","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-029151","identifier":[{"id":"85085019954","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000534230500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-e3881038-cb42-4d38-9452-70530338b694","ku-8b9c996e-160c-4e86-a259-1a46e8943d13"],"keyword":["CALIBRATION","Faculty of Science","GROWTH","MANAGEMENT","NITROGEN DILUTION CURVE","SEASON","SENSORS","USE EFFICIENCY","critical N dilution curve","crop physiology","dynamic modelling","nitrogen status","nitrogen stress","winter wheat"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DE607553E4D596A626779CE8325D333B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Environmental Chemistry and Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Glerup","key":"gyldengrenpau","last":"Gyldengren","locid":"c982ca5e-a20f-448e-8781-0c1ba4d0133b","name":"Gyldengren, Jacob Glerup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Per","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"890129b9-995a-458c-bc5d-203846210934","name":"Abrahamsen, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-4804-2758","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen E","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"d3bcf85c-a32d-4169-8f78-b2bf7fe78102","name":"Olesen, Jørgen E","orcid":"0000-0002-6639-1273","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Merete","key":"styczenpau","last":"Styczen","locid":"ff480289-c8d9-48f2-8481-ea97bcdea046","name":"Styczen, Merete Elisabeth","name_org":"Styczen, Merete","orcid":"0000-0003-0420-2577","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"95884c00-416a-4f9f-8b62-c02d5fdf0faf","name":"Hansen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5483-6853","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René","key":"gislumpau","last":"Gislum","locid":"cad294b9-9707-4ac9-9596-aaae83673a95","name":"Gislum, René","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jac.12412","issn":["09312250","1439037X"],"issn_org":["09312250"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Agronomy and Crop Science","pages":"784-805","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Agronomy and Crop Science","volume":"206"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085019954"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e3881038-cb42-4d38-9452-70530338b694","ku-8b9c996e-160c-4e86-a259-1a46e8943d13"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of winter wheat N status on assimilate and N partitioning in the mechanistic agroecosystem model DAISY","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-029151","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Catheter ablation for atrial fibrillation (CAF) improves symptoms, but whether CAF improves outcome is less clear. The purpose of this study was to investigate whether CAF is associated with improved outcome in atrial fibrillation (AF) patients with previous direct current (DC) cardioversion. Methods and results: We performed a nationwide cohort study including all patients who underwent their 1st direct current cardioversion for AF in the period 2003-15 (N = 25 439). End points were all-cause death, cardiovascular death, stroke/thromboembolism, and incident heart failure (HF). Catheter ablation for AF was treated as a time-varying covariate and the association with outcome was assessed using Cox regression. We also constructed a propensity-matched cohort and assessed the association between CAF and outcome. Median follow-up was 5.3 years (inter-quartile range 3.0-8.7 years). A total of 3509 patients (13.8%) underwent CAF during the study period. Following adjustment for age, gender, comorbidities, medications, educational level, household income, and CHA2DS2VASc score, CAF was associated with reduced risks of all-cause death, cardiovascular death, and incident HF [all-cause death: hazard ratio (HR) 0.69, P < 0.001; cardiovascular death: HR 0.68, P = 0.003; incident HF: HR 0.76, P = 0.011]. Catheter ablation for AF was not associated with a reduced risk of stroke/thromboembolism. These results were replicated in a propensity-matched cohort. Conclusion: In AF patients with a prior DC cardioversion, CAF was associated with a reduced risk of all-cause and cardiovascular death. This may be due to a reduced risk of HF.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Modin, Daniel","Claggett, Brian","Gislason, Gunnar","Hansen, Morten Lock","Worck, Rene","Johannessen, Arne","Hansen, Jim","Svendsen, Jesper Hastrup","Pallisgaard, Jannik L","Schou, Morten","Køber, Lars","Solomon, Scott D","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Biering-Sørensen, Tor"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011846"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Catheter ablation","Heart failure","Outcome","Prognosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["TIMI Study Group, Cardiovascular Division, Department of Medicine, Brigham and Women's Hospital, Harvard Medical School, Boston, MA, USA."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"catheter ablation for atrial fibrillation is associated with lower incidence of heart failure and death","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85077666526&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011846","identifier":[{"id":"85077666526","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31595294","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f81588e7-285d-4f2e-88d4-4f8b044a701a","ku-81df3a4d-ebec-4b05-bf3e-547baf24c692"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Catheter ablation","Heart failure","Outcome","Prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DB0A5296363ADA74B83EDADAE8FB1D17"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscel