{"abstract":"Mussel farming has increasingly come into focus as a potential mitigation measure for fish farms and eutrophication, in addition to being a food source. This study presents a GIS-based suitability analysis combined with a farm scale model to identify appropriate mussel farming sites. The sites are investigated in terms of potential mussel harvest, nutrient removal, and effects on water transparency. The model is applied to the south-western Baltic Sea. The identified suitable area is about 5–8% of the case study extent. The model shows that elevated chlorophyll levels stimulate mussel growth and that upon mussel harvest, nutrients can be removed. A single mussel farm cannot compensate for all nutrients emitted by a fish farm, but it can increase water transparency up to at least 200 m from the farm. Potential nutrient removal and water transparency increases are essential criteria for site selection in eutrophic seas, such as the Baltic Sea.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thenen, Miriam von","Maar, Marie","Hansen, Henning Sten","Friedland, René","Schiele, Kerstin S."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-006763"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thenen, Miriam von","von Thenen, Miriam"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Institute for Baltic Sea Research"],"keyword":["Ecological modelling","Eutrophication","Marine spatial planning","Shellfish farming","Spatial suitability analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"applying a combined geospatial and farm scale model to identify suitable locations for mussel farming","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85085296533&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work resulted from the BONUS BASMATI and BONUS OPTIMUS projects. Both are supported by BONUS (Art. 185) funded jointly by the European Union 's Seventh Framework Programme for research, technological development and demonstration, and by Baltic Sea national funding institutions (BONUS BASMATI: Innovation Fund Denmark, Swedish Research Council Formas, Academy of Finland, Latvian Ministry of Education and Science, and Forschungszentrum Jülich GmbH, Germany; BONUS OPTIMUS: Innovation Fund Denmark, the German Ministry for Education and Science (BMBF), the Swedish Agency for Marine and Water Management and the National Centre for Research and Development, Poland)."],"id":"S02-100.00-006763","identifier":[{"id":"85085296533","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32510396","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-8b7d5b5d-5a95-4e59-88c6-81cbe95ea586","au-43ca787f-d3a6-44a2-937a-89387cb2a2c3"],"keyword":["Ecological modelling","Eutrophication","Marine spatial planning","Shellfish farming","Spatial suitability analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B9A9776896F838F843983F80FFE974D5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Land Management And Geoinformatics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz institute for baltic sea research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Institute for Baltic Sea Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Applied Marine Ecology and Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Miriam","key":"vonthenenpau","last":"von Thenen","locid":"cd728136-5f32-4c13-8064-429bab5ab688","name":"Thenen, Miriam von","name_org":"von Thenen, Miriam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie","key":"maarpau","last":"Maar","locid":"82a27bc5-38c0-4f2b-808e-b451f47d5adc","name":"Maar, Marie","orcid":"0000-0001-8594-2993","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning Sten","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c42e2013-4f33-4a85-89e5-701a7f898358","name":"Hansen, Henning Sten","orcid":"0000-0001-7004-0698","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"friedlandpau","last":"Friedland","name":"Friedland, René","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kerstin S.","key":"schielepau","last":"Schiele","name":"Schiele, Kerstin S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32510396"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.marpolbul.2020.111254","issn":["0025326X","18793363"],"issn_org":["0025326X"],"journal":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","paperid":"111254","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","volume":"156"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085296533"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8b7d5b5d-5a95-4e59-88c6-81cbe95ea586","au-43ca787f-d3a6-44a2-937a-89387cb2a2c3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Applying a combined geospatial and farm scale model to identify suitable locations for mussel farming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-006763","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents an introduction to Arne Grøn's existential hermeneutics as a philosophical method, while also attempting to indicate how Grøn's work contributes to and engages in a number of crucial topics in modern continental philosophy. The first section of the paper shows how Grøn draws on Paul Ricoeur and Michael Theunissen to rethink the concept of existence through a reading of Kierkegaard that uncouples this concept from the self-evident status it attained in twenty-century existentialism. The second section of the paper argues that Grøn proposes an existential ethics that takes the Kierkegaardian notion that humans are inherently normative beings and uses this as a basis for a critique of ethics, as well as for establishing an ethics of vision inspired by Kierkegaard. The third section of the paper presents a reading of Grøn's notion of religion as an inextricable part of human existence.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stigel Hansen, Bjarke Mørkøre","Karlsen, Mads Peter","Rosfort, René"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-031513"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Unknown external organisation"],"keyword":["Arne Grøn","Ethics","Existence","Existential hermeneutics","Religion"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"arne grøn s existential hermeneutics existence ethics and religion","src":["cbs","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-031513","identifier":[{"id":"85098544434","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-551f27b3-7d74-4a45-84ad-fb7906105f42","ku-6ca639e6-9c78-4151-99ec-b932596a1da7"],"keyword":["Arne Grøn","Ethics","Existence","Existential hermeneutics","Religion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-64E8854F92E077AABE1969464FC4CF15"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)","Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, The Søren Kierkegaard Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"unknown external organisation","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Unknown external organisation","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"René","key":"rosfortpau","last":"Rosfort","locid":"0068997b-08c9-4fd5-b4b7-89a0c17c248e","name":"Rosfort, René","orcid":"0000-0002-9766-9741","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Peter","key":"karlsenpau","last":"Karlsen","locid":"b9d8e839-6435-45a8-b2af-440a8a65aa53","name":"Karlsen, Mads Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Bjarke Mørkøre Stigel","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2afd8110-8f1e-433f-afa0-b44bb51395d2","name":"Hansen, Bjarke Mørkøre Stigel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1163/24689300-05301003","issn":["00702749","24689300"],"issn_org":["00702749"],"journal":"Danish Yearbook of Philosophy","pages":"108-132","publisher":"Brill Academic Publishers","status":"p","title":"Danish Yearbook of Philosophy","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098544434"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-551f27b3-7d74-4a45-84ad-fb7906105f42","ku-6ca639e6-9c78-4151-99ec-b932596a1da7"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Arne Grøn's Existential Hermeneutics : Existence, Ethics and Religion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-031513","year":"2020","yearsub":2021}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients with rheumatic diseases, routinely consult the outpatient clinic 1-2 times a year to see their rheumatologist. Many of the patients also attend nurse-led consultations to receive instructions, regarding treatment in association to their intravenous treatment, or DMARD dispensing in the clinic. As clinicians we have an assumption of what the textquotedblrightgood practicetextquotedblright is in relation to the patients, but we have little insight, into the patients’ own experience and satisfaction.Objectives: To investigate the patients views on the level of information, and their experience and satisfaction with the doctor and nurse-led consultations in the outpatient clinic.Methods: The approach of the survey was both quantitative and qualitative. A questionnaire was designed with four questions on a matrix scale concerning their information level on their disease/symptoms; their treatment; if they had received written material and if so, it’s value; and their possibility to talk about subjects that matters for them during consultations. To gain a qualitative approach with focus on the patients’ experiences and comments, every question was constructed with space for comments. Comments were transcribed, indexed, analysed, and thematically divided. The inclusion of patients were all patients visiting the clinic within a specific week in January 2019.Results: The results from the four questions, are shown in the figures below, measured in percentage. In total, 283 participated (response rate 60.Four themes covered from the analysis of patients’ comments. textquotedblleftSeeking own answerstextquotedblright, textquotedblleftOwn coping textendash efforttextquotedblright, textquotedblleftConversation with doctor/nursetextquotedblright and textquotedblleftTreatment/medicationtextquotedblright. Comments revealed many descriptions and stories of patients, showered with all types of suggestions of taking control or managing the disease by them self, from their family or media. It also revealed their interest in discussing, these subjects and matters with the doctor/nurse, without being rejected. The feeling of rejection resulted in some patients trying other treatments or introducing changes in their lifestyle, without involving the doctor. The patients also called for more knowledge about physical training, and not only medical treatment.Conclusion: In general, the patients had a very positive perception towards the consultations, and the information from the outpatient clinic. Despite that, the themes indicated a pattern, that needs to be considered, so clinicians acknowledge the patients wish for guidance, besides the medical treatment. To support the patient, without leaving them with a feeling of being rejected, we need to consider how to articulate the subjects the patients are exposed to outside our clinic, so the patients feel free to inform or involve the clinic instead of being silent, in risk of counteracting the medical treatment.Acknowledgments: We are grateful to the participants who shared their experiences. We also thank an internal research group taking part of the investigation.Disclosure of Interests: Ida Lund: None declared, Annette Hansen Consultant of: AbbVie, Speakers bureau: Eli Lily, Betina Stampe: None declared, René Cordtz: None declared, Lene Dreyer: None declared","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lund, I.","Hansen, A.","Stampe, B.","Cordtz, René","Dreyer, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065156"],"event":{"end":"2020-06-03","place":"E-congress, online","start":"2020-06-03","title":"Annual European Congress of Rheumatology: EULAR 2020 (e-congress, online)","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patients view on consultation in outpatient clinic from satisfaction to demand of guidance into more self management","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ard.bmj.com/content/79/Suppl_1/1276.1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-065156","ids":["aau-3416f075-e423-4946-b4d4-9b251f6da1ea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B71329E58EDE61628B84225724BD86DF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Rheumatology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"I.","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, I.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"stampepau","last":"Stampe","name":"Stampe, B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"cordtzpau","last":"Cordtz","locid":"49fa43fa-cc2f-4876-bf14-868a1e2288a5","name":"Cordtz, René","name_org":"Cordtz, R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"dreyerpau","last":"Dreyer","locid":"b12f9d3c-1fa5-4513-8002-c9fd87d60d53","name":"Dreyer, Lene","name_org":"Dreyer, L.","orcid":"0000-0002-5156-2922","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/annrheumdis-2020-eular.422","issn":["00034967","14682060"],"issn_org":["00034967"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","pages":"1276-1276","paperid":"SAT0632-HPR","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3416f075-e423-4946-b4d4-9b251f6da1ea"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Patients view on consultation in outpatient clinic – from satisfaction to demand of guidance into more self-management","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065156","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"SBi-anvisning 272, 2. udgave, forklarer og fortolker bestemmelserne i Bygningsreglement 2018 (BR18) gældende fra 1. juli 2020. Med BR18 er indført en ny kapitelstruktur. Samtidig er kravene til myndighedsbehandlingen ændret, og er for brandforhold og bærende konstruktioner erstattet af en certificeringsordning. Anvisningen har samme kapitelstruktur som bygningsreglementet, og SBi's anvisningstekst ledsages af den fulde reglementstekst samt teksten i Trafik-, Bygge- og Boligstyrelsens hovedvejledninger. Desuden henviser anvisningen til relevante standarder, andre SBi-anvisninger og andet baggrundsmateriale fra det almene tekniske fælleseje med uddybende information. Anvisningen omhandler de samme emner som BR18: administrative bestemmelser, adgangsforhold, affaldssystemer, afløbsinstallationer, brandforhold, brugerbetjente anlæg, byggepladsen, byggeret og helhedsvurdering, bygningers indretning, elevatorer, energiforbrug, energiforsyningsanlæg, forureninger, fugt og vådrum, konstruktioner, legepladser, lydforhold, lys og udsyn, termisk indeklima, ubebyggede arealer, vandinstallationer og ventilation. Anvisningen henvender sig til alle professionelle parter i byggeriet, særligt projekterende og kommunale byggesagsbehandlere.","author_count":20,"contributors":["de Place Hansen, Ernst Jan","Ginnerup, Søren","Sigbrand, Lone","Jensen, Ole Michael","Brandt, Erik","Morelli, Martin","Sørensen, Lars Schiøtt","Buch-Hansen, Thomas Cornelius","Møller, Eva B.","Kirkeby, Inge Mette","Kragh, Jesper","Aggerholm, Søren","Wittchen, Kim Bjarne","Nielsen, Rene Dahl","Gunnarsen, Lars","Rasmussen, Torben Valdbjørn","Aagaard, Niels Jørgen","Rasmussen, Birgit","Johnsen, Kjeld","Bergsøe, Niels Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-090757"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bebyggelsesregulerende bestemmelser","Bygningsindretning","Dokumentation","Energiforbrug","Fugt","Indeklima","Installationer","Konstruktioner","Luftkvalitet","Lyd","Lys","Tilgængelighed","Vand","Ventilation","Vådrum","byggetilladelser"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anvisning om bygningsreglement 000000002018","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://sbi.dk/anvisninger/Pages/272-Anvisning-om-Bygningsreglement-2018-2_1.aspx","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-090757","ids":["aau-8c17256f-a2dd-4f39-b197-8f595ba566e5"],"keyword":["bebyggelsesregulerende bestemmelser","byggetilladelser","bygningsindretning","dokumentation","energiforbrug","fugt","indeklima","installationer","konstruktioner","luftkvalitet","lyd","lys","tilgængelighed","vand","ventilation","vådrum"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-36864969048B368274D5DB55D649A108"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Building Physics Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Building Technology, Management and Indoor Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Den