"key":"dahirpau","last":"Dahir","name":"Dahir, Lula","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"19","first":"Erasmo","key":"rodríguezpau","last":"Rodríguez","name":"Rodríguez, Erasmo","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20 21","first":"Jorge","key":"salgadopau","last":"Salgado","name":"Salgado, Jorge","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A. Britta K.","key":"sannelpau","last":"Sannel","name":"Sannel, A. Britta K.","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"22","first":"Ana Carolina","key":"santospau","last":"Santos","name":"Santos, Ana Carolina","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Samaneh","key":"seifollahiaghmiunipau","last":"Seifollahi-Aghmiuni","name":"Seifollahi-Aghmiuni, Samaneh","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 23","first":"Ylva","key":"sjöbergpau","last":"Sjöberg","locid":"9cda148a-6a53-4119-8065-61ebbc1440b7","name":"Sjöberg, Ylva","orcid":"0000-0002-4292-5808","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 24","first":"Lian","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Lian","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Josefin","key":"thorslundpau","last":"Thorslund","name":"Thorslund, Josefin","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guillaume","key":"vigourouxpau","last":"Vigouroux","name":"Vigouroux, Guillaume","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lan","key":"wangerlandssonpau","last":"Wang-Erlandsson","name":"Wang-Erlandsson, Lan","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 25","first":"Diandian","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Diandian","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"19","first":"David","key":"zamorapau","last":"Zamora","name":"Zamora, David","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"18","first":"Alan D.","key":"zieglerpau","last":"Ziegler","name":"Ziegler, Alan D.","rank":51,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Imenne","key":"åhlénpau","last":"Åhlén","name":"Åhlén, Imenne","rank":52,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/w11030619","issn":["20734441"],"issue":"3","journal":"Water","paperid":"619","status":"p","title":"Water","title_org":"Water (Switzerland)","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-352b6aa8-630e-4dca-9ae6-a5ee72d44cf1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Priorities and interactions of Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) with focus on wetlands","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425029","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Innovation in sport and movement has established itself as a multidisciplinary practice in which part of the innovations are various digital artefacts supporting physical activity, also termed movement games. In this empirical and philosophical study, we examine a multitude of value stances on an ethical-aesthetic continuum. Value stances are defined as philosophically embracing virtues, values, logics or lenses. We find that balancing the multitude of ethical-aesthetical value stances and with respect to “the purposefulness of no purpose” in doing sport, play, and physical movement, is vital in designing sustainable movement-games. Using artefacts such as heart rate monitors, GPS trackers, and other fitness trackers all acts for the quantifiable self. Similarly, mobile games, exergames, exertion-games, and play installations for physical activity have found their way into private and public spaces. These movement-games have a somewhat utilitarian user approach often designed mainly for health gains, not harvesting the full potential of seeing the users as social and physical moving human existences. This restricted user approach raises the question; what value stances may enhance the design of sustainable movement-games? The Danish existentialist philosopher Søren Kierkegaard stated that the aesthetic dimension denotes that humans strive to perform and feel well and to have pleasurable experiences. The ethical dimension refers to the human aspiration to do good based on interhuman normative standards. In our contemporary society we aim mainly at the aesthetic – pleasurable experiences – and perhaps too little \"being\" – \"as an ethical dimension of life\". The analysis in this paper takes its point of departure in sport and health students’ reflections on their stances of doing movement and, further, their forming of value stances for five different proto-personas. The identified value stances that we merged into ten value stances unfolded in an ethical-aesthetic continuum. The identified value stances are; Fellowship, Empathy, Recognition, Play, Compete, Fun & Happiness, Mastery, Self-realisation, Health, and Immersion. The value stances are discussed by drawing on previous work on virtues and lenses in creating movement-games. In conclusion, we propose four distinct movement and design recommendations that we find valuable to include in the development of digital movement-games.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Elbæk, Lars","Hansen, René Engelhardt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-631633"],"event":{"acronym":"ECGBL","end":"2019-10-04","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2019-10-03","title":"13th International Conference on Game Based Learning, ECGBL 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital design","Philosophy","Virtues"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aesthetic and ethical value stances in sport play and movement games","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85075272391","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-631633","identifier":[{"id":"85075272391","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-cbed5b90-7c2d-4ad3-ba33-800f82a4f50b"],"keyword":["Digital design","Digital movement games","Human physical movement","Philosophy","Sport services","Stances","Virtues"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7D26C3DF5D4F632EE2022C4A638C71CC"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Engelhardt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2d887e76-ae82-4a8d-962e-5e927394748e","name":"Hansen, René Engelhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-4940","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"elbaekpedh","last":"Elbaek","name":"Elbaek, Lars","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunver","key":"majgaardpedh","last":"Majgaard","name":"Majgaard, Gunver","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrea","key":"valentepedh","last":"Valente","name":"Valente, Andrea","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Saifuddin","key":"khalidpedh","last":"Khalid","name":"Khalid, Saifuddin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/gbl.19.181","eisbn":["9781912764389"],"issn":["20490992"],"pages":"210-217","publisher":"Academic Conferences and Publishing International","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Games-based Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th International Conference on Game Based Learning, ECGBL 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075272391"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-cbed5b90-7c2d-4ad3-ba33-800f82a4f50b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Aesthetic and ethical value stances in sport, play, and movement-games","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-631633","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Society moves at an ever-increasing pace, and the importance for students to gain 21st century skills to prepare for post-education work life is an important topic. This is also evident in the education of bachelor-level students in Sports and Health in Denmark. The complexity of health issues and challenges with motivating healthy lifestyles is apparent and calls for education that prepares students for post-university work-life, especially due to the need for innovative practice and project-based work. Educating students for the 21st century requires a different teaching approach than traditional teaching domains targeting specific knowledge and academic skills, which challenges educational institutions and educators as their primary role is to increase employability of the students – especially at university level. The aim of this paper is to pinpoint the key learning outcomes regarding student acquisition of skills and competencies in a game-based event design course. The course was completed with 22 second-year bachelor students in Sports and Health at the University of Southern Denmark in 2019. Previous research show that a game-based learning approach can potentially increase student engagement and facilitate soft-skill acquisition. However, few empirical studies explore how role play can be applied at university level to simulate real-world scenarios and enable the acquisition of skills and competencies needed in cross-department projects. An action research approach was utilized to enable flexibility and improvement throughout the course. Inductive thematic analysis was applied to the qualitative data generated during the course, and the results are discussed drawing on concepts of 21st century skills and game-based learning. The results show that the course design created situations with the potential to improve Social Emotional Learning as a central element of 21st skills. Furthermore, the experience of working with a real-life project in a simulated project organization was educational for most of the students who were motivated by the course design and embraced the learning potential. The implications of this paper are especially relevant to teachers, educators and alike who wish to develop teaching that prepare the students for 21st century work-life.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, René Engelhardt","Elbæk, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-640922"],"event":{"acronym":"ECGBL","end":"2019-10-04","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2019-10-03","title":"13th International Conference on Game Based Learning, ECGBL 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["21 century skills","Action research","Employability","Game based learning","Role play","University students"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"educating for the 000000000021st century with role play in event design","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85075314790","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-640922","identifier":[{"id":"85075314790","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ec5e1bad-e641-4344-83ae-eb69a63c0bac"],"keyword":["21 century skills","Action research","Employability","Game-based learning","Role play","University level education","University students"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1D694F50A998361F61C4AA4E43B20D1C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Engelhardt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2d887e76-ae82-4a8d-962e-5e927394748e","name":"Hansen, René Engelhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-4940","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"elbaekpedh","last":"Elbaek","name":"Elbaek, Lars","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunver","key":"majgaardpedh","last":"Majgaard","name":"Majgaard, Gunver","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrea","key":"valentepedh","last":"Valente","name":"Valente, Andrea","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Saifuddin","key":"khalidpedh","last":"Khalid","name":"Khalid, Saifuddin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/gbl.19.117","eisbn":["9781912764389"],"issn":["20490992"],"pages":"317-324","publisher":"Academic Conferences and Publishing International","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Games-based Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th International Conference on Game Based Learning, ECGBL 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075314790"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ec5e1bad-e641-4344-83ae-eb69a63c0bac"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Educating for the 21st century with role play in event design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640922","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Competency-based training has gained ground in surgical training and with it assessment tools to ensure that training objectives are met. Very few assessment tools are available for evaluating performance in thoracoscopic procedures. Video recordings would provide the possibility of blinded assessment and limited rater bias. This study aimed to provide validity evidence for a newly developed and dedicated tool for assessing competency in Video-Assisted Thoracoscopic Surgery (VATS) lobectomy. Methods: Participants with varying experience with VATS lobectomy were included from different countries. Video recordings from participants’ performance of a VATS right upper lobe lobectomy on a virtual reality simulator were rated by three raters using a modified version of a newly developed VATS lobectomy assessment tool (the VATSAT) and analyzed in relation to the unitary framework (content, response process, internal structure, relation to other variables, and consequences of testing). Results: Fifty-three participants performed two consecutive simulated VATS lobectomies on the virtual reality simulator, leaving a total of 106 videos. Content established in previously published studies. Response process Standardized data collection was ensured by using an instructional element, uniform data collection, a special rating program, and automatic generation of the results to a database. Raters were carefully instructed in using the VATSAT, and tryout ratings were carried out. Internal structure Inter-rater reliability was calculated as intra-class correlation coefficients, to 0.91 for average measures (p < 0.001). Test/re-test reliability was calculated as Pearson’s r of 0.70 (p < 0.001). G-coefficient was calculated to be 0.79 with two procedures and three raters. By performing D-theory was found that either three procedures rated by two raters or five procedures rated by one rater were enough to reach an acceptable G-coefficient of ≥ 0.8. Relation to other variables Significant differences between groups were found (p < 0.001). The participants’ VATS lobectomy experience correlated significantly to their VATSAT score (p = 0.016). Consequences of testing The pass/fail score was found to be 14.9 points by the contrasting groups’ method, leaving five false positive (29%) and six false negatives (43%). Conclusion: Validity evidence was provided for the VATSAT according to the unitary framework. The VATSAT provides supervisors and assessors with a procedure-specific assessment tool for evaluating VATS lobectomy performance and aids with the decision of when the trainee is ready for unsupervised performance.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Katrine","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Petersen, René Horsleben","Neckelmann, Kirsten","Vad, Henrik","Møller, Lars Borgbjerg","Pedersen, Jesper Holst","Konge, Lars"],"cuid":["S04-097.07-009369"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Katrine"],"keyword":["Assessment tool","Competence evaluation","Thoracoscopic lobectomy","VATS","VATSAT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluating competency in video assisted thoracoscopic surgery vats lobectomy performance using a novel assessment tool and virtual reality simulation","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85053536138","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-097.07-009369","identifier":[{"id":"30225606","type":"