{"abstract":"Psychogenic nonepileptic seizures (PNES) mimic epileptic seizures with attacks of changes in voluntary movement or sensory function. Psychiatric management including psychoeducation and psychotherapy is the recommended care. Pediatric onset PNES can be challenging to recognize in both the pediatric and psychiatric setting. A thorough examination with focus on the patient history, clinical information and semiology to support the electroencephalographic testing is recommended. Nevertheless, limited knowledge exists on the clinical characteristics of pediatric onset PNES, as prior studies have been conducted on adult populations or small samples of children.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Anne Sofie","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","Rodrigo-Domingo, Maria","Pristed, Sofie Gry","Christensen, Jakob","Nielsen, René Ernst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-115452"],"event":{"end":"2019-07-02","place":"Vienna, at","start":"2019-06-30","title":"18th International Congress of ESCAP","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescents","Children","PNES"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"baseline characteristics of pediatric onset psychogenic nonepileptic seizures pnes","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/310195805/Anne_Sofie_Hansen_Poster_ESCAP_ASH_Baseline_characteristics_of_pediatric_onset_Psychogenic_nonepileptic_seizures.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-115452","ids":["aau-e0eec269-7d91-4a3e-8239-34202ae1f909"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Children","PNES"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8001005D775D1B5E4736F4E04EEDB968"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/310195805/Anne_Sofie_Hansen_Poster_ESCAP_ASH_Baseline_characteristics_of_pediatric_onset_Psychogenic_nonepileptic_seizures.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Psychiatry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Sofie","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"1a4148c3-ca6e-4d92-ac08-e981652a4177","name":"Hansen, Anne Sofie","orcid":"0000-0001-6101-2150","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Ulrikka","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","name":"Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Rodrigo","key":"domingopau","last":"Domingo","locid":"fff908cd-728d-480b-9534-0cd7176b7dfc","name":"Rodrigo-Domingo, Maria","name_org":"Domingo, Maria Rodrigo","orcid":"0000-0001-7661-7195","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Gry","key":"pristedpau","last":"Pristed","locid":"871611e1-8aa7-4e05-b1b2-c8cf77cad0c8","name":"Pristed, Sofie Gry","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jakob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Ernst","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"689bbd5c-f16d-4316-9717-29e68172bb57","name":"Nielsen, René Ernst","orcid":"0000-0002-7982-6352","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e0eec269-7d91-4a3e-8239-34202ae1f909"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Baseline characteristics of pediatric onset psychogenic nonepileptic seizures (PNES)","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-115452","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES The optimal level of suction on digital chest drainage devices after lobectomy using video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) is unknown and varies between thoracic centres. In this randomized controlled trial, we assessed the potential benefits of low suction of-2 cmH 2 O compared to-10 cmH 2 O, using a digital drainage device. METHODS Two hundred and twenty-eight patients were randomized into 2 groups after VATS lobectomy for suspected or confirmed lung cancer. Primary outcome was time to chest drain removal. Drain data were obtained from the digital drainage devices, and patient data were obtained from medical records during admission, with a follow-up until postoperative day 30. RESULTS For the-2 cmH 2 O and-10 cmH 2 O groups, median (interquartile range) drainage duration was 27.4 h (23.3-71.2) and 47.5 h (24.5-117.8) (P = 0.047), and the incidence of prolonged air leak >5 days was 14.4% and 24.3% (P = 0.089), respectively. Median total fluid production was 566 h (329-1155) ml and 795 h (454-1605) ml (P = 0.007). Median time to consistent air leak cessation (<20 ml/min) was 5.2 h (0.3-34.2) and 23.7 h (0.8-90.8) (P < 0.001). There were no differences in the proportion or the size of the pneumothorax or subcutaneous emphysema after drain removal, and no differences were observed in postoperative morbidity. Median length of in-hospital stay was 2.0 days (2.0-5.8) and 3.0 days (2.0-9.0) (P = 0.18). CONCLUSIONS A low suction level significantly shortened drainage duration, time to air leak cessation and total fluid production, without increasing morbidity. Clinical trial registration number NCT02911259.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Holbek, Bo Laksáfoss","Christensen, Merete","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Kehlet, Henrik","Petersen, René Horsleben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-536433"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Chest drains","Enhanced recovery after surgery","Length of Stay","Lung cancer","Prolonged air leak","Video assisted thoracoscopic surgery lobectomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of low suction on digital drainage devices after lobectomy using video assisted thoracoscopic surgery a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-536433","identifier":[{"id":"85063272251","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30445572","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-efa34eac-c981-4376-9ca1-08dc650ae8de"],"keyword":["Chest drains","Enhanced recovery after surgery","Length of stay","Lung cancer","Prolonged air leak","Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery lobectomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E75A2FDADC961D3FDECCC66ECD4D94D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Bo Laksáfoss","key":"holbekpau","last":"Holbek","name":"Holbek, Bo Laksáfoss","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Merete","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30445572"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ejcts/ezy361","issn":["10107940","1873734X"],"issn_org":["10107940"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","pages":"673-681","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063272251"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-efa34eac-c981-4376-9ca1-08dc650ae8de"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of low suction on digital drainage devices after lobectomy using video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery : A randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-536433","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We examined muscle function, muscle architecture, and tendon length bilaterally in persons who experience a functional deficit 2 years after an Achilles tendon rupture. Eleven persons were investigated on the injured compared with the uninjured side 47 ± 7 months (mean ± SD) after a tendon rupture. Heel-rise data, plantar flexion strength, tendon resting angle 3D MRI-determined tendon length and muscle cross-sectional area, ultrasound-determined fascicle length, and pennation angle were obtained. The heel-rise test yielded reduced max height (32%), number of repetitions (54%), and work performed (61%), P ","author_count":10,"contributors":["Svensson, René B.","Couppé, Christian","Agergaard, Anne Sofie","Ohrhammar Josefsen, Christian","Jensen, Mikkel Holm Hjortshøj","Barfod, Kristoffer Weisskirchner","Nybing, Janus D.","Hansen, Philip","Krogsgaard, Michael","Magnusson, S. Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765790"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Exercise","Musculoskeletal system","Tendon injury"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Research Unit of Clinical Nursing, Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg University Hospital"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"persistent functional loss following ruptured achilles tendon is associated with reduced gastrocnemius muscle fascicle length elongated gastrocnemius and soleus tendon and reduced muscle cross sectional area","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/TSM2.103","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765790","identifier":[{"id":"85074830725","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["pha-