{"abstract":"Context. We present the first high-cadence multiwavelength radial-velocity observations of the Sun-as-a-star, carried out during 57 consecutive days using the stellar échelle spectrograph at the Hertzsprung SONG Telescope operating at the Teide Observatory. Aims. Our aim was to produce a high-quality data set and reference values for the global helioseismic parameters ν max,Ȯ and Δν Ȯ of the solar p-modes using the SONG instrument. The obtained data set or the inferred values should then be used when the scaling relations are applied to other stars showing solar-like oscillations observed with SONG or similar instruments. Methods. We used different approaches to analyse the power spectrum of the time series to determine ν max,Ȯ: simple Gaussian fitting and heavy smoothing of the power spectrum. We determined Δν Ȯ using the method of autocorrelation of the power spectrum. The amplitude per radial mode was determined using the method described in Kjeldsen et al. (2008, ApJ, 682, 1370). Results. We found the following values for the solar oscillations using the SONG spectrograph: ν max,Ȯ = 3141 ± 12 μHz, Δν Ȯ = 134.98 ± 0.04 μHz, and an average amplitude of the strongest radial modes of 16.6 ± 0.4 cm s -1. These values are consistent with previous measurements with other techniques.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Andersen, Mads Fredslund","Pallé, Pere","Jessen-Hansen, J.","Wang, Kun","Grundahl, F.","Bedding, Timothy R.","Roca Cortés, T.","Yu, Jie","Mathur, S","García, Rafael A.","Arentoft, T.","Régulo, C.","Tronsgaard Rasmussen, René","Kjeldsen, Hans","Christensen-Dalsgaard, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S02-086.47-014010"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","China","France","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China West Normal University","Instituto de Astrofísica de Canarias","Universite Paris 5","Universite Paris-Saclay","University of La Laguna","University of Sydney","Université Paris-Saclay"],"keyword":["Asteroseismology","Sun oscillations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oscillations in the sun with song setting the scale for asteroseismic investigations","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/201935175","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.47-014010","identifier":[{"id":"85063034605","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000461008000003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-13a347b9-5adc-4c05-93ab-f35edd4618ee","dtu-544915e0-c491-445f-969c-1174af3f73f6"],"keyword":["Asteroseismology","Sun: oscillations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A3C0D955316C4E6D1E6D728E1B4BFDE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/171523159/marac_aa35175_19.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/201935175","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy, Department of Physics and Astronomy - Stellar Astrophysics Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"university of la laguna","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of La Laguna","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"china west normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China West Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"es","key":"instituto de astrofísica de canarias","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Instituto de Astrofísica de Canarias","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"fr","key":"universite paris saclay","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite Paris-Saclay","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"fr","key":"universite paris 5","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite Paris 5","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"fr","key":"université paris saclay","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Paris-Saclay","used":1},{"affno":"10","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Astrophysics and Atmospheric Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Fredslund","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7c8614b6-04a9-4ca6-87fa-be59b5f636f7","name":"Andersen, Mads Fredslund","orcid":"0000-0002-9194-8520","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pere","key":"pallépau","last":"Pallé","name":"Pallé, Pere","rank":2