,"DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-617648a7-d7e0-468e-97b0-198bb9c2d2ad"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Evaluation of temocillin for phenotypic carbapenemase screening of Escherichia coli and Salmonella enterica isolates in relation to the presence of genes encoding ESBLs and carbapenemase production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-333603","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Advanced glycation end-products (AGEs) accumulate with aging and have been associated with tissue modifications and metabolic disease. Regular exercise has several health benefits, and the purpose of this study was to investigate the effect of regular long-term exercise and diet on skin autofluorescence (SAF) as a measure of glycation and on Achilles tendon structure. In connection with the 2017 European Masters Athletics Championships Stadia, high-level male athletes (n = 194) that had regularly trained for more than 10 years were recruited, in addition to untrained controls (n = 34). SAF was non-invasively determined using an AGE Reader. Achilles tendon thickness and vascular Doppler activity were measured by ultrasonography, and diet was assessed by a questionnaire. There was no significant difference in SAF between the athletes and controls. However, greater duration of exercise was independently associated with lower SAF. Diet also had an effect, with a more \"Western\" diet in youth being associated with increased SAF. Furthermore, our data demonstrated that greater Achilles tendon thickness was associated with aging and training. Together, our data indicate that long-term exercise may yield a modest reduction in glycation and substantially increase Achilles tendon size, which may protect against injury.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hjerrild, Joachim Nymann","Wobbe, Alexander","Stausholm, Martin B.","Larsen, Anne Ellegaard","Josefsen, Christian Ohrhammer","Malmgaard-Clausen, Nikolaj M.","Dela, Flemming","Kjaer, Michael","Magnusson, S. Peter","Hansen, Mette","Svensson, Rene B.","Couppé, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014318"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bergen"],"keyword":["Western diet","advanced glycation end products AGEs","skin autofluorescence"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of long term physical activity and diet on skin glycation and achilles tendon structure","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu11061409","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-014318","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6627972","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31234508","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068797874","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1804ec02-dbef-436f-90dc-4a6eaf22ef97","ku-e7bef5bb-e85d-40eb-8f7f-267e46805fb5"],"keyword":["advanced glycation end-products (AGEs)","habitual exercise","skin autofluorescence","ultrasound doppler","western diet"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E881D44713B96B7757117A5E37D4F3B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu11061409","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/237999515/nutrients_11_01409.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Sport Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Healthy Ageing, Web Track 3: Individualized health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Healthy Ageing, Web: Center for Healthy Aging","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Exercise and Muscle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim Nymann","key":"hjerrildpau","last":"Hjerrild","locid":"ea5959e7-d7f2-4c69-992d-c129663751a3","name":"Hjerrild, Joachim Nymann","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"wobbepau","last":"Wobbe","locid":"ac3bf612-c634-4b24-8914-94abf8644571","name":"Wobbe, Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin B","key":"stausholmpau","last":"Stausholm","name":"Stausholm, Martin B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Ellegaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b1ef3716-109a-4b63-a8f3-ea07ffcb30eb","name":"Larsen, Anne Ellegaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian Ohrhammer","key":"josefsenpau","last":"Josefsen","name":"Josefsen, Christian Ohrhammer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nikolaj M","key":"malmgaardclausenpau","last":"Malmgaard-Clausen","name":"Malmgaard-Clausen, Nikolaj M","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Flemming","key":"delapau","last":"Dela","locid":"5d84458e-34c1-4874-a128-7fc3cb13f7f2","name":"Dela, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-9970-9535","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"7937b8ab-7820-4d25-982f-1d2f58b033a3","name":"Kjaer, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"S Peter","key":"magnussonpau","last":"Magnusson","locid":"6f430caa-ac01-4dfe-9a62-e3a49afba21a","name":"Magnusson, S. Peter","name_org":"Magnusson, S Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"35b198ca-caef-48de-8570-21c9fbab1f8f","name":"Hansen, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-9383-8202","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rene B","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"fe236d1a-ef32-4a22-8125-31211110d8c8","name":"Svensson, Rene B.","name_org":"Svensson, Rene B","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"couppépau","last":"Couppé","name":"Couppé, Christian","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31234508"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/nu11061409","issn":["20726643"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nutrients","paperid":"1409","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Nutrients","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068797874"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1804ec02-dbef-436f-90dc-4a6eaf22ef97","ku-e7bef5bb-e85d-40eb-8f7f-267e46805fb5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of Long-Term Physical Activity and Diet on Skin Glycation and Achilles Tendon Structure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-014318","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To investigate whether a whole grain diet alters the gut microbiome and insulin sensitivity, as well as biomarkers of metabolic health and gut functionality. Design: 60 Danish adults at risk of developing metabolic syndrome were included in a randomised cross-over trial with two 8-week dietary intervention periods comprising whole grain diet and refined grain diet, separated by a washout period of ≥6 weeks. The response to the interventions on the gut microbiome composition and insulin sensitivity as well on measures of glucose and lipid metabolism, gut functionality, inflammatory markers, anthropometry and urine metabolomics were assessed. Results: 50 participants completed both periods with a whole grain intake of 179±50 g/day and 13±10 g/day in the whole grain and refined grain period, respectively. Compliance was confirmed by a difference in plasma alkylresorcinols (p<0.0001). Compared with refined grain, whole grain did not significantly alter glucose homeostasis and did not induce major changes in the faecal microbiome. Also, breath hydrogen levels, plasma short-chain fatty acids, intestinal integrity and intestinal transit time were not affected. The whole grain diet did, however, compared with the refined grain diet, decrease body weight (p<0.0001), serum inflammatory markers, interleukin (IL)-6 (p=0.009) and C-reactive protein (p=0.003). The reduction in body weight was consistent with a reduction in energy intake, and IL-6 reduction was associated with the amount of whole grain consumed, in particular with intake of rye. Conclusion: Compared with refined grain diet, whole grain diet did not alter insulin sensitivity and gut microbiome but reduced body weight and systemic low-grade inflammation. Trial Registration Number: NCT 01731366; Results.","author_count":43,"contributors":["Roager, Henrik Munch","Vogt, Josef Korbinian","Kristensen, Mette Bredal","Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","Ibrügger, Sabine","Mærkedahl, Rasmus Baadsgaard","Bahl, Martin Iain","Lind, Mads Vendelbo","Nielsen, Rikke Linnemann","Frøkiær, Hanne","Gøbel, Rikke Juul","Landberg, Rikard","Ross, Alastair B.","Brix, Susanne","Holck, Jesper","Meyer, Anne S.","Sparholt, Morten H.","Christensen, Anders Fogh","Carvalho, Vera","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Rumessen, Jüri Johannes","Linneberg, Allan","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Dalgaard, Marlene D.","Blennow, Andreas","Frandsen, Henrik Lauritz","Villas-Bôas, Silas","Kristiansen, Karsten","Vestergaard, Henrik","Hansen, Torben","Ekstrøm, Claus Thorn","Ritz, Christian","Nielsen, Henrik Bjørn","Pedersen, Oluf","Gupta, Ramneek","Lauritzen, Lotte","Licht, Tine Rask"],"cuid":["S03-099.29-032620"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Gupta, Ramneek"],"country":["New Zealand","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","The University of Auckland"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Blood Glucose metabolism","Colonic microflora","Cross Over Studies","Denmark","Diet","Energy Intake","Feces microbiology","Female","Gastrointestinal Microbiome","Humans","Immune response","Inflammation","Inflammation blood","Insulin Resistance","Interleukin 6 blood","Lipids blood","Male","Metabolomics","Middle Aged","Obesity","Weight loss","Whole Grains"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"whole grain rich diet reduces body weight and systemic low grade inflammation without inducing major changes of the gut microbiome a randomised cross over trial","src":["dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U