{"abstract":"Background and aim: Plasmid-mediated colistin resistance mechanisms have been identified worldwide in the past years. A multiplex polymerase chain reaction (PCR) protocol for detection of all currently known transferable colistin resistance genes (mcr-1 to mcr-5, and variants) in Enterobacteriaceae was developed for surveillance or research purposes. Methods: We designed four new primer pairs to amplify mcr-1, mcr-2, mcr-3 and mcr-4 gene products and used the originally described primers for mcr-5 to obtain a stepwise separation of ca 200 bp between ampli-cons. The primer pairs and amplification conditions allow for single or multiple detection of all currently described mcr genes and their variants present in Enterobacteriaceae. The protocol was validated testing 49 European Escherichia coli and Salmonella isolates of animal origin. Results: Multiplex PCR results in bovine and porcine isolates from Spain, Germany, France and Italy showed full concordance with whole genome sequence data. The method was able to detect mcr-1, mcr-3 and mcr-4 as singletons or in different combinations as they were present in the test isolates. One new mcr-4 variant, mcr-4.3, was also identified. Conclusions: This method allows rapid identification of mcr-positive bacteria and overcomes the challenges of phenotypic detection of colistin resistance. The multiplex PCR should be particularly interesting in settings or laboratories with limited resources for performing genetic analysis as it provides information on the mechanism of colistin resistance without requiring genome sequencing.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Rebelo, Ana Rita","Bortolaia, Valeria","Kjeldgaard, Jette Sejer","Karlsmose, Susanne","Leekitcharoenphon, Pimlapas","Hansen, Inge M.","Guerra, Beatriz","Malorny, Burkhard","Borowiak, Maria","Hammerl, Jens Andre","Battisti, Antonio","Franco, Alessia","Alba, Patricia","Perrin-Guyomard, Agnes","Granier, Sophie A.","de Frutos, Cristina","Escobar, no-firstname","Malhotra-Kumar, Surbhi","Villa, Laura","Carattoli, Alessandra","Hendriksen, Rene S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347453"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hendriksen, Rene S."],"country":["Belgium","France","Germany","Italy","Spain"],"glorg":["Agence nationale de sécurité sanitaire de l'alimentation, de l'environnement et du travail","All Global Affiliations","European Food Safety Authority","Experimental Zooprophylactic Institute of Lazio and Toscana","Federal Institute for Risk Assessment","Istituto Superiore di Sanita","Laboratorio Central de Veterinaria de Algete","Paris-Est Sup","University of Antwerp"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiplex pcr for detection of plasmid mediated colistin resistance determinants mcr 000000000001 mcr 000000000002 mcr 000000000003 mcr 000000000004 and mcr 000000000005 for surveillance purposes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/144529959/eurosurv_23_6_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the European Union Reference Laboratory for Antimicrobial Resistance (EURL-AR) in the context of animal health and food safety, (http://www.eurl-ar. eu/) and the World Health Organization (WHO) Collaborating Centre for Antimicrobial Resistance in Foodborne Pathogens and Genomics including the WHO Advisory Group on Integrated Surveillance of Antimicrobial Resistance (AGISAR) (http://www.who.int/foodsafety/areas_work/antimicrobial-resistance/agisar/en/) and Global Antimicrobial Resistance Surveillance System (GLASS) (http://www.who.int/antimicrobial-resistance/publications/surveillance-system-manual/ en/)."],"id":"S01-000.00-347453","identifier":[{"id":"85041943190","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5824125","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29439754","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-8fbe112c-3a73-4329-8176-c98fed3fd61d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D571E463DCE6CF3B3E66DCE6C987D4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/144529959/eurosurv_23_6_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Genomic Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"european food safety authority","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"European Food Safety Authority","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"federal institute for risk assessment","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Federal Institute for Risk Assessment","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"experimental zooprophylactic institute of lazio and toscana","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Experimental Zooprophylactic Institute of Lazio and Toscana","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"agence nationale de sécurité sanitaire de l alimentation de l environnement et du travail","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Agence nationale de sécurité sanitaire de l'alimentation, de l'environnement et du travail","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fr","key":"paris est sup","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"na