{"abstract":"Within Eastern Europe, African swine fever virus (ASFV) has unexpectedly spread to farms with high biosecurity. In an attempt to explain this process, pigs were allowed to ingest flies that had fed on ASFV-spiked blood, which had a realistic titre for an infected pig. Some of the pigs became infected with the virus. Thus, ingestion of blood-sucking flies, having fed on ASFV-infected wild boar before entering stables, represents a potential route for disease transmission","author_count":9,"contributors":["Olesen, Ann Sofie","Lohse, Louise","Hansen, Mette Frimodt","Boklund, Anette","Hisham Beshara Halasa, Tariq","Belsham, Graham","Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","Bøtner, Anette","Bødker, Rene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-370994"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bødker, Rene"],"keyword":["African swine fever","Haemorrhagic disease","Stomoxys calcitrans","Virus transmission"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infection of pigs with african swine fever virus via ingestion of stable flies stomoxys calcitrans","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/tbed.12918","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-370994","identifier":[{"id":"29877056","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85048995608","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-de1bed08-8e06-4fcf-b164-ebf105eebd7b"],"keyword":["African swine fever","Blood-feeding flies","Haemorrhagic disease","Stomoxys calcitrans","Virus transmission"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E5F44FE6C1CDDC15E877C1D332E6A34"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/tbed.12918","version":"Published Ver