{"abstract":"The objective of this study was to evaluate the potential of predicting the pleural fluid output in patients after video-assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy of the lung. Detailed measurements of continuous fluid output were obtained prospectively using an electronic thoracic drainage device (Thopaz+™, Medela AG, Switzerland). Patients were divided into high (≥500 mL) and low (<500 mL) 24-hour fluid output, and detailed flow curves were plotted graphically to identify arithmetic patterns predicting fluid output in the early (≤24 hours) and later (24-48 hours) post-operative phase. Furthermore, multiple logistic regression analysis was used to predict high 24-hour fluid output using baseline data. Data were obtained from 50 patients, where 52% had a fluid output of <500 mL/24 hours. From visual assessment of flow curves, patients were grouped according to fluid output 6 hours postoperatively. An output ≥200 mL/6 hours was predictive of 'high 24-hour fluid output' (P<0.0001). However, 33% of patients with <200 mL/6 hours ended with a 'high 24-hour fluid output'. Baseline data showed no predictive value of fluid production, and 24-hour fluid output had no predictive value of fluid output between 24 and 48 hours. Assessment of initial fluid production may predict high 24-hour fluid output (≥500 mL) but seems to lack clinical value in drain removal criteria.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Holbek, Bo Laksáfoss","Petersen, René Horsleben","Kehlet, Henrik","Hansen, Henrik Jessen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429316"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early pleural fluid dynamics following video assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy has limited clinical value","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-429316","identifier":[{"id":"85026463065","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28840021","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5543000","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-3c161c83-a41e-40cb-82c9-b380d1061585"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACA414FE733FCAC04B91A3E9895C226C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Cardiothoracic Surgery","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Bo Laksáfoss","key":"holbekpau","last":"Holbek","name":"Holbek, Bo Laksáfoss","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28840021"],"pub":{"doi":"10.21037/jtd.2017.06.107","issn":["20721439","20776624"],"issn_org":["20721439"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Thoracic Disease","pages":"2204-2208","status":"p","title":"Journal of Thoracic Disease","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026463065"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3c161c83-a41e-40cb-82c9-b380d1061585"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Early pleural fluid dynamics following video-assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy has limited clinical value","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-429316","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The 7Cs model by Conole offers a method for discussing educational design. It has gone through several changes ending in a version from 2013 consisting of seven stages gathered in four phases: Vision (conceptualize), Activities (capture, communicate, collaborate, consider), Synthesis (combine), Implementation (consolidate) (eg. Conole, 2014: 74). The latest model seems quite static and we find that it lacks the ‘problem of schooling’. When students enter into a learning environment they often accept the discourse of ‘School’ understood as a semiotic domain “...of specialized representations, modalities, knowledge, and practices” (Gee 2008: 137). In a semiotic domain people are expected to act, talk and position themselves according to the expectations of the domain, framed by Gee as ‘doing being’ someone. Through an analysis of concepts and ideas as well as written communication between teachers and students from completed MOOC courses in our institution we found, that this schooling frame made important changes to the design. When planning the MOOCs, one of the main important concepts was that each student should be provided with their own learning path, ideally to be unique for each of them, because the students accepted into the MOOC seem to have a variety of backgrounds (also see e.g. Gynther 2016). This makes the idea of a personalised learning path necessary. But since our MOOCs were organized through a combination of f2f-teaching and MOOC studying, the students acted like in a school domain which seems to be in opposition to the expected personalised learning pathways, and instead they seem to follow the same, teacher instructed learning path. To bring the 7C’s model alive we suggest that it is taken into consideration that this school discourse plays an important role when planning MOOCs, and we therefore present some changes to the model.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Christiansen, René Boyer","Buch, Bettina","Petersen, Anne Kristine","Sørensen, Randi Skovbjerg","Hansen, Dorrit"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-553071"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000007c s and the problem of schooling and personalized learning paths","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-553071","ids":["pha-0a2a2f52-51f9-4ff2-ac83-dd6375f506c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-6C9A48383EA7DB1F5C9C252807CDBF40"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Pædagogik og Ledelsesområdet, Læreruddannelsen - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Boyer","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"42204c79-a17b-4152-bd0f-e5dfbbf302d5","name":"Christiansen, René Boyer","orcid":"0000-0002-2962-7320","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bettina","key":"buchpau","last":"Buch","locid":"ffe5c49c-02ac-4ed2-91d7-6c9600b09f2a","name":"Buch, Bettina","orcid":"0000-0001-5496-1243","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Kristine","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"f5e451f8-6385-46fb-8e71-45f37a1f7d8c","name":"Petersen, Anne Kristine","orcid":"0000-0002-3109-0227","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Randi Skovbjerg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0e776e0c-4caf-46fd-b597-f1ae0df93bfd","name":"Sørensen, Randi Skovbjerg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorrit","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"392c5883-80e4-4cc6-a7f9-7382e2b31d81","name":"Hansen, Dorrit","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-0a2a2f52-51f9-4ff2-ac83-dd6375f506c8"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"7C's : And the problem of schooling and personalized learning paths","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-553071","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Mette Moustgaard","Jensen, Pernille Tine","Hansen, Dorte Gilså","Christensen, René dePont","Mogensen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-574382"],"event":{"end":"2017-11-07","place":"Wien, at","start":"2017-11-04","title":"ESGO 2017<br/>","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient initiated follow up affects fear of recurrence and health care use results from the opal trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-574382","ids":["sdu-041d0081-0cf9-4651-81fb-d4b397d03796"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B82B9CBA7C9EABF47414C3D9782BA987"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Gynaecology and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"karolinska institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Moustgaard","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"79c59d83-9d4b-4abd-acf5-7085b6c42ffd","name":"Jeppesen, Mette Moustgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7390-5167","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Tine","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ef83b3df-03b5-4eea-9e38-b8ca5467e677","name":"Jensen, Pernille Tine","orcid":"0000-0002-1637-6040","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Gilså","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2826791-eb97-4bca-8af7-448b0940e6e5","name":"Hansen, Dorte Gilså","orcid":"0000-0002-5946-9968","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René dePont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","name":"Mogensen, Ole","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-041d0081-0cf9-4651-81fb-d4b397d03796"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"PATIENT-INITIATED FOLLOW-UP AFFECTS FEAR OF RECURRENCE AND HEALTH CARE USE – RESULTS FROM THE OPAL TRIAL","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-574382","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Precise prognostic and predictive variables allowing improved post-operative treatment stratification are missing in patients treated for stage II colon cancer (CC). Investigation of tumor infiltrating lymphocytes (TILs) may be rewarding, but the lack of a standardized analytic technique is a major concern. Manual stereological counting is considered the gold standard, but digital pathology with image analysis is preferred due to time efficiency. The purpose of this study was to compare manual stereological estimates of TILs with automatic counts obtained by image analysis, and at the same time investigate the heterogeneity of TILs. Methods: From 43 patients treated for stage II CC in 2002 three paraffin embedded, tumor containing tissue blocks were selected one of them representing the deepest invasive tumor front. Serial sections from each of the 129 blocks were immunohistochemically stained for CD3 and CD8, and the slides were scanned. Stereological estimates of the numerical density and area fraction of TILs were obtained using the computer-assisted newCAST stereology system. For the image analysis approach an app-based algorithm was developed using Visiopharm Integrator System software. For both methods the tumor areas of interest (invasive front and central area) were manually delineated by the observer. Results: Based on all sections, the Spearman's correlation coefficients for density estimates varied from 0.9457 to 0.9638 (p < 0.0001), whereas the coefficients for area fraction estimates ranged from 0.9400 to 0.9603 (P < 0.0001). Regarding heterogeneity, intra-class correlation coefficients (ICC) for CD3+ TILs varied from 0.615 to 0.746 in the central area, and from 0.686 to 0.746 in the invasive area. ICC for CD8+ TILs varied from 0.724 to 0.775 in the central area, and from 0.746 to 0.765 in the invasive area. Conclusions: Exact objective and time efficient estimates of numerical densities and area fractions of CD3+ and CD8+ TILs in stage II colon cancer can be obtained by image analysis and are highly correlated to the corresponding estimates obtained by the gold standard based on stereology. Since the intra-tumoral heterogeneity was low, this method may be recommended for quantifying TILs in only one histological section representing the deepest invasive tumor front.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Eriksen, Ann Christina","Andersen, Johnnie Bremholm","Kristensson, Martin","Christensen, René dePont","Hansen, Torben Frøstrup","Kjær-Frifeldt, Sanne","Sørensen, Flemming Brandt"],"cuid":["S02-098.55-014749"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Colon cancer","Colonic Neoplasms pathology","Heterogeneity","Humans","Image Processing Computer Assisted methods","Image analysis","Journal Article","Lymphocytes Tumor Infiltrating pathology","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Stereology","Tumor infiltrating lymphocytes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computer assisted stereology and automated image analysis for quantification of tumor infiltrating lymphocytes in colon cancer","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13000-017-0653-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.55-014749","identifier":[{"id":"28851404","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85028467268","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5575870","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-1dad2fed-a863-44bb-b1f2-e4d12592cfb5","sdu-73f8677a-e79e-40e2-a2f8-1ddabf8273cd"],"keyword":["Aged","CD3 Complex/metabolism","CD8 Antigens/metabolism","Colon cancer","Colonic Neoplasms/pathology","Heterogeneity","Humans","Image Processing, Computer-Assisted/methods","Image analysis","Journal Article","Lymphocytes, Tumor-Infiltrating/pathology","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Stereology","Tumor infiltrating lymphocytes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-84BE9D0AD92785613C2962C7F068A985"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/128885643/Computer_assisted_stereology_and_automated_image_analysis_for_quantification_of_tumor_infiltrating_lymphocytes_in_colon_cancer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13000-017-0653-0","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Clinical Pathology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Stereological Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Visiopharm A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann C","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"c7b52d9f-48c6-46ce-921f-ac56c8e8d22e","name":"Eriksen, Ann Christina","name_org":"Eriksen, Ann C","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johnnie","key":"bremholmandersenpau","last":"Bremholm Andersen","locid":"01a3967f-ee5f-42b5-9d7b-1f0d25fab2b8","name":"Andersen, Johnnie Bremholm","name_org":"Bremholm Andersen, Johnnie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"kristenssonpau","last":"Kristensson","name":"Kristensson, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René dePont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben F","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"72d28643-c440-4bbd-ad2b-eef0903a9438","name":"Hansen, Torben Frøstrup","name_org":"Hansen, Torben F","orcid":"0000-0001-7476-671X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne","key":"kjærfrifeldtpau","last":"Kjær-Frifeldt","locid":"6fdb727e-ac1e-4c28-b933-5510959bbc92","name":"Kjær-Frifeldt, Sanne","orcid":"0009-0009-9594-5042","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming B","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ac3af930-9550-4d18-9269-4dc0a6d649e5","name":"Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","name_org":"Sørensen, Flemming B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28851404"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13000-017-0653-0","issn":["17461596"],"issue":"1","journal":"Diagnostic Pathology","pages":"1-14","paperid":"65","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Diagnostic Pathology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028467268"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","visiopharm a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1dad2fed-a863-44bb-b1f2-e4d12592cfb5","sdu-73f8677a-e79e-40e2-a2f8-1ddabf8273cd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Computer-assisted stereology and automated image analysis for quantification of tumor infiltrating lymphocytes in colon cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.55-014749","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"From exploratory studies and theoretical expectations it is known that simplifying approximations in spectroscopic analysis (local thermodynamic equilibrium (LTE), 1D) lead to systematic biases of stellar parameters and abundances. These biases depend strongly on surface gravity, temperature and, in particular, for LTE versus non-LTE (NLTE), on metallicity of the stars. Here we analyze the [Mg/Fe] and [Fe/H] plane of a sample of 326 stars, comparing LTE and NLTE results obtained using 1D hydrostatic models and averaged models. We show that compared to the NLTE benchmark, the other three methods display increasing biases toward lower metallicities, resulting in false trends of [Mg/Fe] against [Fe/H], which have profound implications for interpretations by chemical evolution models. In our best NLTE model, the halo and disk stars show a clearer behavior in the [Mg/Fe]-[Fe/H] plane, from the knee in abundance space down to the lowest metallicities. Our sample has a large fraction of thick disk stars and this population extends down to at least [Fe/H] ∼ -1.6 dex, further than previously proven. The thick disk stars display a constant [Mg/Fe] ≈ 0.3 dex, with a small intrinsic dispersion in [Mg/Fe] that suggests that a fast SN Ia channel is not relevant for the disk formation. The halo stars reach higher [Mg/Fe] ratios and display a net trend of [Mg/Fe] at low metallicities, paired with a large dispersion in [Mg/Fe]. These indicate the diverse origin of halo stars from accreted low-mass systems to stochastic/inhomogeneous chemical evolution in the Galactic halo.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bergemann, Maria","Collet, Remo","Schoenrich, Ralph","Andrae, Rene","Kovalev, Mikhail","Ruchti, Greg","Hansen, Camilla Juul","Magic, Zazralt"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024511"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bergemann, Maria"],"country":["Germany","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Max Planck Institute for Astronomy","Technische Universität Darmstadt","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Abundance ratios","DATA RELEASE","Evolution","Galaxy abundances","Galaxy evolution","Galaxy kinematics and dynamics","MAFAGS OS","NEARBY STARS","Parameters","Radiative transfer","STANDARD STARS","Stars abundances","Stars late type","VELOCITY EXPERIMENT RAVE","milky way"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non local thermodynamic equilibrium stellar spectroscopy with 000000000001d and lt 000000000003d gt models ii chemical properties of the galactic metal poor disk and the halo","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.07363.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024511","identifier":[{"id":"85030162451","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000410740100002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-a1c8e823-a423-4353-a8d8-47637355ac03","ku-1749fbd7-9dd4-4cbf-a2d3-22de47e4d8f4"],"keyword":["ABUNDANCE RATIOS","DATA RELEASE","EVOLUTION","Galaxy: abundances","Galaxy: evolution","Galaxy: kinematics and dynamics","MAFAGS-OS","MILKY-WAY","NEARBY STARS","PARAMETERS","STANDARD STARS","SUPERNOVA RATE","VELOCITY EXPERIMENT RAVE","radiative transfer","stars: abundances","stars: late-type"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-546E956DD1EA1B3DC5A9B39E83497B0A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.07363.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.07363","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for astronomy","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Astronomy","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy, Department of Physics and Astronomy - Stellar Astrophysics Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, DARK"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"bergemannpau","last":"Bergemann","name":"Bergemann, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Remo","key":"colletpau","last":"Collet","locid":"32d7d42f-26b8-4a76-80ae-db025ab3aae4","name":"Collet, Remo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralph","key":"schoenrichpau","last":"Schoenrich","name":"Schoenrich, Ralph","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rene","key":"andraepau","last":"Andrae","name":"Andrae, Rene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikhail","key":"kovalevpau","last":"Kovalev","name":"Kovalev, Mikhail","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Greg","key":"ruchtipau","last":"Ruchti","name":"Ruchti, Greg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Camilla Juul","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"22f21242-d5eb-4e6e-84ec-b810905ba20b","name":"Hansen, C. J.","name_org":"Hansen, Camilla Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-7277-7922","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Zazralt","key":"magicpau","last":"Magic","locid":"c9f2fb2e-72f4-4453-80cc-f1ffd6b6f1ca","name":"Magic, Zazralt","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3847/1538-4357/aa88b5","issn":["0004637X","00670049"],"issn_org":["0004637X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Astrophysical Journal","paperid":"16","publisher":"American Astronomical Society","status":"p","title":"Astrophysical Journal","volume":"847"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030162451"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a1c8e823-a423-4353-a8d8-47637355ac03","ku-1749fbd7-9dd4-4cbf-a2d3-22de47e4d8f4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Non-local Thermodynamic Equilibrium Stellar Spectroscopy with 1D and &lt;3D &gt; Models. II. Chemical Properties of the Galactic Metal-poor Disk and the Halo","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-024511","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we argue that in contemporary society a form of security emerges that is qualitatively neither technological nor social but that is truly sociotechnical. We argue that everyday security is a form of sociotechnical security co-constituted of both technological protection mechanisms designed to protect assets and of relational social practices that enable people to build and maintain trust in their daily interactions. We further argue that the complexity of real-world information security problems requires security models that are able to articulate and examine security as a sociotechnical phenomenon and that can articulate and examine the results of interaction between these two security constructions. Security must be modelled to acknowledge, at least, the connection between an individual’s security needs and the protection of assets if it is to help design secure services with which citizens can safely engage. We exemplify these attributes from case studies conducted as part of two sociotechnical research projects: the UK government and research council funded Cyber Security Cartographies (CySeCa) project and the EU FP7 funded project TREsPASS. These are introduced to discuss the potential for a family of modelling techniques. In this paper we examine the attributes of everyday security problems and reflect upon how such a modelling family might influence both academic research and practice in contemporary information security.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Coles-Kemp, Lizzie","Hansen, Rene Rydhof"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-109349"],"event":{"acronym":"HCI","end":"2017-07-14","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2017-07-09","title":"5th International Conference on Human Aspects of Information Security, Privacy and Trust, HAS 2017, held as part of 19th International Conference on Human-Computer Interaction, HCI 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Coles-Kemp, Lizzie"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Royal Holloway University of London"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"walking the line the everyday security ties that bind","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-109349","identifier":[{"id":"000431846800032","type":"wos"},{"id":"85025145668","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-cc6ae868-4899-4301-926a-c3c8900efb57"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-43E53C140AEB29648E16550A1D2A8376"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"royal holloway university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Holloway University of London","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lizzie","key":"coleskemppau","last":"Coles-Kemp","name":"Coles-Kemp, Lizzie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","name_org":"Hansen, René Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-58460-7_32","isbn":["9783319584591"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"464-480","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Human Aspects of Information Security, Privacy and Trust - 5th International Conference, HAS 2017 Held as Part of HCI International 2017, Proceedings","volume":"10292 LNCS"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025145668"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cc6ae868-4899-4301-926a-c3c8900efb57"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Walking the line : The everyday security ties that bind","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-109349","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"A series of ammine metal-dodecahydro-closo-dodecaboranes, M xB 12H 12·nNH 3 (M = Li, Na, Ca) were synthesized and their structural and thermal properties studied with in situ time-resolved synchrotron radiation powder X-ray diffraction, thermal analysis, Fourier transformed infrared spectroscopy, and temperature-programmed photographic analysis. The synthesized compounds, Li 2B 12H 12·7NH 3, Na 2B 12H 12·4NH 3 and CaB 12H 12·6NH 3, contain high amounts of NH 3, 43.3, 26.6 and 35.9 wt% NH 3, respectively, which can be released and absorbed reversibly at moderate conditions without decomposition, thereby making the closo-boranes favorable 'host' materials for ammonia or indirect hydrogen storage in the solid state. In this work, fifteen new ammine metal dodecahydro-closo-dodecaborane compounds are observed by powder X-ray diffraction, of which six are structurally characterized, Li 2B 12H 12·4NH 3, Li 2B 12H 12·2NH 3, Na 2B 12H 12·4NH 3, Na 2B 12H 12·2NH 3, CaB 12H 12·4NH 3 and CaB 12H 12·3NH 3. Li 2B 12H 12·4NH 3 and Na 2B 12H 12·4NH 3 are isostructural and monoclinic (P2 1/n) whereas Na 2B 12H 12·2NH 3 and CaB 12H 12·3NH 3 are both trigonal with space groups P3m1 and R3c, respectively. Generally, coordination between the metal and the icosahedral closo-borane anion is diverse and includes point sharing, edge sharing, or face sharing, while coordination of ammonia always occurs via the lone pair on nitrogen to the metal. Furthermore, a liquid intermediate is observed during heating of Li 2B 12H 12·7NH 3. This work provides deeper insight into the structural, physical, and chemical properties related to thermal decomposition and possible ammonia and hydrogen storage.","author_count":9,"contributors":["R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","Tumanov, Nikolay A","Santoru, Antonio","Pistidda, Claudio","Bednarcik, Jozef","Klassen, Thomas","Dornheim, Martin","Filinchuk, Yaroslav","Jensen, Torben René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-141764"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Torben René"],"country":["Belgium","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Universite Catholique de Louvain","Universite de Namur"],"keyword":["Ammonia","Boron","Composites","Hydrogen storage","LI2B12H12","METAL BOROHYDRIDES","Powder diffraction","X ray diffraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synthesis structures and thermal decomposition of ammine m sub x sub b sub 000000000012 sub h sub 000000000012 sub complexes m li na ca","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85021736813","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-141764","identifier":[{"id":"28590005","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85021736813","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000403968300018","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-15739b70-ea6f-4633-b0f1-5715f70caeba"],"keyword":["AMMONIA","BORON","COMPOSITES","DODECAHYDRO-CLOSO-DODECABORATE","HYDROGEN STORAGE","LI2B12H12","METAL BOROHYDRIDES","POWDER DIFFRACTION","SODIUM AMIDE","X-RAY-DIFFRACTION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-76D0A8542DCE34EDF1BEF0BF258C8C66"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Centre for Materials Crystallography (CMC)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, Langelandsgade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"universite de namur","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite de Namur","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"universite catholique de louvain","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite Catholique de Louvain","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"helmholtz association of german research centres","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne R. S.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"95e2932e-526e-4795-b38a-7ab221f891ae","name":"R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","name_org":"Hansen, Bjarne R. S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolay A","key":"tumanovpau","last":"Tumanov","name":"Tumanov, Nikolay A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Antonio","key":"santorupau","last":"Santoru","name":"Santoru, Antonio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudio","key":"pistiddapau","last":"Pistidda","name":"Pistidda, Claudio","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jozef","key":"bednarcikpau","last":"Bednarcik","name":"Bednarcik, Jozef","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"klassenpau","last":"Klassen","name":"Klassen, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"dornheimpau","last":"Dornheim","name":"Dornheim, Martin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaroslav","key":"filinchukpau","last":"Filinchuk","name":"Filinchuk, Yaroslav","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben R.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e0750478-df89-45bf-aa48-b6a86de93fa0","name":"Jensen, Torben René","name_org":"Jensen, Torben R.","orcid":"0000-0002-4278-3221","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28590005"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c7dt01414g","issn":["14779226","14779234"],"issn_org":["14779226"],"issue":"24","journal":"Dalton Transactions","pages":"7770-7781","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Dalton Transactions","title_org":"Dalton Transactions (Print Edition)","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021736813"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-15739b70-ea6f-4633-b0f1-5715f70caeba"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Synthesis, structures and thermal decomposition of ammine M<sub>x</sub>B<sub>12</sub>H<sub>12</sub> complexes (M = Li, Na, Ca)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-141764","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Sodium compounds containing large weakly coordinating anions are explored as ion conductors. The halogenated sodium-closo-dodecaboranes (Na 2B 12Cl 12, Na 2B 12Br 12, and Na 2B 12I 12) are all isostructural (Pa3̅) at room temperature. These compounds undergo an order-disorder polymorphic transition to Fm3̅m where Na + partially occupies two crystallographic sites and [B 12X 12] 2- anions undergo reorientational motion. These dynamic structural properties promote extreme Na + ion conductivity up to 0.162 S/cm at elevated temperature (500 °C). The polymorphic transition temperatures increase down the halogen group (Cl < Br < I). These temperatures are much higher (475, 525, and 570 °C) than for Na 2B 12H 12 (266 °C), which could be related to increasing anion size, mass, and the anisotropic electron density in the covalently bound halogens (B-X). The halogens may form Na-X interactions with increasing strength and directionality, which restrict dynamic motion until high temperature. The halogenated sodium-closo-dodecaboranes demonstrate excellent thermal stabilities (up to 500 °C) and may facilitate the development of new high temperature ion conductors.","author_count":4,"contributors":["R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","Paskevicius, Mark","Jørgensen, Mathias","Jensen, Torben René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263653"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Paskevicius, Mark"],"keyword":["Batteries","Complex hydrides","Crystal structure","Electrolytes","Energy storage","METAL BOROHYDRIDES","Phase transitions","Structural behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"halogenated sodium closo dodecaboranes as solid state ion conductors","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85018624943","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263653","identifier":[{"id":"000400233100011","type":"wos"},{"id":"85018624943","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-eb583f87-a872-447c-a7aa-02809768853c"],"keyword":["BATTERIES","COMPLEX HYDRIDES","CRYSTAL-STRUCTURE","ELECTROLYTES","ENERGY-STORAGE","LITHIUM CLOSOBORANES","METAL BOROHYDRIDES","PHASE-TRANSITIONS","STRUCTURAL BEHAVIOR","SUPERIONIC CONDUCTION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CBFF397E4547B55E6F04E93BE20EC08C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Centre for Materials Crystallography (CMC)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, Langelandsgade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne R. S.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"95e2932e-526e-4795-b38a-7ab221f891ae","name":"R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","name_org":"Hansen, Bjarne R. S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"paskeviciuspau","last":"Paskevicius","locid":"e26eea7d-e55a-4989-80de-dfafd2146511","name":"Paskevicius, Mark","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","locid":"32e93198-01d2-4718-84d6-d305f21bff00","name":"Jørgensen, Mathias","name_org":"Jorgensen, Mathias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben R.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e0750478-df89-45bf-aa48-b6a86de93fa0","name":"Jensen, Torben René","name_org":"Jensen, Torben R.","orcid":"0000-0002-4278-3221","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.chemmater.6b04797","issn":["08974756","15205002"],"issn_org":["08974756"],"issue":"8","journal":"Chemistry of Materials","pages":"3423-3430","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Chemistry of Materials","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018624943"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eb583f87-a872-447c-a7aa-02809768853c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Halogenated Sodium-closo-Dodecaboranes as Solid-State Ion Conductors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263653","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
