":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo Laksafoss","key":"holbekpau","last":"Holbek","name":"Holbek, Bo Laksafoss","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28007878"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ejcts/ezw381","issn":["10107940","1873734X"],"issn_org":["10107940"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","pages":"694-695","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","volume":"51"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017370869"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-435c3179-209b-4f59-8df1-e1e08de0cba1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery : taking a step into the future","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-433672","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The societies of thoracic surgery are working to incorporate simulation and competency-based assessment into specialty training. One challenge is the development of a simulation-based test, which can be used as an assessment tool. The study objective was to establish validity evidence for a virtual reality simulator test of a video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) lobectomy of a right upper lobe. METHODS: Participants with varying experience in VATS lobectomy were included. They were familiarized with a virtual reality simulator (LapSim(®)) and introduced to the steps of the procedure for a VATS right upper lobe lobectomy. The participants performed two VATS lobectomies on the simulator with a 5-min break between attempts. Nineteen pre-defined simulator metrics were recorded. RESULTS: Fifty-three participants from nine different countries were included. High internal consistency was found for the metrics with Cronbach's alpha coefficient for standardized items of 0.91. Significant test-retest reliability was found for 15 of the metrics (p-values <0.05). Significant correlations between the metrics and the participants VATS lobectomy experience were identified for seven metrics (p-values <0.001), and 10 metrics showed significant differences between novices (0 VATS lobectomies performed) and experienced surgeons (>50 VATS lobectomies performed). A pass/fail level defined as approximately one standard deviation from the mean metric scores for experienced surgeons passed none of the novices (0 % false positives) and failed four of the experienced surgeons (29 % false negatives). CONCLUSION: This study is the first to establish validity evidence for a VATS right upper lobe lobectomy virtual reality simulator test. Several simulator metrics demonstrated significant differences between novices and experienced surgeons and pass/fail criteria for the test were set with acceptable consequences. This test can be used as a first step in assessing thoracic surgery trainees' VATS lobectomy competency.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jensen, Katrine","Bjerrum, Flemming","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Petersen, René Horsleben","Pedersen, Jesper Holst","Konge, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-437914"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using virtual reality simulation to assess competence in video assisted thoracoscopic surgery vats lobectomy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-437914","identifier":[{"id":"27655381","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84988667497","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4a7c0a6a-b327-4207-b872-7be42e5e59cf"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFFA754103454B2C8D9EE8AAFCAD8B74"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Cardiothoracic Surgery","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Katrine","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Katrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Flemming","key":"bjerrumpau","last":"Bjerrum","name":"Bjerrum, Flemming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Holst","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Jesper Holst","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"kongepau","last":"Konge","locid":"e1c287e3-4cd2-43d2-887d-f2f77fd5daf8","name":"Konge, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-1258-5822","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27655381"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00464-016-5254-6","issn":["09302794","14322218"],"issn_org":["09302794"],"issue":"6","journal":"Surgical Endoscopy","pages":"2510-2518","status":"p","title":"Surgical Endoscopy","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988667497"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4a7c0a6a-b327-4207-b872-7be42e5e59cf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using virtual reality simulation to assess competence in video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) lobectomy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-437914","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Microlobectomy is a novel form of videoscopic-assisted thoracic surgery lobectomy. Strict inclusion criteria consist of the following: no intercostal incisions greater than 5 mm, 12 mm subxiphoid port, subxiphoid removal of the specimen, total endoscopic technique with CO2 insufflation, vision through a 5-mm camera, stapling via the subxiphoid port, or with 5-mm stapling devices. METHODS: The combined early experiences of six hospitals from three countries were combined from September 2014 to May 2016. During that time, the study represents a consecutive cohort study of this technique. RESULTS: Seventy-two patients underwent microlobectomy. The median (range) age was 66 (27-82). Half of the patients were female. There were 48 right-sided resections and 24 on the left. There were four segmental resections and there was one right pneumonectomy. Four operations were performed robotically (with 8-mm intercostal incisions). The median (range) operative time was 180 (94-285) minutes and the blood loss was 118 (5-800) mL. There were three conversions to thoracotomy and two conversions to videoscopic-assisted thoracic surgery by means of an intercostal utility incision to complete the operation. The median (range) length of stay was 3 (1-44) days and 30 patients (42%) when home by day 2 and 16 patients (22%) were discharged on day 1. There were no deaths. Five patients (7%) had a prolonged airleak. There were no wound infections and there was one incisional hernia. CONCLUSIONS: We believe that microlobectomy is an interesting novel form of videoscopic-assisted thoracic surgery lobectomy and has several theoretical advantages. We have presented our early results and hope that this will stimulate others to investigate this type of videoscopic-assisted thoracic surgery lobectomy further.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Dunning, Joel","Elsaegh, Mohamed","Nardini, Marco","Gillaspie, Erin A","Petersen, René Horsleben","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Helsel, Bryan","Naase, Hatam","Kornaszewska, Malgorzata","Will, Malcolm B","Walker, William S","Wigle, Dennis","Blackmon, Shanda Haley"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-457075"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microlobectomy a novel form of endoscopic lobectomy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-457075","identifier":[{"id":"85032356211","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28763351","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6a8e7401-eeb2-4aec-9967-5e9a3194ce1c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-B03987DC53CA59A3F9F970474BEE7109"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Cardiothoracic Surgery","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Joel","key":"dunningpau","last":"Dunning","name":"Dunning, Joel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohamed","key":"elsaeghpau","last":"Elsaegh","name":"Elsaegh, Mohamed","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"nardinipau","last":"Nardini","name":"Nardini, Marco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erin A","key":"gillaspiepau","last":"Gillaspie","name":"Gillaspie, Erin A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rene Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","name_org":"Petersen, Rene Horsleben","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bryan","key":"helselpau","last":"Helsel","name":"Helsel, Bryan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hatam","key":"naasepau","last":"Naase","name":"Naase, Hatam","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Malgorzata","key":"kornaszewskapau","last":"Kornaszewska","name":"Kornaszewska, Malgorzata","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Malcolm B","key":"willpau","last":"Will","name":"Will, Malcolm B","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"William S","key":"walkerpau","last":"Walker","name":"Walker, William S","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dennis","key":"wiglepau","last":"Wigle","name":"Wigle, Dennis","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shanda Haley","key":"blackmonpau","last":"Blackmon","name":"Blackmon, Shanda Haley","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28763351"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/imi.0000000000000394","issn":["15569845","15590879"],"issn_org":["15569845"],"issue":"4","journal":"Innovations","pages":"247-253","status":"p","title":"Innovations","title_org":"Innovations (Philadelphia)","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85032356211"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6a8e7401-eeb2-4aec-9967-5e9a3194ce1c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microlobectomy : A Novel Form of Endoscopic Lobectomy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457075","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Due to generally high discard rates in Norway lobster (Nephrops norvegicus) fisheries, a discard ban coming up and to the cod recovery plan in several areas, selective sorting grids have been tested in many areas and are specified by legislation for use in the Kattegat and Skagerrak area bordering Norway, Denmark and Sweden. Grids are very selective, but they can lead to loss of landable Norway lobster and valuable fish species. To improve retention of these species, we developed three new grids using made by polyurethane to make them flexible: One grid had horizontal bars, one had vertical bars, and one had vertical bars and a guiding funnel in front of the grid. Four unselective net bags were used to collect the catch escaping through different parts of the grid or escaping without passing through the grid. Water flow around the grid bars was measured in a flume tank. The three grids were tested from a commercial trawler in the Kattegat and Skagerrak area. Underwater filming was conducted to assess grid performance and fish behavior. Results showed that a bottom hole in the lower part of the grid allowed species in the lower part of the gear to pass and retained in the bag behind the hole. More flatfish passed the grid with horizontal bars compared to that with vertical bars, but the retention rate was still low. Use of the guiding funnel increased the contact with the grid considerably for both target and unwanted species. In all three grid designs, there were losses of Norway lobster above minimum landing size.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Madsen, Niels","Holst, René","Frandsen, Rikke","Hansen, Kurt"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-001853"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","SINTEF","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Sintef Fisheries and Aquaculture, Hirtshals"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development and test of selective sorting grids used in the norway lobster nephrops norvegicus fishery","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fishres.2016.10.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-001853","identifier":[{"id":"84992418296","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000388780600005","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-24dff1c3-3d09-4d31-8a4c-bc1b4b132cdd","dtu-c3aff26f-f4b7-48da-8df3-7c9ef28500d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-109B92A5143ECE8F76F1B7EF9E28BEB0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139801619/Postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fishres.2016.10.002","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/295461060/Postprint_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biology and Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U