{"abstract":"This study describes the first molecular characterization of a bacteriophage infecting a member of the environmentally important Sphingomonadaceae family. Both bacteriophage Lacusarx and its host Sphingobium sp. IP1 were isolated from activated sludge from a wastewater treatment plant. Genome sequencing revealed that the phage genes display little similarity to other known phages, despite a remarkable conservation of the synteny in which the functional genes occur among distantly related phages. Phylogenetic analyses confirmed that Lacusarx represents a hitherto undescribed genus of phages. A classical lysis cassette could not be identified in Lacusarx, suggesting that the genes encoding endolysin, holin, and spanin are host-specific and not found in phages infecting other bacteria. The virus harbors 24 tRNA genes corresponding to 18 different amino acids and furthermore has a significantly different codon usage than its host. Proteomic analysis of Lacusarx revealed the protein components of the phage particle. A lysogeny test indicated that Lacusarx is not a temperate phage.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Tue Kjærgaard","Carstens, Alexander Byth","Browne, Patrick Denis","Lametsch, René","Neve, Horst","Kot, Witold","Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-023119"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Rubner Institut"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the first characterized phage against a member of the ecologically important sphingomonads reveals high dissimilarity against all other known phages","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-017-13911-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-023119","identifier":[{"id":"000413191500005","type":"wos"},{"id":"85031922870","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29051555","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5648845","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-8f48ac45-4b20-42a9-b806-832c69862742","ku-f68d60c0-4664-4da0-a088-7ffa8b9b412a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8CE8B1EC49A06D857018C8D3F0F149EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-017-13911-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/120844306/s41598_017_13911_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/185405989/The_first_characterized_phage_against_a_member_of_the_ecologically_important_sphingomonads_reveals_high_dissimilarity_against_all_other_known_phages.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Ingredient and Dairy Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max rubner institut","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Rubner Institut","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tue Kjærgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d463554f-2fb0-42e9-b6c1-8c95df444946","name":"Nielsen, Tue Kjærgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Byth","key":"carstenspau","last":"Carstens","locid":"81f6700a-35fb-44a8-9e01-0fe288bbcb72","name":"Carstens, Alexander Byth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick Denis","key":"brownepau","last":"Browne","locid":"3074e4a1-ad60-4f0e-b649-c94a01b64b9b","name":"Browne, Patrick Denis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rene","key":"lametschpau","last":"Lametsch","locid":"70bd350a-6869-4a4a-b9bc-56a756376784","name":"Lametsch, Rene","orcid":"0000-0002-4189-806X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Horst","key":"nevepau","last":"Neve","name":"Neve, Horst","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Witold","key":"kotpau","last":"Kot","locid":"1ed8825e-1c59-4e9b-bcd7-974d5f6d8f01","name":"Kot, Witold","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Hestbjerg","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"f1afca6a-5a5a-4fec-b0f5-cc7bbb39a088","name":"Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29051555"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-017-13911-1","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"13566","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031922870"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8f48ac45-4b20-42a9-b806-832c69862742","ku-f68d60c0-4664-4da0-a088-7ffa8b9b412a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The first characterized phage against a member of the ecologically important sphingomonads reveals high dissimilarity against all other known phages","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-023119","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this national population-based study of glioma, we present epidemiologic data on incidence, demographics, survival, clinical characteristics and symptoms, and evaluate the association of specific indicators with the grade of glioma. We included 1930 patients registered in the Danish Neuro-Oncology Registry (DNOR) from 2009 to 2014. DNOR is a large-scale national population-based database including all adult glioma patients in Denmark. The age-adjusted annual incidence of histologic verified glioma was 7.3 cases pr. 100,000 person-years. High-grade gliomas were present in 85% and low-grade glioma in 15%. The overall male:female ratio was 3:2 and the mean age at onset was 60 years. Data for WHO grade I, II, III and IV glioma showed several important differences regarding age and sex distribution and symptomatology at presentation. The mean age increased with the grade of glioma and males predominated in all grades. Focal deficits were the most frequent presenting symptom, but among patients with glioma, grade II epileptic seizures were the most frequent symptom. Headache was a rare mono-symptomatic onset symptom. At presentation, higher age, focal deficits and cognitive change for <3 months duration, and headache <1 month were significant independent indicators of high-grade gliomas. Younger age and epileptic seizures for more than 3 months were indicative for low-grade gliomas. Survival rates for glioma grade I-IV showed decreasing survival with increasing grade. Glioma grade I-IV showed high diversity regarding several demographic and clinical characteristics emphasizing the importance of individually tailored disease treatments and support.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Birthe Krogh","Hansen, Steinbjørn","Laursen, Rene Johannes","Kosteljanetz, Michael","Schultz, Henrik","Nørgård, Bente Mertz","Guldberg, Rikke","Gradel, Kim Oren"],"cuid":["S03-098.67-010900"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Steinbjorn"],"keyword":["ADULTS","Brain tumors","Central nervous system","Classification","Denmark","Disease","Epidemiology","Glioma","Headache","Isocitrate dehydrogenase 1","Journal Article","Prognosis","RATES","Survival","Symptoms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Department of Neurology, Nordsjællands Hospital, University of Copenhagen, Hillerød, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epidemiology of glioma clinical characteristics symptoms and predictors of glioma patients grade i iv in the the danish neuro oncology registry","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85028775705","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-098.67-010900","identifier":[{"id":"28861666","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000416160300017","type":"wos"},{"id":"85028775705","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e3ea629f-a22a-47bd-827e-2d2b0498cfbb","au-5c1f093e-5479-4142-9acc-c306a147f319","sdu-3eaf4eee-d61b-4144-9a3a-7c9080f45cf9"],"keyword":["ADULTS","BRAIN-TUMORS","CENTRAL-NERVOUS-SYSTEM","CLASSIFICATION","DENMARK","DISEASE","Epidemiology","Glioma","HEADACHE","ISOCITRATE DEHYDROGENASE 1","Journal Article","Prognosis","RATES","Survival","Symptoms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-E98F310B8A6046F312B88ACEA3430806"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3"