{"author_count":8,"contributors":["Shanbhogue, Vikram Vinod","Støving, René Klinkby","Frederiksen, Katrine Diemer","Andersen, Stine","Brixen, Kim","Gram, Jeppe","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Hansen, Stinus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-583934"],"event":{"end":"2017-01-28","place":"Esbjerg, dk","start":"2016-01-27","title":"Dansk Endokrinologisk Selskabs Årsmøde 2017","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone changes after roux en y gastric bypass surgery a two year longitudinal study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-583934","ids":["sdu-254d1cce-22e3-4cfe-aeaf-c4b3c72786f0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DF7E8A20C1EC44138FF52EB3BD70C2F2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vikram Vinod","key":"shanbhoguepau","last":"Shanbhogue","locid":"31ae137f-794b-4090-a860-0b55d7528f44","name":"Shanbhogue, Vikram Vinod","orcid":"0000-0001-8841-2808","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Klinkby","key":"støvingoth","last":"Støving","locid":"4aab81f6-352f-4c74-82a2-23589beb9fd5","name":"Støving, René Klinkby","orcid":"0000-0002-4255-5544","rank":2,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Diemer","key":"frederiksenoth","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Katrine Diemer","rank":3,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"andersenoth","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Stine","rank":4,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"brixenoth","last":"Brixen","locid":"9f3c3042-e186-46aa-966a-d39df3e49bb0","name":"Brixen, Kim","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe","key":"gramoth","last":"Gram","name":"Gram, Jeppe","rank":6,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenoth","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cc73de9e-169b-4cd1-8e1c-1a2c3827b3e8","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":7,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stinus","key":"hansenoth","last":"Hansen","locid":"55fbaeae-64f0-4d31-b356-1ca840e82ed8","name":"Hansen, Stinus","orcid":"0000-0001-9486-0316","rank":8,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-254d1cce-22e3-4cfe-aeaf-c4b3c72786f0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bone changes after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery. A two-year longitudinal study.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-583934","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Organic semiconductors (OSC) such as thiophene-based oligomers exhibit useful electronic and optical properties making them applicable in photo-sensing devices. Generally, thiophene-based photodetectors exhibit a decent responsivity with a spectral sensitivity determined by the OSC's absorption properties. We present a simple, yet efficient method to enhance and spectrally tune the photoresponsivity of organic phototransistors (OPTs) utilizing the plasmonic properties of embedded metallic nanoparticles. The ability to fabricate and characterize nanostructures with high accuracy allows for tailoring of the optical properties of metal nanoparticles (NPs) and thereby tuning of the spectral range of enhanced photoresponsivity. In this work we have investigated OPTs based on the molecule 5,5″-bis(naphth-2-yl)-2,2':5′,2″-terthiophene (NaT3). We have fabricated OPTs with electron beam lithography-defined arrays of silver NPs under the organic thin-film. The photoconductivity of OPTs with and without NPs was characterized under spectrally resolved illumination. The OPTs exhibit significant responsivity at wavelengths below 500nm essentially coinciding with the absorption spectrum of NaT3. Finite element simulations of the optical properties of the NPs reveal large electric field enhancement at the plasmon resonances. At these wavelengths (350→500nm) the experimentally measured photoresponsivity of OPTs with NPs is significantly increased compared to the responsivity for OPTs without NPs. Due to a variation in particle size and shape of the fabricated silver NPs, a spectrally broad enhancement is predicted, which is in agreement with the experimental results. The results show that the photoresponsivity is dominantly enhanced in a spectral region of low OSC absorption coinciding with the localized surface plasmon resonances of the NPs. This work demonstrates that it is possible to improve and tailor the responsivity spectrum of photoactive organic devices by integration of metal nanoparticles.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Linnet, Jes","Runge Walther, Anders","Albrektsen, Ole","Tavares, Luciana","Eriksen, René Lynge","Jensen, Per Baunegaard With","Osadnik, Andreas","Hassing, Søren","Lützen, Arne","Kjelstrup-Hansen, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-593869"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bonn"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced photoresponsivity in organic field effect transistors by silver nanoparticles","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85018286329","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-593869","identifier":[{"id":"85018286329","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-47e8de7a-adb7-4ff4-83a1-480dda663f05"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-759FB0195316219776FD671EF41AD4EA"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU NanoSyd","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bonn","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jes","key":"linnetpau","last":"Linnet","locid":"e3c6ebc2-9f06-423a-8957-b49fd5f568dd","name":"Linnet, Jes","orcid":"0000-0002-4147-3694","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rungewaltherpau","last":"Runge Walther","locid":"494c61e9-83fd-4c1a-b19f-9f86435f3a15","name":"Runge Walther, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4940-2644","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"albrektsenpau","last":"Albrektsen","locid":"e5131670-9f40-49d6-97a0-a8da6817bd3c","name":"Albrektsen, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luciana","key":"tavarespau","last":"Tavares","locid":"2f76d8ef-e056-4d4a-bc63-0eac9d9bf7c0","name":"Tavares, Luciana","orcid":"0000-0002-1432-524X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Lynge","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"b3e301d7-bbe7-448f-bb53-09968ed57b02","name":"Eriksen, René Lynge","orcid":"0000-0003-4405-5831","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Baunegaard With","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"38bfe396-c870-419d-ad2d-93cabec84c5b","name":"Jensen, Per Baunegaard With","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"osadnikpau","last":"Osadnik","name":"Osadnik, Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"hassingpau","last":"Hassing","locid":"77eb7baa-299b-43f8-8dd6-a2237a76a7d7","name":"Hassing, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-1755-4782","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Arne","key":"lützenpau","last":"Lützen","name":"Lützen, Arne","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"kjelstruphansenpau","last":"Kjelstrup-Hansen","locid":"ed21fea6-c9a9-425c-8318-fc5f2eb277b5","name":"Kjelstrup-Hansen, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0003-4482-4979","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.orgel.2017.04.019","issn":["15661199"],"journal":"Organic Electronics","pages":"270-275","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Organic Electronics","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018286329"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-47e8de7a-adb7-4ff4-83a1-480dda663f05"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Enhanced photoresponsivity in organic field effect transistors by silver nanoparticles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-593869","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Danish craftsmen and workers are considered an at-risk group for developing lifestyle diseases due to low levels of physical activity and unhealthy dietary consumption. To date, no intervention has proven successful in creating lasting change in health behavior for this target group, which necessitates innovative and broad-reaching approaches. Technology is a relatively novel approach to facilitate health behavior change. By adding game design elements, also termed “gamification”, it has shown a potential to encourage users towards target behavior and learning across use-contexts. Gamification is a new research field in health and exercise, and there is a need for more research in the context of male health behavior change. “Sjakket” is an online platform which has been developed to facilitate health behavior change for men aged 35-55 through fellowship and competition. Men are invited to sign up, and organize in teams of 3-7 to form a fellowship. Gamification is utilized through virtual rewards and social comparison which is deployed through awarding points and generating leaderboards based on logged behavior, physical tests and completion of team-challenges. The purpose of this project is to analyze how the gamified platform encourages users to change health behavior. An explorative case-study approach was adopted to seek in-depth understanding of the case in its natural use-context. Participant observations and interviews were used to gather insights sensitive to the culture and social context of the target users. The preliminary findings suggest that users generally find that the platform has encouraged them to initiate health behavior change by facilitating exercise activities, nutritional tips and the creation of fellowships. Being a part of a fellowship seems to be essential for encouraging users to exercise regularly. The gamified aspects only seem to influence encouragement during the start of participation, and users generally express that they do not feel encouraged to log their behavior to receive points. Users seem to prefer to meet in person, and view the platform as a source of information and facilitation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, René Engelhardt","Elbæk, Lars","Bredahl, Thomas Viskum Gjelstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-596427"],"event":{"end":"2017-10-06","place":"Graz, at","start":"2017-10-05","title":"11th European Conference on Games Based Learning","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Behavior change","Gamification","Motivation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the motivational effect of a gamified online platform for real men","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-596427","ids":["sdu-510c939f-f7f6-4c91-a116-409bfa9752bb"],"keyword":["Game-based health learning","behavior change","context sensitive methods","gamification","motivation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A252D687E167951E54B805316A29E1EC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Engelhardt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2d887e76-ae82-4a8d-962e-5e927394748e","name":"Hansen, René Engelhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-4940","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Viskum Gjelstrup","key":"bredahlpau","last":"Bredahl","locid":"da24d6ab-b60f-42e7-8ad9-30144fea384c","name":"Bredahl, Thomas Viskum Gjelstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-4392-9763","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-510c939f-f7f6-4c91-a116-409bfa9752bb"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The motivational effect of a gamified online platform for “Real men”","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-596427","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Anorexia nervosa (AN) is associated with decreased bone mineral density and increased risk of fracture. The aim of this study was to assess bone geometry, volumetric bone mineral density (vBMD), trabecular microarchitecture and estimated failure load in weight-bearing vs. non-weight-bearing bones in AN. We included twenty-five females with AN, and twenty-five female controls matched on age and height. Bone geometry, vBMD and trabecular microarchitecture were assessed using high-resolution peripheral quantitative computed tomography of the distal radius and tibia. At both sites, cortical perimeter and total bone area were similar in patients and controls. Total vBMD was lower in the AN group in the tibia (p < 0.0005) but not in the radius. In the tibia, cortical thickness was approximately 25% lower (p < 0.0005) in the AN group, whereas there was no significant difference in the radius. In terms of trabecular microarchitecture, all indices [bone volume/tissue volume (BV/TV); trabecular thickness (Tb.Th.), trabecular number (Tb.N) and trabecular spacing (Tb.Sp.)] were impaired in AN in the tibia (p values range < 0.01-0.0001). In the radius, BV/TV and Tb.N were lower (p < 0.05 and p < 0.001, respectively); Tb.Sp. was higher (p < 0.001), whereas Tb.Th. did not differ, compared to controls. Estimated failure load was lower in patients in both the radius and the tibia (p < 0.0005 and p < 0.0001, respectively), most pronounced in the tibia. In conclusion, the impairment of cortical thickness and estimated failure load were significantly more pronounced in the weight-bearing tibia, compared to the non-weight-bearing radius, implying a direct effect of low body weight on bone loss in AN.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Frølich, Jacob Stampe","Hansen, Stinus","Winkler, Laura Vad","Andresen, Andreas Duch Kiilerich","Hermann, Anne Pernille","Støving, René Klinkby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-630927"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Frølich, Jacob Stampe"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of body weight on bone in anorexia nervosa a hr pqct study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00223-017-0254-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-630927","identifier":[{"id":"85013389529","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5486942","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28224178","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-c96a70a0-56e7-4c97-8e92-4d0c1858cf7c"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52F142B18A3B6D3BDCE89E4EE81DA0D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/125455163/The_Role_of_Body_Weight_on_Bone_in_Anorexia_Nervosa.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00223-017-0254-7","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Psychiatry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"frølichpau","last":"Frølich","locid":"fe87c12c-6766-45fe-874f-7ea5f269ad5c","name":"Frølich, Jacob Stampe","name_org":"Frølich, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-8156-2424","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stinus","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"55fbaeae-64f0-4d31-b356-1ca840e82ed8","name":"Hansen, Stinus","orcid":"0000-0001-9486-0316","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Al-Dakhiel","key":"winklerpau","last":"Winkler","locid":"7b9b47e9-c528-4f6b-938a-a9d46af5c6fe","name":"Winkler, Laura Vad","name_org":"Winkler, Laura Al-Dakhiel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Kiilerich","key":"andresenpau","last":"Andresen","locid":"10ea3ce3-06be-49af-a76d-449459fae641","name":"Andresen, Andreas Duch Kiilerich","name_org":"Andresen, Andreas Kiilerich","orcid":"0000-0002-1757-3302","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Pernille","key":"hermannpau","last":"Hermann","locid":"a306ee40-8a29-43f6-a6ce-ca9d14a68142","name":"Hermann, Anne Pernille","orcid":"0000-0001-6701-0981","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René K","key":"støvingpau","last":"Støving","locid":"4aab81f6-352f-4c74-82a2-23589beb9fd5","name":"Støving, René Klinkby","name_org":"Støving, René K","orcid":"0000-0002-4255-5544","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28224178"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00223-017-0254-7","issn":["0171967X","14320827"],"issn_org":["14320827"],"issue":"1","journal":"Calcified Tissue International","pages":"24-33","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Calcified Tissue International","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013389529"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c96a70a0-56e7-4c97-8e92-4d0c1858cf7c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Role of Body Weight on Bone in Anorexia Nervosa : A HR-pQCT Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-630927","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: A breast cancer (BC) diagnosis can profoundly affect the sex life of patient and partner within a couple. The purpose of the present study is to examine whether individual and partner sexual functioning, affectionate behavior, emotional closeness and depressive symptoms are associated with change over time in satisfaction with sex life of sexually active heterosexual couples dealing with BC and to explore whether the associations differ between patients and partners after adjustment for basic sociodemographic characteristics, comorbidity and BC treatment. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Women with BC and their male partners participated in a longitudinal study (Time 1, ≤4 months after surgery; Time 2, 5 months later). Participants completed items from the PROMIS(®) Sexual Function and Satisfaction measure (version 1.0), two items measuring affectionate behavior, a single item measuring emotional closeness and the Center for Epidemiologic Studies-Depression Scale. Registers provided sociodemographic and medical information. Multilevel models were used, which take the interdependency of couples' scores into account. RESULTS: A total of 287 sexually active couples were included in the analyses. Less vaginal discomfort and more vaginal lubrication were associated with increases in patients' satisfaction with sex life. Patients' and partners' satisfaction increased with higher ratings of their own orgasm ability and of partners' timing of ejaculation. Patients' reports of affectionate behavior were positively associated with their partners' satisfaction, and vice versa for partners. Patients' satisfaction increased the more emotional closeness their partner experienced. Partners' depressive symptoms were negatively associated with their satisfaction. Sociodemographic factors and BC treatment were not significantly associated with change in satisfaction. CONCLUSION: Satisfaction with sex life in sexually active couples dealing with BC needs to be seen as a couple issue. Health professionals should take the partner into account when addressing sexuality issues. Couples' functioning and relationship-related factors may be promising targets for couple interventions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rottmann, Nina","Gilså Hansen, Dorte","dePont Christensen, René","Hagedoorn, Mariet","Frisch, Morten","Nicolaisen, Anne","Kroman, Niels","Flyger, Henrik","Johansen, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S02-080.99-010114"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-20","place":"København, dk","start":"2016-09-19","title":"European Cancer Rehabilitation and Survivorship Symposium","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"satisfaction with sex life in sexually active heterosexual couples dealing with breast cancer a nationwide longitudinal study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-080.99-010114","identifier":[{"id":"28080186","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85009286797","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000395159600014","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-d3249309-780a-4fda-8b9b-0a6f02a69dbd","ku-899c6fe1-e9a2-45a5-b5c0-1033a5fde5bc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-F05820AAA741EE900C0266C012AF887B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for Sexology Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"rottmannpau","last":"Rottmann","name":"Rottmann, Nina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte","key":"gilsåhansenpau","last":"Gilså Hansen","name":"Gilså Hansen, Dorte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"depontchristensenpau","last":"dePont Christensen","name":"dePont Christensen, René","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mariet","key":"hagedoornpau","last":"Hagedoorn","name":"Hagedoorn, Mariet","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"frischpau","last":"Frisch","locid":"b1c441cd-cdda-46b2-888b-008e851c0503","name":"Frisch, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"nicolaisenpau","last":"Nicolaisen","name":"Nicolaisen, Anne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Niels","key":"kromanpau","last":"Kroman","locid":"e120d8b8-6f8e-4b09-a51f-4eca94999f55","name":"Kroman, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-6631-2993","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"flygerpau","last":"Flyger","name":"Flyger, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"18d62c73-2f35-499d-ac94-134ecd806296","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28080186"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2016.1266086","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"212-219","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009286797"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d3249309-780a-4fda-8b9b-0a6f02a69dbd","ku-899c6fe1-e9a2-45a5-b5c0-1033a5fde5bc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Satisfaction with sex life in sexually active heterosexual couples dealing with breast cancer : a nationwide longitudinal study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.99-010114","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE, DESIGN AND METHODS: Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB) has proved successful in attaining sustained weight loss but may lead to metabolic bone disease. To assess impact on bone mass and structure, we measured a real bone mineral density at the hip and spine by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, and volumetric BMD (vBMD) and bone microarchitecture at the distal radius and tibia by high-resolution peripheral quantitative CT in 25 morbidly obese subjects (15 females, 10 males) at 0, 12 and 24 months after RYGB. Bone turnover markers (BTMs), calciotropic and gut hormones and adipokines were measured at the same time points. RESULTS: After a 24.1% mean weight loss from baseline to month 12 (P < 0.001), body weight plateaued from month 12 to 24 (-0.9%,P = 0.50). However, cortical and trabecular vBMD and microarchitecture deteriorated through the 24 months, such that there was a 5 and 7% reduction in estimated bone strength at the radius and tibia respectively (bothP < 0.001). The declines observed in the first 12 months were matched or exceeded by declines in the 12- to 24-month period. While a significant increase in BTMs and decrease in leptin and insulin were seen at 24 months, these changes were maximal at month 12 and stabilized from month 12 to 24. CONCLUSIONS: Despite weight stabilization and maintenance of metabolic parameters, bone loss and deterioration in bone strength continued and were substantial in the second year. The clinical importance of these changes in terms of increased risk of developing osteoporosis and fragility fractures remain an important concern.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Shanbhogue, Vikram V","Støving, René Klinkby","Frederiksen, Katrine Hartmund","Hanson, Stine","Brixen, Kim","Gram, Jeppe","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Hansen, Stinus"],"cuid":["S02-097.21-044053"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Shanbhogue, Vikram Vinod"],"keyword":["Absorptiometry Photon","Adiponectin metabolism","Adult","Bone Density","Bone Remodeling","Collagen Type I metabolism","Female","Follicle Stimulating Hormone metabolism","Gastric Bypass adverse effects","Hip Joint diagnostic imaging","Humans","Insulin metabolism","Journal Article","Leptin metabolism","Longitudinal Studies","Lumbar Vertebrae diagnostic imaging","Luteinizing Hormone metabolism","Male","Middle Aged","Obesity Morbid surgery","Osteoporosis diagnostic imaging","Parathyroid Hormone metabolism","Peptide Fragments metabolism","Peptides metabolism","Postoperative Complications diagnostic imaging","Procollagen metabolism","Radius diagnostic imaging","Tibia diagnostic imaging","Tomography X Ray Computed","Vitamin D analogs derivatives","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone structural changes after gastric bypass surgery evaluated by hr pqct a two year longitudinal study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-17-0014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.21-044053","identifier":[{"id":"85021308783","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28289103","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5425940","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-85463c84-bfa8-4a6c-8cf9-d1b2e0e581e1","sdu-bd40dc01-1287-44c2-9575-fe7e768f7abf"],"keyword":["Absorptiometry, Photon","Adiponectin/metabolism","Adult","Bone Density","Bone Diseases, Metabolic/diagnostic imaging","Bone Remodeling","Collagen Type I/metabolism","Female","Follicle Stimulating Hormone/metabolism","Gastric Bypass/adverse effects","Hip Joint/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Insulin/metabolism","Journal Article","Leptin/metabolism","Longitudinal Studies","Lumbar Vertebrae/diagnostic imaging","Luteinizing Hormone/metabolism","Male","Middle Aged","Obesity, Morbid/surgery","Osteoporosis/diagnostic imaging","Parathyroid Hormone/metabolism","Peptide Fragments/metabolism","Peptides/metabolism","Postoperative Complications/diagnostic imaging","Procollagen/metabolism","Radius/diagnostic imaging","Tibia/diagnostic imaging","Tomography, X-Ray Computed","Vitamin D/analogs & derivatives","Weight Loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4AA299358C47A227323EFB76F262AE14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/194526968/685.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/125359556/Bone_structural_changes_after_gastric_bypass_surgery_evaluated_by_HR_pQCT.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-17-0014","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Glostrup Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vikram Vinod","key":"shanbhoguepau","last":"Shanbhogue","locid":"31ae137f-794b-4090-a860-0b55d7528f44","name":"Shanbhogue, Vikram Vinod","orcid":"0000-0001-8841-2808","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Klinkby","key":"støvingpau","last":"Støving","locid":"4aab81f6-352f-4c74-82a2-23589beb9fd5","name":"Støving, René Klinkby","orcid":"0000-0002-4255-5544","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Diemer","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"8e385a35-8615-426f-be00-93d36233be00","name":"Frederiksen, Katrine Diemer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"hansonpau","last":"Hanson","locid":"bba8709c-7b49-489b-ad24-64d9019447a9","name":"Hanson, Stine","orcid":"0000-0002-7699-8001","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"brixenpau","last":"Brixen","locid":"9f3c3042-e186-46aa-966a-d39df3e49bb0","name":"Brixen, Kim","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe","key":"grampau","last":"Gram","locid":"a5fd241d-294b-4fa7-82be-6492051b2406","name":"Gram, Jeppe","orcid":"0000-0003-2584-1132","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","locid":"cc73de9e-169b-4cd1-8e1c-1a2c3827b3e8","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","name_org":"Jorgensen, Niklas Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stinus","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"55fbaeae-64f0-4d31-b356-1ca840e82ed8","name":"Hansen, Stinus","orcid":"0000-0001-9486-0316","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28289103"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1530/eje-17-0014","issn":["08044643","1479683X"],"issn_org":["08044643"],"issue":"6","journal":"European Journal of Endocrinology","pages":"685-693","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Endocrinology","volume":"176"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021308783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-85463c84-bfa8-4a6c-8cf9-d1b2e0e581e1","sdu-bd40dc01-1287-44c2-9575-fe7e768f7abf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bone structural changes after gastric bypass surgery evaluated by HR-pQCT : a two-year longitudinal study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.21-044053","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Bacteriophages are the main cause of fermentation failures in dairy plants. The majority of Streptococcus thermophilus phages can be divided into either cos- or pac-type phages and are additionally characterized by examining the V2 region of their antireceptors. We screened a large number of S. thermophilus phages from the Chr. Hansen A/S collection, using PCR specific for the cos- or pac-type phages, as well as for the V2 antireceptor region. Three phages did not produce positive results with the assays. Analysis of phage morphologies indicated that two of these phages, CHPC577 and CHPC926, had shorter tails than the traditional S. thermophilus phages. The third phage, CHPC1151, had a tail size similar to those of the cos- or pac-type phages, but it displayed a different baseplate structure. Sequencing analysis revealed the genetic similarity of CHPC577 and CHPC926 with a subgroup of Lactococcus lactis P335 phages. Phage CHPC1151 was closely related to the atypical S. thermophilus phage 5093, homologous with a nondairy streptococcal prophage. By testing adsorption of the related streptococcal and lactococcal phages to the surface of S. thermophilus and L. lactis strains, we revealed the possibility of cross-interactions. Our data indicated that the use of S. thermophilus together with L. lactis, extensively applied for dairy fermentations, triggered the recombination between phages infecting different bacterial species. A notable diversity among S. thermophilus phage populations requires that a new classification of the group be proposed.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Szymczak, Paula","Janzen, Thomas","Neves, Ana Rute","Kot, Witold","Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg","Lametsch, René","Neve, Horst","Franz, Charles M. A. P.","Vogensen, Finn K."],"cuid":["S02-098.49-021820"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Rubner Institut"],"keyword":["Bacteriophages","Classification","Journal Article","Streptococcus thermophilus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel variants of em streptococcus thermophilus em bacteriophages are indicative of genetic recombination among phages from different bacterial species","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/AEM.02748-16","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.49-021820","identifier":[{"id":"28039135","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85013456437","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000393962500012","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5311409","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-7d869986-f3e7-444e-8536-c07d3281f6e8","ku-db750b70-cf6d-44e0-9923-58f33b8584ec"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Streptococcus thermophilus","bacteriophages","classification","structural genes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-648780F3AAAF3AC566C46427F041EFBB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/AEM.02748-16","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/203454493/e02748_16.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/120340132/Appl._Environ._Microbiol._2017_Szymczak_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"Univers