Witold","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Hestbjerg","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"f1afca6a-5a5a-4fec-b0f5-cc7bbb39a088","name":"Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rene","key":"lametschpau","last":"Lametsch","locid":"70bd350a-6869-4a4a-b9bc-56a756376784","name":"Lametsch, Rene","orcid":"0000-0002-4189-806X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Horst","key":"nevepau","last":"Neve","name":"Neve, Horst","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Charles M. A. P.","key":"franzpau","last":"Franz","name":"Franz, Charles M. A. P.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Finn Kvist","key":"vogensenpau","last":"Vogensen","locid":"337bf47b-655e-4e27-a5e0-04dd672a0876","name":"Vogensen, Finn Kvist","orcid":"0000-0003-2151-7802","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28039135"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/aem.02748-16","issn":["00992240","10985336"],"issn_org":["00992240"],"issue":"5","journal":"Applied and Environmental Microbiology","paperid":"e02748-16","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Applied and Environmental Microbiology","volume":"83"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013456437"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7d869986-f3e7-444e-8536-c07d3281f6e8","ku-db750b70-cf6d-44e0-9923-58f33b8584ec"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Novel Variants of Streptococcus thermophilus Bacteriophages Are Indicative of Genetic Recombination among Phages from Different Bacterial Species","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.49-021820","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background Safety in the operating room is dependent on the team's non-technical skills. The importance of non-technical skills appears to be different for minimally invasive surgery as compared with open surgery. The aim of this study was to identify which non-technical skills are perceived by team members to be most important for patient safety, in the setting of video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) lobectomy. Methods This was an explorative, semistructured interview-based study with 21 participants from all four thoracic surgery centers in Denmark that perform VATS lobectomy. Data analysis was deductive, and directed content analysis was used to code the text into the Oxford Non-Technical Skills system for evaluating operating teams’ non-technical skills. Results The most important non-technical skills described by the VATS teams were planning and preparation, situation awareness, problem solving, leadership, risk assessment, and teamwork. These non-technical skills enabled the team to achieve shared mental models, which in turn facilitated their efforts to anticipate next steps. This was viewed as important by the participants as they saw VATS lobectomy as a high-risk procedure with complementary and overlapping scopes of practice between surgical and anesthesia subteams. Conclusions This study identified six non-technical skills that serve as the foundation for shared mental models of the patient, the current situation, and team resources. These findings contribute three important additions to the shared mental model construct: planning and preparation, risk assessment, and leadership. Shared mental models are crucial for patient safety because they enable VATS teams to anticipate problems through adaptive patterns of both implicit and explicit coordination.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Gjeraa, Kirsten","Mundt, Anna S.","Spanager, Lene","Hansen, Henrik J.","Konge, Lars","Petersen, René Horsleben","Østergaard, Doris"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443053"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"important non technical skills in video assisted thoracoscopic surgery lobectomy team perspectives","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-443053","identifier":[{"id":"28587738","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85020059660","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-532014d2-182f-494f-9992-7ce990b58871"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8EA30537A954328F3B2528AC23F0CE4B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Cardiothoracic Surgery","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Kirsten","key":"gjeraapau","last":"Gjeraa","name":"Gjeraa, Kirsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna S.","key":"mundtpau","last":"Mundt","name":"Mundt, Anna S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"spanagerpau","last":"Spanager","name":"Spanager, Lene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik J.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"kongepau","last":"Konge","locid":"e1c287e3-4cd2-43d2-887d-f2f77fd5daf8","name":"Konge, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-1258-5822","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René H.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","name_org":"Petersen, René H.","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Doris","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"b7ae7286-fc61-49c5-8bae-d683f6b71152","name":"Østergaard, Doris","orcid":"0000-0001-8542-6999","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28587738"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.athoracsur.2017.03.010","issn":["00034975","15526259"],"issn_org":["00034975"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Annals of Thoracic Surgery","pages":"329-335","status":"p","title":"The Annals of Thoracic Surgery","title_org":"Annals of Thoracic Surgery","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020059660"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-532014d2-182f-494f-9992-7ce990b58871"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Important Non-Technical Skills in Video-Assisted Thoracoscopic Surgery Lobectomy : Team Perspectives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443053","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: A breast cancer (BC) diagnosis can profoundly affect the sex life of patient and partner within a couple. The purpose of the present study is to examine whether individual and partner sexual functioning, affectionate behavior, emotional closeness and depressive symptoms are associated with change over time in satisfaction with sex life of sexually active heterosexual couples dealing with BC and to explore whether the associations differ between patients and partners after adjustment for basic sociodemographic characteristics, comorbidity and BC treatment. Material and methods: Women with BC and their male partners participated in a longitudinal study (Time 1, ≤4 months after surgery; Time 2, 5 months later). Participants completed items from the PROMIS® Sexual Function and Satisfaction measure (version 1.0), two items measuring affectionate behavior, a single item measuring emotional closeness and the Center for Epidemiologic Studies-Depression Scale. Registers provided sociodemographic and medical information. Multilevel models were used, which take the interdependency of couples’ scores into account. Results: A total of 287 sexually active couples were included in the analyses. Less vaginal discomfort and more vaginal lubrication were associated with increases in patients’ satisfaction with sex life. Patients’ and partners’ satisfaction increased with higher ratings of their own orgasm ability and of partners’ timing of ejaculation. Patients’ reports of affectionate behavior were positively associated with their partners’ satisfaction, and vice versa for partners. Patients’ satisfaction increased the more emotional closeness their partner experienced. Partners’ depressive symptoms were negatively associated with their satisfaction. Sociodemographic factors and BC treatment were not significantly associated with change in satisfaction. Conclusion: Satisfaction with sex life in sexually active couples dealing with BC needs to be seen as a couple issue. Health professionals should take the partner into account when addressing sexuality issues. Couples’ functioning and relationship-related factors may be promising targets for couple interventions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rottmann, Nina","Hansen, Dorte Gilså","Christensen, René dePont","Hagedoorn, Mariët","Frisch, Morten","Nicolaisen, Anne","Kroman, Niels","Flyger, Henrik","Johansen, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-623609"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Groningen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"satisfaction with sex life in sexually active heterosexual couples dealing with breast cancer a nationwide longitudinal study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85009286797","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-623609","identifier":[{"id":"28080186","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85009286797","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-afef47a5-bb10-4802-8486-884ade6a8a25"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-F05820AAA741EE900C0266C012AF887B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, INSIDE","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university medical center groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Kræftens Bekæmpelse"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nina","key":"rottmannpau","last":"Rottmann","locid":"16e7c8cc-cee3-43aa-8651-e2a1414f2426","name":"Rottmann, Nina","orcid":"0000-0002-7262-6788","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Gilså","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2826791-eb97-4bca-8af7-448b0940e6e5","name":"Hansen, Dorte Gilså","orcid":"0000-0002-5946-9968","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René dePont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mariët","key":"hagedoornpau","last":"Hagedoorn","name":"Hagedoorn, Mariët","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"frischpau","last":"Frisch","name":"Frisch, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"nicolaisenpau","last":"Nicolaisen","locid":"1c1d730b-acab-4f96-a824-90f2fcb3017d","name":"Nicolaisen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-5696-7144","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"kromanpau","last":"Kroman","name":"Kroman, Niels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"flygerpau","last":"Flyger","name":"Flyger, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28080186"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2016.1266086","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"212-219","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009286797"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-afef47a5-bb10-4802-8486-884ade6a8a25"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Satisfaction with sex life in sexually active heterosexual couples dealing with breast cancer : a nationwide longitudinal study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-623609","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We have previously shown higher-than-expected rates of schizophrenia in relatives of patients with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), suggesting an aetiological relationship between the diseases. Here, we investigate the genetic relationship between ALS and schizophrenia using genome-wide association study data from over 100,000 unique individuals. Using linkage disequilibrium score regression, we estimate the genetic correlation between ALS and schizophrenia to be 14.3% (7.05-21.6; P=1 × 10(-4)) with schizophrenia polygenic risk scores explaining up to 0.12% of the variance in ALS (P=8.4 × 10(-7)). A modest increase in comorbidity of ALS and schizophrenia is expected given these findings (odds ratio 1.08-1.26) but this would require very large studies to observe epidemiologically. We identify five potential novel ALS-associated loci using conditional false discovery rate analysis. It is likely that shared neurobiological mechanisms between these two disorders will engender novel hypotheses in future preclinical and clinical studies.","author_count":50,"contributors":["McLaughlin, Russell L.","Schijven, Dick","Van Rheenen, Wouter","Van Eijk, Kristel R.","O'Brien, Margaret","Kahn, René S.","Ophoff, Roel A.","Goris, An","Bradley, Daniel G.","Al-Chalabi, Ammar","Van Den Berg, Leonard H.","Luykx, Jurjen J.","Hardiman, Orla","Veldink, Jan H.","Shatunov, Aleksey","Dekker, Annelot M.","Diekstra, Frank P.","Pulit, Sara L.","Van Der Spek, Rick A.A.","Van Doormaal, Perry T.C.","Sproviero, William","Jones, Ashley R.","Nicholson, Garth A.","Rowe, Dominic B.","Pamphlett, Roger","Kiernan, Matthew C.","Bauer, Denis","Kahlke, Tim","Williams, Kelly","Eftimov, Filip","Fogh, Isabella","Ticozzi, Nicola","Lin, Kuang","Millecamps, Stephanie","Salachas, Francois","Meininger, Vincent","Carvalho, Mamede De","Pinto, Susana","Mora, Jesus S.","Rojas-Garcyá, Ricardo","Polak, Meraida","Chandran, Siddharthan","Andersen, Peter M.","Pers, Tune H.","Hansen, Mark","Hansen, Thomas","Li,