odus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-184288","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To compare the incidence of major adverse cardiac events (MACE) and mortality following video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) lobectomy in patients with and without coronary artery disease (CAD). METHODS: Multicentre retrospective analysis of 1699 patients undergoing VATS lobectomy (January 2012-March 2015). CAD definition: previous acute myocardial infarct (AMI), angina, percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) or coronary artery bypass graft (CABG). MACE definition: postoperative acute myocardial ischemia, cardiac arrest or any cardiac death. Propensity score analysis was performed to match patients with and without CAD. Outcomes of the 2 matched groups were compared. RESULTS: The incidence of MACE and mortality for the entire population was 0.4% (7 patients) and 1.7% (29 patients); 218 patients (13%) had a history of CAD: 106 previous AMI, 55 angina, 32 CABG, and 81 PCI. The propensity score yielded 2 well-balanced groups of 218 pairs with and without CAD. MACE (CAD 2 [0.9%] vs no-CAD 1 [0.5%]; P = 1), cardiovascular and pulmonary complications (CAD 61 [28%] vs no-CAD 51 [23%]; P = .3) and postoperative stay (CAD 7.3 days vs no-CAD 6.2 days; P = .3) were not different between the groups. The incidence of atrial fibrillation (CAD 31 [14%] vs no-CAD 18 [8.2%]; P = .07), 30-day mortality (CAD: 11 [5%] vs no-CAD 2 [0.9%]; P = .02) and death among complicated patients (CAD 18% vs no-CAD 3.9%; P = .009) were higher in the CAD group. CONCLUSIONS: The incidence of MACE following VATS lobectomy in patients with CAD is low and similar to patients without CAD. However, their risk of postoperative mortality is fivefold higher compared with non-CAD patients, warranting refined preoperative functional evaluation and more intense postoperative monitoring.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sandri, Alberto","Petersen, René Horsleben","Decaluwé, Herbert","Moons, Johnny","Ferguson, Mark K","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Brunelli, Alessandro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489170"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coronary artery disease is associated with an increased mortality rate following video assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-489170","identifier":[{"id":"85017429706","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28412122","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a01e9f5a-b291-433a-b2c7-9ff72c5fff6c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA4F51E85B2A0BC945978718DA3685A2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Cardiothoracic Surgery","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Alberto","key":"sandripau","last":"Sandri","name":"Sandri, Alberto","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rene Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","name_org":"Petersen, Rene Horsleben","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Herbert","key":"decaluwépau","last":"Decaluwé","name":"Decaluwé, Herbert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Johnny","key":"moonspau","last":"Moons","name":"Moons, Johnny","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mark K","key":"fergusonpau","last":"Ferguson","name":"Ferguson, Mark K","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alessandro","key":"brunellipau","last":"Brunelli","name":"Brunelli, Alessandro","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28412122"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jtcvs.2017.03.042","issn":["00225223","10858687"],"issn_org":["00225223"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Journal of Thoracic and Cardiovascular Surgery","pages":"352-357","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Thoracic and Cardiovascular Surgery","volume":"154"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017429706"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a01e9f5a-b291-433a-b2c7-9ff72c5fff6c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coronary artery disease is associated with an increased mortality rate following video-assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-489170","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE: In this study we investigated the interchangeability of planning CT and cone-beam CT (CBCT) extracted radiomic features. Furthermore, a previously described CT based prognostic radiomic signature for non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients using CBCT based features was validated. MATERIAL AND METHODS: One training dataset of 132 and two validation datasets of 62 and 94stage I-IV NSCLC patients were included. Interchangeability was assessed by performing a linear regression on CT and CBCT extracted features. A two-step correction was applied prior to model validation of a previously published radiomic signature. Results 13.3% (149 out of 1119) of the radiomic features, including all features of the previously published radiomic signature, showed an R(2) above 0.85 between intermodal imaging techniques. For the radiomic signature, Kaplan-Meier curves were significantly different between groups with high and low prognostic value for both modalities. Harrell's concordance index was 0.69 for CT and 0.66 for CBCT models for dataset 1. Conclusions The results show that a subset of radiomic features extracted from CT and CBCT images are interchangeable using simple linear regression. Moreover, a previously developed radiomics signature has prognostic value for overall survival in three CBCT cohorts, showing the potential of CBCT radiomics to be used as prognostic imaging biomarker.","author_count":10,"contributors":["van Timmeren, Janna E","Leijenaar, Ralph T H","van Elmpt, Wouter","Reymen, Bart","Oberije, Cary","Monshouwer, René","Bussink, Johan","Brink, Carsten","Hansen, Olfred","Lambin, Philippe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-573923"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Maastricht University Medical Center+","Radboud University Medical Center"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"survival prediction of non small cell lung cancer patients using radiomics analyses of cone beam ct images","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.radonc.2017.04.016","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-573923","identifier":[{"id":"85018938163","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28506693","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-02743f30-94f1-475c-9482-49cf5c1876c3"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4CA048E1EA47D200E47D21634CD38F1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/125139895/Survival_prediction_of_non_small_cell_lung_cancer_patients_using_radiomics_analyses_of_cone_beam_CT_images.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.radonc.2017.04.016","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"maastricht university medical center","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Maastricht University Medical Center+","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"radboud university medical center","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Janna E","key":"vantimmerenpau","last":"van Timmeren","name":"van Timmeren, Janna E","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralph T H","key":"leijenaarpau","last":"Leijenaar","name":"Leijenaar, Ralph T H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wouter","key":"vanelmptpau","last":"van Elmpt","name":"van Elmpt, Wouter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bart","key":"reymenpau","last":"Reymen","name":"Reymen, Bart","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cary","key":"oberijepau","last":"Oberije","name":"Oberije, Cary","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"monshouwerpau","last":"Monshouwer","name":"Monshouwer, René","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"bussinkpau","last":"Bussink","name":"Bussink, Johan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"brinkpau","last":"Brink","locid":"1392b95d-bbe7-4a00-bc48-aa402170385e","name":"Brink, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3906-1962","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olfred","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3c005a52-6edc-4112-b87b-e353b545a354","name":"Hansen, Olfred","orcid":"0000-0003-0396-1424","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philippe","key":"lambinpau","last":"Lambin","name":"Lambin, Philippe","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28506693"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.radonc.2017.04.016","issn":["01678140"],"issue":"3","journal":"Radiotherapy & Oncology","pages":"363-369","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Radiotherapy & Oncology","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018938163"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-02743f30-94f1-475c-9482-49cf5c1876c3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Survival prediction of non-small cell lung cancer patients using radiomics analyses of cone-beam CT images","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-573923","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Danish craftsmen and workers are considered an at-risk group for developing lifestyle diseases due to low levels of physical activity and unhealthy dietary consumption. To date, no intervention has proven successful in creating lasting change in health behavior for this target group, which necessitates innovative and broad-reaching approaches. Technology is a relatively novel approach to facilitate health behavior change. By adding game design elements, also termed “gamification”, it has shown a potential to encourage users towards target behavior and learning across use-contexts. Gamification is a new research field in health and exercise, and there is a need for more research in the context of male health behavior change. “Sjakket” is an online platform which has been developed to facilitate health behavior change for men aged 35-55 through fellowship and competition. Men are invited to sign up, and organize in teams of 3-7 to form a fellowship. Gamification is utilized through virtual rewards and social comparison which is deployed through awarding points and generating leaderboards based on logged behavior, physical tests and completion of team-challenges. The purpose of this project is to analyze how the gamified platform encourages users to change health behavior. An explorative case-study approach was adopted to seek in-depth understanding of the case in its natural use-context. Participant observations and interviews were used to gather insights sensitive to the culture and social context of the target users. The preliminary findings suggest that users generally find that the platform has encouraged them to initiate health behavior change by facilitating exercise activities, nutritional tips and the creation of fellowships. Being a part of a fellowship seems to be essential for encouraging users to exercise regularly. The gamified aspects only seem to influence encouragement during the start of participation, and users generally express that they do not feel encouraged to log their behavior to receive points. Users seem to prefer to meet in person, and view the platform as a source of information and facilitation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Elbæk, Lars","Hansen, René Engelhardt","Bredahl, Thomas Viskum Gjelstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-579706"],"event":{"end":"2017-10-06","place":"Graz, at","start":"2017-10-05","title":"11th European Conference on Games Based Learning","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to become a real man health behavior change for men through gamification","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134191699/ECGBL_Poster_A1_v._2.0_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-579706","ids":["sdu-16b68e2f-21dc-4350-bedd-733e443f5ac8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-31903D17F95AE4A79195E88F1C58824C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134191699/ECGBL_Poster_A1_v._2.0_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Engelhardt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2d887e76-ae82-4a8d-962e-5e927394748e","name":"Hansen, René Engelhardt","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-4940","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Viskum Gjelstrup","key":"bredahlpau","last":"Bredahl","locid":"da24d6ab-b60f-42e7-8ad9-30144fea384c","name":"Bredahl, Thomas Viskum Gjelstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-4392-9763","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-16b68e2f-21dc-4350-bedd-733e443f5ac8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How to become a ”real man” : Health behavior change for men through gamification","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-579706","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We report the first asteroseismic results obtained with the Hertzsprung Stellar Observations Network Group Telescope from an extensive high-precision radial-velocity observing campaign of the subgiant μ Herculis. The data set was collected during 215 nights in 2014 and 2015. We detected a total of 49 oscillation modes with l values from zero to three, including some l = 1 mixed modes. Based on the rotational splitting observed in l = 1 modes, we determine a rotational period of 52 days and a stellar inclination angle of 63°. The parameters obtained through modeling of the observed oscillation frequencies agree very well with independent observations and imply a stellar mass between 1.11 and 1.15 M o and an age of 7.8 +0.3 -0.4 Gyr. Furthermore, the high-quality data allowed us to determine the acoustic depths of the He ii ionization layer and the base of the convection zone.","author_count":40,"contributors":["Grundahl, F.","Andersen, Mads Fredslund","Christensen-Dalsgaard, Jørgen","Antoci, Victoria","Kjeldsen, Hans","Handberg, Rasmus","Houdek, G.","Bedding, Timothy R.","Pallé, P. L.","Jessen-Hansen, J.","Silva Aguirre, Victor","White, T. R.","Frandsen, Søren","Albrecht, Simon","Andersen, M. I.","Arentoft, T.","Brogaard, K.","Chaplin, W. J.","Harpsøe, K.","Jørgensen, U. G.","Karovicova, I.","Karoff, Christoffer","Kjærgaard Rasmussen, Per","Lund, Mikkel N.","Lundkvist, M.","Skottfelt, J.","Norup Sørensen, A.","Rasmussen, René Tronsgaard","Weiss, Eric"],"cuid":["S02-093.14-020372"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Germany","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Heidelberg University ","Open University Milton Keynes","University of Birmingham","University of La Laguna","University of Sydney"],"keyword":["Asteroseismology","Instrumentation spectrographs","Method