{"abstract":"Software Defined Radio (SDR) devices are becoming increasingly popular due to their support for mode-, standardand application-flexibility. At the same time however, the energy consumption of such devices typically suffers from the use of reconfigurable real-time platforms which are known to be severely power hungry. In this work we therefore show how to use tools and techniques developed by the formal methods community to minimize the energy consumption of Finite Impulse Response (FIR) filters which are extensively used in SDR front-ends. We conduct experiments with four different FIR filter structures where we initially derive data flow graphs and precedence graphs using the Synchronous Data Flow (SDF) notation. Based on actual measurements on the Altera Cyclone IV FPGA, we derive power and timing estimates for addition and multiplication, including idling power consumption. We next model the FIR structures in UPPAAL CORA and employ model checking to find energyoptimal solutions in linearly priced timed automata. In conclusion we state that there are significant energy-versus-time differences between the four structures when we experiment with varying numbers of adders and multipliers. Similarly, we find that idle power becomes an important parameter when a high number of functional units are allocated.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Koch, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065570"],"event":{"acronym":"DDECS","end":"2016-04-22","place":"Košice, sk","start":"2016-04-20","title":"International Symposium on Design and Diagnostics of Electronic Circuits &amp; Systems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["FIR Filter","FPGA","Power consumption","Timed automata","UPPAAL","VHDL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy aware scheduling of fir filter structures using a timed automata model","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/241229094/Koch_DDECS16.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-065570","identifier":[{"id":"84978468570","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-356f5489-14c9-416f-9cd6-647aa06b13df"],"keyword":["FIR Filter","FPGA","Power Consumption","Timed automata","UPPAAL","VHDL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61C40B9CA7F356FDFB8A8CDC453C792E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/241229094/Koch_DDECS16.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Ramsgaard","key":"wognsenpau","last":"Wognsen","locid":"5ff613ea-45c3-4201-924b-67606a027557","name":"Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Guldstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","locid":"b798b1cd-ece9-40b2-bec2-ab2f46bf7a1d","name":"Koch, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-5328-7127","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ddecs.2016.7482468","eisbn":["9781509024667"],"pages":"163-168","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"2016 IEEE 19th International Symposium on Design and Diagnostics of Electronic Circuits &amp; Systems (DDECS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978468570"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-356f5489-14c9-416f-9cd6-647aa06b13df"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Energy-Aware Scheduling of FIR Filter Structures using a Timed Automata Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065570","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
