{"abstract":"The behaviour of two optical instruments, scilicet a laser scanning confocal microscope and a focus-variation microscope, was investigated considering measurements of tilted surfaces. The measured samples were twelve steel artefacts for mould surface finish reference, covering Sa roughness parameter in the range (101—103) nm. The 3D surface texture parameters considered were Sa, Sq and Sdq. The small working distance of the confocal microscope objectives influenced the measurement setup, preventing from selecting a high tilting angle. The investigation was carried out comparing measurements of flat surfaces (0° tilt) with measurements of 12.5° tilted surfaces. The confocal microscope results showed a high sensitivity to tilting due to the laser beam reflection on the metal surfaces. The focus variation microscope results were more robust with respect to the considered angular variation, although they were out of the instrument operating range except for one of the twelve artefacts.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Quagliotti, Danilo","Baruffi, Federico","Tosello, Guido","Gasparin, Stefania","Annoni, Massimiliano","Parenti, Paolo","Sobiecki, Rene","Hansen, Hans Nørgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-375680"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-03","place":"Nottingham, gb","start":"2016-05-30","title":"16th International Conference of the European Society for Precision Engineering and Nanotechnology","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan"],"keyword":["Confocal","Optical microscope"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LEGO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LEGO","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performance verification of focus variation and confocal microscopes measuring tilted ultra fine surfaces","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84984619775","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-375680","identifier":[{"id":"84984619775","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-edb53368-eefc-47ef-b225-825134e20d97"],"keyword":["Confocal","Focus variation","Optical microscope","Tilted surface"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CB9BD3C2DBFC54F6AE7DE02D6FA60515"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lego","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LEGO","l3nn":"LEGO","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LEGO","namevar":["Lego Group"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LEGO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Danilo","key":"quagliottipau","last":"Quagliotti","locid":"2abc1dc9-c1b1-4c94-9904-be78e2b9a3fd","name":"Quagliotti, Danilo","orcid":"0000-0002-8347-2884","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Federico","key":"baruffipau","last":"Baruffi","locid":"d5ca2074-1934-4833-9988-70638689035c","name":"Baruffi, Federico","orcid":"0000-0002-1799-7906","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guido","key":"tosellopau","last":"Tosello","locid":"3e8b054c-7043-42aa-8b6c-57177bd403b6","name":"Tosello, Guido","orcid":"0000-0002-5071-7830","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefania","key":"gasparinpau","last":"Gasparin","name":"Gasparin, Stefania","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Massimiliano","key":"annonipau","last":"Annoni","name":"Annoni, Massimiliano","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"parentipau","last":"Parenti","name":"Parenti, Paolo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene","key":"sobieckipau","last":"Sobiecki","locid":"61422ae6-8f15-4544-bfc4-4d4aa5669512","name":"Sobiecki, Rene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Nørgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"04ac6d96-df2f-44fb-a89e-7e76b5e460de","name":"Hansen, Hans Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7829-6962","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 16th International Conference of the European Society for Precision Engineering and Nanotechnology, EUSPEN 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-edb53368-eefc-47ef-b225-825134e20d97"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Performance verification of focus variation and confocal microscopes measuring tilted ultra-fine surfaces","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-375680","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery (RYGB) is an effective treatment of morbid obesity, with positive effects on obesity-related complications. The treatment is associated with bone loss, which in turn might increase fracture risk. The aim of this study was to evaluate changes in bone mineral density (BMD) and bone architecture assessed using dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DXA) and high-resolution peripheral quantitative computed tomography (HR-pQCT), 6 and 12 months after RYGB, and correlate them to changes in selected biochemical markers. A prospective cohort study included 25 morbidly obese patients (10 males, 15 females). Patients were examined with DXA of the hip and spine, HR-pQCT of radius and tibia, and blood sampling before and 6 and 12 months after RYGB. Patients lost in average 33.5 ± 12.1 kg (25.8 ± 8.5 %) in 12 months. In tibia, we found significant loss of total, cortical and trabecular volumetric BMD after 12 months (all p < 0.001). Microarchitectural changes involved lower trabecular number, increased trabecular separation, and network inhomogeneity along with thinning of the cortex. Estimated bone failure load was decreased after 12 months (p = 0.005). We found only minor changes in radius. Results demonstrate significant alterations of bone microarchitecture suggesting an accelerated endosteal resorption along with disintegration of the trabecular structure which resulted in a loss of estimated bone strength in tibia. Such changes may underlie the recently reported increased risk of fracture in bariatric patients after surgery. We only observed bone structural changes in the weight-bearing bone, which indicates that mechanical un-loading is the primary mediator.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Katrine Diemer","Hanson, Stine","Hansen, Stinus","Brixen, Kim","Gram, Jeppe","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Støving, René Klinkby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-613441"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone structural changes and estimated strength after gastric bypass surgery evaluated by hr pqct","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84957846605","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-613441","identifier":[{"id":"26661530","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84957846605","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-8c66b11c-b376-49e3-9eb2-8ae7823db426"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-27E20ECF51F97B352D556E34784F11CC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"n