{"abstract":"The mass-replication nature of the process calls for fast monitoring of process parameters and product geometrical characteristics. In this direction, the present study addresses the possibility to develop a micro manufacturing platform for micro assembly injection moulding with real-time process/product monitoring and metrology. The study represent a new concept yet to be developed with great potential for high precision mass-manufacturing of highly functional 3D multi-material (i.e. including metal/soft polymer) micro components. The activities related to HINMICO project objectives proves the importance of using tool geometries as reference calibrated artefacts to establish effective process technology development and control. The results allow identifying the correct process windows for optimal part quality reducing product dimensional variation in the micrometer dimensional range. The proposed metrological approach enabled to quantify product dimensional variations based on process and tooling capabilities.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Calaon, Matteo","Tosello, Guido","Elsborg, René","Hansen, Hans Nørgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-345564"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-15","place":"Lyngby, dk","start":"2016-09-13","title":"4M/IWMF2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high accuracy and precision micro injection moulding of thermoplastic elastomers micro ring production","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126857439/High_accuracy_and_precision_micro_injection_moulding_of_TPE_micro_ring_production.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-345564","ids":["dtu-8983a6f4-19c5-41ac-aa9e-e4f989abc1c4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-13201F15D4887415B29B405529C49FFA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126857439/High_accuracy_and_precision_micro_injection_moulding_of_TPE_micro_ring_production.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Ortofon A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"calaonpau","last":"Calaon","locid":"9f1e0434-7bf4-4d6e-ad77-063d5a641b87","name":"Calaon, Matteo","orcid":"0000-0002-9437-9829","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guido","key":"tosellopau","last":"Tosello","locid":"3e8b054c-7043-42aa-8b6c-57177bd403b6","name":"Tosello, Guido","orcid":"0000-0002-5071-7830","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"elsborgpau","last":"Elsborg","name":"Elsborg, René","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Nørgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"04ac6d96-df2f-44fb-a89e-7e76b5e460de","name":"Hansen, Hans Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7829-6962","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3850/978-981-11-0749-8_730","isbn":["9789811107498"],"pages":"23-26","publisher":"Research Publishing Services","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of 11th International Conference on Multi-Material Micro Manufacture","title":"4M/IWMF2016 Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","ortofon a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8983a6f4-19c5-41ac-aa9e-e4f989abc1c4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"High accuracy and precision micro injection moulding of thermoplastic elastomers micro ring production","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-345564","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Suggestions of overprescribing of proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) for long-term treatment in primary care have been raised. This study aims to analyse associations between general practice characteristics and initiating long-term treatment with PPIs. Methods: A nationwide register-based cohort study of patients over 18 years redeeming first-time prescription for PPI issued by a general practitioner in Denmark in 2011. Patients redeeming more than 60 defined daily doses (DDDs) of PPI within six months were defined first-time long-term users. Detailed information on diagnoses, concomitant drug use and sociodemography of the cohort was extracted. Practice characteristics such as age and gender of the general practitioner (GP), number of GPs, number of patients per GP, geographical location and training practice status were linked to each PPI user. Logistic regression analysis was used to determine associations between practice characteristics and initiating long-term prescribing of PPIs. Results: We identified 90 556 first-time users of PPI. A total of 30 963 (34.2 %) met criteria for long-term use at six months follow-up. GPs over 65 years had significantly higher odds of long-term prescribing (OR 1.32, CI 1.16-1.50), when compared to younger GPs (<45 years). Furthermore, feMale GPs were significantly less likely to prescribe long-term treatment with PPIs (OR 0.87, CI 0.81-0.93) compared to Male GPs. Conclusions: Practice characteristics such as GP age and gender could explain some of the observed variation in prescribing patterns for PPIs. This variation may indicate a potential for enhancing rational prescribing of PPIs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Haastrup, Peter","Rasmussen, Sanne","Hansen, Jane Møller","Christensen, René dePont","Søndergaard, Jens","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-596307"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Age Factors","Aged","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Drug Prescriptions statistics numerical data","Female","General Practice statistics numerical data","General Practitioners statistics numerical data","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Practice Patterns Physicians statistics numerical data","Prescribing patterns","Proton Pump Inhibitors therapeutic use","Proton pump inhibitors","Registries","Sex Factors","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"general practice variation when initiating long term prescribing of proton pump inhibitors a nationwide cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12875-016-0460-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-596307","identifier":[{"id":"85008392248","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27233634","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4884377","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-509e2c35-cfa0-4583-8115-e272c893a444"],"keyword":["Age Factors","Aged","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Drug Prescriptions/statistics & numerical data","Female","General Practice/statistics & numerical data","General Practitioners/statistics & numerical data","General practice variation","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Practice Patterns, Physicians'/statistics & numerical data","Prescribing patterns","Proton Pump Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Proton pump inhibitors","Registries","Sex Factors","Time Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-00B64444F42924DB8619191628871A21"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12875-016-0460-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121991477/General_practice_variation_when_initiating_long_term_prescribing_of_proton_pump_inhibitors.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","locid":"03dbf65e-75df-4540-b951-0d05e7a60cde","name":"Haastrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7265-743X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sanne","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"145204b6-2eb0-4fc4-9489-9158d6bd5a89","name":"Rasmussen, Sanne","orcid":"0000-0002-6965-3347","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane Møller","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c2ebd30a-89b3-4305-b8d3-9abd10323385","name":"Hansen, Jane Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René dePont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27233634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12875-016-0460-9","issn":["14712296"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Family Practice","paperid":"57","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Family Practice","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85008392248"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-509e2c35-cfa0-4583-8115-e272c893a444"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"General practice variation when initiating long-term prescribing of proton pump inhibitors: a nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-596307","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Studies of the increasing use of proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) have mainly focused on prevalent long-term use and associations with gastrointestinal morbidity and comedication. Little is known about non-medical characteristics of first-time users of PPI, and predictors of initiating long-term use of PPIs. Aims: To describe medical and non-medical characteristics of first-time PPI users during a 10-year period and to analyse predictors of initiation of long-term use (>60 defined daily doses (DDDs) within 6 months) of PPIs. Methods: A nationwide cohort study of first-time users of PPI. Data were collected from Danish national registers. Individuals redeeming their first prescription for a PPI (omeprazole, lansoprazole, pantoprazole, rabeprazole, esomeprazole) in 2001 and 2011 were identified. Redemption of more than 60 DDDs of PPI within 6 months defined long-term use. Logistic regression models were used to determine the associations between previous diagnoses, comedication and socio-economic characteristics and initiation of long-term use of PPIs in 2011. Results: From 2001 to 2011 incidence of first-time users increased with an incidence rate ratio of 1.53 and mean quantity of PPI redeemed at first prescription increased by 44.6%. In 2011 a total of 37.6% redeemed >60 DDDs within 6 months, and 96% of the long-term users did not have a diagnosis registered which indicated treatment. New onset long-term use was significantly associated with low income and low educational level when adjusting for other predisposing variables. Conclusions: Proton pump inhibitor treatment is increasingly initiated with larger quantities prescribed for indications that are unidentifiable from the registers. Morbidity and comedication seem to be the strongest predictors of new onset long-term use of PPIs. However, there is also an independent social gradient.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Haastrup, Peter","Paulsen, Maja Skov","Christensen, René dePont","Søndergaard, Jens","Hansen, Jane Møller","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-640024"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["2 Pyridinylmethylsulfinylbenzimidazoles therapeutic use","Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cohort Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Omeprazole therapeutic use","Pantoprazole","Proton Pump Inhibitors therapeutic use","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"medical and non medical predictors of initiating long term use of proton pump inhibitors a nationwide cohort study of first time users during a 000000000010 year period","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84977629768","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-640024","identifier":[{"id":"84977629768","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27137875","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-e9576e4a-c5b6-48b9-9583-51c0d6fdd2dd"],"keyword":["2-Pyridinylmethylsulfinylbenzimidazoles/therapeutic use","Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cohort Studies","Esomeprazole/therapeutic use","Female","Humans","Lansoprazole/therapeutic use","Male","Middle Aged","Omeprazole/therapeutic use","Pantoprazole","Proton Pump Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Rabeprazole/therapeutic use","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3831C8942E83E58FE2F5ABFDB9CD467A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","locid":"03dbf65e-75df-4540-b951-0d05e7a60cde","name":"Haastrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7265-743X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Skov","key":"paulsenpau","last":"Paulsen","locid":"7288551b-43b2-4400-bdc3-b78ad9c0ccc3","name":"Paulsen, Maja Skov","orcid":"0000-0003-0360-0039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René dePont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane Møller","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"c2ebd30a-89b3-4305-b8d3-9abd10323385","name":"Hansen, Jane Møller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27137875"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apt.13649","issn":["02692813","09530673"],"issn_org":["02692813"],"issue":"1","journal":"Alimentary Pharmacology and Therapeutics","pages":"78-87","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Alimentary Pharmacology and Therapeutics","title_org":"Alimentary Pharmacology & Therapeutics","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84977629768"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e9576e4a-c5b6-48b9-9583-51c0d6fdd2dd"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Medical and non-medical predictors of initiating long-term use of proton pump inhibitors : a nationwide cohort study of first-time users during a 10-year period","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640024","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The use of a mentor mentee relation in the course of a not well known design programme in Bachelor of Applied Science will strengthen the establishment of the student’s professional identity, with the overall purpose of the student positioning themselves as a professional. The relation to the mentor is made through regular meetings where the mentee gradually positions himself professionally. This research addresses the student perspective and the students’ transition to become a part of the profession and to position themselves as professionals. The focus in this research is to facilitate the student’s job entry in the industry as opposed to professional mentoring within the industry where professionals mentor professionals for career development In conclusion this article is seeking to present an example of how a student becomes aware of a professional identity by being a legitimate peripheral participant in the run of the education. A modified version of Grounded theory represents the methodical approach as the collected empirical data has formed the overall basis for this project. The descriptive and evaluation codings give an indication of which elements are relevant in regards to the establishment of a professional identity for the student. The mentor mentee meetings is facilitated through a series of activities throughout the educational programme. The Activities arising from categories of practice, social relation and professional environment, which encapsulate the creation of the professional identity. The findings indicates that the three different mentee activities during the mentee mentor relation, helps the students positioning themselves as professional thereby creating their professional identity. The findings also shows that the students who engaged actively in a mentor mentee relation find it easier to navigate in the professional environment within the industry.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bennyson, René","Hansen, Birgitte Kjølner","Blond, Malene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-650459"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-09","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2016-09-08","title":"E&amp;PDE 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Mentor","Uddannelse professioner og erhverv"],"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"establishing a professional identity via mentoring in design programmes","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://epde.info/epde2016/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-650459","ids":["ucn-2854304e-98bd-4939-8222-db877e4e85ad"],"keyword":["Uddannelse, professioner og erhverv","mentor"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-A8F0F426A4F516076BF11F52780BE585"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Erhverv, Design- og Produktionsuddannelserne"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"bennysonpau","last":"Bennyson","locid":"5c893591-1c3c-40f9-b515-ac8e43c0af71","name":"Bennyson, René","orcid":"0000-0002-0481-7654","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte Kjølner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"531f46a6-8ae8-4f65-b84d-f332bc166adf","name":"Hansen, Birgitte Kjølner","orcid":"0000-0002-2213-2712","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"blondpau","last":"Blond","locid":"eb6f8ca3-20c4-43c8-b1cf-d81290482181","name":"Blond, Malene","orcid":"0000-0001-6295-027X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik","key":"bohemiapedh","last":"Bohemia","name":"Bohemia, Erik","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ahmed","key":"kovacevicpedh","last":"Kovacevic","name":"Kovacevic, Ahmed","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lyndon","key":"buckpedh","last":"Buck","name":"Buck, Lyndon","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"tollestruppedh","last":"Tollestrup","name":"Tollestrup, Christian","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kaare","key":"eriksenpedh","last":"Eriksen","name":"Eriksen, Kaare","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nis","key":"ovesenpedh","last":"Ovesen","name":"Ovesen, Nis","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781904670629"],"pages":"584-589","publisher":"The Design Society Institution of Engineering Designers","status":"p","subtitle":"Design Education: Collaboration and Cross-Disciplinarity, Aalborg, Denmark, 8th-9th September 2016","title":"DS 83: Proceedings of the 18th International Conference on Engineering and Product Design Education (E&amp;PDE16)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-2854304e-98bd-4939-8222-db877e4e85ad"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Establishing a Professional Identity via Mentoring in Design Programmes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-650459","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate the risk of virus-associated cancer in female arthritis patients ever treated with biological DMARDs (bDMARDs) compared with never bDMARD-treated patients and ever and never treated with bDMARD compared with the general population. METHODS: This was a cohort study that included 13 905 female patients with RA (72%), PsA (12%), AS (4%) or other arthritides (12%) identified in the DANBIO registry. Ever (n = 5647) and never (n = 10 331) bDMARD-treated patients were followed for virus-associated cancers during 2000-11 by linkage to the Danish Cancer Registry. Hazard ratios and standardized incidence ratios (SIRs) were calculated. RESULTS: In total, 24 and 32 virus-associated cancers were identified among ever and never bDMARD users, respectively (hazard ratio = 0.9, 95% CI: 0.7, 1.2). Oropharyngeal (n = 3, SIR = 4.0, 95% CI: 1.3, 12.4) and anal (n = 2, SIR = 2.5, 95% CI: 0.6, 10.0) cancer only occurred among bDMARD-treated patients. SIR was not increased for cervical cancer, either in ever or never bDMARD-treated patients. SIRs for Hodgkin's and non-Hodgkin's lymphomas were increased in never bDMARD-treated patients (SIR = 2.5, 95% CI: 1.5, 4.0). CONCLUSION: bDMARD therapy was not associated with an overall excess of virus-associated cancers in female arthritis patients. The observed increased occurrence of oropharyngeal cancer needs further investigation. Lymphoma incidence was increased in patients unexposed to bDMARD treatment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Cordtz, René","Mellemkjaer, Lene","Glintborg, Bente","Hetland, Merete Lund","Madsen, Ole Rintek","Jensen Hansen, Inger Marie","Dreyer, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-087.88-039889"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Adverse events","Aged","Antirheumatic Agents adverse effects","Arthritis Rheumatoid complications","Biological DMARD","Cancer","Cohort Studies","DMARD","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Human papilloma virus","Humans","Immunosuppressive Agents","Incidence","Journal Article","Middle Aged","Neoplasms chemically induced","Proportional Hazards Models","Registries","Rheumatoid arthritis","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of virus associated cancer in female arthritis patients treated with biological dmards a cohort study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84974824287","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-087.88-039889","identifier":[{"id":"84974824287","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26912584","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-06c277f3-37c1-48d1-9876-24e153033988","sdu-71e721d1-0813-4609-8601-488f15f314cc"],"keyword":["Adult","Adverse events","Aged","Antirheumatic Agents/adverse effects","Arthritis, Rheumatoid/complications","Biological DMARD","Biological Factors/adverse effects","Cancer","Cohort Studies","DMARD","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Human papilloma virus","Humans","Immunosuppressive agents","Incidence","Journal Article","Middle Aged","Neoplasms/chemically induced","Proportional Hazards Models","Registries","Rheumatoid arthritis","Risk Factors","Virus-associated cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-34D07D5E7FA00A2E5C3264ECC0043975"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Kræftens Bekæmpelse"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Medicine (Svendborg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"cordtzpau","last":"Cordtz","name":"Cordtz, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"mellemkjaerpau","last":"Mellemkjaer","name":"Mellemkjaer, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"mellemkjærpau","last":"Mellemkjær","name":"Mellemkjær, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"glintborgpau","last":"Glintborg","name":"Glintborg, Bente","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Merete Lund","key":"hetlandpau","last":"Hetland","locid":"3407b4a7-174d-43db-bae6-74e7f035a81f","name":"Hetland, Merete Lund","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Ole Rintek","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"69eac85e-ed5d-4571-86b1-7498674fffaf","name":"Madsen, Ole Rintek","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Inger Marie","key":"jensenhansenpau","last":"Jensen Hansen","locid":"e6350066-c71d-48a0-945e-259b7989d1c6","name":"Jensen Hansen, Inger Marie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Lene","key":"dreyerpau","last":"Dreyer","locid":"d9f655af-c3aa-4ec1-bfd7-c61f0cd51219","name":"Dreyer, Lene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26912584"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/rheumatology/kew012","issn":["14620324","14620332"],"issn_org":["14620324"],"issue":"6","journal":"Rheumatology","pages":"1017-1022","paperid":"kew012","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Rheumatology","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84974824287"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-06c277f3-37c1-48d1-9876-24e153033988","sdu-71e721d1-0813-4609-8601-488f15f314cc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Risk of virus-associated cancer in female arthritis patients treated with biological DMARDs-a cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.88-039889","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The Danish Blood Donor Study (DBDS) is a prospective, population-based study and biobank. Since 2010, 100,000 Danish blood donors have been included in the study. Prior to July 2015 all participating donors had to complete a paper-based questionnaire. Here we describe the establishment of a digital tablet-based questionnaire platform implemented in blood bank sites across Denmark. METHODS: The digital questionnaire was developed using the open source survey software tool LimeSurvey. The participants accesses the questionnaire online with a standard SSL encrypted HTTP connection using their personal civil registration numbers. The questionnaire is placed at a front-end web server and a collection server retrieves the completed questionnaires. Data from blood samples, register data, genetic data and verification of signed informed consent are then transferred to and merged with the questionnaire data in the DBDS database. RESULTS: The digital platform enables personalized questionnaires, presenting only questions relevant to the specific donor by hiding unneeded follow-up questions on screening question results. New versions of questionnaires are immediately available at all blood collection facilities when new projects are initiated. CONCLUSION: The digital platform is a faster, cost-effective and more flexible solution to collect valid data from participating donors compared to paper-based questionnaires. The overall system can be used around the world by the use of Internet connection, but the level of security depends on the sensitivity of the data to be collected.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Burgdorf, K S","Felsted, N","Mikkelsen, S","Nielsen, M H","Thørner, L W","Pedersen, O B","Sørensen, E","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Bruun, M T","Werge, T","Erikstrup, C","Hansen, T","Ullum, H"],"cuid":["S04-099.62-001118"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["Blood Donors","Denmark","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital questionnaire platform in the danish blood donor study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cmpb.2016.07.023","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-099.62-001118","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000383295600010","type":"wos"},{"id":"27586483","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84978943481","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-15bbbd65-5366-43c2-ab44-ae0208d17db2","au-bc81bc4f-1772-4714-ac01-62e28cbf04d6","ku-3d9fc472-eeec-4dc6-9f96-8a43511ba664","sdu-1f2412d2-a389-4740-a90e-3e0c5e9a1f36"],"keyword":["Blood Donors","Denmark","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-4CB2BA798C58C045DDE125366597994F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cmpb.2016.07.023","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/128917129/Digital_questionnaire_platform_in_the_Danish_Blood_Donor_Study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/265546288/1_s2.0_S0169260716301572_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"201