{"abstract":"Boron and hydrogen have a rich chemistry that has attracted a significant, but mainly academic, interest during the past century. However, research over the past decades has revealed new applications for metal boranes including their implementation as ‘energy materials’ and as neutron capture agents in cancer treatment. The energy applications involve the use of boron–hydrogen compounds as ion-conductors for batteries, as hydrogen storage materials, or even rocket fuels. The intensive research focus on metal borohydrides in the early 21st century has recently broadened to encompass higher metal boranes such as metal–B 10H 10's and B 12H 12's. This review summarizes the recent breakthroughs in the area of higher metal boranes in these last few years, in addition to highlighting core research from the mid-20th century.","author_count":5,"contributors":["R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","Paskevicius, Mark","Li, Haiwen","Akiba, Etsuo","Jensen, Torben René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-176836"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kyushu University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metal boranes progress and applications","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2015.12.003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-176836","identifier":[{"id":"84952066117","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-534eae55-204e-496e-9778-08232cbf6d59"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-978CD5FC0C79E315244644BF3F308BB3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2015.12.003","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Centre for Materials Crystallography (CMC)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"jp","key":"kyushu university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Kyushu University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne","key":"rshansenpau","last":"R. S. Hansen","locid":"95e2932e-526e-4795-b38a-7ab221f891ae","name":"R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"paskeviciuspau","last":"Paskevicius","locid":"e26eea7d-e55a-4989-80de-dfafd2146511","name":"Paskevicius, Mark","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Haiwen","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Haiwen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Etsuo","key":"akibapau","last":"Akiba","name":"Akiba, Etsuo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben René","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e0750478-df89-45bf-aa48-b6a86de93fa0","name":"Jensen, Torben René","orcid":"0000-0002-4278-3221","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ccr.2015.12.003","issn":["00108545","18733840"],"issn_org":["00108545"],"journal":"Coordination Chemistry Reviews","pages":"60-70","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Coordination Chemistry Reviews","volume":"323"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84952066117"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-534eae55-204e-496e-9778-08232cbf6d59"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Metal boranes: Progress and applications","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-176836","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Objectives To provide a short overview of fast-track video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) and to identify areas requiring further research. Design A literature search was made using key words including: fast-track, enhanced recovery, video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery, robot-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (RATS), robotic, thoracotomy, single-incision, uniportal, natural orifice transluminal endoscopic surgery (NOTES), chest tube, air-leak, digital drainage, pain management, analgesia, perioperative management, anaesthesia and non-intubated. References from articles were screened for further articles. Using abstracts, areas of interest for developing a fast-track protocol were selected. Results The minimally invasive approach can be divided into several surgical methods that need further research to establish superiority. The role of intubation has to be further examined as well as the role of chest drains. Multimodal analgesic treatment including preoperative methylprednisolone seems promising and requires further research. Conclusions The fast-track data from other procedures may support future development and improvement of fast-track VATS.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Holbek, Bo Laksafoss","Petersen, René Horsleben","Kehlet, Henrik","Jessen Hansen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477594"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast track video assisted thoracoscopic surgery future challenges","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-477594","identifier":[{"id":"84948755868","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26514281","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8cb9b048-e261-42d6-80af-68600352e4a9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D95DD9649AF2D0624BAFC546DA84DA54"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Bo Laksafoss","key":"holbekpau","last":"Holbek","name":"Holbek, Bo Laksafoss","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"jessenhansenpau","last":"Jessen Hansen","name":"Jessen Hansen, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26514281"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/14017431.2015.1114665","issn":["14017431"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Cardiovascular Journal","pages":"78-82","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Cardiovascular Journal","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84948755868"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8cb9b048-e261-42d6-80af-68600352e4a9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fast-track video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery : future challenges","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-477594","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"An example of how students who master taking the roles of respectively student and mentee fast track into the industry based on the ideas of legitimate peripheral participation and mentoring as opposed to a traditional approach within a curriculum.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bennyson, René","Hansen, Birgitte Kjølner","Blond, Malene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-651934"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-03","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2016-06-01","title":"2016 UIIN Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Students"],"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"walking the line in the attempt of catalyzing the student s professional identity through mentoring","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-651934","ids":["ucn-af6e135a-802f-46c1-a994-9e601c9443d4"],"keyword":["students"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-2B21FD58A8C8DBA1F9FBA06E8F7FB989"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Erhverv, Design- og Produktionsuddannelserne"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"bennysonpau","last":"Bennyson","locid":"5c893591-1c3c-40f9-b515-ac8e43c0af71","name":"Bennyson, René","orcid":"0000-0002-0481-7654","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte Kjølner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"531f46a6-8ae8-4f65-b84d-f332bc166adf","name":"Hansen, Birgitte Kjølner","orcid":"0000-0002-2213-2712","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"blondpau","last":"Blond","locid":"eb6f8ca3-20c4-43c8-b1cf-d81290482181","name":"Blond, Malene","orcid":"0000-0001-6295-027X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-af6e135a-802f-46c1-a994-9e601c9443d4"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Walking the line in the attempt of catalyzing the student’s professional identity through mentoring","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-651934","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The Danish Neuro-Oncology Registry (DNOR) is a nationwide clinical cancer database that has prospectively registered data on patients with gliomas since January 2009. The purpose of this study was to describe the establishment of the DNOR and further to evaluate the database completeness of patient registration and validity of data. METHODS: The completeness of the number of patients registered in the database was evaluated in the study period from January 2009 through December 2014 by comparing cases reported to the DNOR with the Danish National Patient Registry and the Danish Pathology Registry. The data validity of important clinical variables was evaluated by a random sample of 100 patients from the DNOR using the medical records as reference. RESULTS: A total of 2241 patients were registered in the DNOR by December 2014 with an overall patient completeness of 92 %, which increased during the study period (from 78 % in 2009 to 96 % in 2014). Medical records were available for all patients in the validity analyses. Most variables showed a high agreement proportion (56-100 %), with a fair to good chance-corrected agreement (k = 0.43-1.0). CONCLUSIONS: The completeness of patient registration was very high (92 %) and the validity of the most important patient data was good. The DNOR is a newly established national database, which is a reliable source for future scientific studies and clinical quality assessments among patients with gliomas.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Steinbjørn","Nielsen, Jan","Laursen, Rene Johannes","Rasmussen, Birthe Krogh","Nørgård, Bente Mertz","Gradel, Kim Oren","Guldberg, Rikke"],"cuid":["S02-098.35-007133"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Brain Neoplasms","Clinical quality indicators","Completeness","Database research","Glioma","Journal Article","Validity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish neuro oncology registry establishment completeness and validity","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13104-016-2233-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.35-007133","identifier":[{"id":"84984849079","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27576510","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5006621","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-93220519-31bb-4980-810c-90592b9947a6","sdu-26cff0a0-8e00-4e1c-b77b-a82cc95d489d"],"keyword":["Brain neoplasms","Clinical quality indicators","Completeness","Database research","Glioma","Journal Article","Validity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A6B9180B40138BEF3CD96449C1BDF091"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 3.0","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5006621/pdf/13104_2016_Article_2233.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13104-016-2233-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121340720/The_Danish_Neuro_Oncology_Registry_establishment_completeness_and_validity.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Neurosurgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["​Nordsjællands Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steinbjørn","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"83278fe8-4bec-48ef-b43e-22417e8f4623","name":"Hansen, Steinbjørn","orcid":"0000-0001-5651-6493","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"014149d9-906e-4c74-ac91-2ffd5cd77a49","name":"Nielsen, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-7634-6812","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"René J","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"0ab2e1c6-3018-44ee-b207-a30494b52f5b","name":"Laursen, Rene Johannes","name_org":"Laursen, René J","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Birthe Krogh","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Birthe Krogh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Mertz","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","locid":"3d41d6fb-8f1c-4899-9ebd-b72f88e3935d","name":"Nørgård, Bente Mertz","orcid":"0000-0002-9514-3033","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim Oren","key":"gradelpau","last":"Gradel","locid":"1d28d7bc-60bb-46f5-8143-bc6508387a8f","name":"Gradel, Kim Oren","orcid":"0000-0002-5611-2031","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Guldberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"971944ff-2c6b-4abc-9bb0-d914d8e42778","name":"Sørensen, Rikke Guldberg","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"guldbergpau","last":"Guldberg","name":"Guldberg, Rikke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27576510"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13104-016-2233-x","issn":["17560500"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Research Notes","paperid":"425","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Research Notes","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84984849079"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-93220519-31bb-4980-810c-90592b9947a6","sdu-26cff0a0-8e00-4e1c-b77b-a82cc95d489d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Danish Neuro-Oncology Registry : establishment, completeness and validity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.35-007133","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Chemotherapy- induced gastrointestinal (GI) toxicity is a common adverse effect of cancer treatment. We used preweaned piglets as models to test our hypothesis that the immunomodulatory and GI trophic effects of bovine colostrum would reduce the severity of GI complications associated with doxorubicin (DOX) treatment. Five-day-old pigs were administered DOX (1 × 100 mg/m 2) or an equivalent volume of saline (SAL) and either fed formula (DOX-Form, n a 9, or SALForm, n a 7) or bovine colostrum (DOX-Colos, n a 9, or SAL-Colos, n a7). Pigs were euthanized 5 days after initiation of chemotherapy to assess markers of small intestinal function and inflammation. All DOX-treated animals developed diarrhea, growth deficits, and leukopenia. However, the intestines of DOX-Colos pigs had lower intestinal permeability, longer intestinal villi with higher activities of brush border enzymes, and lower tissue IL-8 levels compared with DOXForm (all P< 0.05). DOX-Form pigs, but not DOX-Colos pigs, had significantly higher plasma C-reactive protein, compared with SALForm. Plasma citrulline was not affected by DOX treatment or diet. Thus a single dose of DOX induces intestinal toxicity in preweaned pigs and may lead to a systemic inflammatory response. The toxicity is affected by type of enteral nutrition with more pronounced GI toxicity when formula is fed compared with bovine colostrum. The results indicate that bovine colostrum may be a beneficial supplementary diet for children subjected to chemotherapy and subsequent intestinal toxicity.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Shen, R. L.","Pontoppidan, P. E.","Rathe, M.","Jiang, P.","Hansen, C. F.","Buddington, R. K.","Heegaard, Peter M. H.","Müller, K.","Sangild, P. T."],"cuid":["S03-099.68-036032"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Memphis"],"keyword":["Animals","Animals Newborn","Antibiotics Antineoplastic","Bovine colostrum","C Reactive Protein metabolism","Cattle","Chemotherapy induced mucositis","Colostrum metabolism","Disease Models Animal","Doxorubicin","Enteral Nutrition","Enteral Nutrition adverse effects","Female","Humans","Infant Newborn","Inflammation Mediators blood","Interleukin 8 metabolism","Intestinal Mucosa metabolism","Intestinal toxicity","Journal Article","Male","Milk","Mucositis chemically induced","Nutritional Status","Permeability","Sus scrofa","Weight Gain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"milk diets influence doxorubicin induced intestinal toxicity in piglets","src":["dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/125615715/Document_3718096_29945.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.68-036032","identifier":[{"id":"84984633377","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27445347","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-969a523e-503d-44c0-99c1-6c5567455ea6","ku-6f61b262-6b2d-4a39-8125-11e3c5fd578c","sdu-57421291-aa54-4260-9d2a-3de4a6c03030"],"keyword":["Animals","Animals, Newborn","Antibiotics, Antineoplastic","C-Reactive Protein/metabolism","Cattle","Colostrum/metabolism","Disease Models, Animal","Doxorubicin","Enteral Nutrition/adverse effects","Female","Humans","Infant Formula/toxicity","Infant, Newborn","Inflammation Mediators/blood","Interleukin-8/metabolism","Intestinal Mucosa/metabolism","Intestine, Small/metabolism","Journal Article","Male","Microvilli/enzymology","Mucositis/chemically induced","Nutritional Status","Permeability","Sus 