title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949034887"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fe8a605b-7de1-4675-aca2-7eb698adc260"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"microRNA-17 Is the Most Up-Regulated Member of the miR-17-92 Cluster during Early Colon Cancer Evolution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-646108","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"An ever increasing share of embedded systems is powered by rechargeable batteries. These batteries deteriorate with the number of charge/discharge cycles they are subjected to, the so-called cycle life. In this paper, we propose the wear score function to compare and evaluate the relative impact of usage (charge and discharge) profiles on cycle life. The wear score function can not only be used to rank different usage profiles, these rankings can also be used as a criterion for optimizing the overall lifetime of a battery-powered system. We perform such an optimization on a nano-satellite case study provided by the company GomSpace. The scheduling of the system is modelled as a network of (stochastic) weighted timed games. In a stochastic setting, exact optimization is very expensive. However, the recently introduced Uppaal Stratego tool combines symbolic synthesis with statistical model checking and reinforcement learning to synthesize near-optimal scheduling strategies subject to possible hard timing-constaints. We use this to study the trade-off between optimal short-term dynamic payload selection and the operational life of the satellite.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","Haverkort, Boudewijn","Jongerden, Marijn","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-057615"],"event":{"acronym":"FORMATS","end":"2015-09-04","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2015-09-02","title":"International Conference, FORMATS 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Twente"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a score function for optimizing the cycle life of battery powered embedded systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007%2F978-3-319-22975-1_20","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-057615","identifier":[{"id":"84944673978","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000363677200020","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-19d15fec-5de0-4d78-b55b-7c6519aec170"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D2C5E3E2176A490B01A46321FD38AB9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of twente","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Twente","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Ramsgaard","key":"wognsenpau","last":"Wognsen","locid":"5ff613ea-45c3-4201-924b-67606a027557","name":"Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Boudewijn","key":"haverkortpau","last":"Haverkort","name":"Haverkort, Boudewijn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"jongerdenpau","last":"Jongerden","name":"Jongerden, Marijn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Guldstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-22975-1_20","eisbn":["9783319229751"],"isbn":["9783319229744"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"305-320","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"13th International Conference, FORMATS 2015, Madrid, Spain, September 2-4, 2015, Proceedings","title":"Formal Modeling and Analysis of Timed Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944673978"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-19d15fec-5de0-4d78-b55b-7c6519aec170"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Score Function for Optimizing the Cycle-Life of Battery-Powered Embedded Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-057615","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"New sample environments and techniques specifically designed for in situ powder X-ray diffraction studies up to 1000 bar (1 bar = 105 Pa) gas pressure are reported and discussed. The cells can be utilized for multiple purposes in a range of research fields. Specifically, investigations of gas–solid reactions and sample handling under inert conditions are undertaken here. Sample containers allowing the introduction of gas from one or both ends are considered, enabling the possibility of flow-through studies. Various containment materials are evaluated, e.g. capillaries of single-crystal sapphire (Al2O3), quartz glass (SiO2), stainless steel (S316) and glassy carbon (Sigradur K), and burst pressures are calculated and tested for the different tube materials. In these studies, high hydrogen pressure is generated with a metal hydride hydrogen compressor mounted in a closed system, which allows reuse of the hydrogen gas. The advantages and design considerations of the in situ cells are discussed and their usage is illustrated by a case study.","author_count":12,"contributors":["R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","Møller, Kasper Trans","Paskevicius, Mark","Dippel, Ann-Christin","Walter, Peter","Webb, Colin James","Pistidda, Claudio","Bergemann, Nils","Dornheim, Martin","Klassen, Thomas","Jørgensen, Jens-Erik","Jensen, Torben René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-139933"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Griffith University Queensland","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"em in situ em x ray diffraction environments for high pressure reactions","src":["au"],"src-code":["D