Seyd Payam","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben René","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e0750478-df89-45bf-aa48-b6a86de93fa0","name":"Jensen, Torben René","orcid":"0000-0002-4278-3221","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a4c0d933-6bcf-455c-8e3c-cf9ca1cb511a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Metal borohydrides for hydrogen storage; synthesis and characterization","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-223214","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Dataflow formalisms are widely used for modeling and analyzing streaming applications. An important distinction is between static and dynamic formalisms, the latter allowing for the workload to change on-the-fly. The recently introduced finite-state machine based scenario aware dataflow (FSM-SADF) is a dynamic dataflow formalism that increases the expressiveness of the static synchronous dataflow (SDF) formalism, by allowing finite-state control, while to a large extent retaining its designtime analyzability. This paper reports on the translation of the FSM-SADF formalism to UPPAAL timed automata that enables a more general verification than currently supported by existing tools. We base our translation on a compositional approach where the input FSM-SADF model is represented as a parallel composition of its integral components modeled as automata. Thereafter, we show how to model check quantitative and qualitative properties both supported and not supported by the existing tools. We demonstrate our approach on a realistic case study from the multimedia domain.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Skelin, Mladen","Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","Olesen, Mads Chr.","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-075984"],"event":{"acronym":"SIES","end":"2015-06-10","place":"Siegen, de","start":"2015-06-08","title":"10th IEEE International Symposium on Industrial Embedded Systems, SIES 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Automata","Computational modeling","Detectors","Kernel","Presses","Semantics","Switches"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model checking of finite state machine based scenario aware dataflow using timed automata","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/articleDetails.jsp?arnumber=7185065","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-075984","identifier":[{"id":"84959457556","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-596ff1f9-313e-44f5-8999-e2d05ed5b612"],"keyword":["Automata","Computational modeling","Detectors","Kernel","Presses","Semantics","Switches"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3153D72E623C5D9E517D1D51823D0DDA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mladen","key":"skelinpau","last":"Skelin","name":"Skelin, Mladen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Ramsgaard","key":"wognsenpau","last":"Wognsen","locid":"5ff613ea-45c3-4201-924b-67606a027557","name":"Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Chr","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"c2e63d48-efc8-4e23-9dbf-509a20de7dc3","name":"Olesen, Mads Chr.","name_org":"Olesen, Mads Chr","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk