"","first":"Michael A","key":"hollingsworthpau","last":"Hollingsworth","name":"Hollingsworth, Michael A","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans H","key":"wandallpau","last":"Wandall","locid":"05df527d-13fd-4de9-9bb6-1a7b604bc6fa","name":"Wandall, Hans H","orcid":"0000-0003-0240-9232","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25118277"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1406619111","issn":["00278424","10916490"],"issn_org":["00278424"],"issue":"39","journal":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84907572385"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0d9da85b-48f3-4dd5-ab19-028cb5d48514"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Immature truncated O-glycophenotype of cancer directly induces oncogenic features","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-401551","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The GABA-mimetic anti-epileptic drug substance vigabatrin is used against infantile spasms. In vitro and in vivo experiments have shown that vigabatrin is transported via the proton coupled amino acid transporter (PAT1) mediating at least parts of the intestinal absorption of the drug. However, such evidence does not preclude the involvement of other transporters. The aim of the present study was, therefore, to investigate if vigabatrin interacts with taurine transport. The uptake of taurine was measured in intestinal human Caco-2 and canine MDCK cell monolayers in the absence or presence of amino acids such as GABA and vigabatrin. Vigabatrin inhibits the uptake of taurine in Caco-2 and MDCK cells to 34±3 and 53±2%, respectively, at a concentration of 30mM. In Caco-2 cells the uptake of vigabatrin under neutral pH conditions is concentration-dependent and saturable with a Km-value of 27mM (logKm is 1.43±0.09). In conclusion, the present study shows that vigabatrin was able to inhibit the uptake of taurine in intestinal and renal cell culture models. Furthermore, uptake of vigabatrin in Caco-2 cells under neutral pH conditions was concentration-dependent and saturable and suggesting that vigabatrin partly was transported via a taurine transporter, which is likely to be TauT.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Plum, Jakob","Nøhr, Martha Kampp","Hansen, Steen H","Holm, René","Nielsen, Carsten Uhd"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460327"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the anti epileptic drug substance vigabatrin inhibits taurine transport in intestinal and renal cell culture models","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpharm.2014.07.023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-460327","identifier":[{"id":"25062867","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84905168402","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6ff36abe-f1bb-43c0-994a-d6741753797f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A5F3B58C9FFB5CD208AB5728AC8FFBFA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijpharm.2014.07.023","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jakob Munk","key":"plumpau","last":"Plum","locid":"d2a8659d-2255-49f2-b9be-3d320e191fb3","name":"Plum, Jakob","name_org":"Plum, Jakob Munk","orcid":"0000-0002-8148-8129","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martha Kampp","key":"nøhrpau","last":"Nøhr","locid":"2a6fe9c4-f17f-4475-8d13-bb056ca1ae72","name":"Nøhr, Martha Kampp","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen H","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Steen H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, René","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten Uhd","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5162a14c-9a34-499b-ac59-8dd6ff9464fc","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25062867"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijpharm.2014.07.023","issn":["03785173","18733476"],"issn_org":["03785173"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","pages":"395-397","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Pharmaceutics","volume":"473"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905168402"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6ff36abe-f1bb-43c0-994a-d6741753797f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The anti-epileptic drug substance vigabatrin inhibits taurine transport in intestinal and renal cell culture models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-460327","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Obesity is associated with high bone mineral density (BMD), but whether obesity-related higher bone mass increases bone strength and thereby protect against fractures is uncertain. We estimated effects of obesity on bone microarchitecture and estimated strength in 36 patients (12 males and 24 females, age 25-56 years and BMI 33.2-57.6 kg/m(2)) matched with healthy controls (age 25-54 years and BMI 19.5-24.8 kg/m(2)) in regard to gender, menopausal status, age (±6 years) and height (±6 cm) using high resolution peripheral quantitative computed tomography and dual energy X-ray absorptiometry. In radius, total bone area and trabecular area were significantly higher in obese patients (both p < 0.04). In tibia, cortical area was larger in obese patients (p < 0.001) compared with controls. Total BMD was higher in tibia (p = 0.03) but not in radius. Trabecular integrity was strengthened in obese patients compared with controls in radius and tibia with higher trabecular number (p = 0.002 and p < 0.001) and lower trabecular spacing (p = 0.01 and p < 0.001). Finite element analysis estimated failure load (FL) was higher in tibia (p < 0.001), but not in radius in obese patients. FL was significantly lower per kg body weight in radius and tibia in obese patients compared with controls (p = 0.007 and p < 0.001). Furthermore, the ratios of FLs between groups were comparable in both sites. These findings suggest that mechanical loading is not the primary mediator of the effects of obesity on estimated FL, and suggest that bone strength adaptations in morbid obesity may be inadequate with respect to the increased mechanical demands.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andersen, Stine","Frederiksen, Katrine Diemer","Hansen, Stinus","Brixen, Kim","Gram, Jeppe","Støving, René Klinkby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-578560"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone structure and estimated bone strength in obese patients evaluated by high resolution peripheral quantitative computed tomography","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00223-014-9857-4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-578560","identifier":[{"id":"84902370768","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24736885","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-12e1f8ea-f0ce-4756-8574-6da2d0ee6551"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31914540D358806A3DCAB9FFCAE1FB72"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00223-014-9857-4","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Stine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Diemer","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Katrine Diemer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stinus","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"55fbaeae-64f0-4d31-b356-1ca840e82ed8","name":"Hansen, Stinus","orcid":"0000-0001-9486-0316","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"brixenpau","last":"Brixen","locid":"9f3c3042-e186-46aa-966a-d39df3e49bb0","name":"Brixen, Kim","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe","key":"grampau","last":"Gram","locid":"a5fd241d-294b-4fa7-82be-6492051b2406","name":"Gram, Jeppe","orcid":"0000-0003-2584-1132","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"René Klinkby","key":"støvingpau","last":"Støving","locid":"4aab81f6-352f-4c74-82a2-23589beb9fd5","name":"Støving, René Klinkby","orcid":"0000-0002-4255-5544","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24736885"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00223-014-9857-4","issn":["0171967X","14320827"],"issn_org":["14320827"],"issue":"1","journal":"Calcified Tissue International","pages":"19-28","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Calcified Tissue International","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902370768"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-12e1f8ea-f0ce-4756-8574-6da2d0ee6551"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bone Structure and Estimated Bone Strength in Obese Patients Evaluated by High-Resolution Peripheral Quantitative Computed Tomography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-578560","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The reliability of immunohistochemically-determined biomarkers using tissue microarrays (TMAs) of clinical specimens has long been open to question. Heterogeneity related to tumor biology might compromise determination of accurate biomarker expression in tumors, especially in small core biopsies. We evaluated the reliability of immunohistochemical staining scoring in small core biopsies using 11 biomarkers in non-small-cell lung cancer (NSCLC). MATERIALS AND METHODS: Four 1-mm tumor cores from 178 NSCLCs, 2 representing peripheral areas close to the border of normal lung tissue and 2 representing central areas, were examined. The biomarkers analyzed included p63, p40, cytokeratin 1/5/10/14, cytokeratin 7, thyroid transcription factor-1, napsin A, cyclin-D1, p53, Ki-67, integrin beta-1, and thymidylate synthase. RESULTS: Using a random intercept logistic regression model, immunohistochemical marker expression of TMAs had a moderate to high reliability measured using the intraclass correlation coefficient (0.67-0.99) between cores within the same tumor. Reliability was dependent on the selected biomarker, with lineage-specific biomarkers being less heterogeneously expressed than functional biomarkers. Expressions of most biomarkers showed no significant difference between central versus peripheral tumor cores. CONCLUSION: Our results demonstrated that biomarkers involved in clinical tumor classification (cell lineage markers) of NSCLC can be adequately assessed using 1 or 2 biopsy samples. However, the optimal number of cores required for biomarkers with functional properties varied from 1 to > 4 cores. The results indicate that the optimal number of biopsies required to compensate for potential biomarker heterogeneity should be determined individually for each biomarker used in clinical settings.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pøhl, Mette","Olsen, Karen Ege","Holst, René","Ditzel, Henrik","Hansen, Olfred"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-588403"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tissue microarrays in non small cell lung cancer reliability of immunohistochemically determined biomarkers","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cllc.2013.09.004","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-588403","identifier":[{"id":"24486059","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84898007321","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3514f5ac-be48-4eab-b9de-c57b4bebf961"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A5A3A5598CD4201243640B87C0630126"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cllc.2013.09.004","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Pathology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Medical Department"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"pøhlpau","last":"Pøhl","locid":"6e2a6d50-108e-4f53-85a1-313379d9a71b","name":"Pøhl, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen Ege","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d5fca320-8add-498f-84e5-80054d45cc66","name":"Olsen, Karen Ege","orcid":"0000-0002-6517-1172","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"4e7351b7-b587-4782-a080-beefad358b0b","name":"Holst, René","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Jørn","key":"ditzelpau","last":"Ditzel","locid":"f10637d7-ca3b-4956-a007-100f66737838","name":"Ditzel, Henrik","name_org":"Ditzel, Henrik Jørn","orcid":"0000-0003-3927-5135","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olfred","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3c005a52-6edc-4112-b87b-e353b545a354","name":"Hansen, Olfred","orcid":"0000-0003-0396-1424","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24486059"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cllc.2013.09.004","issn":["15257304","19380690"],"issn_org":["15257304"],"issue":"3","journal":"Clinical Lung Cancer","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Clinical Lung Cancer","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84898007321"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3514f5ac-be48-4eab-b9de-c57b4bebf961"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Tissue Microarrays in Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer: Reliability of Immunohistochemically-Determined Biomarkers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-588403","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The aim of the present study was to analyse the prognostic value of microRNA-21 (miRNA-21) in patients with stage II colon cancer aiming at a risk index for this group of patients. METHODS: A population-based cohort of 554 patients was included. MicroRNA-21 was analysed by qPCR based on tumour tissue. An index was created using the coefficients obtained from a collective multiple Cox regression. The entire procedure was cross-validated (10-fold). The performance of the index was quantified by time-dependent receiver operating characteristics curves. RESULTS: High miRNA-21 expression was associated with an unfavourable recurrence-free cancer-specific survival (RF-CSS), hazard ratio 1.35 (95% confidence interval, 1.03-1.76) (P=0.028). The generated RF-CSS index divided the traditional high-risk patients into subgroups with 5-year RF-CSS rates of 87% and 73%, respectively (P<0.001). The overall survival (OS) index identified three different subgroups (P<0.001). Cross-validated 5-year OS rates were 88%, 68%, and 50%, respectively. CONCLUSIONS: This population-based study supports miRNA-21 as an additional prognostic biomarker in patients with stage II colon cancer. Furthermore, the introduction of a risk index may guide the use of postoperative adjuvant treatment in a more appropriate way compared with current practice.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Torben Frøstrup","Kjær-Frifeldt, Sanne","Christensen, René dePont","Morgenthaler, S","Blondal, T","Lindebjerg, Jan","Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","Jakobsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-610705"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Biomarkers Tumor genetics","Colonic Neoplasms metabolism","Disease Free Survival","Female","Gene expression","Humans","Male","MicroRNAs genetics","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","ROC Curve","Real Time Polymerase Chain Reaction","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"redefining high risk patients with stage ii colon cancer by risk index and microrna 000000000021 results from a population based cohort","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/bjc.2014.409","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-610705","identifier":[{"id":"84910011677","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25051407","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4183843","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-831c9da5-b785-4cfb-b1cb-a13b569cc6f7"],"keyword":["Aged","Biomarkers, Tumor/genetics","Colonic Neoplasms/metabolism","Disease-Free Survival","Female","Gene Expression","Humans","Male","MicroRNAs/genetics","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","ROC Curve","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction","Risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D86BB468D2AB48640BBD2A306C39783A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/bjc.2014.409","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Vejle Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Exiqon A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"T F","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"72d28643-c440-4bbd-ad2b-eef0903a9438","name":"Hansen, Torben Frøstrup","name_org":"Hansen, T F","orcid":"0000-0001-7476-671X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"kjærfrifeldtpau","last":"Kjær-Frifeldt","locid":"6fdb727e-ac1e-4c28-b933-5510959bbc92","name":"Kjær-Frifeldt, Sanne","name_org":"Kjær-Frifeldt, S","orcid":"0009-0009-9594-5042","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R D","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","name_org":"Christensen, R D","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"morgenthalerpau","last":"Morgenthaler","name":"Morgenthaler, S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"T","key":"blondalpau","last":"Blondal","name":"Blondal, T","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"lindebjergpau","last":"Lindebjerg","locid":"5de10dbb-de45-4c38-8ed2-35bd614d5459","name":"Lindebjerg, Jan","name_org":"Lindebjerg, J","orcid":"0000-0002-2055-4241","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F B","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ac3af930-9550-4d18-9269-4dc0a6d649e5","name":"Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","name_org":"Sørensen, F B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"6c772581-e8fe-48bc-a932-1d1c5122c25a","name":"Jakobsen, Anders","name_org":"Jakobsen, A","orcid":"0000-0003-2110-2615","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25051407"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/bjc.2014.409","issn":["00070920","15321827"],"issn_org":["00070920"],"issue":"7","journal":"British Journal of Cancer","pages":"1285-1292","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Cancer","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84910011677"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","exiqon a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-831c9da5-b785-4cfb-b1cb-a13b569cc6f7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Redefining high-risk patients with stage II colon cancer by risk index and microRNA-21: results from a population-based cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-610705","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In order to fulfil the requirements of the EU Water Framework Directive nitrate load from agricultural areas to surface water in Denmark needs to be reduced by about 40%. The regulations imposed until now have been uniform, i.e. the same restrictions for all areas independent of the subsurface conditions. Studies have shown that on a national basis about 2/3 of the nitrate leaching from the root zone is reduced naturally, through denitrification, in the subsurface before reaching the streams. Therefore, it is more cost-effective to identify robust areas, where nitrate leaching through the root zone is reduced in the saturated zone before reaching the streams, and vulnerable areas, where no subsurface reduction takes place, and then only impose regulations/restrictions on the vulnerable areas. Distributed hydrological models can make predictions at grid scale, i.e. at much smaller scale than the entire catchment. However, as distributed models often do not include local scale hydrogeological heterogeneities, they are typically not able to make accurate predictions at scales smaller than they are calibrated. We present a framework for assessing nitrate reduction in the subsurface and for assessing at which spatial scales modelling tools have predictive capabilities. A new instrument has been developed for airborne geophysical measurements, Mini-SkyTEM, dedicated to identifying geological structures and heterogeneities with horizontal and lateral resolutions of 30–50 m and 2 m, respectively, in the upper 30 m. The geological heterogeneity and uncertainty are further analysed by use of the geostatistical software TProGS by generating stochastic geological realisations that are soft conditioned against the geophysical data. Finally, the flow paths within the catchment are simulated by use of the MIKE SHE hydrological modelling system for each of the geological models generated by TProGS and the prediction uncertainty is characterised by the variance between the predictions of the different models.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Refsgaard, Jens Christian","Auken, Esben","Bamberg, C.A.","Christensen, Britt Stenbøg Baun","Clausen, T.","Dalgaard, Esben Borch","Effersø, F.","Ernstsen, Vibeke","Gertz, F.","Hansen, A.L.","He, Xin","Jacobsen, Brian H.","Jensen, Karsten Høgh","Jørgensen, Flemming","Jørgensen, Lisbeth Flindt","Koch, J.","Nilsson, B.","Petersen, C.","De Schepper, G.","Schamper, Cyril Noel Clarence","Sørensen, K.I.","Therrien, R.","Thirup, C.","Viezzoli, Andrea"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-029443"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","Laval University","Universite Laval"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"OT":["Institut for Geoscience - Geoscience, C.F. Møllers Allé"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-RAM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-GV-GEUS","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-RAM","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nitrate reduction in geologically heterogeneous catchments a framework for assessing the scale of predictive capability of hydrological models","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2013.07.042","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-029443","identifier":[{"id":"84889601972","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23953482","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-e77d229d-bad0-4578-9333-ca836c47b43e","ku-c1c1fbc7-6100-48e9-83db-5d822e6ddecf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Me