{"abstract":"Variation in Surfactant Protein D (SP-D) is associated with lung function in tobacco smoke-induced chronic respiratory disease. We hypothesized that the same association exists in the general population and could be used to identify individuals sensitive to smoke-induced lung damage. The association between serum SP-D (sSP-D) and expiratory lung function was assessed in a cross-sectional design in a Danish twin population (N=1,512, 18-72 years old). The adjusted heritability estimates for expiratory lung function, associations between SP-D gene (SFTPD) single-nucleotide polymorphisms or haplotypes, and expiratory lung function were assessed using twin study methodology and mixed-effects models. Significant inverse associations were evident between sSP-D and the forced expiratory volume in 1 second and forced vital capacity in the presence of current tobacco smoking but not in non-smokers. The two SFTPD single-nucleotide polymorphisms, rs1923536 and rs721917, and haplotypes including these single-nucleotide polymorphisms or rs2243539, were inversely associated with expiratory lung function in interaction with smoking. In conclusion, SP-D is phenotypically and genetically associated with lung function measures in interaction with tobacco smoking. The obtained data suggest sSP-D as a candidate biomarker in risk assessments for subclinical tobacco smoke-induced lung damage. The data and derived conclusion warrant confirmation in a longitudinal population following chronic obstructive pulmonary disease initiation and development.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Johansson, Sofie L.","Tan, Qihua","Holst, René","Christiansen, Lene","Hansen, Niels C G","Højland, Allan Thomas","Wulf-Johansson, Helle","Schlosser, Anders","Titlestad, Ingrid L.","Vestbo, Jørgen","Holmskov, Uffe","Kyvik, Kirsten O.","Sorensen, Grith L."],"cuid":["S02-098.97-000580"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Biomarkers analysis","Cross Sectional Studies","Denmark","Female","Forced Expiratory Volume","Forced expiratory volume in one second","Genetic Association Studies","Haplotypes genetics","Humans","Lung Diseases chemically induced","Lung injury","Male","Middle Aged","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide genetics","Prognosis","Pulmonary Surfactants metabolism","Single nucleotide polymorphism","Single nucleotide polymorphisms","Smoking adverse effects","Surfactant protein D","Tobacco smoking","Vital Capacity","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surfactant protein d is a candidate biomarker for subclinical tobacco smoke induced lung damage","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajplung.00340.2013","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.97-000580","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000336597500008","type":"wos"},{"id":"24610936","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84900535443","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0afbc6f6-76f5-4b27-b1da-a971ec15ac10","sdu-c9671ffc-d384-44cf-8cd2-00c0f3605dd9"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Biomarkers/analysis","Cross-Sectional Studies","Denmark","Female","Forced Expiratory Volume","Forced expiratory volume in one second","Genetic Association Studies","Haplotypes/genetics","Humans","Lung Diseases/chemically induced","Lung injury","Male","Middle Aged","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide/genetics","Prognosis","Pulmonary Surfactant-Associated Protein D/genetics","Pulmonary Surfactants/metabolism","Single-nucleotide polymorphism","Single-nucleotide polymorphisms","Smoking/adverse effects","Surfactant protein D","Tobacco smoking","Vital Capacity","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-01D74FE661F5E1B13ED4823328B27BAE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajplung.00340.2013","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Cardiovascular and Renal Research Unit","University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Genetics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sofie","key":"lockjohanssonpau","last":"Lock Johansson","locid":"71fb7f1b-e46c-4333-8a12-3fb7ad0772c9","name":"Johansson, Sofie Lock","name_org":"L