{"abstract":"PURPOSE: This study aims to investigate possible associations between cancer survivors' comorbidity status and their (1) need for rehabilitation, (2) participation in rehabilitation activities and (3) unmet needs for rehabilitation in a 14-month period following date of diagnosis. METHODS: We performed a population-based cohort study including incident cancer patients diagnosed from 1 October 2007 to 30 September 2008 in two regions in Denmark. Fourteen months after diagnosis, participants completed a questionnaire measuring different aspects and dimensions of rehabilitation. Individual information on comorbidity was based on hospital contacts from 1994 and until diagnosis, subsequently classified according to the Charlson comorbidity index. Logistic regression analyses were used to explore the association between comorbidity and outcomes for rehabilitation. Analyses were conducted overall and stratified for gender, age and cancer type. RESULTS: A total of 3,439 patients responded (70 %). Comorbidity at all levels was statistically significant associated with a physical rehabilitation need, and moderate to severe comorbidity was statistically significant associated with a need in the emotional, family-oriented and financial areas as well as participation in physical-related rehabilitation activities. Stratified analyses showed that significant results in most cases were related to being older than 65 years or having colorectal or prostate cancer. CONCLUSIONS: Comorbidity at all levels was significantly associated with needs for physical rehabilitation. Moderate to severe comorbidity was further associated with other areas of need and participation in physical area activities. This should be taken into account when planning rehabilitation interventions for cancer survivors. Differences among subgroups could help target interventions and should be explored further.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Holm, Lise Vilstrup","Hansen, Dorte Gilså","Kragstrup, Jakob","Johansen, Christoffer","Christensen, Rene Depont","Vedsted, Peter","Søndergaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S03-088.75-024676"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Cohort Studies","Patient","Patients","semrap 2014 1"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of comorbidity on cancer patients rehabilitation needs participation in rehabilitation activities and unmet needs a population based cohort study","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-014-2188-1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-088.75-024676","identifier":[{"id":"24643775","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84905114497","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a3f44b25-4d01-4a4d-b85f-be5d3cbb65e6","ku-45f7ef1b-bac4-44b8-9673-641c6251e92a","sdu-3475ea1d-1663-409d-a3da-e31dc87c20bb"],"keyword":["Cohort Studies","PATIENT","Patients","semrap-2014-1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-1A0D7ED80BB9F6F5FB2738C400674518"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-014-2188-1","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, External Centres, Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of General Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Det Sundhedsvidenskabelige Fakultet AU (historisk)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Vilstrup","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"f7e88236-ef88-4946-9ba9-3fb30b221586","name":"Holm, Lise Vilstrup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Gilså","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2826791-eb97-4bca-8af7-448b0940e6e5","name":"Hansen, Dorte Gilså","orcid":"0000-0002-5946-9968","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jakob","key":"kragstruppau","last":"Kragstrup","locid":"d3150c49-08de-40a2-99d2-80c7045ede11","name":"Kragstrup, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-0197-454X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rene Depont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","name_org":"Christensen, Rene Depont","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vedstedpau","last":"Vedsted","locid":"bb00d9e7-866c-4f04-8e3b-a71c913c39b0","name":"Vedsted, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2113-5599","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24643775"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00520-014-2188-1","issn":["09414355","14337339"],"issn_org":["09414355"],"issue":"8","journal":"Supportive Care in Cancer","pages":"2095-2105","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Supportive Care in Cancer","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905114497"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a3f44b25-4d01-4a4d-b85f-be5d3cbb65e6","ku-45f7ef1b-bac4-44b8-9673-641c6251e92a","sdu-3475ea1d-1663-409d-a3da-e31dc87c20bb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Influence of comorbidity on cancer patients' rehabilitation needs, participation in rehabilitation activities and unmet needs : a population-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-088.75-024676","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"With the large, and rapidly increasing, number of smartphones based on the Android platform, combined with the open nature of the platform that allows “apps” to be downloaded and executed on the smartphone, misbehaving and malicious (malware) apps are set to become a serious problem. To counter this problem, automated tools for analysing and verifying apps are essential. Furthermore, to ensure high-fidelity of such tools, it is essential to formally specify both semantics and analyses. In this paper we present, to the best of our knowledge, the first formalisation of the complete Dalvik bytecode language including reflection features and the first formally specified control flow analysis for the language, including advanced control flow features such as dynamic dispatch, exceptions, and reflection. To determine which features to include in the formalisation and analysis, 1700 Android apps from the Google Play app market (formerly known as Android Market) were downloaded and examined.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","Karlsen, Henrik Søndberg","Olesen, Mads Chr.","Hansen, Rene Rydhof"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-062084"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formalisation and analysis of dalvik bytecode","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167642313003304","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-062084","identifier":[{"id":"84902267940","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000338597900003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-299ef8b6-4d24-4015-8be9-35ff88625f7c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3D9AF92EB5E867A138B6A11A680758F7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Ramsgaard","key":"wognsenpau","last":"Wognsen","locid":"5ff613ea-45c3-4201-924b-67606a027557","name":"Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Søndberg","key":"karlsenpau","last":"Karlsen","locid":"a25582be-a318-4202-b9ac-f9993ddba358","name":"Karlsen, Henrik Søndberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Chr.","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"c2e63d48-efc8-4e23-9dbf-509a20de7dc3","name":"Olesen, Mads Chr.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scico.2013.11.037","issn":["01676423","18727964"],"issn_org":["01676423"],"issue":"Part A","journal":"Science of Computer Programming","pages":"25-55","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Science of Computer Programming","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902267940"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-299ef8b6-4d24-4015-8be9-35ff88625f7c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Formalisation and analysis of Dalvik bytecode","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-062084","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Wireless systems such as satellites and sensor networks are often battery-powered. To operate optimally they must therefore take the performance properties of real batteries into account. Additionally, these systems, and therefore their batteries, are often exposed to loads with uncertain timings. Mixed criticality and soft real-time systems may accept deadline violations and therefore enable trade-offs and evaluation of performance by criteria such as the number of tasks that can be completed with a given battery. We model a task set in combination with the kinetic battery model as a stochastic hybrid system and study its performance under battery-aware scheduling strategies. We believe that this evaluation does not scale with current verification techniques for stochastic hybrid systems. Instead statistical model checking provides a viable alternative with statistical guarantees. Based on our model we also calculate an upper bound on the attainable number of task instances from a battery, and we provide a battery-aware scheduler that wastes no energy on instances that are not guaranteed to make their deadlines.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-082968"],"event":{"acronym":"ISoLA","end":"2014-10-11","place":"Corfu, gr","start":"2014-10-08","title":"6th International Symposium On Leveraging Applications of Formal Methods, Verification and Validation","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"battery aware scheduling of mixed criticality systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-662-45231-8_15","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-082968","identifier":[{"id":"84910635213","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000345509600015","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-7118c06a-a803-4599-b4f2-578608fa5dad"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E3EFE0537DE4DF1CC4F0D659DE43BF28"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed Systems and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Ramsgaard","key":"wognsenpau","last":"Wognsen","locid":"5ff613ea-45c3-4201-924b-67606a027557","name":"Wognsen, Erik Ramsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Guldstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tiziana","key":"margariapedh","last":"Margaria","name":"Margaria, Tiziana","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bernhard","key":"steffenpedh","last":"Steffen","name":"Steffen, Bernhard","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-45231-8_15","eisbn":["9783662452318"],"isbn":["9783662452301"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"208-222","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"6th International Symposium, ISoLA 2014, Imperial, Corfu, Greece, October 8-11, 2014, Proceedings, Part II","title":"Leveraging Applications of Formal Methods, Verification and Validation. Specialized Techniques and Applications","volume":"8803"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84910635213"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7118c06a-a803-4599-b4f2-578608fa5dad"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Battery-Aware Scheduling of Mixed Criticality Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-082968","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Møller, Kasper Trans","R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","Webb, Colin Jim","Jensen, Torben René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-183531"],"event":{"end":"2014-01-16","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2014-01-16","title":"Inano Annual Meeting 2014","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Griffith University Queensland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high pressure equipment for investigation of hydrogen storage materials","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-183531","ids":["au-5efe0cd5-25fe-4a3a-a5fc-62829f5f17de"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-51B87A0FA98DFAF7A652EA535B84E17A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Centre for Materials Crystallography (CMC)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, Langelandsgade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"griffith university queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Griffith University Queensland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper Trans","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"a0126e94-4bb1-46c4-9692-5269054851d7","name":"Møller, Kasper Trans","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne Rosenlund Søndertoft","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"95e2932e-526e-4795-b38a-7ab221f891ae","name":"R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","name_org":"Hansen, Bjarne Rosenlund Søndertoft","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Colin Jim","key":"webbpau","last":"Webb","name":"Webb, Colin Jim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben René","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e0750478-df89-45bf-aa48-b6a86de93fa0","name":"Jensen, Torben René","orcid":"0000-0002-4278-3221","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5efe0cd5-25fe-4a3a-a5fc-62829f5f17de"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"High-Pressure Equipment for Investigation of Hydrogen Storage Materials","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-183531","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Video-assisted thoracic surgery is gradually replacing conventional open thoracotomy as the method of choice for the treatment of early-stage non-small cell lung cancers, and thoracic surgical trainees must learn and master this technique. Simulation-based training could help trainees overcome the first part of the learning curve, but no virtual-reality simulators for thoracoscopy are commercially available. This study aimed to investigate whether training on a laparoscopic simulator enables trainees to perform a thoracoscopic lobectomy. METHODS: Twenty-eight surgical residents were randomized to either virtual-reality training on a nephrectomy module or traditional black-box simulator training. After a retention period they performed a thoracoscopic lobectomy on a porcine model and their performance was scored using a previously validated assessment tool. RESULTS: The groups did not differ in age or gender. All participants were able to complete the lobectomy. The performance of the black-box group was significantly faster during the test scenario than the virtual-reality group: 26.6 min (SD 6.7 min) versus 32.7 min (SD 7.5 min). No difference existed between the two groups when comparing bleeding and anatomical and non-anatomical errors. CONCLUSION: Simulation-based training and targeted instructions enabled the trainees to perform a simulated thoracoscopic lobectomy. Traditional black-box training was more effective than virtual-reality laparoscopy training. Thus, a dedicated simulator for thoracoscopy should be available before establishing systematic virtual-reality training programs for trainees in thoracic surgery.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Katrine","Ringsted, Charlotte","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Petersen, René Horsleben","Konge, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412990"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Animals","Carcinoma Non Small Cell Lung","Computer Assisted Instruction","Computer Simulation","Female","Humans","Internship and Residency","Learning Curve","Male","Pneumonectomy","Swine","Thoracic Surgery Video Assisted","Thoracoscopy","User Computer Interface"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulation based training for thoracoscopic lobectomy a randomized controlled trial virtual reality versus black box simulation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-412990","identifier":[{"id":"24442678","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84903634836","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-20cbefc2-fc4f-4f46-b78a-8c66cf81cb1f"],"keyword":["Adult","Animals","Carcinoma, Non-Small-Cell Lung","Computer Simulation","Computer-Assisted Instruction","Female","Humans","Internship and Residency","Learning Curve","Male","Pneumonectomy","Swine","Thoracic Surgery, Video-Assisted","Thoracoscopy","User-Computer Interface"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31EA4B307013C4ED1365404DC2CD09AD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Katrine","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Katrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"ringstedpau","last":"Ringsted","name":"Ringsted, Charlotte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars","key":"kongepau","last":"Konge","locid":"e1c287e3-4cd2-43d2-887d-f2f77fd5daf8","name":"Konge, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-1258-5822","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24442678"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00464-013-3392-7","issn":["09302794","14322218"],"issn_org":["09302794"],"issue":"6","journal":"Surgical Endoscopy","pages":"1821-1829","status":"p","title":"Surgical Endoscopy","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84903634836"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-20cbefc2-fc4f-4f46-b78a-8c66cf81cb1f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Simulation-based training for thoracoscopic lobectomy : a randomized controlled trial: virtual-reality versus black-box simulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-412990","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Vigabatrin is an anti-epileptic drug substance. The oral bioavailability of vigabatrin is high (60-70%), however, little is known about the mechanism(s) mediating the intestinal absorption. The aim of the present study was to identify which solute carrier(s) are involved in the absorption of vigabatrin in Caco-2 cells, a cell culture model of the small intestinal epithelium. The uptake and transepithelial flux of vigabatrin was measured using an LC-MS method for quantification. Transepithelial transport of vigabatrin was shown to be proton-dependent and polarized in the apical-to-basolateral (A-B) direction. The A-B flux of vigabatrin had a saturable component and a passive component, indicating the presence of a carrier system in parallel with a passive permeability. The Michaelis constant, Km, of the transepithelial A-B flux of vigabatrin was estimated to be 32.8±7.4mM (n=3-5), whereas the Km of the apical uptake was found to be 12.7±3.7mM (n=3). The carrier-mediated transepithelial A-B flux of vigabatrin accounted for 80-95% (50.0-1.0mM) of the total A-B flux. The transepithelial A-B flux (as well as apical uptake) of vigabatrin was significantly decreased upon addition of substrates or inhibitors of the human proton-coupled amino acid transporter (hPAT1) to the apical solution. The present study indicates that the transepithelial A-B flux of vigabatrin is mainly mediated by hPAT1 in Caco-2 cells at dose-relevant concentrations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nøhr, Martha Kampp","Hansen, Steen Honoré","Brodin, Birger","Holm, René","Nielsen, Carsten Uhd"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485144"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the absorptive flux of the anti epileptic drug substance vigabatrin is carrier mediated across caco 000000000002 cell monolayers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejps.2013.08.034","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-485144","identifier":[{"id":"24008184","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84884918413","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-99640c50-442b-4038-a229-20511a02c17e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ED88298505EC396D458CB8D732B2ECEE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejps.2013.08.034","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martha Kampp","key":"nøhrpau","last":"Nøhr","locid":"2a6fe9c4-f17f-4475-8d13-bb056ca1ae72","name":"Nøhr, Martha Kampp","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen Honoré","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"665ce563-c12a-4ba3-a5c3-45076aafc490","name":"Hansen, Steen Honoré","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birger","key":"brodinpau","last":"Brodin","locid":"5cbca78f-7ea7-45f1-bf9b-52b468d2aa84","name":"Brodin, Birger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"René","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, René","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten Uhd","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5162a14c-9a34-499b-ac59-8dd6ff9464fc","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24008184"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejps.2013.08.034","issn":["09280987","18790720"],"issn_org":["09280987"],"journal":"European Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","pages":"1-10","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884918413"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Lundbeck Pharma","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-99640c50-442b-4038-a229-20511a02c17e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The absorptive flux of the anti-epileptic drug substance vigabatrin is carrier-mediated across Caco-2 cell monolayers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-485144","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Eating disorders (EDs) comprise a variety of symptoms and have a profound impact on everyday life. They are associated with high morbidity and mortality. The objective of this study was to analyse published data on health-related quality of life (HRQoL) in EDs so as to compare the results to general population norm data and to investigate potential differences between ED diagnostic groups. A systematic review of the current literature was conducted using a keyword-based search in PubMed and PsychInfo. The search covered anorexia nervosa (AN), bulimia nervosa (BN), eating disorders not otherwise specified (EDNOS) and binge eating disorder (BED) and used the Medical Outcomes Study Short Form-36 Health Survey (SF-36) as a measure of HRQoL. Of the 102 citations identified, 85 abstracts were reviewed and seven studies were included in the meta-analysis. AN patients were included in five studies (n=227), BN in four studies (n=216), EDNOS in two studies (n=166) and BED in four studies (n=148). We tested for between-study variation and significant differences between the diagnostic groups. The results confirmed a significantly lower level of HRQoL in all EDs compared to a population mean. It was not possible to establish any differences between the diagnostic groups.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Winkler, Laura Vad","Christiansen, Erik","Lichtenstein, Mia Beck","Beck Hansen, Nina","Bilenberg, Niels","Støving, René Klinkby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-633844"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality of life in eating disorders a meta analysis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psychres.2014.05.002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-633844","identifier":[{"id":"24857566","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84902553561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d3bcc326-0445-4b95-9138-0d585e82a11d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5566D4D88E633809DC19A4C4CE6D1911"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psychres.2014.05.002","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Vad","key":"winklerpau","last":"Winkler","locid":"7b9b47e9-c528-4f6b-938a-a9d46af5c6fe","name":"Winkler, Laura Vad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"27110069-e170-4271-b2fe-80789cdad06f","name":"Christiansen, Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-3562-9506","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia Beck","key":"lichtensteinpau","last":"Lichtenstein","locid":"2b24df11-a1e7-4a80-8355-6f2f633eaca6","name":"Lichtenstein, Mia Beck","orcid":"0000-0002-7885-9187","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina Beck","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"9e8ddeb7-5e9f-4dd2-bff8-ea0b98c03257","name":"Beck Hansen, Nina","name_org":"Hansen, Nina Beck","orcid":"0000-0002-2962-3311","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"bilenbergpau",