{"abstract":"Writing correct C programs is well-known to be hard, not least due to the many low-level language features intrinsic to C. Writing secure C programs is even harder and, at times, seemingly impossible. To improve this situation the US CERT has developed and published a set of coding standards, the “CERT C Secure Coding Standard”, that (currently) enumerates 122 rules and 180 recommendations, with the aim of making C programs (more) secure. The large number of rules and recommendations makes automated tool support essential for certifying that a given system complies with the standard. In this paper, we report on ongoing work on adapting the Coccinelle bug-finder and program transformation tool, into a tool for analysing and certifying C programs according to, e.g., the CERT C Secure Coding Standard or the MISRA (the Motor Industry Software Reliability Association) C standard. We argue that such a tool must be highly adaptable and customisable to each software project as well as to the certification rules required by a given standard. Furthermore, we present current work on integrating Clang (the LLVM C front-end) as a program analysis component into Coccinelle. Program analysis information, e.g., from data-flow or pointer analysis, is necessary both for more precise compliance checking, i.e., with fewer false positives, and also for enabling more complete checking, i.e., with fewer false negatives, e.g., resulting from pointer aliasing.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Olesen, Mads Chr.","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Lawall, Julia L.","Palix, Nicolas Jean-Michel"],"cuid":["S02-099.69-007173"],"event":{"end":"2010-09-18","place":"Pisa, it","start":"2010-09-17","title":"4th International Workshop on Foundations and Techniques for OPEN SOURCE SOFTWARE CERTIFICATION (OpenCert 2010)","year":"2010"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Certification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coccinelle tool support for automated cert c secure coding standard certification","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/72448505/olesen_final_scp_opencert2010.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-099.69-007173","identifier":[{"id":"000338401600002","type":"wos"},{"id":"WOS:000338401600002","type":"wos"},{"id":"84901806730","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-94166dee-a3ad-4c39-93e1-3dbcaf6532b7","ku-e20e3e76-e263-4e62-85f0-72332eebbec5"],"keyword":["Automated tool support","CERT C Secure Coding","Certification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-92F67B7A8FA83F60A7678554064373F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/72448505/olesen_final_scp_opencert2010.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed Systems and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Datalogisk Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Chr.","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"c2e63d48-efc8-4e23-9dbf-509a20de7dc3","name":"Olesen, Mads Chr.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Julia","key":"lawallpau","last":"Lawall","locid":"5f9037c5-84e6-46b1-92d1-1632cb352c34","name":"Lawall, Julia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","country":"dk","first":"Nicolas Jean-Michel","key":"palixpau","last":"Palix","locid":"6d3fa37e-7fd9-4dd5-9542-7575fae75345","name":"Palix, Nicolas Jean-Michel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scico.2012.10.011","issn":["01676423","18727964"],"issn_org":["01676423"],"issue":"Part B","journal":"Science of Computer Programming","pages":"141-160","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Science of Computer Programming","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901806730"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-94166dee-a3ad-4c39-93e1-3dbcaf6532b7","ku-e20e3e76-e263-4e62-85f0-72332eebbec5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coccinelle : Tool support for automated CERT C Secure Coding Standard certification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.69-007173","year":"2014","yearsub":2015}
{"abstract":"Life-long regular endurance exercise is known to counteract the deterioration of cardiovascular and metabolic function and overall mortality. Yet it remains unknown if life-long regular endurance exercise can influence the connective tissue accumulation of advanced glycation endproducts (AGEs) that is associated with aging and lifestyle-related diseases. We therefore examined two groups of healthy elderly men: 15 master athletes (64 ± 4 years) who had been engaged in life-long endurance running and 12 old untrained (66 ± 4 years) together with two groups of healthy young men; ten young athletes matched for running distance (26 ± 4 years), and 12 young untrained (24 ± 3 years). AGE cross-links (pentosidine) of the patellar tendon were measured biochemically, and in the skin, it was assessed by a fluorometric method. In addition, we determined mechanical properties and microstructure of the patellar tendon. Life-long regular endurance runners (master athletes) had a 21 % lower AGE cross-link density compared to old untrained. Furthermore, both master athletes and young athletes displayed a thicker patellar tendon. These cross-sectional data suggest that life-long regular endurance running can partly counteract the aging process in connective tissue by reducing age-related accumulation of AGEs. This may not only benefit skin and tendon but also other long-lived protein tissues in the body. Furthermore, it appears that endurance running yields tendon tissue hypertrophy that may serve to lower the stress on the tendon and thereby reduce the risk of injury.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Couppé, Christian","Svensson, René B","Grosset, Jean-Francois","Kovanen, V","Nygaard, Rie Harboe","Olsen, MR","Larsen, JO","Praet, Stephan F E","Skovgaard, Dorthe","Hansen, Mette","Aagaard, P","Kjaer, M.","Magnusson, P"],"cuid":["S03-084.02-022925"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3