"key":"stadiepau","last":"Stadie","name":"Stadie, N.","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"charalambopouloupau","last":"Charalambopoulou","name":"Charalambopoulou, G.","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"stubospau","last":"Stubos","name":"Stubos, A.","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"steriotispau","last":"Steriotis","name":"Steriotis, T.","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-298c5939-d5a7-4dee-b49a-8a05d10a41ef"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"BOR4STORE: Fast, Reliable and Cost effective Boron Hydride based high capacity Solid state Hydrogen Storage Materials","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-153178","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A detailed investigation of the decomposition reactions and decay in the hydrogen storage capacity during repeated hydrogen release and uptake cycles for the reactive composite LiBH 4-Al (2:3) is presented. Furthermore, the influence of a titanium boride, TiB 2, additive is investigated. The study combines information from multiple techniques: in situ synchrotron radiation powder X-ray diffraction, Sieverts measurements, simultaneous thermogravimetric analysis, differential scanning calorimetry and mass spectroscopy, solid-state magic-angle spinning nuclear magnetic resonance (MAS NMR), and Raman spectroscopy. The decomposition of LiBH 4-Al results in the formation of LiAl, AlB 2, and Li 2B 12H 12 via several reactions and intermediate compounds. The TiB 2 additive appears to have a limited effect on the decomposition pathway of the samples, but seems to facilitate formation of intermediate species at lower temperatures compared to the sample without additive. Solid solutions of Li xAl 1-xB 2 or Al 1-xB 2 are observed during decomposition and from Rietveld refinement the composition of the solid solution is estimated to be Li 0.22Al 0.78B 2. The intercalation of Li in the AlB 2 structure is further investigated by 11B and 27Al MAS NMR spectra of the LiH-AlB 2 and AlB 2 samples (presented in Supporting Information). Hydrogen release and uptake for LiBH 4-Al reveals a significant loss in the hydrogen storage capacity, that is, after four cycles a capacity of about 45% remains, and after 10 cycles, the capacity is degraded to approximately 15% of the theoretically available hydrogen content. This capacity loss may be due to the formation of Li 2B 12H 12, as observed by 11B MAS NMR and Raman spectroscopy. Formation of Li 2B 12H 12 has previously been observed during the decomposition of LiBH 4, but it has not been reported earlier in the LiBH 4-Al (2:3) system.","author_count":7,"contributors":["R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","Ravnsbæk, Dorthe Bomholdt","Reed, D.","Book, D.","Gundlach, Carsten","Skibsted, Jørgen","Jensen, Torben René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-222874"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Torben René"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydrogen storage capacity loss in a libh sub 000000000004 sub al composite","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84876562041","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-222874","identifier":[{"id":"84876562041","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a432f77b-7811-4b7e-9d29-05065afffe17"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-48F33E1AE01A5F9EFE96304D9EA84FC7"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry - Centre for Materials Crystallography (CMC)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"B.R.S.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"95e2932e-526e-4795-b38a-7ab221f891ae","name":"R. S. Hansen, Bjarne","name_org":"Hansen, B.R.S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"D.B.","key":"ravnsbækpau","last":"Ravnsbæk","locid":"58830250-9dd7-43c2-977b-cb8f4b63c15e","name":"Ravnsbæk, Dorthe Bomholdt","name_org":"Ravnsbæk, D.B.","orcid":"0000-0002-8172-3985","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"reedpau","last":"Reed","name":"Reed, D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"bookpau","last":"Book","name":"Book, D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"gundlachpau","last":"Gundlach","name":"Gundlach, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"skibstedpau","last":"Skibsted","locid":"861c686f-c84f-4ad0-8581-c8e4fe22bdf9","name":"Skibsted, Jørgen","name_org":"Skibsted, J.","orcid":"0000-0003-1534-4466","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"T.R.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e0750478-df89-45bf-aa48-b6a86de93fa0","name":"Jensen, Torben René","name_org":"Jensen, T.R.","orcid":"0000-0002-4278-3221","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/jp312480h","issn":["19327447","19327455"],"issn_org":["19327447"],"issue":"15","journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","pages":"7423-7432","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","title_org":"The Journal of Physical Chemistry Part C","volume":"117"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84876562041"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a432f77b-7811-4b7e-9d29-05065afffe17"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hydrogen Storage Capacity Loss in a LiBH<sub>4</sub>-Al Composite","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-222874","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Purpose The anti-epileptic drug substance vigabatrin is used mainly for the treatment of infantile spasms. In spite of its hydrophilic nature (LogD7.0 ; -2.16), vigabatrin is readily absorbed after oral administration to humans. Vigabatrin has been shown in vitro to be a substrate of the intestinal proton coupled amino acid transporter PAT1, however the actual transport mechanisms involved in transepithelial absorption have not been clarified. The aim of the study was to investigate whether the transepithelial absorption of vigabatrin is mediated by PAT1 – in vitro as well as in vivo. Methods The absorption of vigabatrin was investigated using Caco-2 cell monolayers and Sprague Dawley rats as an in vitro and in vivo model, respectively. LC-MS or LC-MS/MS was applied for the quantification. Results The permeability of vigabatrin in Caco-2 cell monolayers was increased at apical pH 6.0 compared to pH 7.4. The transepithelial transport across Caco-2 cell monolayers was polarized in the lumen-to-blood direction in the presence of a proton gradient. The presence of PAT1-ligands significantly decreased the permeability of vigabatrin across Caco-2 cell monolayers. In Sprague Dawley rats the presence of PAT1-ligands altered the pharmacokinetic profile of vigabatrin with an apparent prolonged absorption of vigabatrin. Conclusions Transport of vigabatrin across Caco-2 cell monolayers was polarized in the lumen-to-blood directions, dependent on an acidic pH in the lumen compartment and inhibited by PAT1-ligands. This indicated that PAT1 was the apical entry step in the transepithelial transport pathway. This was supported by in vivo findings, showing that inhibition of PAT1 prolonged the absorption phase of vigabatrin. It is, hence, concluded that PAT1 is involved in vigabatrin transport both in vitro and in vivo.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nøhr, Martha Kampp","Juul, Rasmus Vestergaard","Hansen, Steen Honoré","Brodin, Birger","Holm, René","Kreilgaard, Mads","Nielsen, Carsten Uhd"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-449148"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vigabatrin absorption is mediated via the proton coupled amino acid transporter pat000000000001 in vitro and in vivo","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-449148","ids":["ku-5d0af4a8-50a2-4e67-84f5-219869011a46"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C9BBB79071C6D863BCC5232C36A5350B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martha Kampp","key":"nøhrpau","last":"Nøhr","locid":"2a6fe9c4-f17f-4475-8d13-bb056ca1ae72","name":"Nøhr, Martha Kampp","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Vestergaard","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"b4abf5ce-c7c6-443e-b694-fa3a86989e37","name":"Juul, Rasmus Vestergaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen Honore'","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"665ce563-c12a-4ba3-a5c3-45076aafc490","na