{"abstract":"Background. A cancer diagnosis may lead to psychosocial problems and physical symptoms that can be relieved during rehabilitation. The aim of this study was to analyse patient-perceived unmet needs of rehabilitation close to time of diagnosis, i.e. frequencies of unmet needs and the association with sociodemographic characteristics, cancer type and treatment. Material and methods. All adult residents of Denmark diagnosed with cancer for the first time from 1 May to 31 August 2010 were mailed a patient questionnaire two to five months following diagnosis. The study population was identified by use of national administrative registers. Data on rehabilitation, family situation, education, and cancer treatment were obtained from the questionnaire, while sex, birth year and cancer type were obtained from the Danish National Patient Registry. The association between each type of unmet needs and the variables sex, age, cancer diagnosis, treatment, education, cohabitation status, and children (living at home and away from home) was analysed using multiple logistic regression. Results. Among the 4346 participants (64.7%) unmet needs were reported with regard to talking to patients in the same situation (24.1%), counselling with a psychologist (21.4%), physical rehabilitation (18.8%), practical help (17.3%), and counselling related to work or education (14.8%). Differences were observed with regard to type of unmet needs, sociodemographic and clinical characteristics, but generally, young age, male sex, low educational level and living alone increased the adjusted odds ratios of unmet needs. Breast cancer and to some extent melanoma cancer decreased the odds. Conclusion. Unmet needs of rehabilitation are frequent during the early cancer trajectory and sociodemographic and clinical inequalities exist. The results support guideline recommendations of integration of cancer rehabilitation from the beginning of the cancer trajectory. Early interventions tailored to men, patients with low educational level, living alone, or treated with chemotherapy may help counterbalancing social and clinical inequalities in the long run.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Veloso, Astrid Gisèle","Sperling, Cecilie","Holm, Lise Vilstrup","Nicolaisen, Anne","Rottmann, Nina","Thayssen, Susanne","Christensen, René dePont","Lehmann Knudsen, Janne","Hansen, Dorte Gilså"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-579887"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Critical Pathways","Data Collection","Denmark","Female","Health Services Needs and Demand","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Needs Assessment","Neoplasms","Questionnaires","Time Factors","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unmet needs in cancer rehabilitation during the early cancer trajectory a nationwide patient survey","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/0284186X.2012.745648","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors wish to thank all patients for participating in the study, and all patients, clinicians and researchers for contribution to study design and development of the patient questionnaire. Furthermore, we wish to thank the Research Unit of General Practice, Aarhus University, for identification of study participants, data handling and analyses of selection. We also wish to thank Lise Stark for proofreading the manuscript.The survey ‘ The Experience of Cancer Patients during Diagnosis and Treatment, The Danish Cancer Society, 2011 ’ was funded by the Danish Cancer Society. The National Research Center of Cancer Rehabilitation is funded by the Danish Cancer Society."],"id":"S01-000.00-579887","identifier":[{"id":"84872587377","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23320774","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-17525c2f-7ebf-4e20-9ee4-6461750c61a7"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Critical Pathways","Data Collection","Denmark","Female","Health Services Needs and Demand","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Needs Assessment","Neoplasms","Questionnaires","Time Factors","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6807D81382FF02B2547DD4C9EB7041A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/0284186X.2012.745648","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid Gisèle","key":"velosopau","last":"Veloso","locid":"cfc6d162-efd6-43a9-b7ef-b6449cfed145","name":"Veloso, Astrid Gisèle","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie","key":"sperlingpau","last":"Sperling","name":"Sperling, Cecilie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Vilstrup","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"f7e88236-ef88-4946-9ba9-3fb30b221586","name":"Holm, Lise Vilstrup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"nicolaisenpau","last":"Nicolaisen","locid":"1c1d730b-acab-4f96-a824-90f2fcb3017d","name":"Nicolaisen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-5696-7144","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nina","key":"rottmannpau","last":"Rottmann","locid":"16e7c8cc-cee3-43aa-8651-e2a1414f2426","name":"Rottmann, Nina","orcid":"0000-0002-7262-6788","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"thayssenpau","last":"Thayssen","locid":"3697fd64-78e6-4732-b70a-3c8063c4675b","name":"Thayssen, Susanne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René Depont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","name_org":"Christensen, René Depont","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Janne","key":"lehmannknudsenpau","last":"Lehmann Knudsen","name":"Lehmann Knudsen, Janne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Gilså","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2826791-eb97-4bca-8af7-448b0940e6e5","name":"Hansen, Dorte Gilså","orcid":"0000-0002-5946-9968","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23320774"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/0284186x.2012.745648","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"372-381","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84872587377"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-17525c2f-7ebf-4e20-9ee4-6461750c61a7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Unmet needs in cancer rehabilitation during the early cancer trajectory - a nationwide patient survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-579887","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We present a rationale for a selection of tools that assist developers of hard real-time applications to verify that programs conform to a Java real-time profile and that platform-specific resource constraints are satisfied. These tools are specialised instances of more generic static analysis and model checking frameworks. The concepts are illustrated by two case studies, and the strengths and the limitations of the tools are discussed.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bøgholm, Thomas","Frost, Christian","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Jensen, Casper Svenning","Luckow, Kasper Søe","Ravn, Anders Peter","Søndergaard, Hans","Thomsen, Bent"],"cuid":["S02-093.94-665955"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["It","Java","Model checking","Real time systems","Safety critical","Static analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["VIA College"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards harnessing theories through tool support for hard real time java programming","src":["aau","via"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11334-012-0185-4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.94-665955","identifier":[{"id":"84874246998","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c7174447-92e3-4216-a396-78182932bba0","via-12211c2c-4d74-41b9-a111-4dfc6f1e15da"],"keyword":["Java","Model checking","Real-time systems","Safety-critical","Static analysis","it"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0CEE9811671DF483977C3CBA702271F1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11334-012-0185-4","version":"Other Version"