{"abstract":"Video-assisted thoracic surgery (VATS) is emerging as the standard surgical procedure for both minor and major oncologic lung surgery. Thoracic epidural analgesia (TEA) and paravertebral block (PVB) are established analgesic golden standards for open surgery such as thoracotomy; however there is no gold standard for regional analgesia for VATS. This systematic review aimed to assess different regional techniques in regards to effect on acute post-operative pain following VATS, with emphasis on VATS lobectomy. The systematic review of the PubMed, Cochrane Library and Embase databases yielded unique 1542 abstracts, 17 articles were included for qualitative assessment, of which 3 were studies on VATS lobectomy. The analgesic techniques included TEA, multilevel- and single PVB, paravertebral catheter, intercostal catheter, interpleural infusion and long thoracic nerve block. Overall the studies were heterogeneous with small numbers of participants. In comparative studies TEA and especially PVB showed some effect on pain scores, but were often compared to inferior analgesic treatment. Other techniques showed no unequivocal results. No clear gold standard for regional analgesia for VATS could be demonstrated, but a guide of factors to include in future studies on regional analgesia for VATS is presented.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Julia Steinthorsdottir, Kristin","Wildgaard, Lorna Elizabeth","Jessen Hansen, Henrik","Petersen, René Horsleben","Wildgaard, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-475489"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Pain","post operative","regional analgesia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regional analgesia for video assisted thoracic surgery a systematic review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ejcts/ezt525","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-475489","identifier":[{"id":"84900532873","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-892f1c0c-a381-4906-aa16-dfb5febaf070"],"keyword":["Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Pain","post-operative","regional analgesia","thoracoscopic, VATS, Video-assisted thoracic surgery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A521F01F47A99206AA8A524DA48F2142"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ejcts/ezt525","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ejcts.oxfordjournals.org/content/early/2013/11/27/ejcts.ezt525.abstract","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, External Centres, Det Kgl. Bibliotek - Universitetsbibliotekarens ledelsessekretariat","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication, Department of Information Studies (INF)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristin","key":"juliasteinthorsdottirkristinpau","last":"Julia Steinthorsdottir","name":"Julia Steinthorsdottir, Kristin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lorna","key":"wildgaardlornaelizabethpau","last":"Wildgaard","locid":"6e7eb004-dfd6-47b8-aca9-38cb594ceae4","name":"Wildgaard, Lorna Elizabeth","name_org":"Wildgaard, Lorna","orcid":"0000-0002-3900-5058","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"jessenhansenhenrikpau","last":"Jessen Hansen","name":"Jessen Hansen, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenrenéhorslebenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim","key":"wildgaardkimpau","last":"Wildgaard","name":"Wildgaard, Kim","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ejcts/ezt525","issn":["10107940","1873734X"],"issn_org":["10107940"],"journal":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cardio-Thoracic Surgery","title_org":"European journal of cardio-thoracic surgery : official journal of the European Association for Cardio-thoracic Surgery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84900532873"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-892f1c0c-a381-4906-aa16-dfb5febaf070"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Regional analgesia for video-assisted thoracic surgery – a systematic review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-475489","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Thousands of common single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) are weakly associated with schizophrenia. It is likely that subsets of disease-associated SNPs are associated with distinct heritable disease-associated phenotypes. Therefore, we examined the shared genetic susceptibility modulating schizophrenia and brain volume. METHODS: Odds ratios for genome-wide SNP data were calculated in the sample collected by the Psychiatric Genome-wide Association Study Consortium (8690 schizophrenia patients and 11,831 control subjects, excluding subjects from the present study). These were used to calculate individual polygenic schizophrenia (risk) scores in an independent sample of 152 schizophrenia patients and 142 healthy control subjects with available structural magnetic resonance imaging scans. RESULTS: In the entire group, the polygenic schizophrenia score was significantly associated with total brain volume (R(2)=.048, p=1.6×10(-4)) and white matter volume (R(2)=.051, p=8.6×10(-5)) equally in patients and control subjects. The number of (independent) SNPs that substantially influenced both disease risk and white matter (n=2020) was much smaller than the entire set of SNPs that modulated disease status (n=14,751). From the set of 2020 SNPs, a group of 186 SNPs showed most evidence for association with white matter volume and an explorative functional analysis showed that these SNPs were located in genes with neuronal functions. CONCLUSIONS: These results indicate that a relatively small subset of schizophrenia genetic risk variants is related to the (normal) development of white matter. This, in turn, suggests that disruptions in white matter growth increase the susceptibility to develop schizophrenia.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Terwisscha van Scheltinga, Afke F","Bakker, Steven C","van Haren, Neeltje E M","Derks, Eske M","Buizer-Voskamp, Jacobine E","Boos, Heleen B M","Cahn, Wiepke","Hulshoff Pol, Hilleke E","Ripke, Stephan","Ophoff, Roel A","Kahn, René S","Jakobsen, Klaus Damgaard","Hansen, Thomas","Ingason, Andrés","Duong, Linh","Rasmussen, Henrik Berg","Olsen, Line","Nordentoft, Merete","Jürgens, Gesche","Glenthøj, Birte","Wang, August G","Werge, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-507474"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["the Psychiatric Genome-wide Association Study Consortium"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic schizophrenia risk variants jointly modulate total brain and white matter volume","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2012.08.017","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-507474","identifier":[{"id":"84874542049","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23039932","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3573254","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-bf11d946-7c2c-4cc1-b7ef-8572869264b9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EC8285DC037907D263F0C814FDFF9631"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2012.08.017","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"},{"affno":2,"key":"the psychiatric genome wide association study consortium","name":"the Psychiatric Genome-wide Association Study Consortium","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Afke F","key":"terwisschavanscheltingapau","last":"Terwisscha van Scheltinga","name":"Terwisscha van Scheltinga, Afke F","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steven C","key":"bakkerpau","last":"Bakker","name":"Bakker, Steven C","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Neeltje E M","key":"vanharenpau","last":"van Haren","name":"van Haren, Neeltje E M","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eske M","key":"derkspau","last":"Derks","name":"Derks, Eske M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacobine E","key":"buizervoskamppau","last":"Buizer-Voskamp","name":"Buizer-Voskamp, Jacobine E","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Heleen B M","key":"boospau","last":"Boos","name":"Boos, Heleen B M","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wiepke","key":"cahnpau","last":"Cahn","name":"Cahn, Wiepke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hilleke E","key":"hulshoffpolpau","last":"Hulshoff Pol","name":"Hulshoff Pol, Hilleke E","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stephan","key":"ripkepau","last":"Ripke","name":"Ripke, Stephan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Roel A","key":"ophoffpau","last":"Ophoff","name":"Ophoff, Roel A","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"René S","key":"kahnpau","last":"Kahn","name":"Kahn, René S","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus Damgaard","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Klaus Damgaard","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Thomas","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrés","key":"ingasonpau","last":"Ingason","name":"Ingason, Andrés","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Linh","key":"duongpau","last":"Duong","name":"Duong, Linh","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Berg","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmu