{"abstract":"A mathematical model has been developed for the energy system of the hybrid street lighting making it possible to simulate a given configuration (solar panel performance data, size and orientation - wind turbine performance data, projected area and height - battery data) over a year in an urban environment of a given configuration based on measured wind/solar/temperature data from nearby meteorological station or other relevant weather data. The simulation can show if it is possible to cover the consumption by the light source over the year. The model can be used to evaluate both commercial hybrid systems and to dimension new systems for use in given environments where the weather data are known. Since weather and day/night length are varying a lot around the world the systems should be dimensioned very differently depending on the place of use. By using the simulation tool it is shown that it is possible to create a hybrid street lighting for an urban environment with a maximum of 2 floor height buildings which governs >70% of the luminaires in Copenhagen (the Capital of Denmark) fulfilling the requirements of 2.5 lux on the street over the year. Furthermore the tool is powerful to evaluate hybrid systems on the market (if all the technical data is known) for use in a given urban placement.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Poulsen, Peter Behrensdorff","Dam-Hansen, Carsten","Thorseth, Anders","Thorsteinsson, Sune","Lindén, Johannes","Hansen, Søren Stentoft","Ellermann, Stine","Bak, Christian","Skrzypinski, Witold Robert","Beller, Christina","Kock, Carsten Weber","Bühler, Fabian","Harboe, René Kirstein","Boesgaard, Per","Jensen, Tim","Søndergaard, Ole","Andresen, Christian","Fahlén, Morten","Maare, Thomas","Prestegaard, Hugo","Poulsen, Jan","Kremmer, Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341765"],"event":{"end":"2013-10-04","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2013-09-30","title":"28th European PV Solar Energy Conference and Exhibition (EU PVSEC 2013)","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Gate 21"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-ØR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-ØR","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"copenhybrid development of a co000000000002 neutral hybrid street lighting system for the danish municipalities illumination classes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/60023999/5DO.13.1.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-341765","ids":["dtu-7ca3b5dc-f28d-4b1a-a41d-633e361253ca"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B2D2508D6BD31A6C412A2CB134AED1F1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/60023999/5DO.13.1.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Diode Lasers and LED Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Factor3 A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":