"maarethomaspau","last":"Maare","name":"Maare, Thomas","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo","key":"prestegaardhugopau","last":"Prestegaard","name":"Prestegaard, Hugo","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"poulsenjanpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Jan","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"kremmersusannepau","last":"Kremmer","name":"Kremmer, Susanne","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 28th EU PVSEC"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","alfred priess a/s","factor3 a/s","henning larsen architects a/s","philips lighting a/s","Ørsted"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7ca3b5dc-f28d-4b1a-a41d-633e361253ca"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"CopenHybrid – Development of a CO2 Neutral Hybrid Street Lighting System for the Danish Municipalities’ Illumination Classes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-341765","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Bug-finding tools rely on specifications of what is correct or incorrect code. As it is difficult for a tool developer or user to anticipate all possible specifications, strategies for inferring specifications have been proposed. These strategies obtain probable specifications by observing common characteristics of code or execution traces, typically focusing on sequences of function calls. To counter the observed high rate of false positives, heuristics have been proposed for ranking or pruning the results. These heuristics, however, can result in false negatives, especially for rarely used functions. In this paper, we propose an alternate approach to specification inference, in which the user guides the inference process using patterns of code that reflect the user's understanding of the conventions and design of the targeted software project. We focus on specifications describing the correct usage of API functions, which we refer to as API protocols. Our approach builds on the Coccinelle program matching and transformation tool, which allows a user to construct patterns that reflect the structure of the code to be matched. We evaluate our approach on the source code of the Linux kernel, which defines a very large number of API functions with varying properties. Linux is also critical software, implying that fixing even bugs involving rarely used protocols is essential. In our experiments, we use our approach to find over 3000 potential API protocols, with an estimated false positive rate of under 15% and use these protocols to find over 360 bugs in the use of API functions. Copyright (c) 2012 John Wiley Sons, Ltd.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lawall, Julia","Brunel, Julien Pierre Manuel","Palix, Nicolas Jean-Michel","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Stuart, Henrik","Muller, Gilles"],"cuid":["S02-087.50-005673"],"event":{"end":"2009-07-02","place":"Lissabon, pt","start":"2009-06-29","title":"2009 IEEE/IFIP International Conference on Dependable Systems &amp; Networks","year":"2009"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INRIA/LIP6","Inria"],"keyword":["Bug finding","Linux","Program analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wysiwib exploiting fine grained program structure in a scriptable api usage protocol finding process","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/spe.2102","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-087.50-005673","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000312653300003","type":"wos"},{"id":"84872933779","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-74f4dbcf-c79e-4d9a-9c5e-53c32bd5bba6","ku-ee2a1572-7d00-4c4f-b2a8-95f315eb9b75"],"keyword":["Linux","bug finding","program analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A692F5BD3D3F9D993EB4F2BF56A3C7B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/spe.2102","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"inria","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Inria","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Datalogisk Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed Systems and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"inria lip6","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRIA/LIP6","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Julia","key":"lawallpau","last":"Lawall","locid":"5f9037c5-84e6-46b1-92d1-1632cb352c34","name":"Lawall, Julia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Julien Pierre Manuel","key":"brunelpau","last":"Brunel","locid":"0e806ba2-d01a-4f6d-9140-92ed0159cc60","name":"Brunel, Julien Pierre Manuel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","country":"dk","first":"Nicolas Jean-Michel","key":"palixpau","last":"Palix","locid":"6d3fa37e-7fd9-4dd5-9542-7575fae75345","name":"Palix, Nicolas Jean-Michel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","name":"Stuart, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Gilles","key":"mullerpau","last":"Muller","name":"Muller, Gilles","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/spe.2102","issn":["00380644","1097024X"],"issn_org":["00380644"],"issue":"1","journal":"Software: Practice & Experience","pages":"67-92","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Software: Practice & Experience","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84872933779"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-74f4dbcf-c79e-4d9a-9c5e-53c32bd5bba6","ku-ee2a1572-7d00-4c4f-b2a8-95f315eb9b75"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"WYSIWIB: Exploiting Fine-Grained Program Structure in a Scriptable API-Usage Protocol Finding Process","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.50-005673","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background Cancer often affects the quality of life and well-being of patients as well as their relatives. Previous studies have suggested that relatives should be involved in psychosocial rehabilitation to address the needs for an interpersonal relationship with others in the disease trajectory. We developed an innovative rehabilitation program to be offered to the patient and a relative as a pair. Objective The aim of the present pilot study was to examine the feasibility of the intervention in a randomized controlled trial (RCT) and to evaluate the impact on quality of life. Methods The study was designed as an RCT comparing the new multimodal psychosocial rehabilitation with the usual services. The intervention comprised three ‘supportive talks’ and a residential rehabilitation course. From March 2010 to March 2011, participation was offered at the time of diagnosis to patients with lung or gynecological cancer from two departments at Odense University Hospital in Denmark. Questionnaires were used to estimate changes in quality of life (EORTC-QLQ-C30 on global health status) and well-being (WHO-Five Well-Being Index) at baseline and after 2 and 12 months. Information on the participants’ views about the rehabilitation intervention was obtained from assessment charts and qualitative interviews. Results A total of 209 patients were assessed for eligibility, but only 42 pairs were randomized to the study. The 2-month follow-up was completed by 34 patients and 32 relatives, and 19 patients and 21 relatives completed the 12-month follow-up. A higher dropout rate at the 12-month follow-up was reported in the intervention group compared with controls. Quality of life and well-being increased for patients and relatives in both the intervention and the control group, and no clinically significant difference was observed between the intervention and the control group. Pairs reported that the time of inclusion was inconvenient and that rehabilitation ought to meet their changing needs. Conclusions The pilot study showed that it may be difficult to conduct an RCT of a psychosocial rehabilitation intervention for pairs, and difficulties with inclusion and drop out have to be addressed. Interventions need to be carefully developed and tested before evaluating an effect in a large-scale study.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ledderer, Loni Kraus","la Cour, Karen","Mogensen, Ole","Jakobsen, Erik","Christensen, René dePont","Kragstrup, Jakob","Hansen, Helle Ploug"],"cuid":["S02-089.86-024899"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Denmark","Family Relations","Feasibility Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neoplasms","Pilot Projects","Quality of Life","Sickness Impact Profile","Social Support"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility of a psychosocial rehabilitation intervention to enhance the involvement of relatives in cancer rehabilitation pilot study for a randomized controlled trial","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40271-013-0019-y","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.86-024899","identifier":[{"id":"23821379","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84891502474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a74fea3f-0def-405b-beb3-2388b29d5f3a","sdu-47a7d230-4003-47be-8126-1281128ae8f6"],"keyword":["Denmark","Family Relations","Feasibility Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neoplasms","Pilot Projects","Quality of Life","Sickness Impact Profile","Social Support"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-8F09097BF4BC03A505F8C19191D1509F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40271-013-0019-y","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Department of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Health, Man and Society","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Initiative for Activity Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Loni","key":"leddererpau","last":"Ledderer","locid":"1074e2b5-f8ea-42cb-9a89-f002df9f2510","name":"Ledderer, Loni Kraus","name_org":"Ledderer, Loni","orcid":"0000-0002-2685-4579","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen","key":"lacourpau","last":"la Cour","locid":"b938d806-88f5-44f4-a5a5-84031b5643db","name":"la Cour, Karen","orcid":"0000-0001-7126-0318","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","locid":"ddd33772-ea7a-4f39-87ee-f590fa739d37","name":"Mogensen, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"02052281-ce08-42b0-a620-e444bed0ac71","name":"Jakobsen, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-0052-7705","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"depontchristensenpau","last":"Depont Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","name_org":"Depont Christensen, René","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"René dePont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, René dePont","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"kragstruppau","last":"Kragstrup","name":"Kragstrup, Jakob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle Ploug","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"aff3454d-836b-44db-9a85-391f83361116","name":"Hansen, Helle Ploug","orcid":"0000-0002-5075-8739","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23821379"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s40271-013-0019-y","issn":["11781653","11781661"],"issn_org":["11781653"],"issue":"2","journal":"The Patient - Patient-Centered Outcomes Research","pages":"201-212","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","publisher_org":"Springer Science + Business Media","status":"p","title":"The Patient - Patient-Centered Outcomes Research","title_org":"The Patient","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84891502474"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a74fea3f-0def-405b-beb3-2388b29d5f3a","sdu-47a7d230-4003-47be-8126-1281128ae8f6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Feasibility of a Psychosocial Rehabilitation Intervention to Enhance the Involvement of Relatives in Cancer Rehabilitation: Pilot Study for a Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.86-024899","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: In 2008, a set of 41 quality indicators for antibiotic treatment of respiratory tract infections (RTIs) in general practice were developed in an international setting as part of the European project HAPPY AUDIT. Objectives: To investigate Danish general practitioners' (GPs') assessment of a set of internationally developed quality indicators and to explore if there is an association between the GPs' assessment of the indicators and their practice characteristics as well as their antibiotic prescription pattern. Methods: A total of 102 Danish GPs were invited to assess the 41 quality indicators. The GPs were categorized into two groups according to their assessment of indicators. Data concerning practice characteristics and antibiotic treatment were obtained during a three-week registration of patients with RTIs and were linked to the GPs' assessments of the indicators. Results: A total of 62 (61%) responded. Quality indicators focusing on the frequency of prescribing of narrow-spectrum penicillin were rated as suitable by more than 80% of the Danish GPs, while quality indicators concerning cephalosporins or quinolones were rated suitable by less than half of the GPs. The antibiotic prescribing pattern differed significantly and the GPs who disagreed on most indicators prescribed more macrolides and less narrow-spectrum penicillin than the GPs who agreed on most indicators. Conclusion: Even though an international expert panel agreed on a set of quality indicators for antibiotic treatment of RTIs, only a few of them were rated suitable by the GPs, who are supposed to use them.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Malene Plejdrup","Bjerrum, Lars","Gahrn-Hansen, Bente","Christensen, Rene de-Pont","Davidsen, Jesper Rømhild","Munck, Anders","Jarbol, Dorte Ejg"],"cuid":["S02-093.33-692230"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Antibiotics","General practice","Quality Improvement","Quality indicator","Respiratory tract infection"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Klinisk Mikrobiologi"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality indicators for treatment of respiratory tract infections an assessment by danish general practitioners","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/13814788.2012.730515","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.33-692230","identifier":[{"id":"84878992732","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000320197200003","type":"wos"},{"id":"23072550","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0f608fe4-ebd3-4fa9-8b84-a780ddf366fe","sdu-f567a75d-4207-4571-97f3-d3fcd16a6d5c"],"keyword":["Quality indicator","antibiotics","general practice","quality improvement","respiratory tract infection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-06A99DBB88E5B265FE6A0241D28F601D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/13814788.2012.730515","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["K