{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: No golden standard for analgesia in video-assisted thoracic surgery (VATS) lobectomy exists. A simple multimodal approach using an intercostal catheter (ICC) may be of benefit since acute post-operative pain following VATS lobectomy primarily originates from the chest drain area. METHODS: Prospective observational cohort. Forty-eight consecutive patients received a standardized regimen consisting of paracetamol, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug and gabapentin. Further, surgeons performed a single-shot paravertebral block (PVB) at five levels (15 ml of 0.5% bupivacaine) and inserted an ICC at the drain site level for continuous delivery of 6 ml of 0.25% bupivacaine h(-1). Pain scores at rest, mobilization and with the extended arms were followed until discharge or for 4 days. RESULTS: Forty-eight patients, mean age 64 years (CI: 61-68), were included. The mean time for the PVB and ICC placement was 5 min (CI: 4.7-5.9). The mean pain score at rest using a numerical rating scale (NRS, 0-10) was 85% of patients reporting satisfactory or very satisfactory pain treatment all days. CONCLUSIONS: Acute pain after VATS lobectomy may be adequately controlled using a multimodal non-opioid regime including PVB and an ICC. The low pain scores and reduced time used inserting the ICC may present an alternative to continuous epidural analgesia or conventional PVB.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wildgaard, Kim","Petersen, Rene H","Hansen, Henrik J","Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","Ringsted, Thomas K","Kehlet, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-044998"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multimodal analgesic treatment in video assisted thoracic surgery lobectomy using an intraoperative intercostal catheter","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ejcts/ezr151","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-044998","identifier":[{"id":"22219442","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84863847949","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a47c1693-04fa-4a44-b73d-1828e06207a7","ku-faa2286e-d51e-4c9d-8c76-4058c630714c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4CE0AD0C0F3F59E353E5CD4069088224"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ejcts/ezr151","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"wildgaardpau","last":"Wildgaard","locid":"7a02f381-3a9c-4afa-a64f-22495ec18d69","name":"Wildgaard, Kim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rene H.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa18983b-8811-4b3a-a7bd-b439cc52d3e3","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","name_org":"Petersen, Rene H.","orcid":"0000-0002-3586-1869","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik J.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b356d6b1-e9df-41d2-8001-e4fa6cc000e3","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","name_org":"Hansen, Henrik J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hasse","key":"møllersørensenpau","last":"Møller-Sørensen","name":"Møller-Sørensen, Hasse","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas K","key":"ringstedpau","last":"Ringsted","name":"Ringsted, Thomas K","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau"