{"abstract":"The objective of this study is to report the impact of computed tomography (CT) screening on the use of Video-Assisted Thoracic Surgery (VATS) in a randomized screening trial.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Petersen, René Horsleben","Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Dirksen, Asger","Pedersen, Jesper Holst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514394"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lung cancer screening and video assisted thoracic surgery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/JTO.0b013e31824fe942","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-514394","identifier":[{"id":"84861316780","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ca852664-cd0b-4d78-8b38-2fee1e8642f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-6-FEF6A9FBEFF4049AD3A89767D1CEC57B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/JTO.0b013e31824fe942","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"René Horsleben","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, René Horsleben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik Jessen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Asger","key":"dirksenpau","last":"Dirksen","locid":"2556e6b6-124a-4507-b427-0636d8cfdcbf","name":"Dirksen, Asger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Holst","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"db1db169-87ab-4843-9651-9ef18b28ae62","name":"Pedersen, Jesper Holst","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/jto.0b013e31824fe942","issn":["15560864","15561380"],"issn_org":["15560864"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Thoracic Oncology","pages":"1026-31","status":"p","title":"Journal of Thoracic Oncology","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861316780"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ca852664-cd0b-4d78-8b38-2fee1e8642f1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lung cancer screening and video-assisted thoracic surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514394","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Many drug substances are substrates for membrane transporters, which influence their intestinal absorption. Vigabatrin is a drug substance used in the treatment of epilepsy, mainly for treatment of infantile spasms. Vigabatrin is a substrate for the human proton-coupled amino acid transporter hPAT1. The aim of the project was to identify if transporters are involved in cellular uptake of vigabatrin in Caco-2 cells. Methods: The uptake rate of vigabatrin was measured in Caco-2 cells at pH 6.0 or 7.4 for 15 min after application of 0.1 – 25.0 mM vigabatrin. The inhibitory effect of selected amino acids and -derivatives on the apical vigabatrin uptake in Caco-2 cells was investigated. Vigabatrin samples were analyzed using liquid chromatography (LC) coupled to a mass selective detector (MSD). Results: The uptake rate of vigabatrin in Caco-2 cells was pH-dependent. The uptake of vigabatrin was saturable at pH 6.0 with a Michaelis constant, Km of 12.7 ± 3.7 mM and a maximal flux, Jmax of 3.7 ± 0.5 nmol•min-1•cm-2. The presences of hPAT1 ligands significantly inhibited the uptake of vigabatrin in Caco-2 cells at pH 6.0, whereas hPAT1 non-ligands did not. Discussion: The saturability of the uptake at pH 6.0 indicates involvement of a carrier-mediated process in vigabatrin absorption. The pH-dependency of the vigabatrin uptake suggests that the uptake may be driven by a proton-coupled transporter. The Km-value is comparable to Km- values for other hPAT1 substrates (1-20 mM). The interaction of hPAT1 ligands with the uptake is a further indication of hPAT1 involvement in vigabatrin absorption. It is concluded that the proton-coupled amino acid transporter hPAT1 is the main transporter responsible for absorption of vigabatrin in Caco-2 cells.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nøhr, Martha Kampp","Hansen, Steen Honoré","Brodin, Birger","Holm, René","Nielsen, Carsten Uhd"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527460"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the proton coupled amino acid transporter hpat000000000001 is the main transporter involved in vigabatrin uptake in intestinal caco 000000000002 cells","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-527460","ids":["ku-e052c753-3089-4cf6-8d24-075b62991a49"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D3A17982C9424BC10A1C67286504798F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martha Kampp","key":"nøhrpau","last":"Nøhr","locid":"2a6fe9c4-f17f-4475-8d13-bb056ca1ae72","name":"Nøhr, Martha Kampp","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen Honore'","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"665ce563-c12a-4ba3-a5c3-45076aafc490","name":"Hansen, Steen Honoré","name_org":"Hansen, Steen Honore'","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birger","key":"brodinpau","last":"Brodin","locid":"5cbca78f-7ea7-45f1-bf9b-52b468d2aa84","name":"Brodin, Birger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"René","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, René","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten Uhd","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5162a14c-9a34-499b-ac59-8dd6ff9464fc","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Uhd","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Lundbeck Pharma","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e052c753-3089-4cf6-8d24-075b62991a49"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The proton-coupled amino acid transporter hPAT1 is the main transporter involved in vigabatrin uptake in intestinal Caco-2 cells","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527460","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"BackgroundIn a large collaborative study (n > 50,000), common variants in the natriuretic peptide (NP) genes were found to be associated with circulating NP levels and also with blood pressure (BP) levels based on office BP measurements (OBPMs). It is unknown if determining an individual's BP by 24-h ambulatory BP measurements (ABPMs) will influence the effect of NP gene variations on BP levels.MethodsWe used rs632793 at the NPPB (NP precursor B) locus to investigate the relationship between genetically determined serum N-terminal pro-brain NP (NT-proBNP) concentrations and BP levels determined by both 24-h ABPMs and OBPMs in a population consisting of 1,397 generally healthy individuals taking no BP-lowering drugs.Resultsrs632793 was significantly correlated with serum Nt-proBNP levels (r = 0.10, P = 0.0003), and participants with the A:A genotype had lower serum Nt-proBNP levels than participants with the G:G genotype (geometric mean (95% confidence interval (CI)): 34.8 (31.5-38.4) pg/ml vs. 48.1 (41.9-55.3) pg/ml, P = 0.0002), but higher 24-h ambulatory BP levels (mean difference (95% CI): 2.0 (0.1-4.1) mm Hg, P = 0.043, for systolic BP and 1.7 (0.4-3.1) mm Hg, P = 0.011, for diastolic BP). Office BP decreased across the genotypes from A:A to G:G, but the differences did not reach statistical significance (P = 0.12).ConclusionsThis study suggests that 24-h ABPMs is a better method than OBPMs to detect significant differences in BP levels related to genetic variance and provides further evidence that the NP system plays an important role in BP regulation.American Journal of Hypertension 2012; doi:10.1038/ajh.2012.96.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Jørgen","Nielsen, Søren J","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Hansen, Tine W","Olsen, Michael H","Berg, Nikolaj D","Linneberg, Allan","Madsbad, Sten","Fenger, Mogens","Berg, Nikolaj D"],"cuid":["S02-081.21-043948"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic variation in the natriuretic peptide system circulating natriuretic peptide levels and blood pressure an ambulatory blood pressure study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ajh.2012.96","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-081.21-043948","identifier":[{"id":"84866390391","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22785411","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8236c45c-0c2e-4df3-8ac9-da0525836953","sdu-cd54bc9c-b3f4-449b-9d22-2e9f0a00b44f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4EA4C397F631CDA2150E346B187C6763"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ajh.2012.96","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of C