{"abstract":"This report has been prepared for the Danish Energy Agency. It summarizes the results of the project entitled: “Development of HCCI engines for DME”. The project has been financed by “EFP 06”. The chapters about theoretical and experimental studies have been written using the language and terminology typical for this field of research but the introduction and the final chapters have been written in a language focused on communicating the topics to a wide audience to make the report as useful as possible.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Kim Rene","Pedersen, Troels Dyhr","Schramm, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-330746"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of hcci engines for dimethyl ether","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/52916634/Development_of_HCCI_Engines.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-330746","ids":["dtu-580a9fa6-6579-4253-84db-a9aa02ff20fe"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3595C15A1BEC35C119E98FD19D7D3472"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/52916634/Development_of_HCCI_Engines.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Thermal Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Rene","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"16beb9c6-c0e1-42e6-93df-307d740d5dbd","name":"Hansen, Kim Rene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels Dyhr","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b6b626e0-f7fe-448c-aea3-faf1077b89d2","name":"Pedersen, Troels Dyhr","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"schrammpau","last":"Schramm","locid":"fb1feeee-ad9a-444e-9329-08d8daa50e1d","name":"Schramm, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-0771-5415","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"74","publisher":"DTU Mechanical Engineering","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-580a9fa6-6579-4253-84db-a9aa02ff20fe"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Development of HCCI Engines for Dimethyl Ether","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-330746","year":"2011","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with schizophrenia often suffer from cognitive dysfunction, including impaired learning and memory. We recently demonstrated that long-term potentiation in rat hippocampus, a mechanistic model of learning and memory, is linked to gene expression changes in immunity-related processes involved in complement activity and antigen presentation. We therefore aimed to examine whether key regulators of these processes are genetic susceptibility factors in schizophrenia. METHODS: Analysis of genetic association was based on data mining of genotypes from a German genome-wide association study and a multiplex GoldenGate tag single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP)-based assay of Norwegian and Danish case-control samples (Scandinavian Collaboration on Psychiatric Etiology), including 1133 patients with schizophrenia and 2444 healthy control subjects. RESULTS: Allelic associations were found across all three samples for eight common SNPs in the complement control-related gene CSMD2 (CUB and Sushi Multiple Domains 2) on chromosome 1p35.1-34.3, of which rs911213 reached a statistical significance comparable to that of a genome wide threshold (p value = 4.0 × 10(-8); odd ratio = .73, 95% confidence interval = .65-.82). The second most significant gene was CSMD1 on chromosome 8p23.2, a homologue to CSMD2. In addition, we observed replicated associations in the complement surface receptor CD46 as well as the major histocompatibility complex genes HLA-DMB and HLA-DOA. CONCLUSIONS: These data demonstrate a significant role of complement control-related genes in the etiology of schizophrenia and support disease mechanisms that involve the activity of immunity-related pathways in the brain.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Håvik, Bjarte","Le Hellard, Stephanie","Rietschel, Marcella","Lybæk, Helle","Djurovic, Srdjan","Mattheisen, Manuel","Mühleisen, Thomas W","Degenhardt, Franziska","Priebe, Lutz","Maier, Wolfgang","Breuer, Rene","Schulze, Thomas G","Agartz, Ingrid","Melle, Ingrid","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Bramham, Clive R","Nöthen, Markus M","Stevens, Beth","Werge, Thomas","Andreassen, Ole A","Cichon, Sven","Steen, Vidar M"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438062"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the complement control related genes csmd000000000001 and csmd000000000002 associate to schizophrenia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2011.01.030","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-438062","identifier":[{"id":"21439553","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79958839837","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4abaafd8-93e4-4d50-a910-1bdf5863ace5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A059F8595489A3A05EC0E238EF57DAC4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2011.01.030","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Bjarte","key":"håvikpau","last":"Håvik","name":"Håvik, Bjarte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stephanie","key":"lehellardpau","last":"Le Hellard","name":"Le Hellard, Stephanie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marcella","key":"rietschelpau","last":"Rietschel","name"