{"abstract":"Just like other software, Java profiles benefits from refactoring when they have been used and have evolved for some time. This paper presents a refactoring of the Real-Time Specification for Java (RTSJ) and the Safety Critical Java (SCJ) profile (JSR-302). It highlights core concepts and makes it a suitable foundation for the proposed levels of SCJ. The ongoing work of specifying the SCJ profile builds on sub classing of RTSJ. This spurred our interest in a refactoring approach. It starts by extracting the common kernel of the specifications in a core package, which defines interfaces only. It is then possible to refactor SCJ with its three levels and RTSJ in such a way that each profile is in a separate package. This refactoring results in cleaner class hierarchies with no superfluous methods, well defined SCJ levels, elimination of SCJ annotations like @SCJAllowed, thus making the profiles easier to comprehend and use for application developers and students.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Søndergaard, Hans","Thomsen, Bent","Ravn, Anders Peter","Hansen, Rene Rydhof","Bøgholm, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-081.25-011461"],"event":{"end":"2011-03-31","place":"Newport Beach, California, us","start":"2011-03-28","title":"14th IEEE International Symposium on Object/Component/Service-Oriented Real-Time Distributed Computing","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["It","Real time Java","Real time embedded systems","Refactoring","Safety critical Java"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"refactoring real time java profiles","src":["aau","via"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ISORC.2011.23","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-081.25-011461","identifier":[{"id":"79957989691","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-eff0477f-558c-48fb-aece-194d24c6789f","via-b39e7cff-7b0a-4059-b1fa-09049de4e23f"],"keyword":["Java profiles","RTSJ","Real-Time Specification for Java","Real-time Java","Real-time embedded systems","Refactoring","SCJ","Safety Critical Java","it"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-17DD6B1344FA054F6A8EC3D77F607623"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/articleDetails.jsp?arnumber=5753598","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ISORC.2011.23","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Uddannelser, Ingeniør- og businessuddannelserne, Software Technology Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, CISS - Center for Embedded Software Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Daisy - Center for Data-intensive Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Database and Programming Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"b6cbfca1-82d7-456b-90c0-4f5c76d359c9","name":"Søndergaard, Hans","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"e47d25c8-df5c-453f-bcd7-0921f9915911","name":"Thomsen, Bent","orcid":"0000-0002-5853-7973","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Peter","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"6aded57b-47a6-4a4a-abac-b2631717a2b7","name":"Ravn, Anders Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Rydhof","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d92ec90d-a8b7-4c01-acbe-ebab21f3f0c3","name":"Hansen, Rene Rydhof","orcid":"0000-0002-5688-6432","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"bøgholmpau","last":"Bøgholm","locid":"0a4826c4-54e1-49f2-8ec7-7c95d1770346","name":"Bøgholm, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/isorc.2011.23","pages":"109-116","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"Object/Component/Service-Oriented Real-Time Distributed Computing (ISORC), 2011 14th IEEE International Symposium on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79957989691"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-eff0477f-558c-48fb-aece-194d24c6789f","via-b39e7cff-7b0a-4059-b1fa-09049de4e23f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","VIA University College"],"title":"Refactoring Real-Time Java Profiles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.25-011461","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Lobectomy using video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) still is a controversial operation despite its many observed benefits. The controversy may be due to difficulties performing the procedure. This study addresses a standardized anterior approach facilitating the operation. METHODS: This report describes 156 VATS lobectomies performed with a uniform anterior three-port technique. The surgeon and the assistant stand on the abdominal side of the patient, and the setup is independent of the lobe to be resected. RESULTS: From 2005 to 2007, 156 VATS lobectomies and 13 conversions (7.7%) were performed with an anterior three-port technique. No mortality occurred among the VATS lobectomies during a 30-day period. The major comorbidity rate was 78%. The comorbidities included former thoracic surgery (9%) or a history of another cancer (22%), indicating potentially difficult surgery and a nonselected population. The majority (92%) of the patients had lung cancer. The major postoperative problem was air leakage, which usually prolongs the tube time and the in-hospital stay, but a \"no-touch fissure\" technique significantly reduced the median tube time to 4 days and the postoperative hospital stay to 5 days. CONCLUSIONS: This study shows that VATS lobectomies can be performed using a standardized anterior approach with low rates of conversion and morbidity. A \"no-touch fissure\" technique lowers the postoperative tube time, the in-hospital stay, and the number of patients with prolonged air leakage. A uniform anterior approach facilitates VATS lobectomy and makes this advanced procedure more easily adaptable by many surgeons familiar with an open anterior approach. The findings show that VATS lobectomy can be performed safely for a large proportion of lung cancer patients.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Henrik Jessen","Petersen, René Horsleben","Christensen, Merete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-504820"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma surgery","Blood Loss Surgical","Comorbidity","Dissection methods","Humans","Length of Stay statistics numerical data","Lung Neoplasms secondary","Lymph Node Excision methods","Middle Aged","Pneumonectomy methods","Postoperative Complications epidemiology","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Surgical Stapling","Thoracic Surgery Video Assisted methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"video assisted thoracoscopic surgery vats lobectomy using a standardized anterior approach","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-504820","identifier":[{"id":"79954427379","type":"scopus"},{"id":"20927543","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ba93e645-838f-4762-8b3a-d3ccc2f93277"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma/surgery","Blood Loss, Surgical","Comorbidity","Dissection/methods","Electrocoagulation/methods","Humans","Length of Stay/statistics & numerical data","Lung Neoplasms/secondary","Lymph Node Excision/methods","Middle Aged","Pneumonectomy/methods","Postoperative Complications/epidemiology","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Surgical Stapling","Thoracic Surgery, Video-Assisted/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-244585C84211001B778A4127526308D3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Jessen","key":"hansenpa